\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 : the abrasive justice taking  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights back to the 17th century\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington \par \uc2 1,248 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par 06:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The man who wrote the draft supreme court opinion overturning Roe v Wade is known for his quick temper and \u8216\'20\'18traditional\u8217\'20\'19 values\par \par \uc2 For a member of one of the most august and venerable institutions in American public life, \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has provoked an astonishing outpouring of jarring adjectives this week. \u8220\'20\'1CAppalling and heinous\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2022/05/samuel-alito-roe-v-wade-abortion-draft?utm_source=nl&utm_brand=vf&utm_mailing=VF_Hive_050422&utm_medium=email&bxid=5be9eaa224c17c6adf09becd&cndid=31644352&hasha=0f96eec32ab131eaf106dcf2a52fd67a&hashb=cfab8fe082106889b4571d5088ac065b89fc3a26&hashc=93df1d59dd8381253acc03a96b6458f2390e081c225d587853d09e8df84ea9b1&esrc=newsletteroverlay&source=EDT_VYF_NEWSLETTER_0_HIVE_ZZ&utm_campaign=VF_Hive_050422&utm_content=B&utm_term=VYF_Hive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vanity Fair}}}\uc2  ; \u8220\'20\'1Cacidic and extreme\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://slate.com/news-and-politics/2022/05/supreme-court-draft-abortion-leak-roe-overturned-explained.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Slate}}}\uc2  ; \u8220\'20\'1Cdreadful and repugnant\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/05/03/supreme-court-might-never-recover-overturning-roe-v-wade/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post}}}\uc2  ; \u8220\'20\'1Cscathing and dismissive\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/opinion/story/2022-05-03/editorial-the-supreme-court-overturn-roe-vs-wade-its-time-to-stand-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The strong words were directed at the draft ruling written by Alito and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked to Politico}}}\uc2  that, barring a possible but unlikely change of heart by any of Alito\u8217\'20\'19s conservative peers on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , will eviscerate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in America.\par \par \uc2 Though millions had been bracing themselves for the court\u8217\'20\'19s newly emboldened rightwing majority to deliver a blow to Roe v Wade, the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has been law of the land for half a century, Alito\u8217\'20\'19s attack was so brutal and direct it still left many dumbstruck.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe and Casey must be overruled,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito wrote, referring to the 1973 landmark ruling along with its 1992 affirmation in Planned Parenthood v Casey. \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is conceivable that some of the sharper edges of Alito\u8217\'20\'19s devastating 98-page screed will be smoothed out before the final ruling is delivered in coming weeks. Other supreme court justices, notably \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , might demand as much in order to spare their own blushes.\par \par \uc2 But none of that will alter the fact that Alito will forever be known as the supreme court justice who destroyed a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her own body and who set the US on a regressive course pointing back to the 17th century.\par \par \uc2 At least that\u8217\'20\'19s what is suggested by some of the juridical reasoning that Alito deploys in his draft ruling. As Emily Bell, director of the Tow Center for Digital Journalism at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , noted, the draft draws heavily from two treatises written by an English jurist, Sir Matthew Hale, describing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat crime\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat misprision\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 No matter that Hale was writing in 1673. Or that, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emilybell/status/1521450341983739904?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1521450341983739904%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.vanityfair.com%2Fnews%2F2022%2F05%2Fsamuel-alito-roe-v-wade-abortion-draft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bell pointed out}}}\uc2 , his distinguished career included securing the executions of two women as witches and writing the definitive text for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/emilybell/status/1521452342318612480/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marital rape exemption}}}\uc2  that said that husbands cannot be culpable of raping their wives because \u8220\'20\'1Cby their mutual matrimonial consent and contract the wife hath given up herself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alito leans on Hale and other voices from the distant past to underline his main contention: that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Constitution makes no reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D and as a result there can be no constitutional right. He glides over the fact that the constitution, written in 1787, equally makes no reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.yahoo.com/supreme-court-rejects-bid-block-145558280.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 airplanes}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wearechange.org/u-s-supreme-court-says-no-license-necessary-to-drive-automobile-on-public-highwaysstreets/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 car license plates}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/04/28/supreme-court-snapchat-case-484925"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Snapchat}}}\uc2 , though that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t prevented the nine justices applying constitutional laws to those fields.\par \par \uc2 Alito\u8217\'20\'19s other central argument in scuppering Roe is that constitutional rights have to be \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply rooted in the Nation\u8217\'20\'19s history and traditions\u8221\'20\'1D. Yet, interestingly, that standard makes no appearance in the US constitution either.\par \par \uc2 That Alito should have made such an abrasively aggressive, no-holds-barred, demolition of Roe v Wade comes as no surprise to those who have observed his style of jurisprudence up close. The justice has a famously quick temper and razor-sharp tongue that he\u8217\'20\'19s even prepared to turn against his colleagues on the conservative side of the court \u8211\'20\'13 especially the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , who is looking increasingly isolated amid the rightward march of the majority.\par \par \uc2 Alito responded derisively to a recent opinion written by Roberts in a religious liberty case relating to same-sex couples fostering children. The ruling sided with the religious group, but for Alito that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision might as well be written on the dissolving paper sold in magic shops,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito complained.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s very intelligent, extremely aggressive, often sarcastic,\u8221\'20\'1D one lawyer who has argued a case in front of Alito told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s not pleasant to argue in front of. Other justices are incisive but conversational questioners \u8211\'20\'13 he is combative and hostile towards people he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alito, 72, was born in Trenton, New Jersey, to an immigrant Italian father and Italian-American mother. Educated at Princeton and Yale law school, he rose up the legal ladder through the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  (DoJ) in the Ronald Reagan years.\par \par \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  nominated him for a seat on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court in 2006.\par \par \uc2 His anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  tendencies stretch far back. In 1985, in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.archives.gov/files/news/samuel-alito/accession-060-97-761/Acc060-97-761-box1-Alito.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 job application for a post at the DoJ}}}\uc2 , he boasted about his contribution arguing before the supreme court that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe constitution does not protect a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the exact same line he pursues in his draft ruling 37 years later.\par \par \uc2 In the same job application he also bragged about having argued before the court that \u8220\'20\'1Cracial and ethnic quotas should not be allowed\u8221\'20\'1D. That presents a chilling portent of his position in a separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/jan/24/us-supreme-court-affirmative-action-cases-college-admission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blockbuster case}}}\uc2  scheduled to be heard by the supreme court next term that challenges affirmative action at Harvard and the University of North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Since joining the court he has staked his position, alongside \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , as the gatekeeper of the court\u8217\'20\'19s reactionary wing. With the recent addition of fellow conservatives nominated by Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , Kavanaugh and Amy Coney Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 his star is now in the ascendant.\par \par \uc2 In 2007 he wrote the majority opinion that declined an appeal from Lilly Ledbetter that would have established equal pay for women, on grounds that she had missed a filing deadline. \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s riposte came in his very first act as president when he signed into law the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://obamawhitehouse.archives.gov/the-press-office/remarks-president-barack-obama-lilly-ledbetter-fair-pay-restoration-act-bill-signin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lilly Ledbetter Fair Pay Restoration Act}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bad blood between the two men thickened in 2010 when Obama used his State of the Union speech to criticize the supreme court for unleashing corporate money into elections with its contentious \uc2 Citizens United\uc2  ruling, which Alito supported. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ZrANnq3OaM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot true\u8221\'20\'1D,}}}\uc2  lip readers could clearly discern the justice muttering.\par \par \uc2 A lifelong Catholic who has frequently expressed his fear that the US is moving away from traditional values, the justice has also been at the forefront of the conservative push to advantage religious belief against individual liberty. He wrote the majority opinion in the 2014 \uc2 Hobby Lobby\uc2  case that allowed Christian-run companies to forgo contraception in their health insurance packages.\par \par \uc2 That leaning could prove significant should Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling overturning Roe become final, potentially unleashing a whirlwind of regressive opinions from the court.\par \par \uc2 Top of the list of vulnerable targets is same-sex marriage. In his draft ruling, Alito goes out of his way to reassure those concerned about the future of gay marriage by saying that his stance on Roe was unique as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fundamentally different\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not what he wrote in his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/576/14-556/#tab-opinion-3427257"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dissent to Obergefell}}}\uc2 , the 2015 ruling that guaranteed the right of same-sex couples to marry. In it, he asked whether the constitution gives a view on what to do about gay marriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt does not,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe Constitution leaves that question to be decided by the people of each state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If that argument sounds familiar, that\u8217\'20\'19s because it is. It\u8217\'20\'19s identical to the reasoning he presents in his draft ruling eviscerating the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220506ei56000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
