\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 After victory in the US, now the far right is coming for  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws in Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 Sian Norris \par \uc2 984 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 17:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The attack on Roe v Wade has roots in well-funded organisations whose tentacles have spread across the Atlantic\par \par \uc2 For those of us who have been watching the assault against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US for years, this week\u8217\'20\'19s leaked supreme court draft opinion \u8211\'20\'13 which could pave the way for an overturning of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 came as no surprise.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US up to the point a foetus can survive outside the womb, and the religious and far-right have been gunning for it since it was introduced in 1973. Evangelical ideologues, far-right actors and radical-right billionaires have organised to undermine women\u8217\'20\'19s right to safe, legal abortions through a combination of violence against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2015/11/29/us/30abortion-clinic-violence.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clinics}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/may/30/he-gave-so-much-the-woman-fighting-the-abortion-wars-begun-by-george-tiller"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doctors}}}\uc2 , dark money and political influence.\par \par \uc2 So, how did the US get here?\par \par \uc2 After years of legal assaults that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/evidence-you-can-use/targeted-regulation-abortion-providers-trap-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricted \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  and targeted clinics in Republican states; years of disinformation spread by \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis pregnancy centres\u8221\'20\'1D, where women are persuaded to not have abortions; and years of burdensome demands on women to endure ultrasounds, gain parental consent and put up with counselling in order to have a termination, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election opened the door for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to end in the US.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, it required courts, not politicians, to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s where the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/05/trump-abortion-supreme-court?utm_term=Autofeed&CMP=twt_gu&utm_medium&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federalist Society}}}\uc2  comes in. Headed by \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2 , the legal organisation supported anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers across the US into positions of influence where they could draft laws to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks \u8230\'20\'26 12 weeks \u8230\'20\'26 six weeks \u8230\'20\'26 and completely. The end goal was for anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  states to try to implement one of these laws, where it would be challenged again and again until it reached the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 To do that, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement needed supreme court justices who would enact its agenda. They got their way with the help of the leader of the Senate, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , who blocked President Obama from nominating a supreme court judge, leaving the field open for Trump to promote the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 . After that came two more Trump-appointed justices: \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 That was the judicial assault on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. But that assault could only happen with the help of money \u8230\'20\'26 and lots of it. Luckily for the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, there are plenty of wealthy foundations keen to fund the cause. They include the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epfweb.org/sites/default/files/2021-06/Tip%20of%20the%20Iceberg%20June%202021%20Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeVos, Prince, and the Templeton Foundation}}}\uc2 , which have helped to support organisations such as the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  (ADF), \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  and Focus on the Family.\par \par \uc2 Backed by billionaire funding, organisations such as the ADF took the fight against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the courts \u8211\'20\'13 helping to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adfmedia.org/case/mccullen-v-coakley#:~:text=WASHINGTON%20%E2%80%94%20The%20U.S.%20Supreme%20Court,filed%20the%20lawsuit%20McCullen%20v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 secure a ban on buffer zones}}}\uc2  and so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cpartial birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, and supporting the notorious {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/feb/20/alliance-defending-freedom-multimillion-dollar-conservative-christian-group-attacking-lgbtq-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hobby Lobby case}}}\uc2 , which stated that employers should not have to cover birth control on employees\u8217\'20\'19 healthcare plans if it was against the owner\u8217\'20\'19s religious beliefs.\par \par \uc2 These organisations and their billionaire backers have transatlantic reach. Take the DeVos and Koch Foundation-supported Heritage Foundation, which has welcomed a range of Conservative MPs to discuss free speech \u8211\'20\'13 including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.conservatives.com/news/2022/standing-up-for-our-values"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Dowden}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/priti-patels-speech-to-heritage-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Priti Patel}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/2010-06-30-heritage-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liam Fox}}}\uc2 . It was announced on the day of the supreme court leak that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/europe/event/last-exit-freedom-britain-after-brexit-and-the-future-conservative-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lord David Frost}}}\uc2  would soon be addressing the organisation.\par \par \uc2 Then there\u8217\'20\'19s the ADF, which spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epfweb.org/sites/default/files/2021-06/Tip%20of%20the%20Iceberg%20June%202021%20Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $23.3m}}}\uc2  in Europe between 2008 and 2019, when its European arm\u8217\'20\'19s youth conference played host to the Conservative MP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm/cmregmem/191105/bruce_fiona.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fiona Bruce}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ADF International {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bylinetimes.com/2022/01/07/the-global-religious-right-network-behind-the-gay-marriage-cake-battle/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intervened}}}\uc2  in Belfast\u8217\'20\'19s notorious \u8220\'20\'1Cgay cake\u8221\'20\'1D case and is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/ultra-conservative-institute-has-infiltrated-polish-state-to-ban-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allied}}}\uc2  with organisations that lobbied to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Poland. The US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legal organisation, the American Center for Law and Justice (ACLJ), a second religious freedom organisation that takes on legal cases to challenge \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights, has also operated in Europe. Set up by the Republican \uc2 Pat Robertson\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2013/07/09/us/pat-robertson-facebook-remark/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 famously accused}}}\uc2  feminism of turning women into lesbians, ACLJ\u8217\'20\'19s chief counsel is a former Trump defence attorney, Jay Sekulow. ACLJ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epfweb.org/sites/default/files/2021-06/Tip%20of%20the%20Iceberg%20June%202021%20Final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent}}}\uc2  $15.7m in Europe from 2008-2019.\par \par \uc2 So far you can see how big money, the judiciary and religious freedom movements have come together in the US and Europe. But there\u8217\'20\'19s another active force that has pushed us towards the end of Roe: the far right.\par \par \uc2 Across the far-right infosphere, men discuss the need to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to reverse what they term the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/aug/16/the-myth-of-eurabia-how-a-far-right-conspiracy-theory-went-mainstream"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great replacement}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a conspiracy theory that posits white people are being \u8220\'20\'1Creplaced\u8221\'20\'1D by migration from the global south, and that, in the US in particular, this replacement is aided by feminists repressing the white birthrate via \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Conspiracy theories such as the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat replacement\u8221\'20\'1D sound extreme. But when it comes to the US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  row, such views are mainstream. Take this quote from the former Republican congressman \uc2 Steve King\uc2 , who represented Iowa between 2003-2021. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/iowa-rep-steve-king-austria-white-nationalist_n_5bca4851e4b0a8f17eec6001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He claimed}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe US subtracts from its population a million of our babies in the form of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We add to our population approximately 1.8 million of \u8216\'20\'18somebody else\u8217\'20\'19s babies\u8217\'20\'19 who are raised in another culture before they get to us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Far-right theories circulate globally \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why people outside the US shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t just act in solidarity with American women at this time, but prepare to stand up against the possible erosion of their own hard-won rights.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sian Norris is the chief social and European affairs reporter at Byline Times. She is writing a book about the far-right attack on productive rights called Bodies Under Siege\par \par \uc2 Do you have an opinion on the issues raised in this article? If you would like to submit a letter of up to 300 words to be considered for publication, email it to us at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:guardian.letters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 guardian.letters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55002k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
