\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Louisiana Republicans advance bill to make  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 808 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 17:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 24\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since supreme court draft ruling was published, Democrats have warned of a likely torrent of challenges to established rights\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Louisiana have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2022/05/05/louisiana-abortion-bill-would-make-crime-murder/9656102002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advanced}}}\uc2  a bill to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a crime of murder, as a draft decision that would end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights continues to spark nationwide protests and police in Washington raised \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/non-scalable-fence-erected-supreme-court-abortion-related-protests-rcna27452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 non-scalable}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D fences around the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Supporters admitted the bill, under which a woman terminating a pregnancy or anyone assisting her could be charged, was unconstitutional \u8211\'20\'13 as long as Roe v Wade was law.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to formally overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 case which established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in June.\par \par \uc2 Danny McCormick, the state representative behind the Louisiana bill, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t wait on the supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the draft ruling that seems set to overturn {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1971/70-18"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe}}}\uc2  was published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2  on Monday night, Democrats have warned of a likely torrent of challenges to established rights.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has sounded the alarm about threats to privacy-based rights including the rights to contraception ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1964/496"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Griswold v Connecticut, 1965}}}\uc2  ) and to same-sex marriage ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/2014/14-556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obergefell v Hodges, 2015}}}\uc2  ). The president also raised the prospect of attacks on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/biden-lgbtq-children-next-target-maga-crowd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teaching}}}\uc2  of LGTBQ+ children.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Biden said Republicans pushing such cases constituted \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organisation \u8230\'20\'26 in recent American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The same day in Texas, the Republican governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/story/news/2022/05/04/gov-greg-abbott-supreme-court-case-requiring-education-undocumented-children/9652463002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised}}}\uc2  the possibility of challenging a 1982 ruling which said states must provide free education to all children, including those of undocumented migrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we will resurrect that case and challenge this issue again,\u8221\'20\'1D Greg Abbott said.\par \par \uc2 Abbott is a prominent figure on the hard right of that Republican party, with rumoured presidential ambitions.\par \par \uc2 Undocumented migration is a key issue in his re-election fight against \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , a former congressman, and a central part of the national Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/01/republicans-politics-us-immigration-midterm-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 approach to midterm elections}}}\uc2  in which they are favoured to take back Congress.\par \par \uc2 Abbott was speaking to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/story/news/2022/05/04/gov-greg-abbott-supreme-court-case-requiring-education-undocumented-children/9652463002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative radio host}}}\uc2  Joe Pagliarulo.\par \par \uc2 Pagliarulo said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re talking about public tax dollars, public property tax dollars going to fund these schools to teach children who are five, six, seven, 10 years old, who don\u8217\'20\'19t even have remedial English skills. This is a real burden on communities. What can you do about that?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Abbott said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe challenges put on our public systems is extraordinary. Texas already long ago sued the federal government about having to incur the costs of the education program, in a case called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1981/80-1538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plyler v Doe}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the supreme court ruled against us on the issue about denying, or let\u8217\'20\'19s say Texas having to bear that burden. I think we will resurrect that case and challenge this issue again, because the expenses are extraordinary and the times are different than when Plyler v Doe was issued many decades ago.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most progressive concern has focused on rulings which protect privacy rights, among them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/2002/02-102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawrence v Texas (2003)}}}\uc2 , which said it was unconstitutional to make gay sex a crime.\par \par \uc2 Charles Kaiser, a leading historian of gay life in the US, said the draft Roe opinion \u8220\'20\'1Cso blithely disregards past precedents, it could suggest a willingness to overturn previous court decisions enshrining certain fundamental rights for LGBTQ+ people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne passage in particular set off alarm bells for activists who think its reasoning could jeopardise the court\u8217\'20\'19s decisions legalising sodomy and the right of members of the same sex to marry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , Kaiser said, \u8220\'20\'1Ccited those decisions and denigrated them by saying they used criteria \u8216\'20\'18which at a higher level of generality could license fundamental rights to rights to illicit drug use, prostitution, and the like\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/us-law-week/abortion-draft-raises-alarm-over-future-of-privacy-lgbt-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to Bloomberg Law}}}\uc2 , Cynthia Soohoo, co-director of the Human Rights and Gender Justice Clinic at the \uc2 City University of New York\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe same arguments that Justice Alito makes against recognising constitutional protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be made about \u8230\'20\'26 the right to access contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Katherine Franke, director of the Center for Gender and Sexuality Law at \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 , told the same site: \u8220\'20\'1COnce you kick out the stilts underneath Roe there\u8217\'20\'19s nothing to rest those other decisions on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no constitutional foundation for the Lawrence decision saying that criminalising same-sex sex is unconstitutional, or the Obergefell decision that says same-sex couples have a constitutional right to marry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the far right, Peter Brimelow, the founder of the VDare nativist website whom the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/30/business/media/tucker-carlson-fox-news-takeaways.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 linked}}}\uc2  to the Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jezebel.com/former-national-review-editor-calls-for-supreme-court-t-1848879685?utm_medium=sharefromsite&utm_source=_twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  to have greeted news of the draft Roe ruling by writing: \u8220\'20\'1CNext stop Brown vs Board!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was a reference to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1940-1955/347us483"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brown v Board of Education}}}\uc2 , the 1954 case which ended racial segregation in public schools.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55002k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
