\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Guardian view on what follows Roe v Wade: it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stop here\b0\par\par\uc2 Editorial \par \uc2 620 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 17:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Further attempts to restrict rights should be expected following state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. And they won\u8217\'20\'19t be limited to women in the US\par \par \uc2 It has taken anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners a concerted five-decade campaign to get here: the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s provisional decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to overturn Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 . More than half of America\u8217\'20\'19s women can expect to live in states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is banned or greatly restricted}}}\uc2  if, as anticipated, next month\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is largely unchanged. Yet that will not mark the climactic triumph of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby. In their eyes, it is merely a staging post to further restrictions on other matters too, affecting more people \u8211\'20\'13 including outside the US.\par \par \uc2 First, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2022/may/05/us-supreme-court-ready-to-overturn-right-to-abortion-what-happens-next-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 they will not be satisfied}}}\uc2  with pre-Roe laws or even the trigger laws waiting for Roe v Wade to fall. There will be a new drive to remove exemptions from bans, such as for rape and incest. While many state laws have so far targeted providers, we can expect increasing attempts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fairtrials.org/articles/news/roe-wade-mass-criminalisation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminalise}}}\uc2  women who have abortions \u8211\'20\'13 or are suspected of having done so. Louisiana already has a trigger law in place to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/case/scotus-june-medical-services/abortion-in-louisiana/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after six weeks}}}\uc2  ; on Wednesday, a House committee voted for a bill that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-crime-louisiana-1530c0893084e84fd83728329278d536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would make \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  a homicide}}}\uc2  and allow women to be charged for obtaining one.\par \par \uc2 Strikingly, the bill would also change the state\u8217\'20\'19s legal definition of a person from a fertilised egg implanted in the womb to simply a fertilised egg. That points to a second issue: activists are already beginning to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 target forms of birth control}}}\uc2 , such as emergency contraception and some intrauterine devices that can stop fertilised eggs from being implanted, by wrongly framing them as abortifacients. Third, the draft opinion drives a bulldozer through the foundations of other rights similarly rooted in privacy protections, such as LGBTQ+ rights; even if it adds that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unique because it concerns life or potential life, those all become more vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 Finally, this is not just about the symbolic power of overturning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections in the world\u8217\'20\'19s superpower. US anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have long been spreading their message abroad, through direct activism and funding. They have coordinated and poured {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2017/oct/26/us-groups-pour-millions-into-anti-abortion-campaign-in-latin-america-and-caribbean"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millions of dollars}}}\uc2  into campaigns for restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Latin America. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/opinions/2021/12/14/the-us-war-on-abortion-rights-will-harm-women-everywhere"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Africa has been another prime target}}}\uc2 . According to openDemocracy, US Christian organisations have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opendemocracy.net/en/5050/trump-us-christian-spending-global-revealed/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent at least $280m of \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  supporting campaigns to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LGBTQ+ rights internationally. Bans kill. Almost all unsafe abortions and related deaths occur in Africa, Latin America and south and west Asia.\par \par \uc2 Globally, the trend has overwhelmingly been for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  liberalisation: about 50 countries have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/sites/default/files/documents/World-Abortion-Map-AcceleratingProgress.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relaxed laws}}}\uc2  in the last two and a half decades, with only a handful increasing restrictions. US funding played a part in the near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that came into force {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jan/23/death-threats-and-phone-calls-the-women-answering-cries-for-help-one-year-on-from-polands-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Poland}}}\uc2  last year. There, as in the US, the right has captured state institutions; the public opposed further restrictions. In both places, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby took root and found victory in specific conditions.\par \par \uc2 Not everything is transplantable. The American groups that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/sexes/archive/2013/01/why-american-pro-life-dollars-are-pouring-into-ireland/266981/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 funded the anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  lobby in Ireland}}}\uc2  were repaid with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/may/26/ireland-votes-by-landslide-to-legalise-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landslide vote for legalisation}}}\uc2 . But the rise of misogynistic rightwing populism in many places, and attempts to inflame culture wars in the UK and elsewhere by Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s admirers, remind us that there is no room for complacency; 50 years ago, few US evangelicals saw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue. The supreme court draft decision has given anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners new momentum. Their targets and actions must now be monitored closely by opponents outside the US as well as within.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55002k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
