\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a hell of a scary time\u8217\'20\'19: leading US feminists on the threat to Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Sirin Kale, Leah Harper and Ann Lee \par \uc2 3,083 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 17:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in jeopardy, Judy Chicago, Bonnie Greer, Rebecca Solnit and more explain why they are determined to fight back\par \par \uc2 The US was shaken earlier this week by the news that Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 the ruling that gives American women the constitutionally protected right to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could be overturned.\par \par \uc2 If the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000180-874f-dd36-a38c-c74f98520000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked ruling}}}\uc2  by the supreme court does come into effect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a matter for individual state legislatures and Congress to rule upon. The change would mean women and girls no longer having the same rights their mothers and grandmothers fought for if Republican-controlled states move quickly to end \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and Republicans in Congress attempt to enact a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Leading US women\u8217\'20\'19s rights activists and scholars tell us how they feel about the news.\par \par \uc2 Bonnie Greer, playwright and novelist\par \par \uc2 When I heard the news of the draft decision, I went back to the time when I had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1969. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal in Illinois, my home state until the day Roe v Wade was affirmed in 1973. I was brought up to be law-abiding. Brought up Roman Catholic to believe that I was committing murder. But I wanted to go to university, to have a life. The doctor was a Black man, so I felt safe.\par \par \uc2 It happened in his office after hours. It was a simple procedure for him. He was even jaunty about it. He made a joke about the gender of the foetus. So, wrapped in my Catholic guilt, was this: a Black man was killed. By me. There was no aftercare. If I had caught an infection, there was nowhere I could go. Because I had broken the law. There was no counselling to help me through a kind of grief.\par \par \uc2 Women now don\u8217\'20\'19t know that world \u8211\'20\'13 and I really don\u8217\'20\'19t want them to know it. Taking away Roe v Wade, affirmed under the due process clause of the 14th amendment, protects the right to privacy. To agency. For an American citizen\u8217\'20\'19s right to their own person.\par \par \uc2 What I mourn the most is that we women, under the law, are not equal to men. We\u8217\'20\'19re in the wind. Again.\par \par \uc2 Judy Chicago, feminist artist\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s amazing and incomprehensible that a draft of a supreme court decision was leaked. That talks to the unusual times we\u8217\'20\'19re living in. The potential overturning of Roe v Wade is symbolic of a larger worldwide push against progress that manifested as much in the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  restricting women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to education again. It\u8217\'20\'19s the story of pushing forward and pushing backwards. We\u8217\'20\'19re in a period of pushing back.\par \par \uc2 The fight for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights is a long historic struggle against a set of values that restricts the rights of, not only women, but LGBTQ people, trans people and people of colour. When I was young, I had the money to pay for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There\u8217\'20\'19s a quote that I encountered when we were working on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.judychicago.com/gallery/holocaust-project/hp-artwork/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Holocaust Project}}}\uc2 , that those who have the least to say about human events suffer the gravest of consequences. So it\u8217\'20\'19s going to gravely affect women who do not have the resources to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s going to affect them horribly.\par \par \uc2 You know, we have been living through the #MeToo movement. Well, there\u8217\'20\'19s another kind of #MeToo movement, particularly in the US. It has to do with me too and what I ate. Me too and what I want. Too many young people get wrapped up in that kind of me too. So I guess for them, this is going to be a rude awakening.\par \par \uc2 Are young people willing to stand up for their rights? Without that, we\u8217\'20\'19re lost.\par \par \uc2 V (formerly Eve Ensler), playwright and activist\par \par \uc2 When I heard the news that the supreme court was poised to overturn Roe V Wade I thought: no, fucking no. The supreme court does not represent the majority of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and it has no moral authority to control women\u8217\'20\'19s bodies.\par \par \uc2 I have been getting emails all day and night from women around the world who are panicked, raging, saying this cannot happen in the US, for if it does, it will catalyse and amplify the rightwing misogynist project that is taking away the rights of women everywhere, having a devastating impact on their lives and now escalated during the pandemic. If we allow the erasure of this central right for women, it will escalate the erasure of them all.\par \par \uc2 It is absurd for this country \u8211\'20\'13 with one of the highest maternal mortality rates and no paid maternity leave \u8211\'20\'13 to be forcing childbirth on women. And there is also no accountability for the people impregnating women \u8211\'20\'13 which is because this is not about babies, it is about destroying women\u8217\'20\'19s agency and autonomy. And we know that this will most harshly affect the lives of Black and Brown women and marginalised people.\par \par \uc2 That this ruling appears engineered by three Republican appointees to the court \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/sep/27/brett-kavanaugh-clarence-thomas-anita-hill-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , two accused predators (both denied the allegations), together with avowed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/14/anti-abortion-group-indiana-amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-abortionist Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 , is no surprise.\par \par \uc2 We are seeing the greatest pushback of rights I\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced in my lifetime. Those of us who have fought to live in a world where women have choices and bodily independence know that the patriarchy is endlessly aggressive and brutal. If we are not radical, bold and vigilant, rights are destroyed.\par \par \uc2 Young and old people \u8211\'20\'13 those who have never lived without Roe v Wade and those who have \u8211\'20\'13 need to join together now and rise up \u8211\'20\'13 this is our future. Forcing women to have a baby is a form of control and violence. This MUST be a wakeup call, the alarm where we take to the streets and stay in the streets until this patriarchal madness ends.\par \par \uc2 V is the founder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vday.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 V-Day}}}\uc2 , a global movement to end violence against all women, girls and the planet\par \par \uc2 Mona Eltahawy, author and activist\par \par \uc2 A part of me is like, this is a fucking disaster. But the other part of me knew this was going to happen. Ever since Trump was elected, we knew this was coming. The white supremacist Christian right has been working on this for nearly 50 years, and they\u8217\'20\'19ve won.\par \par \uc2 I had an illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996 in Egypt and a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US in 2000. I can\u8217\'20\'19t believe that my past is becoming the present in the United States. This is the most powerful country in the world, and this fundamental right for pregnant people is being stripped away.\par \par \uc2 Those who can afford to get a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to do so, and mostly Black, Indigenous and Brown people, and working-class people, will not. But that\u8217\'20\'19s been the reality for many years now. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/03/sb8-south-texas-clinic-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas had already shrivelled the number of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics it had}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ever since I moved to the US from Egypt, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.feministgiant.com/p/if-amy-coney-barrett-was-a-muslim?r=50le&s=w&utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web&utm_source=direct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19d been saying}}}\uc2  that the United States is a theocracy, but no one is paying attention. The Christian right is more powerful in the US than the \uc2 Muslim Brotherhood\uc2  in Egypt ever dreamed of being. But because they\u8217\'20\'19re predominantly white and Christian, they\u8217\'20\'19re considered to be less dangerous. As an Egyptian feminist, I have to call out the role of women in creating this theocracy. Look at supreme court associate justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2 . It is not just men taking away our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/609114/the-seven-necessary-sins-for-women-and-girls-by-mona-eltahawy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Seven Necessary Sins for Women and Girls}}}\uc2  is out now, published by \uc2 Penguin Random House\par \par \uc2 Robin Morgan, author and activist\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a terrible blow. It was not unexpected, but there\u8217\'20\'19s an element of sheer disbelief at the audacity of this move by the ultra right. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/alisondurkee/2021/11/30/how-americans-really-feel-about-abortion-the-sometimes-surprising-poll-results-as-supreme-court-weighs-overturning-roe-v-wade/?sh=7323cc0036c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eighty per cent}}}\uc2  of the American public believes a woman has the right to do with her own body as she chooses, but it is still not respected. It affects everybody because it\u8217\'20\'19s coming in under the privacy aspect of the constitution. This means that they are now going to be moving [in] on medical abortions, same-sex marriage, gay rights in general. I mean, it just takes your breath away.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s an old phrase about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://winstonchurchill.hillsdale.edu/americans-will-always-right-thing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Americans always doing the right thing}}}\uc2 , but at the very last moment. We do adapt but, God, we could die waiting. The hope is that this will galvanise us at the polls, not just in 2024, but this coming fall. The 80% of the country that thought rather sensibly that this was a done deal, that this was a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right under the constitution, will be galvanised and we will have a very different outcome at the election. But it\u8217\'20\'19s a hell of a scary time.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no time to despair. You do everything you can think of to change the situation. New legislation is already being introduced by Democrats in the house because the Republican party has totally gone down the tube. It\u8217\'20\'19s Trump\u8217\'20\'19s party now.\par \par \uc2 There will be marching, demonstrations, sit-ins, petitions. Women will go ahead and disobey the law. What are they going to do when half the population is in revolt? Not 20%, not the ultra right wing, not the evangelicals. Women are going to control what happens to our own bodies. No matter how many thousands of us have to go to jail. We are not turning back the clock. No way.\par \par \uc2 Robin Morgan is the editor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.robinmorgan.net/book/sisterhood-is-powerful/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sisterhood Is Powerful}}}\uc2  : An Anthology of Writings from the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Liberation Movement\par \par \uc2 Katha Pollitt, poet and essayist\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade was a life-changing ruling, probably one of the most important \u8211\'20\'13 from the ground level \u8211\'20\'13 supreme court rulings there has ever been. It meant that women could stay in school. It meant women could work in a consistent way. It meant women could leave abusive partners. It meant that women didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to marry the man who got them pregnant.\par \par \uc2 I felt horrified when I found out it could be overturned. This really allows states to do whatever they want with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and 26 states is a lot of people. This is going to affect women whether or not they have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because it says, basically, you\u8217\'20\'19re here to procreate, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t care if there are health concerns, or rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 If a man can get you pregnant, you have to have that child. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s a tremendous statement that women do not have that human right any more.\par \par \uc2 One thing that is in our control is how much work, time and money we\u8217\'20\'19re willing to spend on re-enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. I think there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a tremendous need for money to help women in places where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will now be unavailable \u8211\'20\'13 we have to work on getting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to those women.\par \par \uc2 There is a very active network of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abortionfunds.org"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  funds}}}\uc2 , which raise money for low-income women to pay for their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. People don\u8217\'20\'19t realise it\u8217\'20\'19s not just the cost of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s also travel, childcare, lodging, food, being able to take time off work. It would be really great if people started giving significantly to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds.\par \par \uc2 Katha Pollitt is the author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.co.uk/Pro-Reclaiming-Abortion-Katha-Pollitt/dp/1250072662"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro: Reclaiming \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights}}}\par \par \uc2 Mara Clarke\uc2 , activist\par \par \uc2 I started my \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activism in the US in 2002. In 2010, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu-il.org/en/news/13-us-women-have-abortions-87-us-counties-have-no-provider"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 87% of US counties}}}\uc2  did not have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider. By 2017, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/report/abortion-incidence-service-availability-us-2017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was closer to 90%}}}\uc2 . Most people in the US think Roe v Wade has protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, but it\u8217\'20\'19s mostly protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for wealthy people, and women with the ability to travel large distances. So this news for those of us who\u8217\'20\'19ve been in this work for years is horrifying and sickening and rage-inducing, but it is not surprising.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s easy for people in the UK and Europe to think this is an American problem. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not. Northern Ireland still does not have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/mar/24/uk-government-to-override-northern-ireland-on-abortion-services"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commissioned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  services}}}\uc2 . In Europe last year, Poland enforced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jan/27/poland-to-implement-near-total-ban-on-abortion-imminently"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Women there die of preventable causes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/jan/26/poland-death-of-woman-refused-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 because doctors won\u8217\'20\'19t give them abortions}}}\uc2 . There\u8217\'20\'19s no \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Malta and Andorra, and it\u8217\'20\'19s highly restricted in Liechtenstein. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not even considering the global south.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s disheartening. But after the initial punch to the gut I will do my best to feel hopeful because maybe it will motivate people to make systemic change. That systemic change may be abortions being self-managed with pills, and grassroots networks of activists helping women and pregnant people exercise their right to obtain safe abortions.\par \par \uc2 Mara Clarke\uc2  is the founder of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asn.org.uk/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Support Network}}}\par \par \uc2 Jill Filipovic, author and lawyer\par \par \uc2 Underpinning this judgment is, very clearly, not a fealty to the law. It\u8217\'20\'19s not even a fealty to the idea that foetal life is particularly valuable. Instead, what underpins it is a deeply misogynistic worldview that seeks to restore traditional gender roles, male dominance over public, economic and political life, and female subservience and dependence. If women can\u8217\'20\'19t control their own bodies, they can\u8217\'20\'19t control their own futures. The justices are not stupid people. They know that.\par \par \uc2 The judgment is going to open a huge can of worms. It will throw the entire country into chaos. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a legislative circus. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists will frankly make sure that women have access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether legal or not. In an already deeply polarised country that\u8217\'20\'19s already experienced serious challenges to democratic norms and systems, this is another kick towards greater division, and a greater fraying of US democracy.\par \par \uc2 All of the women I know are sad, and absolutely livid. One in four American women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2017/abortion-common-experience-us-women-despite-dramatic-declines-rates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will have an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in her life. The women in my life have been talking about how different so many of our lives would have been if we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have access to safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . About all the career opportunities that would never have happened. The men we would never have married. All the novels that weren\u8217\'20\'19t written, and the inventions never dreamed up. The wanted children that never come into the world. The big loves that women never find, and the abusive relationships they never leave. The stability that low-income women are never able to claw their way to. There is a tremendous amount that is foreclosed upon, when women can\u8217\'20\'19t make these fundamental choices about their bodies.\par \par \uc2 Sydney Calkin, academic\par \par \uc2 I was horrified when I heard the news, but not surprised; it was clear that a lot of the justices wanted to overturn Roe v Wade entirely. It\u8217\'20\'19s worth pointing out that, for a lot of people, Roe hasn\u8217\'20\'19t meant much in practice, because states that are hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have already made it all but impossible to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Plenty of states already have burdensome laws that make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  logistically or procedurally impossible, or really expensive.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to go back to the dark days of the coathanger \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . What we\u8217\'20\'19ll see is an acceleration in self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  using medication. Thankfully, self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is much safer now with pills, not that that\u8217\'20\'19s a replacement for safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it\u8217\'20\'19s still a horrible decision that will endanger people.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court likes to say it\u8217\'20\'19s not political, which I find funny. This decision has been the result of the conservative legal movement packing the court with extreme anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  conservatives for decades. It\u8217\'20\'19s been their long-term strategic goal. There\u8217\'20\'19s also talk of overturning same-sex marriage, and some rightwing politicians even want to look at the right to contraception. They will be coming for other laws. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think this stops at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s horrifying.\par \par \uc2 Dr Sydney Calkin is a senior lecturer in human geography at Queen Mary University of London\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Solnit, writer, historian and activist\par \par \uc2 We have been expecting this for some time: despite what he said, it was clear that \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and the others were going to try to overturn Roe v Wade if they could. I was shocked, but not surprised. The American right wing is patient and methodical \u8211\'20\'13 it has been building power from the ground up and spreading its propaganda for a long time.\par \par \uc2 We have already seen access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in some states be so radically curtailed it is effectively nonexistent. If Roe v Wade is overturned, it will create a patchwork United States where rights in some states are very different to those in others.\par \par \uc2 I do not have to worry about pregnancy at this point in my life, but I do see this as an attack on every person who is capable of becoming pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 an attempt to make women unequal, unfree and second-class citizens.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are based on lies and the pretence that those getting abortions are all reckless, hypersexual, irresponsible hussies \u8211\'20\'13 whereas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/jun/03/lies-anti-abortion-laws-rebecca-solnit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the majority are, in fact, women who are already mothers}}}\uc2 . We must draw attention to the realities of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The argument that it is easy to carry a child to term and then give it up for adoption is another anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lie \u8211\'20\'13 pregnancy itself is life-altering and it can be life-threatening. It can injure and incapacitate bodies, and it has an enormous emotional impact.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s already a huge amount of fury among those who support access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and my great hope is that people can hang on to that fury long enough to produce {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/nov/16/the-democratic-blue-wave-was-real"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the kind of blue wave that took back the house in 2018}}}\uc2 . We often talk about right-wing \u8220\'20\'1Cbacklashes\u8221\'20\'1D, but there are progressive backlashes, too.\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Solnit is the author of numerous books, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://rebeccasolnit.net/books/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Mother of All Questions}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 4 May 2022. The contribution from Bonnie Greer was updated to better and more fully reflect her views. A previous version also referred to \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett as having been appointed to the supreme court by President Trump; Thomas was in fact nominated by President George HW Bush in 1991.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220504ei5400133\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
