\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Do something, Democrats\u8217\'20\'19: party struggles to rise to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  challenge\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino and Lauren Burke in Washington \par \uc2 1,189 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 15:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Despite controlling the White House and Congress, Democrats seem powerless to fight the assault on Roe v Wade but hope it will energise midterm voters\par \par \uc2 Visibly shaking with fury and brandishing megaphones and posters, thousands of women defending reproductive rights in America thronged below the marbled columns of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to protest against what appears to be the imminent demise of the 1973 Roe v Wade ruling recognizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo something, Democrats,\u8221\'20\'1D the crowd {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/do-something-democrats-abortion-rights-supporters-chant-us-supreme-court-2022-05-03/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chanted}}}\uc2  at one point.\par \par \uc2 In the hours that followed, Democrats, who control the House, the Senate and the White House, echoed their outrage and vowed a response.\par \par \uc2 The urgency follows a leak late on Monday evening of a draft opinion from the court that a majority of the nine judges on the bench \u8211\'20\'13 all conservative-leaning appointees of Republican presidents \u8211\'20\'13 support not just more restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services but the overturning of the landmark Roe ruling that guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when final opinions are issued in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am furious \u8211\'20\'13 furious that Republicans could be this cruel, that the supreme court could be this heartless, that in legislatures across the country, extreme Republicans are ready for their trigger bans to go into effect,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , a Democrat of Washington and a longtime advocate of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights, said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking from the steps of the US Capitol, she was referring to states that have legislative bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepared and waiting to be \u8220\'20\'1Ctriggered\u8221\'20\'1D into effect as soon as Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is craven and we won\u8217\'20\'19t stand for it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to sit quietly and neither should any of you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yet, infuriatingly for the pro-choice voters who helped elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and a Democratic Congress, the party finds itself largely powerless at present, without a legislative path forward to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the likely event the court reverses its decision in Roe.\par \par \uc2 Biden said it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical decision\u8221\'20\'1D by the court and called on Congress to act to enshrine the rights afforded by Roe into federal law via legislation.\par \par \uc2 And Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , speaking to attendees at a gala hosted by Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, which works to elect Democrats who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, railed that a ruling overturning Roe would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect assault on freedom\u8221\'20\'1D in America.\par \par \uc2 Barring swift legislative action, nearly half of US states are likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or severely restrict access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 But the reality of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 thin congressional majorities is that they don\u8217\'20\'19t have enough support in the evenly divided \uc2 US Senate\uc2  to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, nor do they have the votes to eliminate the so-called filibuster rule, thus allowing legislation to pass with a simple majority.\par \par \uc2 Biden has resisted pressure from progressives to use his bully pulpit to call for eliminating the filibuster, following recent demands to do so to pass voting rights legislation. And on Tuesday, he said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot prepared\u8221\'20\'1D to do so to protect reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , a New York Democrat, vowed to forge ahead with a vote on legislation that is stalled in Congress but if passed would establish a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to end her pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 But the measure, a version of which passed the Democratic-controlled House last year, was already rejected once this year, when it fell far short of the 60 votes needed to break a filibuster. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t even win the support of all 50 Democrats, so even if the filibuster were scrapped the bill, called the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, would not have passed in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrat from West Virginia, voted with Republicans to block consideration of the bill. The bill also failed to attract the support of two pro-choice Senate Republicans, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska, who have introduced separate legislation that they say would codify Roe.\par \par \uc2 Yet Schumer argued that it was important to put every senator on the record.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA vote on this legislation is no longer an abstract exercise. This is as urgent and real as it gets,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The leaked draft decision, written by the conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , would shift the question of whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal to the individual states.\par \par \uc2 The effect would dramatically alter the US landscape almost overnight, with restrictions and bans going into effect across much of the south and midwest while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain legal in many north-eastern and western states.\par \par \uc2 Emboldened by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative super-majority, Republican legislatures have enacted a flurry of new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws as conservative activists begin to lay the groundwork for a nationwide ban.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, as the country reeled from the revelation that the supreme court was likely to dismantle Roe, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/abortion-us-supreme-court-health-texas-oklahoma-528aede70223d68dd5ed09160098445f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed into law }}}\uc2  a bill that would ban abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, a copycat version of a Texas law enacted last year.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, liberal states have moved to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/30/nyregion/connecticut-texas-abortion-law.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Connecticut}}}\uc2  lawmakers approved a bill that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state. And states like California and New York have vowed to be a \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D for people seeking reproductive care from places where the procedure is banned.\par \par \uc2 With few options, Democrats have implored Americans shocked and angered by the seemingly impending loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to vote in the midterm elections. Majorities of Americans say they want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain legal in some or most cases. Few say they want the court to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats face steep headwinds in November, weighed down by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings, rising inflation and a sour national mood.\par \par \uc2 The Republican reaction to the news that the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court was prepared to strike down Roe was relatively subdued. In the Senate, lawmakers were far more focused on the source of the leaked document than the decision, which is the culmination of a decades-long drive by the conservative movement to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 The response suggested that there may be some concern that Republicans are worried about provoking a political backlash among more moderate and independent voters who broadly support a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s an answer,\u8221\'20\'1D the Illinois senator \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , the majority whip, said at a press conference. \u8220\'20\'1CThe answer is in November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But many Democrats and activists believe November is too late for millions of women in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will banned almost immediately. They want the party \u8211\'20\'13 from the president on down \u8211\'20\'13 to throw every ounce of their political capital at finding a legislative solution.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople elected Democrats precisely so we could lead in perilous moments like these \u8211\'20\'13 to codify Roe, hold corruption accountable, & have a President who uses his legal authority to break through Congressional gridlock on items from student debt to climate,\u8221\'20\'1D Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a progressive Democrat from New York, wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s high time we do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55000p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
