\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Latin American feminists vow to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights at home after shock US ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Natalie Alcoba in Buenos Aires \par \uc2 892 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 12:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s movements have fought hard to reverse anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in their countries and say it\u8217\'20\'19s not the end for the US\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights activists across Latin America have vowed to protect hard-fought gains in their own territories as they brace for potential ripple effects if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US supreme court overturns Roe vs Wade}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the 1973 ruling which guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Latin America has some of the most draconian anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the world. But feminist movements have fought for decades to chip away at the prohibitions, and in recent years a younger, diverse generation of activists has mobilized in massive numbers to help clinch a string of victories in traditionally conservative countries.\par \par \uc2 Now, the possibility that the US could be moving in the opposite direction has prompted bewilderment, fear and indignation among campaigners from Mexico to Argentina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe segment of society that wants to return us to the dark ages is real,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ana Cristina Gonz\u225\'00\'E1lez V\u233\'00\'E9lez, a Colombian doctor and co-founder of Mesa por la Vida, an organization that was part of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/feb/22/colombia-legalises-abortion-in-move-celebrated-as-historic-victory-by-campaigners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the successful campaign for decriminalization of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in Colombia. }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThis has to be a wake-up call, that a legal victory is not a cultural one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A February ruling by Colombia\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional court \u8211\'20\'13 which decriminalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the 24th week of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 was the latest in a series of gains by reproductive rights activists.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Argentina\u8217\'20\'19s marea verde \u8211\'20\'13 green wave \u8211\'20\'13 protests pushed the country\u8217\'20\'19s congress to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalize elective \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  until the 14th week of pregnancy}}}\uc2 . Less than a year later, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/07/mexico-abortion-law-struck-down-supreme-court-penalties-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s highest court declared a complete \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban was unconstitutional}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 although statutes outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still on the books in most of Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s 32 states.\par \par \uc2 Brazil \u8211\'20\'13 where terminations are only allowed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/aug/17/brazil-protest-abortion-recife-hospital"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cases of rape, risk to the woman\u8217\'20\'19s life and certain congenital conditions}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and Chile are also facing pivotal moments in the fight for legalization.\par \par \uc2 But the importance of Roe vs Wade across the region cannot be overstated, said Debora Diniz, a Brazilian law professor and human rights activist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a country that is a political, financial, military empire, a supreme court decision has a contagious effect. Because everything moves together,\u8221\'20\'1D said Diniz, who co-founded Anis \u8211\'20\'13 Institute of Bioethics, Human Rights and Gender, an NGO pushing for the court in Brazil to decriminalize elective \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Argentina was able to secure change through legislation, but the effort took years and has been difficult to replicate in other democracies ravaged by past military dictatorships or still governed by a patriarchal ruling class, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor Latin American countries, like Brazil, like Mexico, like Colombia, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  was a very important precedent behind the simple idea that courts are a legitimate space in which to decide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  [rights],\u8221\'20\'1D said Diniz.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican lawyer and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights campaigner Melissa Ayala said that the courts in Mexico were strongly on the side of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights now. But she warned that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups that have been gathering forces in the region will now take a page out of the US playbook. Mariela Belski, executive director of Amnesty International Argentina, agreed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe threat has been there since the legalization [allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] was passed,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are very worried about the strong anti-rights groups that we are seeing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such concerns are all the more pressing because while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be legal in Argentina, access still varies dramatically between regions.\par \par \uc2 Women in Argentina are not prepared to cede any ground, Belski said, adding that they would flood the streets at the first sign of any fresh threat to their legal rights.\par \par \uc2 Her advice to US counterparts was exactly that. \u8220\'20\'1CTake to the streets. Mobilize in massive numbers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, and work in a bipartisan way. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that the secret in Argentina was the cross-section of legislators who were fighting for the same cause. There wasn\u8217\'20\'19t political division.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Added Diniz: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to believe in the green wave. The situation in Latin America was so desperate, and we managed to bring about change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In several Latin American countries the situation remains desperate: Honduras, Nicaragua and El Salvador maintain absolute prohibitions in all circumstances, and women have been given long prison sentences even in cases where they suffered miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 In Honduras, the government responded to the growing strength of legalization campaigns by enshrining its total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in its constitution. \u8220\'20\'1CThings couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be worse,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neesa Medina, a member of feminist collective Somos Muchas.\par \par \uc2 It was not lost on Medina that the people most affected by an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the United States will be the most vulnerable: minorities, migrants, the undocumented.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLatinas,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are so many stories that link us as societies. It\u8217\'20\'19s our neighbors, our families, our cousins, aunts, who are going to feel the repercussions directly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But activists across the region said that their own recent histories offer proof that progress can be fought for. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re so used to looking to the United States, but this is a very good moment to look to the south,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ayala.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 5 May 2022 to correct the spelling of Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei550018i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
