\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18Maga crowd\u8217\'20\'19 could target LGBTQ+ children next\b0\par\par\uc2 Jem Bartholomew \par \uc2 1,576 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 10:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President warns of new Republican party attacks on rights after supreme court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leak. Plus, Amber Heard takes witness stand against Johnny DeppDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Hello and good morning,\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/biden-lgbtq-children-next-target-maga-crowd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned of new attacks on civil rights}}}\uc2  as the supreme court prepares to strike down the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , telling reporters at the White House that LGBTQ+ children could be the next targets of a Trump-dominated Republican party he called \u8220\'20\'1Cthis Maga crowd\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organisation \u8230\'20\'26 in recent American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, if \u8220\'20\'1Ca state changes the law saying that children who are LGBTQ can\u8217\'20\'19t be in classrooms with other children? Is that legit under the way the decision is written?\u8221\'20\'1D There are also fears {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contraception could come under fire}}}\uc2  next.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks followed the leaked draft of a ruling by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . One of six conservatives on the supreme court, Alito was writing on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/05/trump-justices-abortion-roe-v-wade-gorsuch-kavanaugh-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi case which aims to overturn both Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the 1973 ruling which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Planned Parenthood v Casey, a 1992 ruling which buttressed it.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds rallied again in Washington, DC, to protest against the draft decision, with polling showing the supreme court is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/may/04/abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade-public-opinion-biden-trump-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-62727f5c8f08a298acd03347#block-62727f5c8f08a298acd03347"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 out of step with the majority}}}\uc2  of Americans.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Biden is facing criticism within his own party for seeming reluctant to contemplate changes needed to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in legislation: namely abolishing the Senate filibuster, the rule that requires 60 votes for most bills to pass.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 When will the Mississippi case conclude? It\u8217\'20\'19s expected to be resolved in June. The leaked draft is not final.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will be the immediate impact? More than half of US states will outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as soon as practicable. There are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states hostile to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , with 13 having passed so-called trigger laws, effectively banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as soon as Roe v Wade is overturned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What can you do? Essayist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/03/heres-how-americans-can-fight-back-to-protect-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rebecca Solnit writes how Americans can fight back}}}\uc2  to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Fierce fighting under way in Mariupol\u8217\'20\'19s Azovstal plant, says Azov commander\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian forces were fighting \u8220\'20\'1Cdifficult, bloody battles\u8221\'20\'1D against Russian troops for a second day, said Denys Prokopenko, commander of the Azov regiment, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/contact-lost-ukraine-troops-staging-last-stand-mariupol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more civilians fled the city of Mariupol on evacuation buses}}}\uc2  following weeks of brutal bombardment that had reduced much of it to rubble.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am proud of my soldiers who are making superhuman efforts to contain the pressure of the enemy \u8230\'20\'26 The situation is extremely difficult,\u8221\'20\'1D Prokopenko said.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, David Arakhamia, the head of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ruling party in parliament, told RFE/RL that Russian forces had entered the plant, but he said that the country\u8217\'20\'19s government remained in contact with the Ukrainian troops making a last stand.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s official spokesperson, Dmitry Peskov, denied reports that Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s forces were trying to storm the Azovstal plant.\par \par \uc2 Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-71-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 344 people had been rescued from besieged Mariupol in a second evacuation operation}}}\uc2 , the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , confirmed in a national address.\par \par \uc2 In other developments, Ukraine claimed on Thursday morning it had regained control over several settlements surrounding Mykolaiv and Kherson in the country\u8217\'20\'19s south, military officials said.\par \par \uc2 And an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/04/russia-ukraine-war-russia-attacks-azovstal-steel-plant-after-first-evacuated-civilians-reach-safety-live?page=with:block-6272b3808f08bc8c65c74dc7#block-6272b3808f08bc8c65c74dc7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation by Associated Press}}}\uc2  found as many as 600 people were killed in the Russian bombing of a theatre in Mariupol in March, twice as many as once suspected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How are civilians being evacuated from the Mariupol steel plant? Russia has said it will implement a daytime ceasefire for three days from Thursday to allow more civilian evacuations from the Azovstal plant.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What further evidence of potential war crimes has emerged? The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/04/russia-ukraine-war-russia-attacks-azovstal-steel-plant-after-first-evacuated-civilians-reach-safety-live?page=with:block-62729fc68f08a5c31f5b2239#block-62729fc68f08a5c31f5b2239"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bodies of 20 more civilians}}}\uc2  were found in the past 24 hours in the Kyiv region, according to Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s regional police chief, Andriy Nebytov.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What new measures are western leaders taking? The UK said it was providing $56m in funding to help the most vulnerable in Ukraine and at its borders; Biden said he would speak with other \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders about additional sanctions. The \uc2 European Union\uc2  is proposing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-71-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban all Russian oil imports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What are Russia and its allies saying? The Kremlin dismissed speculation that it would declare all-out war in Ukraine in the coming days as \u8220\'20\'1Cnonsense\u8221\'20\'1D. Brazilian presidential frontrunner, \uc2 Luiz In\u225\'00\'E1cio Lula da Silva\uc2 , said Zelenskiy and the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/brazil-lula-zelenskiy-blame-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bore equal responsibility for the war}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  testifies before the committee on the events of January 6\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s oldest son has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/donald-trump-jr-us-capitol-attack-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met with the congressional committee investigating the January 6 insurrection}}}\uc2 , according to two people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  was interviewed on Tuesday as the bipartisan House committee moved closer to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle of family members and political advisers.\par \par \uc2 The younger Trump is of likely interest to the committee because of his proximity to his father on the day of the riot. \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  was seen backstage at the rally on the White House Ellipse that took place shortly before supporters of the then president marched to the Capitol and breached the building.\par \par \uc2 Trump Jr is one of nearly 1,000 witnesses the committee has interviewed as it works to compile a record of the worst attack on the Capitol in more than two centuries.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the justice department has alleged in court papers that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/trump-oath-keepers-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a militia group leader tried to ask Trump to authorize them to stop the transfer of power}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stewart Rhodes, the Oath Keepers militia group leader charged with seditious conspiracy over the January 6 attack, asked an intermediary to get \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to allow his group to forcibly stop the transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Amber Heard took the witness stand in court\par \par \uc2 on Wednesday in\par \par \uc2 Johnny Depp\u8217\'20\'19s defamation lawsuit against her.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/amber-heard-testifies-johnny-depp-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is horrible for me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said}}}\uc2 . Heard testified to the jury about the first time Depp allegedly hit her, repeatedly. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll never forget it. It changed my life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The premier of the British Virgin Islands, who is accused of cocaine trafficking, and whom US prosecutors described in court as \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt to the core\u8221\'20\'1D, has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/04/bvi-premier-accused-of-cocaine-trafficking-granted-bail-in-miami"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 given a $500,000 bond}}}\uc2  that would allow him to be released from prison as he awaits trial.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Real Madrid staged a stunning late comeback against Manchester City\par \par \uc2 on Wednesday night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/may/04/real-madrid-manchester-city-champions-league-semi-final-second-leg-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressing to the final of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s top soccer tournament}}}\uc2 , the Champions League. Karim Benzema\u8217\'20\'19s penalty sunk their opponents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rescuers in central China have pulled a woman alive from the rubble of a building that partially collapsed almost six days earlier. She is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/05/survivor-found-in-rubble-six-days-after-china-building-collapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10th survivor}}}\uc2  but potentially dozens are still missing.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Oil giant \uc2 Shell\uc2  has almost tripled its quarterly profits, as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2022/may/05/shells-profits-energy-crisis-bank-of-england-interest-rates-inflation-business-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surge in oil and gas prices drive up earnings}}}\uc2  and intensify calls in the UK for a windfall tax on excess profits.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: US is recycling just 5% of its plastic waste\par \par \uc2 Around 85% of US plastics end up in landfill, 10% are incinerated, and just 5% to 6% are actually recycled, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-recycling-plastic-waste"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report by the Last Beach Cleanup (LBC) and Beyond Plastics}}}\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s compared with recycling rates of 66% for paper and 50% for aluminum cans. The LBC founder Jan Dell said plastic producers had duped consumers by adding triangular \u8220\'20\'1Cchasing arrows\u8221\'20\'1D shapes on to products without actually recycling. \u8220\'20\'1CThey leveraged the heartstrings of consumers and said this stuff was recyclable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: were crop circles actually great art?\par \par \uc2 Dismissed as the work of pranksters, these mysterious flattenings were anonymous, anti-capitalist and awe-inspiring \u8211\'20\'13 stunning examples of non-profit art for all, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2022/may/05/anonymous-anti-capitalist-awe-inspiring-crop-circles-benjamin-myers-great-art"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Benjamin Myers}}}\uc2 . Their scale was staggering: at their largest, some designs measured 900ft (270 metres) across, almost as long as the Eiffel Tower is tall. They were completely at odds with the messages being relayed from politicians and businesses in the 1980s: profit at all costs.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: populations of up to 48% of bird species\par \par \uc2 declining\par \par \uc2 There are about 11,000 species of bird spanning the globe, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/may/05/canaries-in-the-coalmine-loss-of-birds-signals-changing-planet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the populations of half of them are falling}}}\uc2 , while just 6% are increasing and 39% are flat. That\u8217\'20\'19s according to a review published in the journal Annual Review of Environment and Resources. This is due to the destruction of wild habitat, pesticides and other pollution, overhunting and the effects of alien species and disease. Bird populations in the US and Canada have fallen by 3 billion since 1970.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: I thought it was weird to have a favourite spoon. Then I realised I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t alone...\par \par \uc2 I have started getting feelings for my spoons, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/may/04/ive-no-fewer-than-17-wooden-spoons-but-i-have-a-favourite-and-id-miss-it-for-ever-if-it-went-missing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Adrian Chiles}}}\uc2 . I have 17 wooden spoons. Sorting through them, I realised I do have a favourite. It\u8217\'20\'19s more of a spatula than a spoon, but it suits me very well. I had always looked out for it without knowing I was doing so and felt a twinge of disappointment if it didn\u8217\'20\'19t come to hand. If ever I lost it for good, I now understood, I would miss it for ever.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55001bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
