\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump the hero for anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement after bending supreme court his way\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,107 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 07:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The former president was once pro-choice \u8211\'20\'13 but the threat he posed to reproductive rights was hiding in plain sight\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very pro-choice.\u8221\'20\'1D So said \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/meet-the-press/video/trump-in-1999-i-am-very-pro-choice-480297539914"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview}}}\uc2  on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press in 1999, attributing his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Ca little bit of a New York background\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Two decades later, the businessman and reality TV star is the unlikeliest of heroes for social conservatives and Christian evangelicals because he delivered the ultimate prize: the end of America\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leak this week}}}\uc2  of a draft supreme court opinion showing that the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority is poised to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision legalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , represented a vivid aftershock of the Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 He had reversed his position on the issue by the time he reached the White House and, with uncharacteristic discipline, spent his four years in office bending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/may/23/us-supreme-court-trump-judicial-appointments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the federal judiciary to the right}}}\uc2 , including with three supreme court appointments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court will be his most important and long-lasting political legacy,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pomona.edu/directory/people/amanda-l-hollis-brusky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amanda Hollis-Brusky}}}\uc2 , an associate professor of politics at Pomona College in Claremont, California.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the number of supreme court justices stays at nine, Trump will have appointed a third of the supreme court having been a one-term president who lost the popular vote by 3 million. And yet those justices will have a greater and a longer-lasting impact than anything else he did as president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The threat he posed to reproductive rights was always hiding in plain sight. As a Republican candidate running for president in 2016, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2016/05/19/us/politics/donald-trump-supreme-court-nominees.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released a list}}}\uc2  of 11 potential supreme court nominees after heeding advice from conservative groups such as the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  and \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The unusual move was seen as a way of reassuring conservatives troubled by his boorish behaviour and past views on issues such as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Then, during the last presidential debate with his Democratic opponent, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , Trump was asked if he wanted to see the supreme court overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/the-fix/wp/2016/10/19/the-final-trump-clinton-debate-transcript-annotated/?utm_term=.c2faf853d121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 He replied}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWell, if we put another two or perhaps three justices on, that\u8217\'20\'19s really what\u8217\'20\'19s going to be \u8211\'20\'13 that will happen. And that\u8217\'20\'19ll happen automatically, in my opinion, because I am putting pro-life justices on the court. I will say this: it will go back to the states, and the states will then make a determination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Once in office, Trump followed through by appointing \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett to the highest court, handing conservatives a 6-3 majority. In all he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Federal_judges_nominated_by_Donald_Trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointed 234 judges,}}}\uc2  including 54 appellate judges, outpacing \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first-term total of 172 and \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 204.\par \par \uc2 The process was guided by two men: \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , then Republican majority leader in the Senate, and \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fedsoc.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Federalist Society}}}\uc2 , which counts among its members four supreme court justices, dozens of federal judges and every Republican attorney general since it was created in 1982.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pomona.edu/directory/people/amanda-l-hollis-brusky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hollis-Brusky}}}\uc2 , author of Ideas with Consequences: \uc2 The Federalist Society\uc2  and the Conservative Counterrevolution, said: \u8220\'20\'1COne of the interesting things about Trump, McConnell, \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  and the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  is that Trump made appointments based on friendships, brought his buddies into the administration, had loyalty tests for his appointees and fired people who displeased him but, when it came to the operation of finding, selecting and confirming judges, it was a completely professionalised shop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf anyone worked in lockstep, it was McConnell and Leo, and Trump just largely got out of the way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump gained further kudos in the eyes of conservatives when he resisted calls to withdraw his nomination of Kavanaugh, who was accused of having committed sexual assault as a teenager. The president also moved swiftly to replace the late justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  despite pressure to wait for the 2020 election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.committeeforjustice.org/curt-levey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Curt Levey}}}\uc2 , president of the conservative advocacy group the Committee for Justice, said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe showed some backbone that I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure other Republican presidents would have shown. He stuck by Kavanaugh when frankly there were Republicans on the Hill who did not want him to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people said, \u8216\'20\'18Oh, you can\u8217\'20\'19t nominate anyone to fill Ginsburg\u8217\'20\'19s seat, it\u8217\'20\'19s too close to the election,\u8217\'20\'19 he said, \u8216\'20\'18I disagree\u8217\'20\'19. He showed courage. Whether you like the guy or hate the guy, he was known for the courage of his convictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When the draft opinion {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked to the Politico website}}}\uc2  on Monday, Democrats expressed outrage while most Republicans focused on the breach of court secrecy, perhaps aware that premature triumphalism could result in political backlash.\par \par \uc2 But Madison Cawthorn, a Republican congressman from North Carolina, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CawthornforNC/status/1521292725856919554?s=20&t=oLUblfjB6YI1GYKJ02HOeQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Twitter }}}\uc2  that the ex-president deserved the credit. Others may eventually follow suit in praising Trump for delivering on his campaign promises and succeeding where other Republican presidents failed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/profiles/michael-dantonio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael D\u8217\'20\'19Antonio}}}\uc2 , a political commentator and Trump biographer, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey will regard him as heroic. He\u8217\'20\'19ll be the fallen man who redeemed himself by this advocacy and forevermore he\u8217\'20\'19ll be worshipped in certain corners of the Christian right. Their fanaticism knows no bounds and they\u8217\'20\'19ve been looking for this kind of person to come along forever. What\u8217\'20\'19s ironic is that he\u8217\'20\'19s proving that a profane man can accomplish what devout ones could not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If Roe v Wade falls, about half of the states in the US are certain or likely to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The political impact on November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections remains uncertain. But such an outcome could give Trump a ready-made applause line at campaign rallies for a White House bid in 2024.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.marquette.edu/faculty-and-staff-directory/detail/1996511"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Fallone}}}\uc2 , an associate professor at Marquette University Law School in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, said: \u8220\'20\'1C It increases the likelihood Trump will run again because he\u8217\'20\'19ll see this as a monumental issue for generating enthusiasm and turnout. If he was hesitating at all to run a second time, I would think now he\u8217\'20\'19s going to feel a bit emboldened.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot imagine a scenario where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not take credit for this and repeat endlessly that he alone made it happen .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fallone added: \u8220\'20\'1CSeismic events like Roe versus Wade on the way to being overturned have all kinds of ancillary repercussions. I\u8217\'20\'19m worrying about the legal landscape and the future of constitutional law but the entire political landscape and the leadership of the Republican party could also be impacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an earthquake and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to have repercussions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
