\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Victorian upper house MP\u8217\'20\'19s post about  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  described as \u8216\'20\'18deplorable\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Benita Kolovos \par \uc2 559 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par 06:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bernie Finn\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post came after the leak of draft decision suggesting \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  may overturn Roe v WadeFollow our Australia news live blog for the latest updatesDownload the free Guardian app ; get our morning email briefing\par \par \uc2 Victoria\u8217\'20\'19s minister for women, Gabrielle Williams, has described a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post by Liberal MP Bernie Finn as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeplorable\u8221\'20\'1D after he wrote that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cpraying\u8221\'20\'1D for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be banned in Australia.\par \par \uc2 The post was published on the upper house MP\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page on Wednesday night, after the leak of a draft decision showing a majority of \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices may overturn Roe v Wade, which makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo excited the US is on the verge of a major breakthrough to civilisation. Praying it will come here soon. Killing babies is criminal,\u8221\'20\'1D Finn said in the post.\par \par \uc2 When a woman, who commented she didn\u8217\'20\'19t support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but believed there should be an option for victims of sexual assault, Finn replied: \u8220\'20\'1CBabies should not be killed for the crime of his or her parent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement to Guardian Australia, Williams said there was no place for Finn\u8217\'20\'19s comments in the community and urged the opposition leader, \uc2 Matthew Guy\uc2 , to take action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are deplorable comments, that show an appalling lack of respect for women and completely disregard the trauma experienced by victims of sexual assault \u8211\'20\'13 instead prioritising the decisions of perpetrators over the needs of women victims of crime,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe support all women to make choices that are right for them \u8211\'20\'13 women have the right to access reproductive services safely, legally and with dignity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Guy said the social media comments reflected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/mar/18/victorian-politician-rape-justification-abortion-bernie-finn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Finn\u8217\'20\'19s longstanding personal views on the issue}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am not interested in commenting on social policy in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he told reporters on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can talk to Bernie about his points of view, but the Liberal party in Victoria focuses on matters in Victoria, not social policy in the United States. That is not on my radar in the slightest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked about the Liberal party\u8217\'20\'19s stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Guy said the party had allowed a conscience vote on the matter for many years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had free votes for many, many years on this matter \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19ll always continue,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to receive an email with the top stories from Guardian Australia every morning}}}\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Law Reform Act 2008 decriminalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Victoria. Under the act, a woman can legally terminate a pregnancy up to 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time Finn has been criticised for his social media posts. Last year, he deleted a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post in which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2021/nov/17/jewish-leaders-condemn-shocking-nazi-references-in-debate-on-victorias-pandemic-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he compared premier Daniel Andrews to Adolf Hitler}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He has also expressed support for Donald Trump and the rioters who stormed the US Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Guardian Australia earlier this year, Guy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/mar/15/its-not-2018-matthew-guy-learns-to-open-up-and-unite-his-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed reports Finn would be challenged}}}\uc2  for the No 1 position on the Western Metropolitan upper house ticket.\par \par \uc2 He described Finn as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery loud and proud conservative\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust because most of the mainstream media don\u8217\'20\'19t like his views, that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that people who have his views shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have a place in parliament,\u8221\'20\'1D Guy said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220505ei55000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
