\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Biden warns LGBTQ+ children could be next target of Republican \u8216\'20\'18Maga crowd\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly \par \uc2 768 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 21:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President warns of new attacks by Trump-dominated political party after supreme court ruling draft leak on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has warned of new attacks on civil rights as the supreme court prepares to strike down the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , telling reporters at the White House that LGBTQ+ children could be the next targets of a Trump-dominated Republican party he called \u8220\'20\'1Cthis Maga crowd\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organisation \u8230\'20\'26 in recent American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens,\u8221\'20\'1D the president asked, if \u8220\'20\'1Ca state changes the law saying that children who are LGBTQ can\u8217\'20\'19t be in classrooms with other children? Is that legit under the way the decision is written?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, at the end of a brief session on deficit reduction, referred to a leaked draft of a ruling by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 . One of six conservatives on the supreme court, Alito was writing on a Mississippi case which aims to overturn both Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and Casey v Planned Parenthood from 1992, which buttressed it.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi case is expected to be resolved in June. The leak of the draft ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/04/democrats-scotus-abortion-midterms-00029810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to Politico}}}\uc2 , which reported that four other conservatives on the nine-justice court supported it, caused a storm of controversy and anger.\par \par \uc2 In a statement and remarks on Tuesday, Biden condemned Alito\u8217\'20\'19s reasoning and intentions and called for legislation to codify Roe into law.\par \par \uc2 But the president has faced criticism within his own party for seeming reluctant to contemplate reform such legislation would require, namely abolishing the Senate filibuster, the rule that requires 60 votes for most bills to pass.\par \par \uc2 A lifelong Catholic who nonetheless supports a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, Biden has been eclipsed as a strong voice against the attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by high-profile Democratic women including the Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren, who spoke angrily outside the court on Tuesday, and the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s struggles as vice-president have been widely reported but on Tuesday night, speaking to the Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List advocacy group in Washington, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.org/details/CSPAN_20220504_024100_Vice_Pres._Harris_Addresses_Emilys_List_Conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she seemed to hit her stride.}}}\par \par \uc2 The former prosecutor and California senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.org/details/CSPAN_20220504_024100_Vice_Pres._Harris_Addresses_Emilys_List_Conference"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThose Republican leaders who are trying to weaponise the use of the law against women. Well, we say, \u8216\'20\'18How dare they?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow dare they tell a woman what she can do and cannot do with her own body? How dare they? How dare they try to stop her from determining her own future? How dare they try to deny women their rights and their freedoms?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She asked: \u8220\'20\'1CWhich party wants to expand our rights? And which party wants to restrict them? It has never been more clear. Which party wants to lead us forward? And which party wants to push us back? You know, some Republican leaders, they want to take us back to a time before Roe v Wade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the White House on Wednesday, Biden took brief questions. He was asked about sanctions on Russia over the invasion of Ukraine and about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next step on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once this case gets settled\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I said when this hit, as I was getting on the plane to go down to Alabama, this is about a lot more than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI hadn\u8217\'20\'19t read the whole opinion at that time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 79-year-old president then gave a lengthy, somewhat rambling answer about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe debate with Robert Bork\u8221\'20\'1D. Bork was nominated to the supreme court by \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  in 1987. Biden was then chair of the Senate judiciary committee. The nomination failed.\par \par \uc2 At the White House, Biden said Bork \u8220\'20\'1Cbelieved the only reason you had any inherent rights was because the government gave them to you\u8221\'20\'1D, a stance with which Biden said he disagreed.\par \par \uc2 Biden also said Bork had opposed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oyez.org/cases/1964/496"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Griswold v Connecticut}}}\uc2 , the 1965 case which established the right to contraception \u8211\'20\'13 a right many on the left fear may be left {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-birth-control"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open to rightwing attack}}}\uc2  once Roe, another case concerning privacy, has been overturned.\par \par \uc2 In her speech the previous night, Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CAt its core, Roe recognises the fundamental right to privacy. Think about that for a minute. When the right to privacy is attacked, anyone in our country may face a future where the government can interfere in their personal decisions. Not just women. Anyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice-president also said: \u8220\'20\'1CLet us fight for our country and for the principles upon which it was founded, and let us fight with everything we have got.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220504ei54003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
