\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden condemns efforts of extremist \u8216\'20\'18Maga crowd\u8217\'20\'19 to overturn Roe v Wade  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  protections \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,826 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 20:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden: \u8216\'20\'18This Maga crowd is really the most extreme political organization that exists in American history\u8217\'20\'19How soon could states outlaw abortions if Roe v Wade is overturned?Protesters swarm outside US supreme courtContraception could come under fire nextCalifornia pledges to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rightsWhat the justices have said and how they\u8217\'20\'19ve voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now, but you can follow developments in the Russia-Ukraine conflict on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/04/russia-ukraine-war-russia-attacks-azovstal-steel-plant-after-first-evacuated-civilians-reach-safety-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour news blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  railed against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -inspired Republicans he said formed the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost extreme political organization that exists in American history\u8221\'20\'1D for their efforts to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LBGTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we followed:\par \par \uc2 * The cost of borrowing increased after the US federal reserve announced Wednesday it was raising its benchmark overnight interest rate 0.5%, the biggest jump in 22 years. Officials said it would help temper soaring inflation.\par \par \uc2 * New York\u8217\'20\'19s congressional primaries are on track for August after a federal judge denied a voters\u8217\'20\'19 group\u8217\'20\'19s demand to force them to take place next month. The state is redrawing district maps after another judge ruled the originals favorable to Democrats and thus unlawful.\par \par \uc2 * Derek Chauvin will receive 20 to 25 years in prison for violating \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil rights as the former Minneapolis officer was murdering him, the judge overseeing a federal civil rights trial said.\par \par \uc2 * Acting homeland security secretary \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  delayed intelligence about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s interference in the 2020 election to protect then-president Trump, a watchdog report has found.\par \par \uc2 * Canada\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  promised to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling to eliminate decades-old protections in the US.\par \par \uc2 * An overwhelming majority of Americans are in favor of preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, new polls have found, voters preferring by a two to one ratio to maintain the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion that safeguarded women\u8217\'20\'19s access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has defended \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments earlier today condemning Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism\u8221\'20\'1D in seeking to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the supreme court and promoting anti-LBGTQ+ legislation in numerous states.\par \par \uc2 Biden was forthright in his criticism at his morning briefing, assailing the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 -inspired wing of the party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Maga crowd\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18make America great again\u8217\'20\'19 electioneering slogan, \u8220\'20\'1Cis really the most extreme political organization that exists in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At her afternoon press briefing, Psaki said Biden was speaking his mind after reading the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling ending almost a half-century of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 What you\u8217\'20\'19re hearing play out is the president\u8217\'20\'19s own reaction to what he found in these documents, and his view that the protection of privacy, and the protection of the ability of women to make decisions about their health care with their doctors, about people to be able to choose who they marry, reminded him how important those protections are.\par \par \uc2 Asked about Biden considering the Republican stance \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D, Psaki said:\par \par \uc2 Republicans have wanted to talk about [the leak of the draft ruling] and not about whether they support the protection of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to make decisions with her doctor about her health care.\par \par \uc2 [That\u8217\'20\'19s] maybe not a surprise given by more than a two to one margin Americans want the supreme court to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has tested positive for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 The White House secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  confirmed the news at her afternoon press briefing, noting he is not considered a close contact of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/secretary-blinken-tests-positive-for-covid-19/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  from the department of state says Blinken is vaccinated and boosted and experiencing only mild symptoms.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Secretary of State \uc2 Anthony Blinken\uc2  tested positive for Covid-19 this afternoon, per spokesman. He tested negative on Tuesday and as recently as this morning. Blinken was at the White House correspondents dinner.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1521938996246589442?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  thanked American athletes from recent summer and winter Olympic games, and the Paralympics, at the White House on Wednesday, hailing Team USA for bringing some unity to a pandemic-weary nation.\par \par \uc2 At a reception on the south lawn, the president and first lady Jill Biden greeted about 600 athletes from this year\u8217\'20\'19s winter games in Beijing and the coronavirus-delayed summer event staged last year in Tokyo, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou represent the very soul of America. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a very divided nation... but you brought us together. No matter the divisions, when we see you compete, we feel a common pride in those three letters: USA,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at the event also attended by vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and first gentleman Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Doug Emhoff welcome Team USA to the White House Wednesday. Photograph: Anadolu Agency/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Among the athletes in attendance were swimmer and seven-time gold medalist Katie Ledecky, bobsledder Elena Meyers Taylor and ice dancer Zachary Donahue, as well as competitors from the past two Paralympic games.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that Team USA athletes won 260 medals in Beijing and Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 The 2020 Tokyo games were delayed one year due to Covid-19 and took place last summer, largely without spectators. Jill Biden led the US delegation to Japan.\par \par \uc2 At the Beijing Olympics this past winter, also held mostly without spectators, the US staged a diplomatic boycott due to China\u8217\'20\'19s human rights abuses against Uyghur Muslims in Xinjiang.\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden said Wednesday Americans were \u8220\'20\'1Cgrateful for the gifts\u8221\'20\'1D they gave the country at a difficult time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese games may not have been exactly as you once imagined with stadiums packed with people and all of your loved ones screaming from the sidelines,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COlympian or a Paralympian is a rare accomplishment in a normal time, but you did it during a global pandemic. You are forever one of the most elite, most celebrated athletes in this world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Guess the supreme court leaker has become something of a parlour game in Washington, not least because Republicans in Congress sought to make it the focus of coverage on Tuesday rather than the immeasurable damage overturning Roe v Wade will do to women\u8217\'20\'19s lives across the US.\par \par \uc2 Mike Brzezinski. Photograph: Jonathan Ernst/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Mika Brzezinski\uc2 , who with Joe Scarborough forms MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Morning Joe power couple, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Morning_Joe/status/1521834981563187200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lambasted}}}\uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe old white guy, Mitch, is going to tell us what the story of the day is?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s rich, Mitch \u8230\'20\'26 the bottom line is this is setting women back in so many different ways with so many different consequences, and you\u8217\'20\'19re going to tell us that the story is the leak?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Other pundits have suggested McConnell might be \u8211\'20\'13 gasp \u8211\'20\'13 playing something of a dastardly double game. In short, the theory is that the leak may not have come from the liberal side of the court, as much of the right is thunderously proclaiming, but instead from someone connected to a conservative justice.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Rick Wilson, of the anti-Trump Lincoln Project and before that countless Republican campaigns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheRickWilson/status/1521658980610813952"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen enough}}}\uc2 . The supreme court leak looks, smells, and tastes like a giant kayfabe. [In pro wrestling, the fact or convention of presenting staged performances as genuine or authentic.]\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not that I have some secret insight into the court. It\u8217\'20\'19s that I\u8217\'20\'19m a damn anthropologist of the rightwing media ecosystem in which I operated for decades.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sweeping media and political class lockstep on the right \u8211\'20\'13 histrionics hair-tearing about the leak \u8211\'20\'13 are just too coordinated given the short timeframe from release-to-presser. The intervals are too tight and the messages too word-for-word.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo quote the political philosopher Ian Fleming, \u8216\'20\'18Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action.\u8217\'20\'19 By 7am ET [on Tuesday], the usual suspects on the rightwing media gulag were on EXACTLY the same outrage \u8216\'20\'18HOW DARE YOU SIR!\u8217\'20\'19 tone and message.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So there you go.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 My colleague Chris Michael has taken a look at each of the nine \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices, and their positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights:\par \par \uc2 With Roe v Wade on the brink of defeat, following the leak of a supreme court opinion written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and signed by four other conservative judges, the court\u8217\'20\'19s views \u8211\'20\'13 and track record \u8211\'20\'13 on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are under extreme scrutiny. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the nine justices have actually said over the years about it:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2022/may/04/how-supreme-court-justices-voted-abortion-alito-roberts-thomas-kavanaugh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court justices on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  \u8211\'20\'13 what they\u8217\'20\'19ve said and how they\u8217\'20\'19ve voted}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal reserve raises interest rate 0.5%, largest hike in 22 years\par \par \uc2 The cost of borrowing is increasing after the US federal reserve announced Wednesday it was raising its benchmark overnight interest rate 0.5%, the biggest jump in 22 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHousehold spending and business fixed investment remain strong. Job gains have been robust,\u8221\'20\'1D the fed\u8217\'20\'19s board of governors said in a statement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/federal-reserve-interest-rate-inflation-8d5e20882cdfd7975ebb3bb48a437f11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government will also begin trimming bond holdings next month as it attempts to temper soaring inflation, the statement added.\par \par \uc2 The announcement follows \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s speech at the White House this morning, in which he promoted his administration\u8217\'20\'19s success in reducing the US federal deficit, but which was more notable for his attacks on the \u8220\'20\'1Cextremism\u8221\'20\'1D of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -inspired Republicans seeking to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and LBGTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  intensified its drive to curb the worst inflation in 40 years by raising its short-term interest rate by a sizable half-percentage point.\par \par \uc2 It is the agency's most aggressive hike since 2000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0H2eDZoyph"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0H2eDZoyph}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Associated Press (@AP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AP/status/1521918030414024705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats see runaway inflation as a vote-loser for November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, at which control of both chambers of Congress is at stake.\par \par \uc2 Raising interest rates so aggressively now could be a double-edged sword, analysts believe. It might help to bring down inflation, but will increase the cost of borrowing, including mortgages and credit card debt.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has reported extensively about the impact of inflation on the US economy and citizens:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/apr/30/us-inflation-price-increases-government-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What am I going to do?\u8217\'20\'19: soaring prices fuel calls for US government to step in}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Stanford University\uc2  is to establish a school of sustainability, focusing on the climate emergency, after receiving a $1.1bn endowment from venture capitalist \uc2 John Doerr\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 John Doerr\uc2 . Photograph: Associated Press\par \par \uc2 The Stanford Doerr school of sustainability will be the university\u8217\'20\'19s first new school in 70 years, and will open in the fall, according to a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClimate and sustainability is going to be the new computer science,\u8221\'20\'1D Doerr told the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/05/04/climate/john-doerr-stanford-climate.html?searchResultPosition=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in an interview}}}\uc2  published Wednesday. He made his estimated fortune of more than $11bn investing in companies including \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Doerr joins billionaires including \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  and \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2 , who in recent years have donated money to combat climate change.\par \par \uc2 Progressive politicians such as the independent Vermont senator Bernie Sanders say the climate crisis cannot be solved by the charity of individual billionaires, and that governments need to set up proper taxation systems to make sure billionaires pay their fair share.\par \par \uc2 Stanford says Doerr\u8217\'20\'19s gift is the largest ever to a university for the establishment of a new school, and is the second largest gift to an academic institution, according to the Chronicle of Higher Education.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Manhattan federal judge is allowing New York to proceed with plans to move June congressional and state Senate primaries to August, but asked the state board of elections to seek final approval from a federal judge in Albany, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Lewis Kaplan on Wednesday rejected the application for a temporary restraining order from a group of New York voters who wanted to keep the possibility of 28 June primaries open.\par \par \uc2 Represented by Democratic attorney Marc Elias, the group there was still time to draft new maps for a June primary after state appeals judges found the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/27/new-york-court-rejects-congressional-maps-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 original maps were unconstitutional}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An independent court expert is crafting new maps by 20 May under the oversight of a state judge in Steuben county, who ordered the delay of the June primaries to 23 August.\par \par \uc2 The voters said a 2012 court order by Albany-based district judge Gary Sharpe compelled the primaries to take place in June, but Kaplan said the New York board can easily talk to Sharpe about moving the date.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s lunchtime, so a chance for a quick back on how the day is going:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -inspired Maga crowd is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organization in history\u8221\'20\'1D as he condemned efforts to overturn Roe v Wade \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections.\par \par \uc2 * Derek Chauvin will receive 20 to 25 years in prison for violating \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s civil rights as the former Minneapolis officer was murdering him, the judge overseeing a federal civil rights trial said.\par \par \uc2 * Acting homeland security secretary \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  delayed intelligence about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s interference in the 2020 election to protect then-president Trump, a watchdog report has found.\par \par \uc2 * Canada\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  promised to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the wake of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling to eliminate decades-old protections in the US.\par \par \uc2 * An overwhelming majority of Americans are in favor of preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, new polls have found, voters preferring by a two to one ratio to maintain the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion that safeguarded women\u8217\'20\'19s access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 The judge overseeing the federal civil rights cases of four former Minneapolis police officers in the killing of \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  said Wednesday that he has accepted the terms of Derek Chauvin\u8217\'20\'19s plea agreement and will sentence him to 20 to 25 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 The George Floyd Memorial seen during a heavy snowstorm at \uc2 George Floyd\uc2  Square in Minneapolis, Minnesota, on February 21, 2022. Photograph: Kerem Yucel/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 When the white former office is sentenced he will serve the term concurrently with the state criminal sentence he is currently serving (and appealing), of 22.5 years, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/20/derek-chauvin-verdict-guilty-murder-george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his conviction}}}\uc2  last spring for the May 2020 murder of Floyd, a Black father who had moved from Houston to Minneapolis to start a new chapter after being released from prison.\par \par \uc2 Chauvin pleaded guilty December 15 to violating Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights, admitting for the first time that he kept his knee on Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s neck even after he became unresponsive resulting in the Black man\u8217\'20\'19s death, The Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 He admitted he willfully deprived Floyd of his right to be free from unreasonable seizure, including unreasonable force by a police officer.\par \par \uc2 Under the plea agreement, which Chauvin signed, both sides agreed Chauvin should face a sentence ranging from 20 to 25 years, with prosecutors saying they would seek 25.\par \par \uc2 He could have faced life in prison on the federal count.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Paul Magnuson deferred accepting the agreement pending the completion of a pre-sentence investigation. He has not set a sentencing date for Chauvin.\par \par \uc2 Chauvin waived his right to contest his federal conviction if Magnuson accepted the plea agreement.\par \par \uc2 Magnuson also has not set sentencing dates for three other ex-officers who were convicted of related federal civil rights charges in February.\par \par \uc2 The pre-sentence investigations for Tou Thao, Thomas Lane and J. Alexander Kueng are still underway. They\u8217\'20\'19re scheduled to go on trial next month in state court on charges of aiding and abetting Chauvin in Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s murder.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s no-show at another debate in Georgia of Republican senate hopefuls on Tuesday saw the Donald-Trump endorsed former football star mercilessly ribbed by his rivals.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to Walker\u8217\'20\'19s empty podium at the Atlanta Press Club, Latham Saddler, a Navy veteran among a crowded field for the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms. said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our fifth debate or forum he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t showed up.\par \par \uc2 A simple question for \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  is, what do you think the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  does? It\u8217\'20\'19s the deliberative body of Congress.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s what you do as a US senator, you get up there and you debate ideas. And \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t get up here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWalker\u8217\'20\'19s empty podium is introduced at the debate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Jvh51diVJt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Jvh51diVJt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1521640105257037827?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The void where Walker should have been has become an almost defining sight of the campaign to challenge Democrat \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 But while his apparent complacency won\u8217\'20\'19t affect him winning the nomination - he leads the field by a country mile according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/senate/ga/2022-georgia-republican-senate-primary-7384.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest RealClearPolitics polling}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 it might cost him in November. Warnock currently leads by five points in a head-to-head matchup.\par \par \uc2 Not that Walker, a controversial character with a turbulent past, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/lifestyle-sports-nfl-college-football-coronavirus-pandemic-5e2875eec11e93f9a3bf1fc859137ff8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , seems too concerned. While his rivals were highlighting his absence, Walker\u8217\'20\'19s communications director Mallory Blount was tweeting out insults:\par \par \uc2 enltrHerschel is meeting with hundreds of voters in Burke County.\par \par \uc2 Hope y\u8217\'20\'19all have fun obsessing over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HerschelWalker?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @HerschelWalker}}}\uc2  at the debate! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gasen?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gasen}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/debate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #debate}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vmkiMd41rl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vmkiMd41rl}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Dm27PPbKys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Dm27PPbKys}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mallory Blount (@malloryblount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/malloryblount/status/1521632983538618374?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Canadian Prime Minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  vowed to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights as the decades-old battle over the issue exploded anew this week in Canada\u8217\'20\'19s southern neighbor, with the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  apparently set to overturn the decades-old ruling that legalized the procedure nationwide, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 A woman\u8217\'20\'19s free choice is a choice to be made by her alone. Every woman in Canada has the right to a legal and safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau told reporters before a meeting of Liberal lawmakers in Ottawa on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/biden-democrats-reaction-codifying-roe-v-wade-reform-scotus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft supreme court decision}}}\uc2 , leaked late on Monday, showed a majority of justices prepared to overturn the 1973 Roe v Wade decision that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The court on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed the authenticity}}}\uc2  of the leaked document and ordered an investigation.\par \par \uc2 We know that unfortunately, what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing with our neighbors in the south and even in debates within the \uc2 Conservative Party of Canada\uc2 , that we need to ensure that there are protections in place so that we never see people backtracking on that right,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau said.\par \par \uc2 He added that Canada will consider legal options if such rights are at risk of violation in the country.\par \par \uc2 We have asked the ministers to take a look at this (review of the legal framework) very quickly and we\u8217\'20\'19ll see what the timeline is for that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau said.\par \par \uc2 Canada\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court\uc2  decriminalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a historic 1988 ruling. Ostensibly, since then, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a medical procedure like any other. But barriers to access persist, especially for people living outside urban areas.\par \par \uc2 Canada\u8217\'20\'19s top court is unlikely to re-criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/us-supreme-court-abortion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 if the supreme court overturns}}}\uc2  Roe v Wade, that could embolden anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements and galvanize pro-choice activists, Canadian observers and advocates on both sides of the divisive issue noted.\par \par \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  attends an Eid celebration in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada May 2, 2022. Photograph: Blair Gable/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: 'Maga crowd most extreme political organization in US history'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just been at the podium in the White House, slamming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -supporting Republicans as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most extreme political organization in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Billed as an economic progress report to tout what he says is a record reduction in the federal deficit, the president wasted no time in attacking \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Maga crowd\u8221\'20\'1D, named for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18make America great again\u8217\'20\'19 electioneering slogan.\par \par \uc2 He slammed Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 economic policies, and saved his fiercest comments for a question on the draft ruling by Republican-appointed judges on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  seeking to overturn almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, and assaults on LBGTQ+ rights in Republican controlled states.\par \par \uc2 What are the next things that are going to be attacked? Because this Maga crowd is really the most extreme political organization that exists in American history.\par \par \uc2 This is about a lot more than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... What happens if you have a state change the law, saying that children who are LGBTQ can\u8217\'20\'19t be in classrooms with other children? Is that legit?\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks at the White House on Wednesday. Photograph: Evelyn Hockstein/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Biden also laid into \u8220\'20\'1Cmy predecessor\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who failed to reduce the federal deficit at any stage of his single term of office.\par \par \uc2 It didn\u8217\'20\'19t happen to single quarter under my predecessor, not once. The bottom line is the deficit went up every year under my predecessor before the pandemic and during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 And it\u8217\'20\'19s gone down both years since I\u8217\'20\'19ve been here. Period. That\u8217\'20\'19s the facts.\par \par \uc2 With soaring inflation, and the economy uppermost in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s midterms, Biden is keen to showcase his achievements. He said the federal deficit had dropped $350bn in his first in office, and was \u8220\'20\'1Con track\u8221\'20\'1D for another record $1.5tn drop this year.\par \par \uc2 But it was his comments on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Maga crowd\u8221\'20\'1D that caught the most attention.\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to hear Republicans talking about deficits and their ultra Maga agenda. I want to hear about fairness. I want to hear about decency... about ordinary people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 DHS secretary 'delayed Russia intelligence' to benefit Trump: report\par \par \uc2 NBC is reporting that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acting homeland security secretary \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2  twice held up intelligence on Russian interference ahead of the 2020 election because it would make the then-president \u8220\'20\'1Clook bad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/trump-appointee-twice-delayed-report-russian-election-interference-fed-rcna27198"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The network cites}}}\uc2  a report by the homeland security department\u8217\'20\'19s watchdog, and claims a \u8220\'20\'1CTrump political appointee\u8221\'20\'1D delayed the release of an intelligence analysis stating that \u8220\'20\'1CRussian malign influence actors\u8221\'20\'1D were spreading unsubstantiated allegations about the health of then-candidate \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to reduce voters\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in him.\par \par \uc2 Chad Wolf\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Russia, NBC states, was using both overt and covert channels and linked the efforts to similar operations during the 2016 presidential election. But Wolf did not want the analysis released because he felt it would reflect badly on Trump, the network says.\par \par \uc2 Trump named Wolf as acting DHS secretary in November 2019, and he remained in office until January 2021, despite a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/15/judge-rules-daca-suspension-invalid-homeland-security-head-in-office-illegally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling his appointment unlawful}}}\uc2  in November 2020.\par \par \uc2 He was not named in the report by the DHS inspector general, but in a Wednesday statement to NBC admitted he was the Trump appointee referenced. He denied his actions were malign.\par \par \uc2 The IG, Wolf said, \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not find any credible evidence that I directed anyone to change the substance of the report because it \u8216\'20\'18made President Trump look bad\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBuried in the report is the fact that the grossly false whistleblower complaint against me was withdrawn\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The inspector general\u8217\'20\'19s report was sparked by a complaint from a worker concerned that \u8220\'20\'1Ctop DHS officials were violating laws and policies by lying to Congress and manipulating intelligence reports to conform with President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/national-security/whistleblower-says-top-dhs-officials-distorted-intel-match-trump-statements-n1239685"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC reported at the time}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voters in Michigan roundly rejected a Republican candidate for the state\u8217\'20\'19s House who said women being raped should \u8220\'20\'1Clie back and enjoy it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Party officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/michigan-gop-condemns-candidates-comment-lie-back-enjoy-rape-1686124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized Robert Regan}}}\uc2  for the comments he made during an online roundtable discussion in March.\par \par \uc2 Robert Regan. Photograph: Jeff Kowalsky/AFP/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving three daughters, and I tell my daughters, \u8216\'20\'18Well if rape is inevitable, you should just lie back and enjoy it so\u8217\'20\'19. That\u8217\'20\'19s not how we roll, that\u8217\'20\'19s not how I won this election. We go right at it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said days after winning his party\u8217\'20\'19s primary for the vacant 74th district seat.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ballot published by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2022/05/03/carol-glanville-upsets-robert-regan-bid-michigan-house/9614211002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit Free Press}}}\uc2 , Regan was upset by Democrat Carol Glanville in a district seat that has only ever been served by Republicans, receiving 40% of the vote to Glanville\u8217\'20\'19s 51%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWest Michigan values of integrity, decency, and care for the common good won tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/caglanville/status/1521672512094019584"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Glanville tweeted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Regan, a rightwing extremist, was previously in the news when he announced his candidacy in July 2020, when his daughter urged voters: \u8220\'20\'1CFor the love of God, please do not vote for my dad,\u8221\'20\'1D as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/26/please-do-not-vote-for-my-dad-republican-daughter-robert-reagan-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Guardian here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrWest Michigan values of integrity, decency, and care for the common good won tonight. The people of the 74th District have spoken, and I hear you. We are united in fundamental ways, and I will take our values and concerns to the Capitol to affect positive change. Thank you! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V1fCaRShFG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/V1fCaRShFG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Carol Glanville (@caglanville) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/caglanville/status/1521672512094019584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 4, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Author JD Vance won the Senate Republican primary in Ohio on Tuesday, securing a victory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/29/jd-vance-senate-ohio-trump-influence-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after receiving Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement}}}\uc2  in the hotly contested race.\par \par \uc2 Vance was leading the crowded pack of primary candidates with 32% of the vote when the Associated Press called the race, about two hours after polls closed. Former state treasurer Josh Mandel looked likely to finish second, and state Senator \uc2 Matt Dolan\uc2 , who saw a last-minute surge in support, rounded out the top three.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance celebrates his senate Republican primary win in Cincinnati, Ohio. Photograph: Drew Angerer/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Addressing supporters in Cincinnati, Vance thanked Trump for his endorsement and attacked the media for highlighting his past criticism of the former president. \u8220\'20\'1CThey wanted to write a story that this campaign would be the death of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s America First agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt ain\u8217\'20\'19t the death of the America First agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance, the bestselling author of the memoir Hillbilly Elegy, will now face Democratic congressman \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  in November to determine who will fill the seat of retiring Republican Senator Rob Portman. Ryan, who ran for president in 2020, easily fended off a primary challenge from progressive candidate Morgan Harper.\par \par \uc2 Delivering a message of unity to his supporters on Tuesday, Ryan promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild a home for Ohioans\u8221\'20\'1D regardless of their political party. \u8220\'20\'1CThe work is just beginning. The fight is just beginning. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to heal the country \u8211\'20\'13 heal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2  and in turn heal the United States of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryan said in Columbus.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio race could prove crucial in determining control of the Senate, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  look to retake the upper chamber this November. The Senate is currently evenly split 50-50, but Democrats have the majority thanks to the tie-breaking vote of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If Republicans can pick up just one seat in the midterm elections, they will regain control of the Senate, and holding Portman\u8217\'20\'19s seat will be key to those efforts.\par \par \uc2 Vance starts his general-election campaigning with a clear advantage in the race, as Trump defeated \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Ohio by 8 points in 2020. Democrats across the country are also at a disadvantage, as the president\u8217\'20\'19s party usually loses seats in the midterm elections and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mired in the low 40s}}}\uc2  for months.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/donald-trump-backed-candidate-jd-vance-wins-ohio-senate-republican-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump-backed candidate JD Vance wins Ohio Senate Republican primary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Lauren Burke was at the supreme court on Tuesday, watching numbers of protestors swell as word spread of justices\u8217\'20\'19 draft ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 Outside the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  the morning after a bombshell leak revealed justices are poised to overturn Roe v Wade, the day began with dozens of protesters. By the afternoon, thousands had arrived to make their voices heard \u8211\'20\'13 with many on opposite sides of America\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 The possibility of a repeal of the landmark 1973 decision brought energized and sometimes emotional supporters of Roe to protests in major cities from New York to San Francisco. But the supreme court was ground zero.\par \par \uc2 Members of the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  closed the street in front of the supreme court building as protesters filled and took over the area, holding signs and large banners.\par \par \uc2 It was a tense atmosphere that brought anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pro-choice protesters into close range, outside the building where nine of the most powerful individuals in the US decide the nation\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 Protestors at the supreme court on Tuesday. Photograph: Anna Moneymaker/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because I was here in 2016 and couldn\u8217\'20\'19t fucking believe that I had to tell people that women are people \u8211\'20\'13 but clearly we do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cindy from Great Falls, Virginia, who asked that her last name be withheld. While she didn\u8217\'20\'19t expect to change the court\u8217\'20\'19s mind, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s really nice to see a bunch of like minded people and get the vibe and I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m here \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that this will motivate people to vote because I think that\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna help,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 As the number of protesters built steadily throughout the morning, Democratic senators gathered nearby on the Senate steps for a press conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a five alarm fire,\u8221\'20\'1D said Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , as demonstrators\u8217\'20\'19 chants rang out across the grassy lawn separating the capitol from the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Read the full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-protests-outside-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tears and tension as protesters swarm outside US supreme court}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 An overwhelming majority of Americans are in favor of preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, two new polls have found, as the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  moves towards ending almost half a century of protections.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/04/poll-roe-v-wade-00029889"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico/Morning Consult study}}}\uc2  found voters are two to one in favor of preserving the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion that safeguarded protected women\u8217\'20\'19s access to abortions.\par \par \uc2 The poll conducted Tuesday, shortly after Politico\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell publication}}}\uc2  of the draft ruling from the supreme court overturning Roe, showed exactly 50% of respondents wanted it maintained. 28% wanted it overturned, and 22% were undecided.\par \par \uc2 A separate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/05/03/most-americans-say-supreme-court-should-uphold-roe-post-abc-poll-finds/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post/ABC poll}}}\uc2  reports 54% in favor of preserving Roe, and 28% against, while an even higher number of Americans, 70%, think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a private issue between patient and doctor.\par \par \uc2 The figures are sure to bolster Democrats who plan to campaign on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue for the upcoming midterm elections. While the party is unlikely to be able to pass legislation enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights because of opposition in the Senate, its base will be fired up by a wave of resistance, already manifesting itself in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-protests-outside-us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests taking place nationwide}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose Republican leaders who are trying to weaponize the use of the law against women, we say, \u8216\'20\'18How dare they? How dare they tell a woman what she can and cannot do with her own body?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said at a conference on women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights in Washington DC on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaks at the Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List national gala in Washington DC on Tuesday evening. Photograph: Yuri Gripas/UPI/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is going further, warning on Tuesday that more freedoms could be at risk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would mean that every other decision relating to the notion of privacy is thrown into question,\u8221\'20\'1D the president told reporters on Tuesday of the draft ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf what is written is what remains, it goes far beyond the concern of whether or not there is the right to choose. It goes to other basic rights, who you marry... whether or not you decide to conceive a child, whether or not you can have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a range of other decisions, how you raise your child.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the Politico poll, 68% of Democrats and 52% of independents say Roe should not be overturned, and a narrow majority of Republicans, 51%, believe it should.\par \par \uc2 And as numerous Republican controlled states introduce or harden anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in expectation of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s final ruling, due in late June or July, a majority of respondents in the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 /ABC poll say they are moving in the wrong direction.\par \par \uc2 Asked if their state should make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  easier to access, 33% said yes, 25% said it should be harder, and 36% want it left as it is.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our midweek politics blog. The nation is still reeling from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/04/first-thing-us-shaken-by-supreme-court-draft-overturning-roe-v-wade-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombshell news}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  that justices appear ready to strike down almost half a century of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, despite overwhelming opposition.\par \par \uc2 Polling suggests the court\u8217\'20\'19s position is vastly at odds with public opinion. In the wake of the leak of the panel\u8217\'20\'19s draft ruling on Monday night, a Politico/Morning Consult study found voters are two to one in favor of preserving the 1973 Roe v Wade opinion that protected women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to abortions.\par \par \uc2 Its findings are almost identical to a separate \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 /ABC poll that reports 54% in favor of preserving Roe, and 28% against, while an even higher number of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a private issue between patient and doctor. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more analysis of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue coming up.\par \par \uc2 Head over to our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/may/04/russia-ukraine-war-russia-attacks-azovstal-steel-plant-after-first-evacuated-civilians-reach-safety-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour news blog here}}}\uc2  for developments in the Ukraine conflict.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at in the US today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s reputation as a kingmaker was enhanced in Ohio, where his preferred candidate JD Vance beat out other Republicans chasing the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination for \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Trump is also under scrutiny in a watchdog report claiming one of his cabinet appointees delayed intelligence about Russian interference in the 2020 election for political gain.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will speak on the economy at lunchtime, specifically the need for \u8220\'20\'1Cfiscal responsibility and deficit reduction\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House says.\par \par \uc2 * The White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will deliver her daily briefing at 2.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220504ei54001xk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
