\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Tears and tension as protesters swarm outside \uc2 US supreme court\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Burke in Washington \par \uc2 805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 14:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 As news broke of the possibility of Roe v Wade being overturned, demonstrators gathered in major cities\par \par \uc2 Outside the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  the morning after a bombshell leak revealed justices are poised to overturn Roe v Wade, the day began with dozens of protesters. By the afternoon, thousands had arrived to make their voices heard \u8211\'20\'13 with many on opposite sides of America\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate.\par \par \uc2 The possibility of a repeal of the landmark 1973 decision brought energized and sometimes emotional supporters of Roe to protests in major cities from New York to San Francisco. But the supreme court was ground zero.\par \par \uc2 Members of the US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  closed the street in front of the supreme court building as protesters filled and took over the area, holding signs and large banners.\par \par \uc2 It was a tense atmosphere that brought anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pro-choice protesters into close range, outside the building where nine of the most powerful individuals in the US decide the nation\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here because I was here in 2016 and couldn\u8217\'20\'19t fucking believe that I had to tell people that women are people \u8211\'20\'13 but clearly we do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cindy from Great Falls, Virginia, who asked that her last name be withheld. While she didn\u8217\'20\'19t expect to change the court\u8217\'20\'19s mind, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s really nice to see a bunch of like minded people and get the vibe and I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m here \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m pissed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that this will motivate people to vote because I think that\u8217\'20\'19s the only thing that\u8217\'20\'19s gonna help,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 As the number of protesters built steadily throughout the morning, Democratic senators gathered nearby on the Senate steps for a press conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a five alarm fire,\u8221\'20\'1D said Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , as demonstrators\u8217\'20\'19 chants rang out across the grassy lawn separating the capitol from the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats are already discussing legislation to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the law, those on the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  side of the debate were relieved to hear Roe could be overturned, and often cited religious concerns.\par \par \uc2 A young Black woman, who asked to be quoted anonymously for privacy reasons, said she cam e from the suburbs near the nation\u8217\'20\'19s Capitol and that she opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m realizing that if people don\u8217\'20\'19t stand for people who can\u8217\'20\'19t stand up for themselves, then we\u8217\'20\'19re not really American. I\u8217\'20\'19m here not representing any political party or any side or left or right or whatever. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to just stand for Jesus and that we are made in the image of God,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, standing on the sidewalk outside the supreme court and holding a handmade sign. \u8220\'20\'1CI did the Black Lives Matter protest because I believe in the sanctity of life and I have to keep that same energy. If you believe in life, it\u8217\'20\'19s sacred at all times. George Floyd mattered in his mother\u8217\'20\'19s womb and he mattered the day he was executed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alan Cohen, who said he lived in the local area, echoed similar religious concerns. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat brings me out here is obedience to Jesus Christ. I\u8217\'20\'19m a Christian, and God commands us to go and make disciples of all the nations, including the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Cohen said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo in big events like this, especially ones that are very emotionally charged, our calling is to proclaim the Gospel, whether or not the crowd is popular with it or not. That\u8217\'20\'19s our obedience and call as Christians,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 While the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision is not yet final, the leak of the draft is set to further enflame political division ahead of the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country is experiencing a full partisan assault on women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and freedom to control our own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Melanie Campbell\uc2 , convener of the Black Women\u8217\'20\'19s Roundtable, which often polls a vital voting block for Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CAs Black women, we stand at the intersection of voting rights and reproductive justice, with the full understanding that the struggle for our right to vote is inextricably tied to our reproductive rights as women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The midterms will decide the fate of who controls the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  and will be held in November. If the supreme court overturns Roe, impact at the ballot box is widely predicted.\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders, standing inside the US Capitol, described it as a make or break moment for the Democratic party. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the Democrats have to do is rally the American people around something the American people feel strongly about. There is very strong majority support that a woman has the right to control their own bodies and that Roe v. Wade should not be repealed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220504ei54000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
