\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We can\u8217\'20\'19t trust \uc2 Scotus\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19: California pledges to protect  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 998 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 05:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said an amendment is being proposed that would \u8216\'20\'18enshrine the right to choose\u8217\'20\'19 in the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution\par \par \uc2 With reproductive rights in peril across the US and a draft supreme court ruling that would overturn Roe v Wade, California is working to further enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and expand access in anticipation of a surge of people seeking care from out of state.\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , has long pledged that the state would become a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/08/california-sanctuary-abortion-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sanctuary}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for people seeking reproductive care if the supreme court were to overturn the 1973 case that guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After a draft ruling leaked showing the court may have decided to do just that, Newsom said he and state leaders were proposing an amendment that would \u8220\'20\'1Censhrine the right to choose\u8221\'20\'1D in California\u8217\'20\'19s constitution. State lawmakers are currently considering recommendations from a council tasked to finding solutions in case Roe is overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t trust \uc2 Scotus\uc2  to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so we\u8217\'20\'19ll do it ourselves,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWomen will remain protected here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NEW: We are proposing an amendment to enshrine the right to choose in the California constitution.\par \par \uc2 We can\u8217\'20\'19t trust \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so we\u8217\'20\'19ll do it ourselves.\par \par \uc2 Women will remain protected here. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WTUpfymLS0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WTUpfymLS0}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  (@GavinNewsom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GavinNewsom/status/1521358301794947072?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In the draft ruling, obtained by Politico in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/chief-justice-roberts-abortion-leak-investigation-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 biggest leak}}}\uc2  in the modern history of the supreme court, Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  describes Roe as \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong from the start. Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences\u8221\'20\'1D. The court confirmed the authenticity of the draft, but said it did not \u8220\'20\'1Crepresent a decision by the court or the final position of any member\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The potential decision has shaken the country, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been legal for nearly 50 years but under constant threat as Republican states significantly reduced access and sought to ban the procedure entirely. The majority of Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal and news of the draft ruling has prompted protests and widespread outrage.\par \par \uc2 If the court ultimately decides to overturn Roe v Wade, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/what-states-abortion-clinics-access-trigger-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half of US states}}}\uc2  will outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , closing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics for 41% of women of reproductive age and forcing hundreds of thousands of people to travel elsewhere to obtain the procedure. Experts warn some states may attempt to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-abortions-travel-wave-of-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban people from traveling}}}\uc2  for abortions.\par \par \uc2 States where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain legal such as California would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/04/blue-states-abortion-rights-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly affected}}}\uc2  if Roe were to fall, with a major influx of out-of-state patients that could increase wait times for abortions. The state has already reported seeing more patients since Texas banned abortions after six weeks. California could see an almost 3,000% increase in the number of people whose nearest legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider is in the state, which could increase the annual patient load from 46,000 people to 1.4 million with many patients coming from as near as Arizona, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://states.guttmacher.org/#california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute report}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jodi Hicks, the CEO and president of Planned Parenthood Affiliates of California, said the draft ruling is a \u8220\'20\'1Cnightmare scenario\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 "Leaked draft shows \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  has voted to strike down Roe v. Wade"\par \par \uc2 This is the nightmare scenario we in the reproductive health, rights, and justice space have been sounding the alarm about -- especially once \uc2 SCOTUS\uc2  had a conservative majority. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/irLELRImdJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/irLELRImdJ}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Jodi Hicks (@jodihicks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jodihicks/status/1521333017238654978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator, warned if the court overturns Roe \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen will be harmed and some will die. It happened before Roe became the law of the land and it will happen again, particularly since this decision will harm low-income and at-risk women more than anyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I remember the days when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal, when we would pass the hat at Stanford to collect money so a classmate could go to Mexico for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Overturning Roe would return us to those dark ages where women don\u8217\'20\'19t have safe, open access to reproductive care.\u8212\'20\'14 Senator \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2  (@SenFeinstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenFeinstein/status/1521501472692879360?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 California has already taken steps to navigate a post-Roe world. Last year, Newsom commissioned the California Future of \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Council, made up of more than 40 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and advocacy groups, which released a list of 45 recommendations for the state to consider if the court overturns Roe.\par \par \uc2 The recommendations, some of which are part of legislation under consideration by state lawmakers, included creating a fund to support care for low-income Californians and people traveling from out of state to obtain abortions.\par \par \uc2 Newsom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2022/03/22/governor-newsom-signs-legislation-to-eliminate-out-of-pocket-costs-for-abortion-services/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed legislation in March}}}\uc2  prohibiting health plans and insurers from charging people a copay or deductible for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related services.\par \par \uc2 The president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Los Angeles, Sue Dunlap, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/politics/2022/04/california-abortion-rights/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CalMatters}}}\uc2  that her organization has been preparing for this moment by expanding and moving facilities near airports and other transit centers and supportive medical providers.\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic states had already taken steps to affirm reproductive rights in anticipation of the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision. Earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newjerseymonitor.com/2022/01/13/murphy-signs-law-solidifying-abortion-rights-in-new-jersey/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Jersey}}}\uc2  passed a law enshrining the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into state law. In Vermont, voters are expected to approve a constitutional amendment guaranteeing the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception later this year.\par \par \uc2 After news of the decision, governors across the US said their states would continue to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is safe and legal. \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2 , the governor of Oregon, said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OregonGovBrown/status/1521320598441406466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monday}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected by state law in Oregon. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fight to keep it that way, no matter what this supreme court decides,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. JB Pritzker, the Illinois governor, said the state would remain a haven for people seeking reproductive care. The Vermont governor, Republican \uc2 Phil Scott\uc2 , said the \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental rights and liberties of all women will be defended, protected and preserved in Vermont\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220504ei54000mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
