\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US shaken to its core by supreme court draft that would overturn Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith, Lauren Gambino and Lauren Burke in Washington, Martin Pengelly and Oliver Milman in New York \par \uc2 1,470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 01:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden condemns \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opinion that, if handed down, would mean \u8216\'20\'18fundamental shift\u8217\'20\'19 in law and imperil many other rightsUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live coverage\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has warned that a leaked draft supreme court ruling overturning Roe v Wade, the 1973 case which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would represent a huge change in America law and could imperil a wide range of other civil rights.\par \par \uc2 In a historic moment that shook the US to the core and highlighted jagged social and political divisions, the court confirmed the draft was authentic but said it did not \u8220\'20\'1Crepresent a decision by the court or the final position of any member on the issues in the case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US president called the provisional court opinion \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D and said the ruling, if handed down, would represent a \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental shift in American jurisprudence\u8221\'20\'1D and could imperil rights including same-sex marriage and access to contraception.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  the draft by justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  on Monday night. The website said the draft was supported by four other right-wingers on a panel conservatives control 6-3.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the chief justice, \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , called its leak a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetrayal of the confidences of the court\u8221\'20\'1D which could \u8220\'20\'1Cundermine the integrity of our operations\u8221\'20\'1D, and promised an investigation.\par \par \uc2 The final ruling of the court will not be made until June.\par \par \uc2 The New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , warned that the court \u8220\'20\'1Cisn\u8217\'20\'19t just coming for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re coming for the right to privacy Roe rests on, which includes gay marriage and civil rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, speaking to reporters on Tuesday morning, said the draft ruling had ramifications for \u8220\'20\'1Call the decisions you make in your private life, who you marry, whether or not you decide to conceive a child, whether or not you can have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a range of other decisions [including] how you raise your child\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The draft ruling would allow states to declare \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal.\par \par \uc2 Protesters gathered outside the court on Tuesday, while demonstrations swelled throughout around the country \u8211\'20\'13 both in support of and against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Thousands have joined rallies in New York, Boston, Nashville, Dallas, New Orleans and more. In San Francisco, a man was arrested after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/san-francisco-salesforce-tower-free-climb-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scaling the 60-floor Salesforce tower}}}\uc2 , in an apparent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protest.\par \par \uc2 Outside the supreme court, some chanted \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D and carried signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CJustices get out of my vagina\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CLegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once and for all\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t go back\u8221\'20\'1D. A smaller group chanted \u8220\'20\'1CHey, hey, ho, ho, Roe v Wade has got to go\u8221\'20\'1D. Amid tense exchanges, barriers were erected.\par \par \uc2 Under cloudy skies at the bottom of the steps leading up to the majestic marble columns of the supreme court building near the US Capitol, Haley Lund, from Woodbridge, Virginia, told the Guardian: \u8220\'20\'1CThis terrifies me. I could not sleep, so I figured I should be here.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis opens a floodgate for everyone \u8230\'20\'26 like the right to privacy, to due process, the right that we\u8217\'20\'19re innocent until proven guilty. All of that can go away if this goes away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/05/03/statement-by-president-joe-biden-4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Biden outlined how Democrats might fight back.\par \par \uc2 First, the president said, his administration would argue Roe was based on precedent and \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18the 14th amendment\u8217\'20\'19s concept of personal liberty\u8217\'20\'19\u8230\'20\'26 against government interference with intensely personal decisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose is fundamental,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CRoe has been the law of the land for almost 50 years, and basic fairness and the stability of our law demand that it not be overturned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said he had directed advisers to prepare responses \u8220\'20\'1Cto the continued attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive rights, under a variety of possible outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will be ready when any ruling is issued,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Politico said it received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a copy of the draft}}}\uc2 , which also dealt with Planned Parenthood v Casey, a 1992 case, from a person familiar with proceedings in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, a Mississippi case due to be decided this summer.\par \par \uc2 The draft ran to 98 pages including a 31-page appendix of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws and included 118 footnotes.\par \par \uc2 Alito wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start. Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences. And far from bringing about a national settlement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, Roe and Casey have enflamed debate and deepened division.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that Roe and Casey must be overruled. It is time to heed the constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As many as 26 states are expected to enact partial or total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans if Roe falls. Some Republican-run states are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-abortions-travel-wave-of-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to attempt}}}\uc2  to make traveling for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal. Democratic-run states have indicated moves to protect and help women who seek an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe rights of all Americans are at risk. If the right to privacy is weakened, every person could face a future in which the government can potentially interfere in the personal decisions you make about your life. This is the time to fight for women and for our country with everything we have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and former first lady Michelle Obama issued a joint statement that read: \u8220\'20\'1CThe consequences of this decision would be a blow not just to women, but to all of us who believe that in a free society, there are limits to how much the government can encroach on our personal lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling shows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/05/06/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clear majority support}}}\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Christian and conservative groups campaign to end it regardless.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am angry, upset and determined,\u8221\'20\'1D said Democratic senator and 2020 presidential hopeful Elizabeth Warren, as she rallied outside the court.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 United States Congress\uc2  can keep Roe vs Wade the law of the land \u8211\'20\'13 they just need to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She was referring to the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell down}}}\uc2  in the Senate in March, opposed by all Republicans and Democratic senator Joe Manchin of West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Warren added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republicans have been working towards this day for decades \u8230\'20\'26 plotting, carefully cultivating these supreme court justices so that they could have a majority on the bench who would accomplish something that a majority of Americans do not want.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If the court overturns Roe, Biden said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit will fall on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s elected officials at all levels of government to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. And it will fall on voters to elect pro-choice officials this November.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But legislative success would require reform to the filibuster, a Senate rule which requires 60 votes for most legislation. Moderate Democrats have blocked such moves on issues including voting rights. Biden himself has expressed opposition.\par \par \uc2 This might not be the final ruling on Roe, the court continues to discuss provisional opinions until it issues its final decisions on the biggest cases before it at the end of the annual term, in June.\par \par \uc2 But reproductive rights advocates are alarmed, also about wider implications, such as the right to same-sex marriage, determined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/jun/02/obama-doma-gay-rights-america-supreme-court-edith-windsor-obergefell-same-sex-marriage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Obergefell v Hodges in 2015}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Laurence Tribe, a Harvard law professor, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Alito opinion savaging Roe and Casey ends up being the opinion of the court,\u8221\'20\'1D Tribe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1521311115392737280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cit will unravel many basic rights beyond \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will go further than returning the issue to the states: it will enable a [Republican] Congress to enact a nationwide ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a sharply divided Washington, Republicans confirmed three right-leaning justices under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and, just weeks before the 2020 election, Amy Coney Barrett, a hardline Catholic conservative.\par \par \uc2 Biden has overseen {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/ketanj-brown-jackson-confirmation-vote-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the confirmation of Ketanji Brown Jackson}}}\uc2 , the first Black female justice, but she has not yet replaced the retiring \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 , another liberal, and her arrival will not change the ideological imbalance.\par \par \uc2 Republicans welcomed the draft ruling and condemned the leak.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , a hardline Missouri senator, called Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft \u8220\'20\'1Ctightly argued, and morally powerful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among Republican moderates, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine \u8211\'20\'13 who under Trump supported the appointments of \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  but voted against Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 pointed to a possible betrayal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf this leaked draft opinion is the final decision,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be completely inconsistent with what Justice Gorsuch and Justice Kavanaugh said in their hearings and in our meetings in my office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among women\u8217\'20\'19s rights campaigners, condemnation of the Alito draft was strong.\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler, president of the advocacy group Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaphonzaB/status/1521332320191619072"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s past time to vote out every official who stands against the pro-choice majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53002e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
