\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 As the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  moves to end  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 , is America still a free country?\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,264 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par 00:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 There is no condition more essential to democratic citizenship than a person\u8217\'20\'19s control over her own body. We can\u8217\'20\'19t call ourselves a free country without it\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the worst possible outcome: according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000180-874f-dd36-a38c-c74f98520000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a draft majority opinion}}}\uc2  published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by Politico}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has voted to overturn Roe v Wade, along with its sister decision Planned Parenthood v Casey. This momentous ruling will result in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becoming immediately illegal in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/abortion-rights-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an estimated 26 states}}}\uc2  when it is officially issued, probably sometime next month.\par \par \uc2 The draft opinion, authored by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the most rabidly hateful member of the court\u8217\'20\'19s arch-conservative wing, will upend 50 years of precedent and undo a landmark ruling that has profoundly shaped legal doctrine, popular conceptions of the law, and millions of American lives. It will make women prisoners to their own bodies, and to men\u8217\'20\'19s ideas of what those bodies must mean. It will make our country weaker, crueler, stupider and less vibrant.\par \par \uc2 Before the court heard oral arguments in the case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/search.aspx?filename=/docket/docketfiles/html/public/19-1392.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson}}}\uc2 , a challenge to a Mississippi law that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestational age, some court watchers \u8211\'20\'13 mostly male \u8211\'20\'13 predicted that this outcome was unlikely. They chin-strokingly declared that judicial nominees like Amy Coney Barrett or \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  were really moderates (both have signed on to the draft opinion) or that chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 incrementalist impulses would temper the passions of his more misogynist colleagues.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/04/america-abortion-crisis-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Feminists, meanwhile, were more consistent}}}\uc2  in measuring the depth of the right\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to sexism and more perceptive in understanding the implications for other areas of the law in a world without Roe.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/02/supreme-court-signalling-end-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after oral arguments on 1 December}}}\uc2 , even those pundits who were most committed to their performance of sophisticated calm had to admit that there was little doubt that this would be the outcome. The hearing, whose audio was live-streamed to the public, turned into a carnival of delusional hypotheticals and nodding insistence on the triviality of precedent.\par \par \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett asked why women needed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now that \u8220\'20\'1Csafe haven\u8221\'20\'1D laws allowed for new mothers to surrender newborns without being arrested. Kavanaugh rattled off long lists all the decisions that the court had overturned in the past. It was a joke, a festival of misogyny, an unserious legal formality providing a gossamer of legitimacy for a preordained outcome. Roe would be overturned.\par \par \uc2 In a way, the leaked opinion didn\u8217\'20\'19t tell us anything we did not already know: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/08/oklahomas-move-to-ban-abortions-is-a-prelude-of-america-without-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 these are the last days of reproductive freedom in America}}}\uc2 , and most states will soon ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright, or restrict it so onerously that it is inaccessible within their borders. But Alito\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion nevertheless represents about as odiously maximalist an approach as the court could have taken.\par \par \uc2 The opinion does not just overturn Roe and Casey; it expresses outright contempt for the notion that the constitution protects bodily autonomy for women. It articulates a rigid and unchanging vision of individual rights, one in which only those freedoms with robust historical precedent and explicit enumeration in the text of the constitution will be recognized by the court.\par \par \uc2 This an interpretation that, if carried to its logical conclusion, would eradicate many of Americans\u8217\'20\'19 other rights that the court has recognized based on so-called substantive due process concerns, among them the right to contraception, the right to gay marriage, and the decriminalization of gay sex. The end of legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not be where the court\u8217\'20\'19s reactionaries stop. They aim to hurt, punish and narrow the lives of Americans in many more cruel and inventive ways.\par \par \uc2 The sudden illegality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most states come June will also create new legal landmines that will rapidly erode other individual rights. As women cross state borders for care, red states will try to limit interstate travel. As activists send \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills through the mail, aggressive searches and seizures of packages and personal belongings will become more frequent.\par \par \uc2 As women find ways to end their pregnancies, many of them will be arrested on criminal charges and some of them will be convicted. As doctors face patients with life-threatening pregnancy complications, many of them will not know what they are legally permitted to do, and in fear, they will let their patients die. Some of those who make the other choice, and help their patients live, will be arrested.\par \par \uc2 All of this will create legal precedents that erode American freedom, making life more burdensome, more brutish and less safe.\par \par \uc2 There are ways to fight. Of course, legal rulings aside, American women do not derive their moral right to control their own bodies from the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 ; they derive it from their human dignity. And many of them will seek and provide abortions, whether the court likes it or not, in accordance with this higher, more noble law. Others will donate to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://abortionfunds.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  funds}}}\uc2  that will be in dire need of support as costs and demand soar. Still others will spread the word about organizations like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aid Access}}}\uc2 , which mails \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to women in the US from abroad.\par \par \uc2 Some will call their senators, and demand that the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seize upon this moment of popular outrage to abolish the filibuster and pass the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/3755/text"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act}}}\uc2  before the moment fades and it\u8217\'20\'19s too late. And some will call their state representatives and urge them to adopt the most aggressive pro-choice laws possible, in advance of what is coming.\par \par \uc2 But none of this changes the fact that the reversal of Roe will come at an intolerable human cost. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so frequently been spoken of as a \u8220\'20\'1Chigh stakes\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Chot button\u8221\'20\'1D political issue that it is easy to lose sight of the foundational dignity that the right provides to women and others. The state compelling a person to be pregnant is not like compelling her to pay taxes. The event doesn\u8217\'20\'19t occur in a courtroom or on a balance sheet; it occurs inside her body.\par \par \uc2 The question at hand is whether half of the country will have control over their own insides, or whether the government can be so intimately evil that it can enforce its vision of gender conformity even within its citizens\u8217\'20\'19 own organs. It is a question of whether an individual American can have the dignity and the freedom to choose her own family, to maintain her own health, and to shape the course of her own life \u8211\'20\'13 or whether that freedom is withheld based on her sex.\par \par \uc2 Some have raised doubts about whether America can call itself a democracy, now that policymaking power has been largely taken over by the unelected courts \u8211\'20\'13 whose decisions, like this one, are so radically out of step with, and indifferent to, public opinion. But it is also worth wondering whether any country can call itself a democracy that does not protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal, the court is imposing a legal status that is so cruel, so personal and so life-altering on half its population, that those subject to this imposition cannot be called free. Is there any condition more essential to democratic citizenship than a person\u8217\'20\'19s control over her own body? Can we call ourselves a free country without it?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 3 May 2022 to clarify that Aid Access, not Plan C, mails \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Plan C is an informational resource only\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53000ma\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
