\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Protesters rush to supreme court to decry draft  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling \u8216\'20\'18disgrace\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Burke in Washington and Oliver Milman and Gloria Oladipo in New York \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 20:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pro-choice campaigners light candles and vent fury at Justice Alito, author of leaked opinion, as anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists celebrateUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live coverage\par \par \uc2 Furious women surged to the steps of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to decry news in a leaked document indicating that the conservative-controlled court intends to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  provided nationally under the 1973 Roe vs Wade ruling.\par \par \uc2 Protesters rushed to demonstrate outside the building\u8217\'20\'19s majestic marble columns in Washington just minutes after the news broke late on Monday night, and more were there on Tuesday, with larger protests planned.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  demonstrators prayed and celebrated but pro-choice protesters lit candles, chanted in support of reproductive rights and shouted expletives about \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , the rightwing justice on the court who wrote the opinion that was leaked to Politico.\par \par \uc2 Under cloudy skies that threatened rain on Tuesday, Haley Lund, from Woodbridge, Virginia, held a sign, standing in front of a metal gate guarding the last step in front of the court, which said: \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis terrifies me. I could not sleep, so I figured I should be here, where it could possibly make a difference or at least make someone aware,\u8221\'20\'1D she told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an important issue for me because of women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive rights, but this opens a floodgate for everyone \u8230\'20\'26 like the right to privacy, to due process, the right that we\u8217\'20\'19re innocent until proven guilty. All of that can go away if this goes away,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 In the draft opinion document {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leaked to the media}}}\uc2 , Alito wrote that Roe was \u8220\'20\'1Cegregiously wrong from the start\u8221\'20\'1D and that the US constitution \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not prohibit the citizens of each state from regulating or prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the darkness of Monday night, pierced by the softly illuminated court building, about 200 people had quickly gathered, carrying signs reading \u8220\'20\'1CJustices get out of my vagina\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1CLegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once and for all\u8221\'20\'1D, and \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t go back\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Monday and Tuesday a slightly smaller group of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CHey, hey, ho, ho, Roe v Wade has got to go\u8221\'20\'1D, leading to tense exchanges between the two groups.\par \par \uc2 Barriers were erected in front of the court shortly after the leaked report was made public.\par \par \uc2 Robin Galbraith, of Maryland, told the Guardian on Tuesday: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the mother of two twentysomething children, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been fighting for healthcare rights, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, since I was 20 and I did not bring my children into this world to have their rights taken away.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added that she was retired and could normally sleep in but on Tuesday launched herself out of bed at 5am to get to the court to protest, she was so motivated, and if the final decision \u8211\'20\'13 expected from the court in June when they announce the main decisions from their previous term \u8211\'20\'13 overturns Roe that she would be out campaigning to help the Democrats keep and increase their hold of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The size and vociferousness of the crowds are more usual just before or just after a major supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 But Hannah Wolfe of Alexandria, Virginia, an area coordinator with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Students for Life of America said that an unplanned pregnancy when she was 18 was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most terrifying situation I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been in in my life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She said that while her pregnancy then ended with a natural miscarriage, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe trauma that I experienced in losing my child is very similar to what a lot of women experience \u8230\'20\'26 I want to show people that there are supportive resources that are non-violent and will help women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pro-choice group Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, which formed to organize the record protests that took place in Washington and elsewhere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jan/21/women-march-washington-protest-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the day after Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential inauguration in 2017}}}\uc2 , is urging supporters to hold rallies all across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, women in this country have been warning about the end of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That day has arrived \u8230\'20\'26 this is a worst-case-scenario come to life. If and when this decision takes effect, the consequences will be unbearable \u8211\'20\'13 and, for many women, lethal. That is no exaggeration,\u8221\'20\'1D read a statement from Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CBut it\u8217\'20\'19s also no exaggeration to say that women will fight back like we always have. We won\u8217\'20\'19t take this lying down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The group is encouraging protests outside the supreme court, which sits near the US Capitol, on Tuesday during the day and more demonstrations outside \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal courthouses, federal buildings, town halls and town squares across the country\u8221\'20\'1D in the evening.\par \par \uc2 In New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/nyc-protests-planned-in-wake-of-bombshell-roe-v-wade-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-choice groups have planned several protests}}}\uc2  in response to the leaked draft. The coalition group NYC for \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights advertised a rally that will be held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CdGUSE1O6VN/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near city hall in Foley Square.}}}\uc2  An additional rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EqualFlatbush/status/1521362420370919424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will take place at Brooklyn\u8217\'20\'19s Barclays Center}}}\uc2 , one of the city\u8217\'20\'19s major sports and entertainment arenas.\par \par \uc2 Activists have also planned counter-protests in Chicago. Following the draft leak, protesters from a number of groups will gather {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RefuseFascismCH/status/1521500007467204612"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on 3 May in the city\u8217\'20\'19s downtown business area}}}\uc2 . Additional rallies have been planned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/events/s/emergency-rally-defend-roe-fig/3197949180451112/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for this weekend on 7 May at Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s federal plaza}}}\uc2 , which hosts a number of federal buildings.\par \par \uc2 In Los Angeles, an emergency rally is being held in front of the city\u8217\'20\'19s courthouse.\par \par \uc2 In addition to protests happening in Minneapolis at the city\u8217\'20\'19s main courthouse, Minnesota pro-choice activists, in partnership with groups in North Dakota and South Dakota, will be holding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UnRestrictMN/status/1521213693165555712?s=20&t=472denX5BCGGaQ_It4JHYA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 teaching sessions on how people can fight for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 New York City organizers will also be holding an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  story share out across this weekend and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/CdCNijyOpX2/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 host a public viewing of art pieces}}}\uc2  associated with people\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  expeirences.\par \par \uc2 Norma Gallegos, an organizer of a planned San Francisco protest, said the court\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating attack on legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a call to hit the streets throughout the land\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Overturning the landmark ruling would allow states that have attempted to severely restrict women\u8217\'20\'19s access to reproductive healthcare to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The case before the court, brought by Mississippi, is expected to be officially decided in the summer.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long been a contentious issue in the US, even though polling finds that a clear majority of the public believes it should be legal.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court, however, has a 6-3 majority of deeply conservative justices.\par \par \uc2 Three of those justices were nominated by Trump. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , whose defeat by Trump in the 2016 election paved the way for the rightwing tilt of the court, said the apparent decision was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdirect assault\u8221\'20\'1D on the rights and lives of women, as well as settled law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt will kill and subjugate women even as a vast majority of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat an utter disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several leading progressives, including Senator Bernie Sanders, have called for a vote in Congress to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in law. Such a vote would have to navigate an evenly split Senate.\par \par \uc2 Protests to defend the rights granted by Roe were being hastily organized to take place this week and into the weekend also in Chicago, Atlanta, Los Angeles, Philadelphia, Dayton, Houston, Minneapolis and other cities across the US.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53001ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
