\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  to become key fight in US midterms after stunning court leak\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,073 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 19:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats condemn supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s draft opinion and urge voters to support them in November to protect reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stunning revelation}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has privately voted to overturn Roe v Wade immediately thrust one of the most polarizing issues in American life to the forefront of the national political debate, and now \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights promises to reshape the dynamics of the coming midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 The draft opinion, written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and obtained by Politico in a highly unusual and possibly unprecedented leak from the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, would strike down Roe, the landmark supreme court decision that has guaranteed access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly half a century, and a subsequent 1992 decision \u8211\'20\'13 Planned Parenthood v Casey \u8211\'20\'13 that largely upheld that right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito wrote in the draft opinion labeled \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst draft\u8221\'20\'1D, which was not expected to be finalized for at least several more weeks and could change in its final form. The question of whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, Alito argues, is best answered by individual states.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Tuesday, the supreme court confirmed the authenticity of the draft report but cautioned that it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not represent a decision by the court or the final position of any member on the issues in the case\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, as the revelation reverberated across Washington, protesters gathered in front of the supreme court on Tuesday morning, shouting loudly enough to be heard by the members of Congress arriving for work at the Capitol. From the White House, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  urged voters to elect political leaders who would act to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and reproductive rights, irrespective of the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s final decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the court does overturn Roe, it will fall on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s elected officials at all levels of government to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it will fall on voters to elect pro-choice officials this November. At the federal level, we will need more pro-choice senators and a pro-choice majority in the House to adopt legislation that codifies Roe, which I will work to pass and sign into law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Strategists were preparing for a decision that either weakened or reversed Roe, but the leak upended the expected timetable and, potentially, the legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , said he would bring legislation to the floor that would codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in federal law. But the measure is unlikely to garner the 60 votes needed to pass the Senate. A similar measure passed by the Democratic-controlled House last year does not even have the support of all 50 Democratic senators.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA vote on this legislation is not an abstract exercise. This is as urgent and real as it gets,\u8221\'20\'1D Schumer said on the Senate floor on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will vote to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose and every American is going to see which side every senator stands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of such a ruling by the supreme court, Republican-led states have proposed, and in many cases already passed, a cascade of restrictive anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. Conservative activists are pushing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/05/02/abortion-ban-roe-supreme-court-mississippi/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nationwide ban }}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Republicans recapture control of Congress in November, as they are favored to do.\par \par \uc2 In a flurry of statements and fundraising emails, Democrats argued that the erosion of reproductive rights was a reason to support them in the November midterms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans just gutted Roe v Wade, the Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s guarantee of reproductive freedom, and will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all 50 states, if they take over Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D the New York congressman \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , the chairman of the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee, wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1COnly Democrats will protect our freedoms. That is now the central choice in the 2022 election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic lawmakers and candidates condemned the expected decision, and vowed to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a pro-choice pastor, I\u8217\'20\'19ve always believed that a patient\u8217\'20\'19s room is way too small for a woman, her doctor, and the \uc2 United States government\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote the Georgia senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , one of the most vulnerable Democrats up for re-election this cycle. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll always fight to protect a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. And that will never change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota senator Tina Smith put it more bluntly: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is bullshit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polls have consistently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/350804/americans-opposed-overturning-roe-wade.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that most Americans want Roe to remain the law of the land, and the vast majority want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain legal in at least some cases.\par \par \uc2 A decision overturning Roe would be the culmination of a 50-year project by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists to remake the federal courts by using their political clout to pressure Republicans to appoint and confirm reliably conservative majorities.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sealed his support among conservative voters by vowing to nominate supreme court justices who opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . His presidency yielded three conservative justices, all of whom are reportedly in the majority voting to strike down Roe. They also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/us-supreme-court-texas-56fe96917e21b53b581005cb30db66e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to block}}}\uc2  a novel Texas law that has effectively outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest state.\par \par \uc2 But instead of celebrating the draft ruling, Republican lawmakers on Tuesday were almost singularly focused on the leak, expressing outrage over the disclosure that was likely to further undermine faith in the judiciary as an independent branch of government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night\u8217\'20\'19s stunning breach was an attack on the independence of the supreme court,\u8221\'20\'1D the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , wrote in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CBy every indication, this was yet another escalation in the radical left\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing campaign to bully and intimidate federal judges and substitute mob rule for the rule of law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  said in a statement that he had ordered the marshal of the court to open an investigation into the source of the leak. \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a singular and egregious breach of that trust that is an affront to the court and the community of public servants who work here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While the nation awaits a final opinion, pro-choice activists are urging supporters to keep making their voices heard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: this is a draft opinion. It\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous, it\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented, but it is not final,\u8221\'20\'1D Planned Parenthood wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is your right \u8211\'20\'13 and it is STILL LEGAL.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei530025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
