\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court voted to overturn Roe v Wade  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law, leaked draft opinion reportedly shows\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,261 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 14:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In an unprecedented revelation, a document written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18Roe was egregiously wrong from the start\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has provisionally voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark ruling that legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in America, according to a draft opinion reported on by Politico.\par \par \uc2 In what appeared to be a stunning and unprecedented leak, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico said}}}\uc2  on Monday evening it had obtained an initial majority opinion written by Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and circulated in the court on 10 February.\par \par \uc2 The opinion strikes down Roe v Wade, the court\u8217\'20\'19s 1973 ruling that enshrined the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a subsequent 1992 decision \u8211\'20\'13 Planned Parenthood v Casey \u8211\'20\'13 that largely upheld that right.\par \par \uc2 Politico quoted Alito as saying: \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start. Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences. And far from bringing about a national settlement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, Roe and Casey have enflamed debate and deepened division.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The justice adds: \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that Roe and Casey must be overruled. It is time to heed the constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Four of the other Republican-appointed justices \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 voted with Alito in the conference held among the justices, the article added.\par \par \uc2 After an initial vote among the justices following the oral argument, one is assigned the majority opinion and writes a draft. It is then circulated among the justices. At times, in between the initial vote and the ruling being released, the vote alignment can change. A ruling is only final when it is published by the court.\par \par \uc2 But if, as expected, it is adopted, the decision would rule in favour of Mississippi in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a highly consequential case}}}\uc2  about that state\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to ban most abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy. That would sound the death knell for the half-century guarantee of nationwide protection of reproductive rights and allow each state to decide whether to restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Several Republican-led states have already passed highly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in anticipation of such a ruling by the supreme court which, thanks to three appointments by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , now has a 6-3 conservative majority.\par \par \uc2 Politico said it received a copy of the draft opinion from a person familiar with the court\u8217\'20\'19s proceedings in the Mississippi case. The draft opinion runs to 98 pages, including a 31-page appendix of historical state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, and includes 118 footnotes.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court declined to confirm what would be the worst security breach in its history \u8211\'20\'13 regarding one of its most consequential rulings in decades that is sure to enflame America\u8217\'20\'19s deep political divisions. After the Politico story broke, footage posted to social media showed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidClosson/status/1521321880631889920"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a crowd of protesters gathering}}}\uc2  outside the supreme court late on Monday night, waving signs and chanting \u8220\'20\'1Cmy body, my choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A massive protest is forming in front of the Supreme Court in support of protecting women\u8217\'20\'19s bodily autonomy. I\u8217\'20\'19m proud our staff members are part. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/I6MyzhoYex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/I6MyzhoYex}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Bill Pascrell, Jr. ???????? (@BillPascrell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BillPascrell/status/1521322449756958720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May 3, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2 , a former US acting solicitor general who has argued many cases before the supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1521292108975513601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve quickly scanned the draft opinion and it appears legitimate. This means there was a preliminary vote to fully overrule Roe v Wade and that a majority of the court agreed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are lots of signals the opinion is legit. The length and depth of analysis, would be very hard to fake. It says it is written by Alito and definitely sounds like him. It\u8217\'20\'19s 60+ pages long. If this is a deep fake, it would require a state actor or someone like that. I can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s possible the Court could pull back from this position, but this looks like they voted that way after the oral argument.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democrats condemned the leaked ruling. The House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , and Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , issued a statement saying overturning Roe v Wade would be \u8220\'20\'1Can abomination , one of the worst and most damaging decisions in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the report is accurate, the Supreme Court is poised to inflict the greatest restriction of rights in the past 50 years \u8211\'20\'13 not just on women but on all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery Republican senator who supported Senator McConnell and voted for Trump justices pretending that this day would never come will now have to explain themselves to the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Christie Roberts, Democratic senatorial campaign executive director, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf this report is true, this Republican attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, birth control and women\u8217\'20\'19s health care has dramatically escalated the stakes of the 2022 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt this critical moment, we must protect and expand Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Senate majority with the power to confirm or reject supreme court justices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am horrified by the apparent draft supreme court opinion leaked this evening \u8230\'20\'26 this should not be the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s final opinion when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said New York\u8217\'20\'19s Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katieglueck/status/1521308590509891587/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 . The governor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovKathyHochul/status/1521308325794697222"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later added}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI refuse to let my new granddaughter have to fight for the rights that generations have fought for & won, rights that she should be guaranteed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is a direct assault on the dignity, rights, & lives of women, not to mention decades of settled law,\u8221\'20\'1D said the former secretary of state \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt will kill and subjugate women even as a vast majority of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal. What an utter disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders tweeted the the news showed \u8220\'20\'1CCongress must pass legislation that codifies Roe v Wade as the law of the land in this country NOW\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights and civil rights advocates also weighed in. Naral Pro-Choice America\u8217\'20\'19s president, Mini Timmaraju, called it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most ominous and alarming sign yet that our nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court is poised to overturn Roe v Wade\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the supreme court does indeed issue a majority opinion along the lines of the leaked draft authored by Justice Alito, the shift in the tectonic plates of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will be as significant as any opinion the court has ever issued,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, however, were exultant. Madison Cawthorn, a congressman from North Carolina, wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of Donald J Trump, Roe v Wade will be overturned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator Tom Cotton condemned the apparent leak but applauded the vote, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Supreme Court & the DOJ must get to the bottom of this leak immediately using every investigative tool necessary. In the meantime, Roe was egregiously wrong from the beginning & I pray the Court follows the Constitution & allows the states to once again protect unborn life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polling has shown that relatively few Americans want to see Roe overturned. In 2020, AP VoteCast found that 69% of voters in the presidential election said the supreme court should leave the Roe v Wade decision as is; just 29% said the court should overturn the decision.\par \par \uc2 Alito said the court can\u8217\'20\'19t predict how the public might react and shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t try. \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow our decisions to be affected by any extraneous influences such as concern about the public\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to our work,\u8221\'20\'1D Alito wrote in the draft opinion, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Gambino and agencies contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei530002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
