\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Through the Trumpian looking glass, forcing women to die from illegal abortions is \u8216\'20\'18pro-life\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Marina Hyde \par \uc2 1,258 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 13:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  leak shows that the levers of power are pulled by those with no skin in the game, at the expense of those with an entire uterus in it\par \par \uc2 An American girl born this week will have fewer rights than an American girl born in 1973. This is the likely import of the leaked US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court draft opinion}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 and cause for a huge thank-you-very-much to all those guys who suggested that women marching on Washington in January 2017 were \u8220\'20\'1Coverreacting\u8221\'20\'1D to the election of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Please make sure to tell women again when they are being overemotional \u8211\'20\'13 even as they sit and watch one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justice picks scream and sob his way through his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/sep/28/brett-kavanaugh-testimony-nominee-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmation hearings}}}\uc2 . In the meantime, resign yourself to yet another \u8220\'20\'1Cquirk\u8221\'20\'1D of the looking-glass world Trump has created. Of course \u8211\'20\'13 OF COURSE \u8211\'20\'13 women\u8217\'20\'19s access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would end up being restricted or removed by the deliberate decisions of a man widely imagined to have personally helped to keep the Manhattan \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sector afloat for decades.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m kidding, of course! We have absolutely no idea whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services have or haven\u8217\'20\'19t ever been accessed by anyone connected with a draft-avoider who described avoiding STDs in the 80s as \u8220\'20\'1Cmy personal Vietnam\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s an interesting question,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/apr/02/donald-trump-marueen-dowd-interview-abortion-past-partners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replied}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  when asked, during the 2016 campaign, if he\u8217\'20\'19d ever been involved with a woman who had undergone a termination during their relationship. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s your next question?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It must be nice for reproductive rights to be an \u8220\'20\'1Cinteresting question\u8221\'20\'1D you have absolutely no interest in answering. As ever, it feels as the levers of power are pulled by those with no skin in the game at the expense of those with an entire uterus in it. Once again, then, a huge bravo to all the extremely rational guys whose \u8220\'20\'1Cconscience\u8221\'20\'1D simply declined to permit them to vote for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , on the basis that she and Trump were basically \u8220\'20\'1Cthe same\u8221\'20\'1D. Women now facing same-old same-old prospects like forced birth and wildly increased medical risks can only thank you and your consciences for doing the hard intellectual yards so they don\u8217\'20\'19t have to.\par \par \uc2 When news of the supreme court draft opinion broke last night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HillaryClinton/status/1521313156685090817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clinton stated}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis decision is a direct assault on the dignity, rights, & lives of women, not to mention decades of settled law. It will kill and subjugate women even as a vast majority of Americans think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal. What an utter disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D We\u8217\'20\'19ve yet to hear Trump\u8217\'20\'19s response \u8211\'20\'13 very, very samey, I imagine \u8211\'20\'13 so let\u8217\'20\'19s use as placeholder his 2011 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qz.com/1623437/trump-shifted-from-pro-choice-to-pro-life-as-he-planned-a-presidential-run/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on the subject: \u8220\'20\'1CI am pro-life, and pro-life people will find out that I will be very loyal to them, just as I am loyal to other people. I would be appointing judges that feel the way I feel.\u8221\'20\'1D Can\u8217\'20\'19t believe he ended up appointing pro-life judges. If only there\u8217\'20\'19d been some clue his daffy media cheerleaders could have latched on to.\par \par \uc2 For those whose interest in reproductive rights is not cerebral but personal and physical \u8211\'20\'13 that is, women \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s a mirthless laugh to be had at some of the reaction to the leak. A lot of people are infinitely more horrified by the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s information security lapse than they are by the information itself. Please take time to appreciate the angry ranting of rightwing pundits who cannot believe the justices\u8217\'20\'19 right to make private decisions has been appallingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1521298708180226062"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violated}}}\uc2 , and that the fricking LEAK is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe gravest, most unforgivable sin\u8221\'20\'1D. Their court, their choice, OK?\par \par \uc2 Out there in the real world beyond, we know from experience abortions will still happen, whether they are outlawed or not \u8211\'20\'13 by some accounts, pretty much the same number of abortions. But illegal abortions will mean that many more women will die from the procedure, which is a funny way of being \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D. But there we are. And of course, should this seismic ruling come to pass, it will only be the start of it, with a number of other rights now under threat again. Marriage rights, contraception, racial freedom \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19d need to be a gullible fool or highly paid star news commentator to think assaults on these aren\u8217\'20\'19t all on the table again. During her confirmation hearings, Amy Coney Barrett wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t even say if she thought IVF treatment was constitutional, which gives you a sense of how deeply backward things could be starting to get.\par \par \uc2 Yet, in some ways, it\u8217\'20\'19s the things that actually were said during the confirmation hearings that illustrate the rot most clearly, with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new justices saying a lot of stuff that now turns out to have meant about as much as one of his promises. We\u8217\'20\'19re looking at a court where justices are no longer particularly different from politicians \u8211\'20\'13 both will say any old shit to get elected or confirmed. In the infrequently lucid moments that peppered his truly deranged performance during his confirmation hearings, \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  suggested Roe v Wade was settled law, that has been affirmed down the decades by \u8220\'20\'1Cprecedent on precedent\u8221\'20\'1D. And now look. I wonder what else in his confirmation hearings he might not have been being entirely candid about.\par \par \uc2 For her part, Coney Barrett assured senators her own personal beliefs were absolutely irrelevant, and in no way likely to lead to the undoing of laws, joking: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not the law of Amy. It\u8217\'20\'19s the law of the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D It\u8217\'20\'19s looking quite like the law of Amy today, all things considered. As the highly predictable majority opinion on Roe v Wade makes landfall, then, spare a thought for supposedly pro-choice Republican senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , who held the deciding vote on Kavanaugh, and who was apparently absolutely satisfied after two long private meetings with him back in 2018 that Roe was safe in his hands. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not naive,\u8221\'20\'1D she explained. Susan: it seems like you\u8217\'20\'19re sensationally, historically, implausibly naive.\par \par \uc2 So here we are again. Today, there is a sense that even restating the arguments feels like something pro-choice women have been doing every day of every decade since they apparently won the argument. We can all understand the political imperative to talk of Roe v Wade as \u8220\'20\'1Csettled law\u8221\'20\'1D, but the honest assessment from most pro-choice American women you care to talk to is that it has never felt truly settled. Women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and autonomies should be their inheritance; instead, they\u8217\'20\'19re just another rented thing they could be evicted from or priced out of at any moment.\par \par \uc2 Far from being \u8220\'20\'1Cliberated\u8221\'20\'1D, American women are in an abusive relationship with partisan lawmakers in which no sense of security is even close to permanent, and nothing is given that cannot be taken away at any point. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have never been allowed to feel like a life goal achieved. Instead, defending them has remained a hugely consuming way of life for a huge number of women. What a vast, intensely limiting drain on their energy and human potential, which is presumably the attraction for those who seek to keep them down. You can be \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, or pro-living \u8211\'20\'13 but you can\u8217\'20\'19t be both.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Marina Hyde is a Guardian columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53001uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
