\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18An abomination\u8217\'20\'19: Pelosi leads outcry on supreme court draft  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in New York \par \uc2 831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 12:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Speaker warns scrapping Roe v Wade would be \u8216\'20\'18greatest restriction of rights in the past 50 years\u8217\'20\'19 as AOC calls for Senate reformUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live coverage\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights reacted with outrage to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the leak on Monday night}}}\uc2  of a supreme court decision overturning Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which has safeguarded the right till now.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to Politico}}}\uc2 , the draft {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/read-justice-alito-initial-abortion-opinion-overturn-roe-v-wade-pdf-00029504"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2 , written by \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , is supported by \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and the three conservative justices appointed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 It would also overturn Planned Parenthood v Casey, a 1992 decision which upheld Roe.\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the Democratic speaker of the House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1521331688944685056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf the report is accurate, the supreme court is poised to inflict the greatest restriction of rights in the past 50 years \u8211\'20\'13 not just on women but on all Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Republican-appointed justices\u8217\'20\'19 reported votes to overturn Roe v Wade would go down as an abomination, one of the worst and most damaging decisions in modern history,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSeveral of these conservative justices, who are in no way accountable to the American people, have lied to the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , ripped up the constitution and defiled both precedent and the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reputation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren, a Massachusetts senator and former candidate for the Democratic presidential nomination, said an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremist supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D was poised to \u8220\'20\'1Cimpose its far-right, unpopular views on the entire country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for the millions who support the constitution and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to stand up and make their voices heard,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back \u8211\'20\'13 not ever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If confirmed, the ruling would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a state matter. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/us-abortions-travel-wave-of-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As many as 26}}}\uc2  Republican-run states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are poised}}}\uc2  to end or restrict access.\par \par \uc2 Congress could codify Roe into law but it would require scrapping the filibuster, the Senate rule that requires a 60-vote majority for most legislation. That seems unlikely, given the 50-50 split in the chamber and opposition from moderate Democrats such as \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  of West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Republican senators including \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska, who have expressed concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, were slower to react to the Politico report than their Democratic counterparts. Their support would be needed for filibuster reform.\par \par \uc2 Among progressives, outrage was fierce.\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , the New York congresswoman, tied her outrage to calls for Senate reform and to impeach Thomas, the senior conservative on the court, over the political activities of his wife around the January 6 insurrection.\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez also warned of possible court moves on other hitherto protected rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[The court] isn\u8217\'20\'19t just coming for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re coming for the right to privacy Roe rests on, which includes gay marriage and civil rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CManchin is blocking Congress codifying Roe. House has seemingly forgotten about \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . These two points must change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ocasio-Cortez also took aim at \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , calling for the use of executive actions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople elected Democrats precisely so we could lead in perilous moments like these \u8211\'20\'13 to codify Roe, hold corruption accountable and have a president who uses his legal authority to break through congressional gridlock on items from student debt to climate. It\u8217\'20\'19s high time we do it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t, what message does that send? We can\u8217\'20\'19t sit around, finger-point and hand-wring as people\u8217\'20\'19s futures and equality are on the line. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to be decisive, lead with confidence, fight for a prosperous future for all and protect the vulnerable. Leave it all on the field.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Campaigners were equally vocal.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Women\u8217\'20\'19s Law Center\uc2  called the \u8220\'20\'1Clanguage in the draft opinion \u8230\'20\'26 outrageous, irresponsible and shocking\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president of the women\u8217\'20\'19s health provider \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , called the draft ruling \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying and unprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Laphonza Butler, president of the advocacy group Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaphonzaB/status/1521332320191619072"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed}}}\uc2  to the effect the draft ruling could have on Democratic campaigning and turnout in the November midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, anti-choice politicians have worked overtime to strip away our fundamental rights and give government control of critical healthcare decisions. They are working to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , full stop. This was the plan all along.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s past time to vote out every official who stands against the pro-choice majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fight harder than ever to make them pay, by electing more Democratic pro-choice women at all levels of government who will protect our rights and ensure that our \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights do not depend on our zip code or our financial situation. And we will work to vote every one of them out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cecile Richards, formerly president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , pointed to polling which shows clear support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not what the American people want,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is Republican politicians putting government in charge of your pregnancy. Full stop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
