\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Supreme court reportedly votes to overturn Roe v Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,341 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 10:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In an unprecedented revelation, a document written by conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18Roe was egregiously wrong from the start\u8217\'20\'19. Plus, politics front and centre at the Met Gala\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has provisionally voted to overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark ruling that legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide in America, according to a draft opinion reported on by Politico.\par \par \uc2 In what appeared to be a stunning and unprecedented leak, Politico said on Monday evening it had obtained an initial majority opinion written by justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and circulated in the court on 10 February.\par \par \uc2 The opinion strikes down Roe v Wade, the court\u8217\'20\'19s 1973 ruling that enshrined the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a subsequent 1992 decision \u8211\'20\'13 Planned Parenthood v Casey \u8211\'20\'13 that largely upheld that right.\par \par \uc2 Politico quoted Alito as saying: \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start. Its reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences. And far from bringing about a national settlement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, Roe and Casey have enflamed debate and deepened division.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The justice adds: \u8220\'20\'1CWe hold that Roe and Casey must be overruled. It is time to heed the constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How have campaigners reacted? The leaked opinion has been described as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-abortion-how-campaigners-reacted-to-report-on-us-supreme-court-draft-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Chorrifying and unprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Could dismantling Roe v Wade imperil other \u8216\'20\'18core, basic human rights\u8217\'20\'19? The decision could potentially affect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/11/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-gay-rights-contraceptives-fertility-treatments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gay rights, contraceptives and fertility treatments}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What will US\u8217\'20\'19s future look like if \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes a crime again? As Roe v Wade faces a direct challenge, criminal defense attorneys, prosecutors, local judges and police begin to lay out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what it would look like to criminalize \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 US says\par \par \uc2 Moscow plans to annex parts of east Ukraine as \uc2 EU\uc2  prepares new sanctions\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  was preparing sanctions on Russian oil sales over its invasion of Ukraine after a major shift by Germany, Russia\u8217\'20\'19s biggest energy customer, that could deprive Moscow of a large revenue stream within days.\par \par \uc2 Attempts to increase economic pressure on Russia come amid hopes of more evacuations from the besieged city of Mariupol, while the US said Moscow was preparing to formally annex the Donetsk and Luhansk regions in the country\u8217\'20\'19s east.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe reports state that Russia plans to engineer referenda upon joining sometime in mid-May,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Carpenter, the US ambassador to the \uc2 Organization for Security and Co-operation in Europe\uc2  on Monday. He said Russia was considering a similar plan in a third region, Kherson, where Moscow has recently solidified control and imposed use of its rouble currency.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Commission\uc2  is expected to propose a sixth package of EU sanctions this week against Russia, including a possible embargo on buying Russian oil.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? The director of the \uc2 United Nations World Food Programme\uc2  in Germany has warned that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/02/millions-tonnes-grain-stuck-ukraine-un-wfp-official-germany"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millions of tonnes of grain is stuck in Ukraine}}}\uc2  due to sea ports being blocked by Russian military action.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else do we know? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-69-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what we know on day 69}}}\uc2  of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 Met Gala 2022: Politics rises to the surface on fashion\u8217\'20\'19s biggest night\par \par \uc2 Politics \u8211\'20\'13 personal, contemporary and historic \u8211\'20\'13 were close to the surface on New York\u8217\'20\'19s Upper East Side on Monday night as 600 guests, invited to celebrate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2022/may/03/met-gala-2022-politics-rises-to-the-surface-in-fashions-biggest-night"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s Gilded Age at the Met Gala}}}\uc2 , offered their own interpretation of style and the multitude of meanings dress carries, then as now.\par \par \uc2 The singer Alicia Keys wore a cape celebrating New York union history. New York\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Eric Adams, who had said he\u8217\'20\'19d been \u8220\'20\'1Cdying to go\u8221\'20\'1D to the fundraiser \u8220\'20\'1Cfor years\u8221\'20\'1D, arrived on the red carpet wearing a jacket with decorative forearms and lapels that paid homage to the city\u8217\'20\'19s transit system. The back of his coat read \u8220\'20\'1CEnd Gun Violence\u8221\'20\'1D in red lettering.\par \par \uc2 The former secretary of state \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  came in a dress inspired by friendship quilts inscribed with the names, she explained, of \u8220\'20\'1Cgutsy women\u8221\'20\'1D of the 19th- and 20th-century liberation movements.\par \par \uc2 Politics at the event returned again when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2022/may/03/kim-kardashian-wears-marilyn-monroes-jfk-dress-as-met-gala-celebrates-gilded-age"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kim Kardashian appeared on the red carpet in the iconic dress Marilyn Monroe wore}}}\uc2  to coo Happy Birthday to President Kennedy in 1962.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What did people wear? Here\u8217\'20\'19s a gallery of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/gallery/2022/may/03/met-gala-2022-red-carpet-from-marilyn-monroes-gown-to-a-fake-moustache-in-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pictures from the red carpet}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A week after \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  finalized a $44bn deal to purchase \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , the billionaire is working to secure outside funding for the acquisition that would tie up less of his personal fortune. Musk is in talks with large investment firms and high net-worth individuals to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/may/02/elon-musk-twitter-personal-fortune"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take on more financing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A body inside a barrel was found over the weekend on\par \par \uc2 the newly exposed bottom of Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Lake Mead as drought depletes one of the largest US reservoirs \u8211\'20\'13 and officials predicted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/lake-mead-barrel-human-remains-nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discovery could be just the first of more grim finds}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Six people are under investigation in Shanghai after an elderly nursing home resident was mistakenly declared dead, put in a body bag and taken by coroners to a waiting van before mortuary workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/outcry-in-shanghai-as-person-declared-dead-and-put-in-body-bag-found-to-be-alive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noticed they were still alive}}}\uc2 . The incident was filmed by onlookers and footage quickly spread online.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The ousted Myanmar leader, \uc2 Aung San Suu Kyi\uc2 , has gone on trial in a new corruption case against her, alleging she took $550,000 in bribes from a construction magnate. She is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/03/aung-san-suu-kyi-on-trial-in-fresh-bribery-case-against-ousted-myanmar-leader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with two counts under the country\u8217\'20\'19s Anti-Corruption Act}}}\uc2 , with each count punishable by up to 15 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: The largest active wildfire in the US has consumed more than 121,000 acres\par \par \uc2 The largest active wildfire in the US has forced thousands from their homes in New Mexico, as unusually fast-spreading blazes dot the drought-stricken south-west. The blaze, dubbed the Calf Canyon fire, has consumed more than 121,000 acres (49,000 hectares), or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/new-mexico-wildfire-calf-canyon-thousands-flee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than half the area of New York City}}}\uc2 , tearing through centuries-old settlements and vacation homes in forested mountains 30 miles (48km) north-east of Santa Fe.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: Graham Nash on groupies, feuds, divorce and ego\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C I feel good,\u8221\'20\'1D a ludicrously youthful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/may/03/graham-nash-on-families-joni-mitchell-and-toxic-masculinity-if-you-could-kill-putin-would-you-i-would"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Graham Nash tells Simon Hattenstone}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CEighty years old and still rocking.\u8221\'20\'1D And some. Nash has rocked his way twice into the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame \u8211\'20\'13 as a member of the pop group the Hollies and as part of the groundbreaking folk-rock super-group Crosby, Stills and Nash. Here the singer talks about the wild early years, Joni Mitchell, his former bandmates and why his children no longer speak to him.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Pakistan and India suffer extreme spring heatwaves\par \par \uc2 As a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/may/02/pakistan-india-heatwaves-water-electricity-shortages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brutal heatwave has swept across India and Pakistan}}}\uc2 , Turbat, in Pakistan\u8217\'20\'19s Balochistan region, has been suffering through weeks of temperatures that have repeatedly hit almost 50C (122F), unprecedented for this time of year. Locals have been driven into their homes, unable to work except during the cooler night hours, and are facing critical shortages of water and power. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are living in hell,\u8221\'20\'1D Nazeer Ahmed told the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: WW2 veteran smashes centenarian 100m world record\par \par \uc2 Nearly a quarter of a century after breaking one sprinting world record aged 76-year-old, Lester Wright was back in form as he set the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/may/02/lester-wright-100m-world-record-100-year-old-age-group"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 official 100m world record for centenarians}}}\uc2 . Competing at the Penn Relays, America\u8217\'20\'19s oldest track and field meet, he surged over the line in a time of 26.34 seconds. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re going to go out to run a race, you should really run the race to try to win,\u8221\'20\'1D Wright, who turned 100 on Friday, said before the race. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know how you can run to be second or third.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei53001e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
