\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law leak: what happened and why does it matter?\b0\par\par\uc2 Archie Bland \par \uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2022\par 10:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leak appears to shows court ready to overturn Roe v Wade ruling that guarantees federal constitutional protections of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s happened?\par \par \uc2 A draft supreme court opinion, apparently by the conservative justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , was leaked to Politico for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/05/02/supreme-court-abortion-draft-opinion-00029473"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a story published late on Monday}}}\uc2 . It appears to show that the court is preparing to rule in favour of Mississippi in a case over whether the state can outlaw nearly all abortions at and after 15 weeks gestation \u8211\'20\'13 a direct challenge to the guarantee of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights enshrined in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The 98-page document, which includes 118 footnotes and a 31-page appendix on historical state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/21835435-scotus-initial-draft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was published in full}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CRoe was egregiously wrong from the start,\u8221\'20\'1D it says. \u8220\'20\'1CIts reasoning was exceptionally weak, and the decision has had damaging consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It says Roe v Wade \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be overruled\u8221\'20\'1D and goes on: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time to heed the constitution and return the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the people\u8217\'20\'19s elected representatives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What is Roe v Wade?\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade is the court decision that protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US up to the point a foetus can survive outside the womb, widely regarded as 24 weeks gestation. A full-term pregnancy is 39 weeks gestation. The 1973 ruling is among the most controversial in American history and has been subjected to many legal challenges over the year \u8211\'20\'13 but has survived until now.\par \par \uc2 For more details on the challenge to the law currently under consideration, take a look at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/TBl-lE0k4WbTlFRn6v-lQXxTpTslqnvUsR2ofAkC00snpGbt7vLS9XNB72BxUhtLNQsw4hz0D1KaYSiat4v0D_cf_dztPLfj3EpaIgm-K58RWxLCyirLLvqf1DIBFqp-YiJUW-D4rly36t1NbaEUiTrSs7GumP0lKC394_2jgudMW65u0R6STJU-AvnvhpIQBBKVHEylNDyIMec31zynuhzE6mszbqwSJtfQBl5yLirMdwottaiWjKCBAHStBLSEcwD034VbUB4c__tyIASUWOzAaL79G1PXCTSaZK28PkxPJe773wR1CfwpMI1c5ykL/3lq/JhSich0zS2qP5KosJ3Yxyw/h34/RvNk8CEZ_stdGjMSMAy5jfNK6TdGyV10ZrdBQ0L9pbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jessica Glenza\u8217\'20\'19s explainer from December}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What does the leak tell us about the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision?\par \par \uc2 While the opinion is purportedly a draft, it would have been written after a vote on the question at hand by the court \u8211\'20\'13 and indicates that a majority of justices reached the same view as Alito. Politico reported that four other Republican-appointed justices supported the decision, meaning a total of at least five votes on the nine-member court.\par \par \uc2 After such a vote, a justice is assigned the majority opinion and then writes a draft, which is then circulated and subject to edits. It is possible for changes to be made to the opinion, or even for votes to change, before the court\u8217\'20\'19s final ruling, which is expected in the next couple of months.\par \par \uc2 How significant is a leak of a draft supreme court ruling?\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Washington correspondent David Smith {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/02/roe-v-wade-abortion-supreme-court-draft-opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the leak}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning and unprecedented\u8221\'20\'1D and said it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst security breach\u8221\'20\'1D in the court\u8217\'20\'19s history. Theories abounded over the possible source of the leak, from a clerk for a liberal justice hoping to raise public pressure on the court before it publishes its decision to a conservative who wants to soften the impact of the decision when it comes \u8211\'20\'13 in other words, nobody knows.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/anB5BDNDuHMZ3XJHP1YCbnofd6W3zPobe6LeAUGnPsdXlSvHpTf-mtfKU82qp37VQZSeeDzRXmZWYlNAPgFzqOW8_pyUcu5ysBLeucsVyCWnAY3uvmaRAOBamyNwgD0w_Jyss5VIkEkDwzuzNe0g6Hq_1CtN7p1bt_EXGRpBN6y7O12VIk0uS_PvHoAbrGBsiMInh62hcbLZbVPpiw6BhtT7iwdIGeqX3kwvGlzKgP9BdKj0umYgrhypIlyGh5c5/3lq/JhSich0zS2qP5KosJ3Yxyw/h35/GSDNi1s9msKAra45B4Pn_gvR2vEq0XZoMQmRSdZmd7g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweet from Scotusblog}}}\uc2 , a respected news and analysis site, said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cimpossible to overstate the earthquake this will cause inside the court, in terms of the destruction of trust among the justices and staff. This leak is the gravest, most unforgivable sin.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 How did reproductive-rights advocates react to the news?\par \par \uc2 With fury. A \uc2 BuzzFeed\uc2  reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/anB5BDNDuHMZ3XJHP1YCbmfUPD_8dRfKVNB1Vz8jnh0Do4C2Y-3lGFb65lIinYytr7ziA3Bx0tuYkbCqnPp3XHr_brgJAPVcU-Qt06QhfQrB0PEs3mIdHhrh_GUTQWfj66J6NHOJ_nIA7Qrz6J11J91UG61Os83PL4gqkZBE9nXZZZBrG-WthP2a2yurbarZH2HU00SGUClUuckupD7fjItvBRTQwLgfJwQ4dpbfHy80pIh5OHtVabTYy4H6jsRH/3lq/JhSich0zS2qP5KosJ3Yxyw/h36/wr_x3Zy-W651d-tZvmKUDQ0wsvTbfiRJ0CDpyPeK_z0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted a video}}}\uc2  of about 200 protesters outside the court chanting slogans such as \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmy body, my choice\u8221\'20\'1D. Another video {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/anB5BDNDuHMZ3XJHP1YCbtfeYhZKLn1cf3AhMoDavKnCixKkK00HSGPzllPk2GvMR7UV3kFETLV0doZ0xwVLGyPE-meZCkpn8hNRyYUJLUj0AQ_6ufrqMFDbADtvGbWm2-w4piHZH-743nJXN5wEpGX8AZvtvtvKs9tBYPlMQfdOVan3LfYHHTEACe1IfKmQF3P4SrHZw7i5051zCfDeKqCAtxjKufnoMVwCrdndulUzCoCFYM70oiAKgg7Kv92y/3lq/JhSich0zS2qP5KosJ3Yxyw/h37/0Bnuq5mbuPBdBA_8grNOyYa3HmIyUqgh0vrHxHgC1vA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed somebody urging attenders}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIf you feel like fucking screaming, then just scream.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What about politicians?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/03/roe-v-wade-abortion-how-campaigners-reacted-to-report-on-us-supreme-court-draft-decision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats said}}}\uc2  overturning Roe v Wade would be a catastrophe. They were led by the House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , and the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , who issued a joint statement saying such a move would be \u8220\'20\'1Can abomination, one of the worst and most damaging decisions in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They also immediately sought to make Roe v Wade an issue for crucial upcoming midterm elections. Christie Roberts, the Democratic senatorial campaign executive director, said: \u8220\'20\'1CAt this critical moment, we must protect and expand Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 Senate majority with the power to confirm or reject supreme court justices.\u8221\'20\'1D Republicans by turns praised the apparent vote and condemned the leak itself.\par \par \uc2 Now what?\par \par \uc2 It is worth reiterating that it is still possible that votes could change and mean that the apparent draft opinion remains just that \u8211\'20\'13 a draft. But if the supreme court does rule along the lines suggested by the leaked document, the consequences will be rapid and hugely consequential.\par \par \uc2 Because the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  has never enshrined the right to terminate a pregnancy, the overturning of Roe v Wade would mean individual states could immediately make their own decisions over the way forward. Twenty-six of them would be expected to move quickly to do so, with many having \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D laws on the books, which would automatically come into effect in those circumstances. That means that women in those states would immediately face severe restrictions on their ability to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the US would become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/TBl-lE0k4WbTlFRn6v-lQbkDDVnCEk3-OmMad1SA3uOuFdpw8MZ7N6MocE7q1GIoVQLndJU5-CYHgXB12zesnn6yJIkigxytDHZ2wbIZlqQ8G6Hxa8PRmQfoNUud6tWXs5Cmd69fjEzjiAbY4XhpwZyc8rwJ8BSkkNzx9r0LgezYoCLuZxk33kCpNQIAuVaYgUDR6OnYPvxNHb4iqmYIeFf-47iya90brJvpA51K9PfcMhyFufo_gFbhnAhTD_Z4u-YKLTVw51ebt0bVp_zAQg/3lq/JhSich0zS2qP5KosJ3Yxyw/h38/gHKn3-FYkDue0Ums6Bbuw5Lk5i2vxrtukE-5gZSBHfo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of only four countries}}}\uc2  to curtail that right in nearly 30 years.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220503ei530018o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
