\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden announces another $800m in military aid for Ukraine: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re in a critical window\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho (now) and Richard Luscombe (earlier) \par \uc2 4,861 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2022\par 20:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President also announces \u8216\'20\'18Unite for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19 refugee programUS will take in 100,000 refugees, says BidenRussia-Ukraine blog \u8211\'20\'13 follow the latest newsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * The Florida legislature approved a congressional map approved by governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  that will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/apr/20/ron-desantis-florida-electoral-map-gerrymandering-republican-advantage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severely curtail Black voting power}}}\uc2  in the state - and also passed a bill dissolving the self-governance status of Disney World. This all took place despite Democrats staging a sit-in on the legislature floor in protest of the new congressional map.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to deliver remarks momentarily in Portland, Oregon on infrastructure. He is then staying in Portland to participate in a fundraiser for the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 , before flying to Seattle to participate in yet another fundraiser for the DNC.\par \par \uc2 * A federal judge temporarily blocked an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in Kentucky that was so restrictive that the two remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics had to halt procedures.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal judge temporarily blocks Kentucky anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked enforcement of a sweeping new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in Kentucky that banned abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy and called for a combination birth-death or stillbirth certificate for each \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The restrictive law forced Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s two remaining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to halt procedures.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEWS: Abortions can happen again in Kentucky \u8212\'20\'14 for now.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked the state's sweeping new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, HB3, which clinics said made it impossible to provide care.\par \par \uc2 If Roe is overturned this summer, KY has a trigger ban that would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Shefali Luthra (@shefalil) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/shefalil/status/1517229842042863623?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite the efforts of Florida Democrats, the Florida legislature approved a congressional map approved by governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  that will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/apr/20/ron-desantis-florida-electoral-map-gerrymandering-republican-advantage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severely curtail Black voting power}}}\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Florida Democrats staged a sit-in on the floor of the state legislature to interrupt the special legislative session.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we see today is an overreach, and it\u8217\'20\'19s something we see as unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic representative Kamia Brown, who chairs the legislative Black caucus, told the Associated Press after the session adjourned. \u8220\'20\'1CToday was one thing we could not just take and stand. We\u8217\'20\'19re sick and tired of being sick and tired.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The congressional map passed today favors the GOP in 20 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 28 congressional districts in an increase of four seats for the party, by eliminating two congressional districts where Black voters have the ability to elect the candidate of their choosing. One of those, the fifth congressional district, which stretches from Jacksonville to Tallahassee and has a voting population that is 46% Black, will be chopped up into four districts where Black voters comprise a much smaller share of the population.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. Al Lawson, whose district is on the chopping block in maps passed by FL legislation, tees off on DeSantis\par \par \uc2 "Once again, DeSantis is showing Florida voters that he is governing the state as a dictator." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TUVALHiV1S"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/TUVALHiV1S}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1517213483624013828?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrFlorida will be sued. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wkoecH0Qbb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/wkoecH0Qbb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marc E. Elias (@marceelias) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marceelias/status/1517196505999974400?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is in the news again, this time for...not being on the news?\par \par \uc2 Trump is denying that he stormed out of a televised interview with Piers Morgan, claiming instead that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/20/donald-trump-appears-to-storm-out-of-piers-morgan-tv-interview-in-advert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clip released yesterday}}}\uc2  promoting \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most explosive interview of the year\u8221\'20\'1D was misleadingly edited to give the impression that he shouted \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the camera off\u8221\'20\'1D while rising from his chair in anger.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team provided audio to US media outlets that suggested that he had said \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the camera off\u8221\'20\'1D after he and Morgan exchanged pleasantries at the end of the interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a pathetic attempt to use President Trump as a way to revive the career of a failed television host,\u8221\'20\'1D said Taylor Budowich, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe says it\u8217\'20\'19s a rigged election, and he now says I have a rigged promo,\u8221\'20\'1D Morgan said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I would say is watch the interview. It will all be there. We won\u8217\'20\'19t be doing any duplicitous editing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/21/donald-trump-denies-storming-out-piers-morgan-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump denies storming out of Piers Morgan interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been quite a day in Florida. First Florida Democrats staged a sit in on the floor of the state legislature, halting a special legislative session in which Republicans are poised to pass new congressional districts that would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/apr/20/ron-desantis-florida-electoral-map-gerrymandering-republican-advantage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severely curtail Black voting power}}}\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 All while this was happening, the Florida legislature passed a bill dissolving the self-governance status of Disney World.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Florida legislature has passed the bill dissolving Disney World\u8217\'20\'19s self-governance status in retaliation for \uc2 Disney\uc2 's (belated) opposition to Florida's Don\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay law. It now heads to DeSantis' desk to be signed into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Tyler Cohen (@briantylercohen) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/briantylercohen/status/1517201711365906434?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 This bill dissolving Disney World\u8217\'20\'19s self-governance came after \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s opposition to what critics call the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D law that bars instruction on sexual orientation and gender identity in kindergarten through third grade.\par \par \uc2 If Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signs the bill into law, it could have huge tax implications for \uc2 Disney\uc2  - but Democrats also warned that the move could cause local homeowners to get hit with big tax bills if they have to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/20/disney-world-florida-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 absorb bond debt from Disney}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrPolitico-Morning Consult poll:\par \par \uc2 75% of voters consider themselves "fans" of \uc2 Disney\uc2 's movies and TV shows\par \par \uc2 31% have a favorable view of \uc2 Ron DeSantis\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Griffin (@kylegriffin1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kylegriffin1/status/1517126009258188800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis week in FL politics:\par \par \uc2 -DeSantis announces a May special session on property insurance (+ other topics?)\par \par \uc2 -DeSantis adds bills affecting \uc2 Disney\uc2  to redistricting special session\par \par \uc2 -Lawmakers take up and pass \uc2 Disney\uc2  bills\par \par \uc2 -Democrats stage unprecedented House sit-in.\par \par \uc2 It's Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kirby Wilson (@KirbyWTweets) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KirbyWTweets/status/1517206735987040256?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report: House select committee investigating 6 January attack to meet with Trump Jr\par \par \uc2 ABC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/donald-trump-jr-expected-meet-jan-committee-sources/story?id=84220239&cid=social_twitter_abcn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reporting }}}\uc2  that in the coming days, \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  is expected to meet with the House select committee tasked with investigating the 6 January attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Sources tell ABC News that the meeting is voluntary and the committee did not have to subpoena the eldest son of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump Jr joins his sister \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and her husband, \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , as the most recent Trump family members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/05/ivanka-trump-capitol-attack-committee-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to speak to the panel}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 An auction of artwork, including pieces by Pablo Picasso and Andy Warhol, and other personal items owned by the late supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ruth-bader-ginsberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg}}}\uc2  is expected to raise hundreds of thousands of dollars next week.\par \par \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 . Photograph: Jessica Hill/AP\par \par \uc2 Much of her collection of paintings and ceramics forms a 115-lot modern art auction hosted by the Potomack company of Alexandria, Virginia, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-catalog/20th-21st-century-art-ruth-bader-ginsburg-ot_40GQJOAB3J"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an online catalog}}}\uc2 . An additional collection entitled \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-catalog/ruth-bader-ginsburg-chambers-home_4DWBHEVOH6#15040B29C0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chambers and home}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D features 145 more lots of miscellaneous curios, including pewter bowls, crystal vases and numerous other personal items.\par \par \uc2 Ginsburg, the iconic human and civil rights pioneer who died in 2020 aged 87 from complications of pancreatic cancer, owned a multitude of artefacts spanning the last two centuries, by artists including Picasso and Warhol.\par \par \uc2 One of the most valuable items is a 1953 oil painting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-lot/gunther-gerzso-mexican-1915-2000-presagio-premoni_014441CBD4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Presagio-Premonition}}}\uc2 , by the Mexican artist Gunther Gerzso, which is expected to raise up to $100,000.\par \par \uc2 Among the most personal is a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-lot/gartenhaus-natural-black-mink-coat-with-ruth-bade_26F4321B93/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gartenhaus natural black mink coat}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D with Ginsburg\u8217\'20\'19s name embroidered in a pocket. By Thursday morning, bidding for that was already above $2,000, more than twice its original estimate.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-catalog/20th-21st-century-art-ruth-bader-ginsburg-lot_40GQJOAB3J?keywords=picasso"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ceramics by Picasso}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.potomackcompany.com/auction-lot/andy-warhol-american-1928-1987-campbells-soup-can_3024E9C981"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Warhol painting of a can of tomato soup}}}\uc2 , are among the other highlights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese items are truly tangible pieces of her life and times as one of America\u8217\'20\'19s greatest supreme court justices,\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 Elizabeth Haynie Wainstein, owner of the Potomack Company, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/21/us/ruth-bader-ginsburg-auction.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/21/ruth-bader-ginsburg-art-collection-auction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\u8217\'20\'19s personal art collection up for auction}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The much vaunted and heavily promoted CNN+ subscription streaming service, which the network intended to be a value-added supplement to its regular news programming, has folded, less than a month after it was launched.\par \par \uc2 The decision to halt the service on 30 April will be seen as a massive humiliation for CNN, which was relying on its big-name presenters to draw in customers at $5.99 a month.\par \par \uc2 Take up was slow, however, and the new corporate owners of CNN+, \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2 , decided to pull the plug on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of 2m subscribers in the first year appeared hugely optimistic, with reports saying it had attracted barely 150,000 in the three weeks since its launch.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to staff attempting to paint the abrupt closure as a reshuffle of resources, CNN\u8217\'20\'19s incoming president Chris Licht said:\par \par \uc2 While today\u8217\'20\'19s decision is incredibly difficult, it is the right one for the long-term success of CNN. It allows us to refocus resources on the core products that drive our singular focus: further enhancing CNN\u8217\'20\'19s journalism and its reputation as a global news leader.\par \par \uc2 enltrBreaking: CNN+, the streaming service that was hyped as one of the most signifiant developments in the history of CNN, will shut down on April 30, just one month after it launched. Here's our initial story \u8211\'20\'13 more to come {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JElI3cVyDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JElI3cVyDF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1517170287435001858?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Black Democrats have staged a sit-in protest in the Florida legislature to disrupt approval of Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s congressional redistricting plans, which they say seeks to eliminate representation for Black voters.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article260624722.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Miami Herald}}}\uc2 , the special legislative session called by DeSantis was adjourned just before lunchtime Thursday as the Black lawmakers began chanting, and were joined in the protest by White colleagues.\par \par \uc2 The Herald reports: \u8220\'20\'1CThe House was halfway through a three-hour debate on the map when Rep Yvonne Hinson, a Gainesville Democrat, was cut off because she had exceeded the five-minute time limit set for member debate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs her microphone was silenced, Rep Angie Nixon, a Jacksonville Democrat, walked on the floor with a T-shirt under her suit jacket that read \u8216\'20\'18Stop the Black Attack\u8217\'20\'19 and held a sign in protest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Black Democrats started chanting and white Democrats joined the protest, House Speaker \uc2 Chris Sprowls\uc2  ordered the House in recess and stunned Republicans slowly walked off the floor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeSantis has proposed his own redrawn map for Florida\u8217\'20\'19s congressional districts, which the Republican-controlled legislature has said it will pass without change, despite it being lawmakers\u8217\'20\'19 responsibility to draw up boundaries.\par \par \uc2 The governor\u8217\'20\'19s proposal would chop up the fifth congressional district into four new ones where Black voters would comprise a much smaller share of the vote. Critics say his \u8220\'20\'1Cracist\u8221\'20\'1D plan would eliminate the seats of two Black congress members.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/apr/20/ron-desantis-florida-electoral-map-gerrymandering-republican-advantage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A racist move\u8217\'20\'19: Florida\u8217\'20\'19s DeSantis threatens Black voter power with electoral maps}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  must act to reduce mounting economic pressure by ditching \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke advisers\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/mittromney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mitt Romney}}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Mitt Romney. Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 The Utah senator and former Republican presidential nominee made the demand in a column {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-errors-inflation-mitt-romney-woke-advisers-government-spending-regulation-fossil-fuels-energy-prices-immigration-border-crossings-11650404949?mod=opinion_major_pos4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA new set of priorities requires a new set of principals,\u8221\'20\'1D Romney wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden needs to ditch his woke advisers and surround himself with people who want to get the economy working again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Romney\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately respond to a request for comment about what a \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke adviser\u8221\'20\'1D was or who might qualify for the title. The White House did not comment.\par \par \uc2 As midterm elections approach, the Biden administration faces strong economic headwinds. Inflation is at long-term highs, adding to a cost-of-living crisis fueled by the coronavirus pandemic and the invasion of Ukraine by Russia.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s favourability rating has plummeted as polling shows disapproval of his handling of economic affairs.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/21/joe-biden-woke-advisers-us-economy-mitt-romney-wall-street-journal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden must ditch \u8216\'20\'18woke advisers\u8217\'20\'19 to fix US economy, Mitt Romney says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced that the US would be providing another $800m military assistance package to Ukraine, in addition to $500m in economic assistance. He acknowledged that he had nearly exhausted the drawdown authority authorized by Congress in a bipartisan spending bill last month, and that he would be making a supplemental budget request in order to continue funding Ukraine as it defends itself from Russia.\par \par \uc2 * In this same address, Biden announced the creation of Unite for Ukraine, a humanitarian parole program to expedite the migration of Ukrainian refugees from Europe to the US through sponsorship.\par \par \uc2 * In addition to more sanctions announced yesterday, Biden announced that Russian-affiliated ships are now banned from American ports.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine prime minister Denys Shmyhal is in Washington, and met briefly with Biden and some of his cabinet members before Biden gave his remarks. Shmyhal then went on to Capitol Hill, where he met with House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new book by reporters Jonathan Martin and Alexander Burns has new details of the days following the 6 January attack on the US Capitol in which Kevin McCarthy and \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the two top Republican leaders in Congress, privately told associates that they believed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should be held responsible for the insurrection.\par \par \uc2 McCarthy has come out strongly against the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/21/us/politics/trump-mitch-mcconnell-kevin-mccarthy.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  on the book\u8217\'20\'19s findings, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally false and wrong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PWi2WkoWzh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PWi2WkoWzh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin McCarthy (@GOPLeader) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPLeader/status/1517164322782433287?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/21/republicans-donald-trump-capitol-attack-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Republicans held \u8216\'20\'18atrocious\u8217\'20\'19 Trump responsible for Capitol attack, book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Delta Airlines\uc2  will restore flight privileges to the 2,000 customers who were barred from flights for failing to comply with the federal mask mandate, Reuters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/delta-restore-flight-privileges-about-2000-passengers-over-mask-violations-2022-04-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is reporting}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Now that a federal judge has ruled the mandate unlawful and the Biden administration will no longer enforce it on public transit - though the justice department appealed the ruling yesterday at the request of public health officials - Delta said it will restore passengers \u8220\'20\'1Conly after each case is reviewed and each customer demonstrates an understanding of their expected behavior when flying with us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny further disregard for the policies that keep us all safe will result in placement on Delta\u8217\'20\'19s permanent no-fly list,\u8221\'20\'1D Delta said.\par \par \uc2 This will not affect the 1,000 or so passengers \u8220\'20\'1Cwho demonstrated egregious behavior and are already on the permanent no-fly list.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Delta joins \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  in overturning a ban on passengers who had been banned for not wearing masks on a \u8220\'20\'1Ccase by case basis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the White House readout of the meeting between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Ukraine prime minister Denys Shmyhal :\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: White House releases readout of Pres. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Ukrainian Prime Minister Denys Shmyhal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden conveyed the continued commitment of the United States to support the people of Ukraine and to impose costs on Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CzlbOnpowT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CzlbOnpowT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/l0z52cIK6z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/l0z52cIK6z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1517162223524888576?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Now Ukraine prime minister Denys Shmyhal is on Capitol Hill with House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 . Earlier, Shmyhal spoke with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , which delayed his remarks.\par \par \uc2 enltrUkrainian PM Denys Shmyhal is here on the Hill with Speaker Pelosi today. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/s7el1TuErZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/s7el1TuErZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1517158520566734848?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 After providing an update on Ukraine, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now off to Portland, Oregon to talk about infrastructure and attend a fundraiser for the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some more details from the defense department on the new $800m military assistance package to Ukraine :\par \par \uc2 enltrAccording to DOD, the capabilities in this package include:\par \par \uc2 -72 155mm Howitzers and 144,000 artillery rounds;\par \par \uc2 -72 Tactical Vehicles to tow 155mm Howitzers;\par \par \uc2 -Over 121 Phoenix Ghost Tactical Unmanned Aerial Systems; and\par \par \uc2 -Field equipment and spare parts\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lara Seligman (@laraseligman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laraseligman/status/1517152452063072257?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 For those keeping track on how much the US has provided Ukraine so far in military assistance:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe U.S. has now given Ukraine $3.4 billion in military aid since Russia's Feb. 24 invasion with President Biden's announcement of $800 million more in U.S. assistance this morning.\par \par \uc2 Nearly half of that aid \u8211\'20\'13 $1.6 billion \u8211\'20\'13 has been approved in the last two weeks alone.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jack Detsch (@JackDetsch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JackDetsch/status/1517147752471293953?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to new sanctions against Russia announced yesterday, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said any Russian-affiliated ships are now banned from entering American ports.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: U.S. is banning Russian-affiliated ships from American ports "to further deny Russia the benefits of the international economic system": President Biden\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jack Detsch (@JackDetsch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JackDetsch/status/1517143998149791746?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden announces expedited humanitarian immigration program for Ukrainian refugees\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the creation of \u8220\'20\'1C Unite for Ukraine, \u8221\'20\'1D a humanitarian parole program that will expedite the migration process from Europe to the US for Ukrainian refugees.\par \par \uc2 Biden has promised that the US will take 100,000 Ukrainian refugees.\par \par \uc2 enltrHow does it work?\par \par \uc2 Starting 4/25 (when portal goes live): US sponsors directly upload an affidavit to sponsor a specific Ukrainian person/family. Sponsor must pass background checks, vetting to prove they can financially support Ukrainians, etc -- could all happen within a week\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133692388397056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThen: Ukrainian person/family gets notified sponsor is approved. Background checks/vetting begin on *that* end. To be eligible: must have a US sponsor, must pass biometric screening, must be vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133694439415808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOnce vetting on both sides complete, sponsored Ukrainians granted travel authorization to US, humanitarian parole protection for two years.\par \par \uc2 US officials envision this program will comprise "the majority of the 100,000 people" President Biden committed to bring to the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133697291628544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis new humanitarian parole program will complement the existing legal pathways available to Ukrainians including immigrant visas and refugee processing,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will provide an expedient channel for secure legal migration from Europe to the United States for Ukrainians who have a US sponsor such as a family or an NGO. This program will be fast, it will be streamlined and it will ensure the United States will honor its commitment to the people of Ukraine and need not go through our southern border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden has nearly exhausted drawdown authority for Ukraine spending\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  acknowledged today that with the latest $800m military assistance package to Ukraine, he has \u8220\'20\'1Calmost exhausted the drawdown authority\u8221\'20\'1D authorized by Congress in a bipartisan spending bill last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to sustain Ukraine for the duration of this fight, next week I will have to send to Congress a supplemental budget request to keep weapons and ammunition flowing without interruption, to continue delivering economic assistance to the Ukrainian people,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy expectation is that Congress will act and move quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said this continued support of Ukraine is necessary in sending a message to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur unity at home, our unity with our allies and partners, our unity with the Ukrainian people is sending an unmistakable message to Putin: He will never succeed in dominating and occupying al of Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat will not happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to military assistance, the US is also sending $500m in economic assistance to Ukraine, bringing the total economic assistance sent to Ukraine in the last two months to $1bn.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke of everything the US has provided Ukraine in the past two months, a \u8220\'20\'1Crecord speed\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have sent thousands of anti-armor and anti-missile helicopters, drones, grenade launchers, machine guns, rifles, radar systems,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CMore than 50m rounds of ammunition has already been sent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not sitting on the funding that Congress has provided for Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are sending it directly to the front lines of freedom, to the fearless and skilled Ukrainian fighters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said he was amazed \u8220\'20\'1Cat the courage of this country, at the resolve that they are showing.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CNot just their military but their average citizen, men and women, young men, young women as well,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sustained and coordinated support of the international community, led and facilitate by the United States, is a significant reason why Ukraine is able to stop Russia from taking over its country thus far,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery American taxpayer, every member of our armed forces, can be proud of the fact that our country\u8217\'20\'19s generosity and the skill and service of our military helped arm and repel Russia\u8217\'20\'19s aggression in Ukraine and beat back Putin\u8217\'20\'19s savagery that tried to seize Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s capital and wipe out Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden announces another $800m military assistance package to Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took to the podium today to announce that the US will provide another $800m military assistance package to Ukraine to \u8220\'20\'1Cto further augment Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ability to fight in the east, in the Donbas region.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re in a critical window of time now where (Russian forces are) going to set the stage for the next phase of this war,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States and our partners and allies are moving as fast as possible to continue to provide Ukraine with the equipment it needs, its forces need, to defend its nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This package will be in addition to the $800m package announced last week by Biden. This package will include \u8220\'20\'1C heavy artillery weapons, dozens of Howitzers and 144,000 rounds of ammunition to go with those Howitzers,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt also includes more tactical drones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 It looks like we have a lot of Ukraine news coming out of the US this morning. In addition to speaking about providing more military assistance, it appears \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be speaking momentarily about at new program that will allow US citizens to directly sponsor the immigration of displaced Ukrainian refugees in Europe, to speed up the travel process.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: President Biden will today announce a new program for US citizens to directly sponsor displaced Ukrainians in Europe, and quickly approve travel to the US\par \par \uc2 More from senior officials this morning ????\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133687938334720?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe program is called "Uniting for Ukraine," part of Biden's commitment to welcome up to 100k Ukrainians into the US. Officials say it's an "expression of solidarity with displaced Ukrainians and a "clear signal of support" for European nations hosting historic number of refugees\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133690396160000?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHow does it work?\par \par \uc2 Starting 4/25 (when portal goes live): US sponsors directly upload an affidavit to sponsor a specific Ukrainian person/family. Sponsor must pass background checks, vetting to prove they can financially support Ukrainians, etc -- could all happen within a week\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133692388397056?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThen: Ukrainian person/family gets notified sponsor is approved. Background checks/vetting begin on *that* end. To be eligible: must have a US sponsor, must pass biometric screening, must be vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133694439415808?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOnce vetting on both sides complete, sponsored Ukrainians granted travel authorization to US, humanitarian parole protection for two years.\par \par \uc2 US officials envision this program will comprise "the majority of the 100,000 people" President Biden committed to bring to the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133697291628544?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat about Ukrainians at the border?\par \par \uc2 US has already allowed in around 15,000 who came to Mexico seeking US entry. Senior DHS official says *beginning 4/25* - once this program is live - Ukrainians at the southern border will be subject to same Title 42 expulsion as anyone else.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133699250331649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI asked if any talk of expanding program to other refugees in Europe- Syria, Afghanistan,etc\par \par \uc2 Snr official says no. "this [Ukrainian] population is really unique" - most requests for refuge "temporary in nature" - diff from others who fled + been living in 3rd countries for yrs.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 amna (@IAmAmnaNawaz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IAmAmnaNawaz/status/1517133701414629378?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ukraine prime minister Denys Shmyhal is in Washington today. As we reported yesterday, he will be meeting with House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  and other bipartisan congressional leaders later, but it appears he will also be meeting with defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrUkraine\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister will be at the Pentagon later today for a meeting with U.S. Defense Secretary Austin.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Idrees Ali (@idreesali114) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/idreesali114/status/1517131599556534272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to provide an update on Ukraine and Russia\par \par \uc2 Howdy, live blog readers. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get to it.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to take to the podium today at the White House at 9.45am ET to provide an update on Ukraine and Russia.\par \par \uc2 An anonymous official told the Associated Press that Biden is planning to detail his plans to build on the roughly $2.6bn in military assistance that his administration has already approved for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 This new package should be similar in size to the $800m package that Biden announced last week, and will include much needed heavy artillery and ammunition for Ukrainian forces in the escalating battle for the Donbas region of eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , told reporters that five flights with military assistance have arrived in the region over the last few days, with more than half a dozen flights from the US scheduled to arrive shortly with even more equipment.\par \par \uc2 Biden yesterday lauded military officials for \u8220\'20\'1Cexceptional\u8221\'20\'1D work arming Ukraine as he gathered the nation\u8217\'20\'19s military brass for their first in-person group meeting at the White House of his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know about you, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve been to Ukraine a number of times before the war... and I knew they were tough and proud but I tell you what: they\u8217\'20\'19re tougher and more proud than I thought,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told military commanders. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m amazed at what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing with your help.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 After we closed the blog down yesterday, the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  asked the justice department to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/20/mask-mandate-cdc-appeal-justice-department-travel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 file an an appeal}}}\uc2  seeking to overturn a judge\u8217\'20\'19s order that voided the federal mask mandate on planes and trains and in travel hubs.\par \par \uc2 Biden administration officials had said they were awaiting the guidance of health officials before determining whether to file an appeal of the ruling made by Florida district court judge Kathryn Kimball Mizelle, the youngest \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointee to the federal bench, and minutes after the CDC asked, notice of appeal was filed in federal court in Tampa.\par \par \uc2 As you can imagine with this highly politicized ruling, reaction to the appeal was staunchly bipartisan, with conservatives rallying against the appeal and Democrats supporting it.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden\u8217\'20\'19s Justice Department (his thugs) want to appeal the removal of their unconstitutional travel mask mandate.\par \par \uc2 LOL.\par \par \uc2 The regime hates freedom and you will continue to suffer while they are in office. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2hIQjVu1fu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2hIQjVu1fu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Candace Owens (@RealCandaceO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RealCandaceO/status/1516908353104105481?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGreat to see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheJusticeDept?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheJusticeDept}}}\uc2  would defend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CDCgov?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CDCgov}}}\uc2  's authority to protect everyone in our nation during a public health crisis. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/94Bj93dmrh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/94Bj93dmrh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2  (@SecBecerra) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBecerra/status/1516569483841781765?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Biden Administration will appeal the ruling that lifted the COVID mask mandate on travel.\par \par \uc2 If it were up to them, they'd keep masks on Americans and their children indefinitely!\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep Andy Biggs (@RepAndyBiggsAZ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepAndyBiggsAZ/status/1516798506329116676?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrA DOJ appeal makes good sense. All but the most ideology-driven panel would reverse the clearly erroneous district court decision, and the case won\u8217\'20\'19t be legally moot even if CDC temporarily lifts its mask mandate in early May because the need could recur. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QXVb0r87LS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QXVb0r87LS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Laurence Tribe (@tribelaw) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1516969952959475712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 21, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 More to come.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 2022-04-21T13:22:02Z 2022-04-21T20:35:21Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/43379b59f69ea34208071801d78fc8362cd00327/0_58_5692_3416/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/43379b59f69ea34208071801d78fc8362cd00327/0_58_5692_3416/500.jpg}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  speaks at the White House on 21 April. \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2 . Mitt Romney.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220421ei4l001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
