\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Ukraine repelling intense Russian offensive in east\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2022\par 10:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Shelling and strikes in Donbas increasing but Russians hampered by logistical problems, UK claims. Plus, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s $6bn effort to save nuclear plants\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Russia has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/20/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-56-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased the intensity of its eastern offensive}}}\uc2  but has been repeatedly repelled by Ukrainian forces, the \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s Ministry of Defence\uc2  (MoD) has said, as western governments pledged to send more artillery, and a new deadline for surrender in Mariupol approached.\par \par \uc2 The MoD said late on Tuesday that shelling and strikes were increasing over the line of control in Donbas but that Russian forces continued to be hampered by logistical and technological problems. It also noted an \u8220\'20\'1Cinability to stamp out resistance\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol as a sign of failure to achieve Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s objectives.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian defence ministry\uc2  has said it will offer the besieged port city a ceasefire today to allow Ukrainian defenders holed up in the Azovstal steelworks to lay down their arms. About 1,000 civilians are reportedly hiding in underground shelters beneath the steel plant in Mariupol, according to the city council. Most of the civilians are believed to be women with children and elderly people.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How are Ukrainian troops faring in Mariupol? A commander for the Ukrainian marines in Mariupol said his forces were \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe facing our last days, if not hours\u8221\'20\'1D and appealed for extraction, in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post published early this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is happening with the diplomatic effort? Western nations are preparing to stage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/20/g20-delegates-to-stage-protests-against-russia-over-ukraine-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coordinated walkouts and other diplomatic snubs}}}\uc2  in protest at Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine at a meeting of G20 finance ministers in Washington. \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , the US treasury secretary, is planning to avoid sessions attended by Russian officials.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/20/russia-ukraine-war-what-we-know-on-day-56-of-the-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what we know on day 56}}}\uc2  of the invasion.\par \par \uc2 January 6 \u8216\'20\'18was a coup organized by the president\u8217\'20\'19, says Jamie Raskin\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attempted a coup on 6 January 2021 as he tried to salvage his doomed presidency, and that will be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/donald-trump-jamie-raskin-january-6-committee-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central focus of forthcoming public hearings}}}\uc2  of the special House panel investigating events surrounding the insurrection at the US Capitol, the congressman Jamie Raskin has said.\par \par \uc2 Raskin is a prominent Democrat on the committee and also led the House efforts when Trump was impeached for a historic second time, in 2021, accused of inciting the storming of the US Capitol by his extremist supporters who were trying to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a coup organized by the president against the vice-president and against the Congress in order to overturn the 2020 presidential election,\u8221\'20\'1D Raskin said in an interview with the Guardian, Reuters news agency and the Climate One radio program.\par \par \uc2 Public hearings by the bipartisan special committee investigating January 6 and related actions by Trump and his White House team and other allies, chaired by the Mississippi Democrat \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , are expected next month.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else did Raskin say? \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to tell the whole story of everything that happened. There was a violent insurrection and an attempted coup and we were saved by \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s refusal to go along with that plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas advocates file new legal challenge to near total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates in Texas have filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/texas-abortion-ban-senate-bill8-legal-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new legal challenge to halt a near total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  that has been in effect for more than half a year.\par \par \uc2 Senate bill 8 bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected \u8211\'20\'13 typically as early as six week of pregnancy, which is before most people are aware they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 and offers no exception for rape or incest. The lawsuit, filed yesterday, asks a federal court to rule the extreme law unconstitutional. It cites public threats and legal action from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists against Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, groups that have been instrumental in helping patients travel out of state for care, arguing that this conduct has chilled their first amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiffs urgently need this court to stop Texas\u8217\'20\'19s brazen defiance of the rule of law, uphold the federal constitutional rights of pregnant Texans, and restore the ability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and their donors, employees and volunteers to fully serve Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients,\u8221\'20\'1D the federal court filing reads.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wendy Davis, a former Texas senator who famously led an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/jun/26/wendy-davis-abortion-filibuster-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11-hour filibuster}}}\uc2  against an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill in 2013, said : \u8220\'20\'1CWe are asking the courts today to stop the unconstitutional harassment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds by confirming SB 8 cannot be used to silence donors with bogus threats.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Prince Harry has said the Queen was \u8220\'20\'1Con great form\u8221\'20\'1D during their recent meeting, and he wanted to make sure she had \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right people around her\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/apr/20/prince-harry-says-queen-on-great-form-during-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Speaking to NBC}}}\uc2  about his meeting with the monarch, Harry said: \u8220\'20\'1CBeing with her it was great, it was just so nice to see her, she\u8217\'20\'19s on great form.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a 59-page opinion on Monday, the US district judge Kathryn Mizelle of Tampa, Florida, overturned the federal requirement that people wear masks on planes and public transportation. She has become an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/trump-judge-kathryn-mizelle-mask-mandate-coronavirus-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 instant heroine of the Republican right}}}\uc2  hailed for \u8220\'20\'1Ccourage\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon sense\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Fantastic Beasts star Ezra Miller has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/ezra-miller-arrested-assault-hawaii"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested on suspicion of assault}}}\uc2  in Hawaii\par \par \uc2 . Miller already faces charges of harassment and disorderly conduct after an incident last month at a karaoke bar on the island.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A growing number of cities and states have restricted the information that local law enforcement departments can exchange with immigration authorities. But new documents reveal that \uc2 US Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) has tapped private technology companies to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/us-immigration-agency-data-loophole-information-deportation-targets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 skirt such sanctuary policies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Netflix\uc2  lost subscribers for the first time in 10 years at the start of the year and said it expects to lose even more in the spring, sending its share price crashing again yesterday. The streaming giant\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/apr/19/netflix-loses-subscribers-first-time-10-years-ukraine-shared-logins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 share price initially fell close to 20%}}}\uc2  on news that ??it had lost 200,000 subscribers globally during the first quarter.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: most workers at large retail and food firms get less than $15 an hour \u8211\'20\'13 study\par \par \uc2 Some of the largest, most profitable companies in retail and food services are still paying most of their workers less than $15 an hour, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/how-much-retail-food-companies-pay-workers-per-hour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many staff still make less than $10 an hour}}}\uc2 , according to a company wage tracker developed by the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2  and the Shift Project. According to a 2021 report by the \uc2 National Low Income Housing Coalition\uc2 , a worker needs to make at least $20.40 an hour to afford the rent of the average one-bedroom apartment in the US.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: the family who endured two true crime stories\par \par \uc2 Ashley Stayner is a self-professed true crime fan. She also happens to have had a front-row seat to two true crime narratives in her own family, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/apr/20/there-was-a-lot-of-torment-the-family-who-endured-two-true-stories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes Radheyan Simonpillai}}}\uc2 . Her father is the abduction victim turned hero Steven Stayner, the subject of the two-part television movie I Know My First Name is Steven, which aired in 1989. Her uncle is Carey Stayner, the serial killer sitting on death row for the Yosemite murders, which have been covered on numerous true crime programs such as American Justice, \uc2 FBI\uc2 : Criminal Pursuit and more.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Biden launches $6bn effort to save America\u8217\'20\'19s distressed nuclear plants\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is launching a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/19/biden-effort-nuclear-plants-energy-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $6bn effort to rescue nuclear power plants}}}\uc2  at risk of closing, citing the need to retain nuclear energy as a carbon-free source of power that helps to combat climate change. \u8220\'20\'1CUS nuclear power plants contribute more than half of our carbon-free electricity, and President Biden is committed to keeping these plants active to reach our clean energy goals,\u8221\'20\'1D said the energy secretary, \uc2 Jennifer Granholm\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re using every tool available to get this country powered by clean energy by 2035.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: humpback whale turns on orca pod in rare encounter\par \par \uc2 An aggressive humpback whale appeared to turn the tables on a pod of orcas off the Canadian coast, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/apr/19/humpback-whale-orca-video-valiant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stalking and then ambushing the group}}}\uc2  that more usually would have been attacking it. The rare occurrence took place in the Salish Sea between British Columbia and Washington state and was witnessed by tourists on a whale-watching trip. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s something happening in front of us that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been seen before,\u8221\'20\'1D Olivia Esqueda told CHEK News. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard not to just kind of be like a kid at Disney World.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220420ei4k0012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
