\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas advocates file new legal challenge to near-total  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,033 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 April 2022\par 22:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit asks court to rule SB 8 unconstitutional, citing public threats and legal action from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights advocates in Texas have filed a new legal challenge to halt a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  that has been in effect for more than half a year.\par \par \uc2 Senate Bill 8 bars \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected \u8211\'20\'13 typically as early as six week of pregnancy, which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before most people}}}\uc2  are aware they are pregnant \u8211\'20\'13 and offers no exception for rape or incest. The lawsuit, filed on Tuesday, asks a federal court to rule the extreme law unconstitutional. It cites public threats and legal action from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists against Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, groups that have been instrumental in helping patients travel out of state for care, arguing that this conduct has chilled their first amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlaintiffs urgently need this court to stop Texas\u8217\'20\'19s brazen defiance of the rule of law, uphold the federal constitutional rights of pregnant Texans, and restore the ability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and their donors, employees and volunteers to fully serve Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawyeringproject.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/2022-04-19-Complaint.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the federal court filing reads}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SB 8 is not directly enforced by government officials, but includes an unprecedented private enforcement provision that allows any individual \u8211\'20\'13 including anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vigilantes with no connection to the patient \u8211\'20\'13 to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers or anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abet\u8221\'20\'1D care. Those who bring successful suits can win at least $10,000 in damages. The scheme \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/10/texas-abortion-law-jonathan-f-mitchell-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meant to evade judicial review}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has thus far allowed the law to remain in effect, despite previous legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 The new lawsuit takes aim at a handful of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists in Texas as well as rightwing state lawmaker \uc2 Briscoe Cain\uc2 , who have all seized on the law\u8217\'20\'19s novel enforcement provision by taking \u8220\'20\'1Csteps\u8221\'20\'1D to sue or publicly threaten Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds. In March, Cain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BriscoeCain/status/1504891954475290624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  sent cease-and-desist letters}}}\uc2  on his official letterhead to Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds, and cited the \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a Texas statute that pre-dates Roe v Wade, the 1973 supreme court decision that guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that is presently under consideration by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cain also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BriscoeCain/status/1509288580681814022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CProsecute Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Funds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers say the hostile actions by Cain and activists are \u8220\'20\'1Cchilling\u8221\'20\'1D the work of plaintiff Stigma Relief Fund, a non-profit that financially assists those who cannot afford \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by causing employees, donors and volunteers to end their relationships with the organization.\par \par \uc2 Wendy Davis, a former Texas senator who famously led an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/jun/26/wendy-davis-abortion-filibuster-chaos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  11-hour filibuster}}}\uc2  against an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill in 2013 and later ran an unsuccessful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/jun/25/wendy-davis-texas-democrats-governor-race-chances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bid for Texas governor}}}\uc2 , and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic director Marva Sadler, are also plaintiffs in the suit. They say they will no longer be donating to Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds as the law is in effect due to the threats. The plaintiffs are represented by the Lawyering Project, who brought the suit in the US western district in Austin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are asking the courts today to stop the unconstitutional harassment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds by confirming SB 8 cannot be used to silence donors with bogus threats,\u8221\'20\'1D said Davis in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is vital we show up for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and practical support organizations as they have shown up for pregnant Texans. If you want to fight back against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans like Texas\u8217\'20\'19s SB 8, donate to your local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fund and practical support organization today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Advocates hope the lawsuit will have more success than earlier challenges, after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  and the Texas supreme court ruled this year that the law could stand.\par \par \uc2 In March, two Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds filed suit against two of the activists named in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s suit in federal court outside of Texas, in order to evade the conservative fifth circuit court of appeals. Advocates hope the pressure of multiple lawsuits with differing strategies, defendants and venues will help legally erode SB 8.\par \par \uc2 Advocates say the law, in effect since 1 September due the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s refusal to block the measure, has inflicted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/03/texas-abortion-ban-six-months-grave-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  irreparable harm}}}\uc2  in a state that is home to 10% of the reproductive age population. Texans have been forced to travel hundreds or even thousands of miles for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, overburdening clinics in surrounding states, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/11/new-evidence-texas-residents-have-obtained-abortions-least-12-states-do-not-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood clinics in Oklahoma alone \u8211\'20\'13 which is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2022/03/oklahomas-house-passes-a-near-total-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  considering its own}}}\uc2  SB 8-style law \u8211\'20\'13 saw a nearly 2,500% increase in patients from Texas.\par \par \uc2 The ban has forced an average of nearly 1,400 Texans to travel out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  each month, nearly equal to the number that traveled every year between 2017 and 2019, according to research from the Texas Policy Evaluation Project. The influx of Texas patients to other states has in turn caused a ripple effect across the US reproductive health network.\par \par \uc2 Providers stress the law disproportionately affects the most vulnerable: low-income people, people of color, immigrants and young Texans, who are less likely to secure the resources necessary to venture out of state, including time off work, childcare and lodging. As a result, they are \u8220\'20\'1Csuffering the physical and psychological impact\u8221\'20\'1D of unwanted pregnancy and giving birth \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst their will or attempting to end their pregnancies without access to licensed healthcare providers\u8221\'20\'1D, the legal complaint says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite the remarkable efforts of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds and practical support organizations, all too many Texans ultimately lack the resources or mobility to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at great distances from home and thus face the devastating consequences of unwanted pregnancy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rupali Sharma, senior counsel and director at the Lawyering Project. \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we are asking the court to end Texas\u8217\'20\'19 defiance of the rule of law and uphold the fundamental rights of its residents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several state legislatures have proposed copycat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans modeled after Texas, with Idaho signing such a measure into law last month. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials throughout the country are hoping such measures, unconstitutional under current precedent, will be allowed to stand, with the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  expected to overturn or significantly chip away at the landmark Roe v Wade ruling in a forthcoming decision over a Mississippi 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220419ei4j0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
