\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden attempts to reboot domestic agenda: \u8216\'20\'18American manufacturing is coming back\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2022\par 20:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President touts \u8216\'20\'18Building a Better America\u8217\'20\'19 in North CarolinaPoll shows Biden\u8217\'20\'19s\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating at 33%Stephen Miller to reportedly testify to Capitol attack panel todayRussia-Ukraine war \u8211\'20\'13 follow the latest newsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap for a particularly lively day in US politics.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sought to kickstart his stalled domestic agenda with a \u8220\'20\'1CBuilding a Better America\u8221\'20\'1D speech in North Carolina, talking up US manufacturing, jobs and technology investments before heading off to spend the Easter break at Camp David.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today, and remember you can follow developments in the Ukraine-Russia war in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/14/russia-ukraine-war-latest-russia-says-warship-seriously-damaged-after-ammunition-explosion-us-to-send-800m-in-military-aid-to-ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we covered today:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former top aide, reportedly testified to the 6 January House panel looking into the deadly Capitol riot and other efforts by the former president to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  voted to withdraw from the commission on presidential debates, which has brought voters unfiltered information from White House hopefuls for decades.\par \par \uc2 * The Republican Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed into law a bill limiting abortions in the state to 15 weeks, with no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval rating plunged to 33% according to a new Quinnipiac poll, equaling his lowest previous rating from January.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s common knowledge that the Texas Republican governor Greg Abbott is no supporter of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/03/us-asylum-policy-immigration-border-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controversial decision}}}\uc2  to end the Trump-era Title 42 immigration policy that blocked refugees at the US southern border because of the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 . Photograph: LM Otero/AP\par \par \uc2 But now the Democrat seeking to replace him, \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , has added his voice to the wave of criticism, ripping \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for having no plan to deal with an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/30/title-42-us-mexico-border-asylum-seekers-plans-end"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected influx of migrants}}}\uc2  when the policy is terminated on 23 May.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt does not make sense to end this until there is a real plan and the capacity in place to handle those and address those that come over,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/04/12/beto-orourke-joe-biden-border-migrants/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with The Texas Tribune}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone is legitimately concerned about the lack of a plan. We should hold the federal government accountable for doing its job, and they\u8217\'20\'19re not doing that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke, who narrowly failed to unseat Republican Ted Cruz in their 2020 US senate race, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.realclearpolitics.com/epolls/2022/governor/tx/texas-governor-abbott-vs-orourke-7376.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trails Abbott in polls}}}\uc2  ahead of November\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial election. Border security will be one of the biggest issues for voters in the midterms and O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke will be careful not to adopt too radical an approach.\par \par \uc2 In comments to the Tribune, he indicated he wanted the Title 42 policy gone, but only when measures were in place to cope with the influx it would cause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat it has done is produced a situation where the same person is crossing multiple times a week, and under Title 42 that Border Patrol agent simply turns that person back around and then that person tries to cross the next day,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not arrested, not detained, there are no consequences for someone who is not following our laws when they try to come into this country, and it means that this country is not following its laws when it comes to those who are trying to make a legitimate claim for asylum.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden was also keen to talk up one the major policy successes of his administration, the bipartisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/nov/10/how-big-a-deal-is-bidens-infrastructure-bill-our-panel-responds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.2tn infrastructure bill}}}\uc2  funding improvements to roads, bridges, mass transit systems and improvements to the ports, water infrastructure and the electricity grid.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 All these investments, infrastructure, research and development, and making it in America, are really about one thing, empowering more communities to do what you\u8217\'20\'19re doing here in Greensboro, transforming yourself into a city of the future, not the past, where instead of shuttered factories, we\u8217\'20\'19re building clean energy technologies that are going to power the future, helping America achieve true energy independence by creating good jobs and fighting for climate change.\par \par \uc2 And if we continue this we\u8217\'20\'19re not only going to be investing here, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to export billions of dollars worth of product to the rest of the world.\par \par \uc2 Technology was a key theme of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech. He praised \uc2 Intel\uc2  for investing $20bn in a new semiconductor manufacturing facility in Columbus, Ohio, and the bus manufacturer Thomas, whose electric fleet of school buses, he said, meant: \u8220\'20\'1Chundreds of thousands of our children will no longer be inhaling the exhausts of diesel school buses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, Biden cautioned, inaction could lead to the US falling behind in race to lead the world in technology:\par \par \uc2 Other countries are racing ahead. We can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to wait. So Congress, get this bipartisan bill on my desk. North Carolina needs it. America needs it. Let\u8217\'20\'19s meet this moment together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden touts 'Building a Better America', demands Congress pass innovation act\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is at the podium in North Carolina talking up his administration\u8217\'20\'19s successes in jobs growth and the economic recovery from the Covid-19 pandemic, while laying out how he proposes to tackle raging inflation.\par \par \uc2 The president is attempting to fire back up his domestic agenda, which has stalled since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/19/joe-manchin-biden-build-back-better-no-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapse of his Build Back Better plans}}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  talks about Building a Better America in Greensboro, North Carolina, on Thursday. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 In Greensboro this afternoon, he is presenting his rebooted plans under the similar-sounding banner of Building a Better America, talking up US leadership in global technology, and pointing to a bright future for industries such as \u8220\'20\'1Ccybersecurity, advanced manufacturing, health care, and so much more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Urging Congress to get the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.science.org/content/article/house-passes-sweeping-u-s-innovation-bill-teeing-talks-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan innovation bill}}}\uc2  to his desk, an act that would provide resources for, among other things, investment in technology-based industries, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Every action I\u8217\'20\'19ve taken to rebuild our economy has been guided by one principle: made in America means using products, parts and materials built right here in the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 It means bringing manufacturing jobs back, building supply chains here at home, not outsourcing from abroad.\par \par \uc2 Turning to inflation, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/apr/12/us-inflation-rate-march-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this week reached 8.5%}}}\uc2 , its highest level in more than four decades, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 Our economy has gone from being on the mend to being on the move. I know that we\u8217\'20\'19re still facing challenges of high prices, inflation. I grew up in a family where the price of gasoline went up at the pump.\par \par \uc2 We need to address these high prices, and urgently, for working folks out there. When we build more in America we increase economic capacity. And ultimately it helps lower everyday prices for families. Look around. American manufacturing is coming back. Once again we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the pride that comes from stamping a product made in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Ohio supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/politics/elections/2022/04/14/ohio-redistricting-supreme-court-scraps-4th-legislative-maps/9467567002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has again blocked}}}\uc2  Republicans from implementing new districts for the state legislature that would be severely distorted in favor of the GOP, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/viewerng/viewer?url=http://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/0/2022/2022-ohio-1235.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sending politicians}}}\uc2  back to the drawing board for a fifth time.\par \par \uc2 Since January, the state court has rejected four proposals for new districts in Ohio, saying all of them violated new language in the state constitution prohibiting gerrymandering \u8220\'20\'1Cprimarily to favor or disfavor a political party\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice Maureen O\u8217\'20\'19Connor, a Republican, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/ohio-republican-judge-blocking-party-from-distorting-electoral-districts?utm_term=625562bbbd5538451cf55dbaba90750e&utm_campaign=GuardianTodayUS&utm_source=esp&utm_medium=Email&CMP=GTUS_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  has been the decisive vote }}}\uc2  in all four of those decision, siding with her three Democratic colleagues. Republicans currently have a 4-3 majority on the Ohio supreme court.\par \par \uc2 The map the supreme court rejected on Thursday came about after a little bit of trickery from Republicans on the 7-member panel that controls the redistricting process. After a bipartisan team of mapmakers was close to producing a final map, the Republicans on the commission {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ohiocapitaljournal.com/2022/03/29/ohio-republicans-abandon-independent-mapmakers-to-pass-slightly-modified-gop-maps/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abruptly decided}}}\uc2  to submit their own proposal, drawn behind the scenes instead. That proposal was very similar to the one the Ohio supreme court had previously rejected.\par \par \uc2 Ohio secretary of state \uc2 Frank LaRose\uc2 , a Republican, has said Ohio needs legislative maps in place by 20 April in order to vote in primary elections on 2 August.\par \par \uc2 In a separate federal lawsuit, Republicans have been pushing a 3-judge panel to implement a map by 20 April. The Ohio supreme court was unmoved by those arguments, noting that lawmakers could delay the August primary. It also warned the federal judges that they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t interfere in a state court\u8217\'20\'19s decision over a state election.\par \par \uc2 The court ordered the panel to produce a new map by 6 May.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pentagon: Russian battleship \u8216\'20\'18significantly damaged and possibly not operational\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon says it is still unable to confirm Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s claim that it fired a missile that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/14/russia-moskva-ship-ukraine-black-sea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severely damaged the Russian battleship Moskva}}}\uc2  in the Black Sea, but defense officials are certain there was \u8220\'20\'1Ca significant explosion\u8221\'20\'1D that has likely left it crippled.\par \par \uc2 John Kirby. Photograph: Alex Brandon/AP\par \par \uc2 John Kirby, the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, has just wrapped up an afternoon briefing in which he expanded on his earlier comments to CNN that the ship was on fire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do know there was a significant explosion on this cruiser. We do believe that the explosion caused a significant fire, which as of this morning was still raging,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe assess that at least some of the crew members evacuated the ship and were placed aboard other Russian navy ships. I can\u8217\'20\'19t tell you if it\u8217\'20\'19s the whole crew.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirby added that Pentagon officials no longer believed the Moskva was fully operational.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis morning, we had assessed that the ship was under way under its own power, we are no longer able to make that certainty,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt remains to be seen exactly what the major impact is going to be. This is a cruiser, they only have three in this class.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Covid cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ng-interactive/2021/sep/02/covid-19-coronavirus-us-map-latest-cases-state-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are on the rise}}}\uc2  in the north-eastern part of the US, as many Americans travel and gather together for spring break and religious holidays.\par \par \uc2 The rise is being driven by BA.2, a subvariant of Omicron which is more transmissible than its sibling BA.1, and was responsible for an estimated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#variant-proportions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 86%}}}\uc2  of new Covid-19 cases nationwide last week, according to the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With precautions having been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/09/us-mask-mandates-covid-omicron-democrats-cdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relaxed}}}\uc2  in many places earlier this year, experts have been looking at whether BA.2 will lead to another surge. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what the beginning of surges have looked like\u8221\'20\'1D in the past, said Julia Raifman, assistant professor at the Boston University School of Public Health.\par \par \uc2 The rise in cases is expected to result in disruptions to school and work as more people become ill. The US is now at \u8220\'20\'1Ca key point to trigger action\u8221\'20\'1D, Raifman said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we take decisive action to reduce the transmission, then we will reduce case growth\u8230\'20\'26 and if we don\u8217\'20\'19t, then we\u8217\'20\'19re really leaving it to the virus to decide what\u8217\'20\'19s next.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Case counts across the US remain comparatively low, and rates are still falling in several parts of the country. But the US overall is seeing a tick upward in numbers, with an average of 30,000 people testing positive in the US each day, compared with about 26,000 last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#trends_dailycases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to the CDC.\par \par \uc2 Washington DC, where the mayor, Muriel Bowser, and the US House speaker, \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , each declared they\u8217\'20\'19d contracted Covid cases last week, has one of the highest two-week average increase. Rhode Island, Maryland, Kansas, Oregon, New Jersey, Connecticut and New York all saw more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2021/us/covid-cases.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 60%}}}\uc2  increases.\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia was the first city to reinstate its indoor mask mandate on Monday, in an attempt to stave off a rise in hospitalizations, which a \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  model {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.med.upenn.edu/anesthesia-critical-care/covid-19-epidemiology.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicts}}}\uc2  may rise in coming weeks. The city will also add requirements to show proof of vaccination if cases continue rising.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/14/ba2-variant-covid-cases-us-rise-north-east-omicron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid cases rise in north-eastern US, driven by the BA.2 subvariant}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re midway through a remarkably busy day in US politics, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has still to deliver his remarks in North Carolina on the economy and America\u8217\'20\'19s global leadership in technology.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick look at where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  has voted to withdraw from the commission on presidential debates, which has brought voters unfiltered information from White House hopefuls for decades.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former top aide, is reportedly testifying today to the 6 January House panel looking into the deadly Capitol riot and other efforts by the former president to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 * The Republican Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has signed into law a bill limiting abortions in the state to 15 weeks, with no exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 * President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval rating has plunged to 33% according to a new Quinnipiac poll, equaling his lowest previous rating from January.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republicans quit presidential debate system\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) voted unanimously on today to withdraw from the \uc2 Commission on Presidential Debates\uc2 , saying the group that has run the debates for decades was biased and refused to enact reforms, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Today, the \uc2 RNC\uc2  voted to withdraw from the biased CPD, and we are going to find newer, better debate platforms to ensure that future nominees are not forced to go through the biased CPD in order to make their case to the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chairwoman, \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear what format those debates would take or whether they would take place as often as in recent decades.\par \par \uc2 The nonprofit commission, which has run the debates since 1987, did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Pinch of salt? \uc2 RNC\uc2  chairwoman \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2  addresses the audience at the Conservative Political Action Conference (CPAC) in Orlando, Florida on February 26, 2022. Photograph: Chris duMond/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The move comes as U.S. political divisions have grown deeper, and the possibility of fewer debates could leave Americans with less access to unfiltered information about their aspiring leaders.\par \par \uc2 enltrStatement from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GOPChairwoman?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GOPChairwoman}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sLwXEYeIRZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sLwXEYeIRZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Asma Khalid (@asmamk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/asmamk/status/1514639685372583945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long accused the debate commission, which was founded to codify the debates as a permanent part of presidential elections, of being biased in favor of Democratic candidates.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s online {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/14/politics/rnc-withdraws-from-presidential-debates/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  adds: Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s vote comes after months of signals from the \uc2 RNC\uc2  that it sought a break from the commission. In June 2021, McDaniel sent a letter outlining several complaints about the commission\u8217\'20\'19s practices, reflecting former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the conduct of the 2020 debates.\par \par \uc2 And in January, McDaniel sent another letter threatening to \u8220\'20\'1Cprohibit future Republican nominees from participating in CPD-sponsored debates\u8221\'20\'1D unless the commission changed its rules.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 RNC\uc2  claims it has not pulled its future nominees out of debates entirely.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more details for you in due course.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also tore into the Texas governor Greg Abbott, who ordered, then appeared to back away from, secondary inspections of trucks that have caused \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/04/13/texas-mexico-border-inspections-delays/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delays, protests and chaos}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D at the US southern border as state officials hunt illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Customs and border protection (CBP) officials say commercial traffic at the Mexico border has dropped 60% since Abbott insisted the Texas department of public safety (DPS) reinspect vehicles already searched by the CBP.\par \par \uc2 The federal agency called the move \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessary\u8221\'20\'1D and Abbott backtracked, at least partially, on Wednesday when he dropped the requirement at one of the crossing points, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statesman.com/story/news/politics/state/2022/04/13/gov-greg-abbott-eases-truck-inspection-requirement-texas-mexico-border/7304391001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Austin American-Statesman}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese truck inspections hurt Texas, and US trade and commerce, and will have no effect on asylum seekers,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said. \u8220\'20\'1CTexas DPS does not need to replace CBP at the southern border and attempting to do so jeopardizes public safety and America\u8217\'20\'19s economic security.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have called on Governor Abbott to stop these unnecessary and duplicative inspections that are choking trade into our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House is slamming Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cradical\u8221\'20\'1D enacting of a 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, urging Congress to send \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  a bill to his desk enshrining women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to the procedure into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional rights are under attack all across the country. That\u8217\'20\'19s why this White House administration is doing everything we can in response to these attacks,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the deputy White House press secretary, told reporters just now in a \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D aboard Air Force One as Biden heads for North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRoe v Wade was reaffirmed nearly five decades ago, and the president again calls on Congress to act and send a bill to his desk to shut down these radical steps being taken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed the bill into law this morning with no exceptions for pregnancies from rape, incest or human trafficking. It will take effect on 1 July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Dozens of federal agencies and every cabinet office on Thursday announced new strategies to \u8220\'20\'1Cadvance equity and racial justice\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a coordinated and comprehensive White House initiative aligned to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive action on equality.\par \par \uc2 According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/04/14/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-releases-agency-equity-action-plans-to-advance-equity-and-racial-justice-across-the-federal-government/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The first-ever Equity Action Plans \u8230\'20\'26 lay out more than 300 concrete strategies and commitments to address the systemic barriers in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s policies and programs that hold too many underserved communities back from prosperity, dignity, and equality.\par \par \uc2 In one example, the justice department is improving language access to its programs so Americans with limited English proficiency can better report crimes, access services, understand their rights.\par \par \uc2 In another, the commerce department says it\u8217\'20\'19s investing nearly $50bn in broadband infrastructure deployment, affordability, and digital inclusion efforts \u8220\'20\'1Cto help close the digital divide, particularly for rural and Tribal communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And the health and human services department \u8220\'20\'1Cis increasing outreach to communities of color to encourage enrollment in free and low-cost health care, and is addressing the maternal mortality crisis that disproportionately impacts Black and Native families\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden signed an executive order on his first day in office in January 2021 requiring the 90 federal agencies and cabinet departments to review racial justice and equity policies and come up with improved strategy proposals.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis enacts 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Florida\par \par \uc2 Florida now has one of the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the nation after its Republican governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  on Thursday signed into law a measure banning the procedure after 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 There is no exemption for incest, rape, or human trafficking, with the only exceptions permitted if the mother\u8217\'20\'19s health is threatened, or if the baby has a \u8220\'20\'1Cfatal fetal abnormality\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are here today to protect life. We are here today to defend those who can\u8217\'20\'19t defend themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said at a signing ceremony in Kissimmee.\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s new 15-week ban, which will take effect on 1 July, is in keeping with a number of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/03/texas-abortion-ban-six-months-grave-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similarly draconian laws}}}\uc2  passed or under consideration in multiple southern Republican states.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is expected to rule in June whether to overturn the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade decision that protected a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide.\par \par \uc2 In a statement after it was approved by legislators last month, the White House called the Florida law \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme by any standard\u8221\'20\'1D. Pro-choice groups have promised to fight it in court.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/04/florida-republicans-abortion-15-weeks-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida Republicans pass bill to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after 15 weeks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Trumpist Republican governor of Florida, has apparently found a way to upstage his Texas counterpart Greg Abbott, who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/07/texas-governor-plans-bus-migrants-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 busing undocumented migrants to Washington DC}}}\uc2  to try to make an example of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies.\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 . Photograph: Joe Cavaretta/AP\par \par \uc2 As the first bus from Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.khou.com/article/news/local/texas/bus-texas-migrants-washington-dc/285-abf4c462-fd51-42e4-b6a7-a522d7a9d853"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unloaded its passengers}}}\uc2  in the capital yesterday, coincidently right outside a Fox News television studio, DeSantis was concocting his own novel plot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonherald.com/2022/04/14/battenfeld-florida-gov-desantis-proposes-sending-illegal-immigrants-to-marthas-vineyard/?utm_email=0562042994036468E4DC95E5D9&g2i_eui=06AoJ4UtWaA2AFGFwbYZABsw4tYh%2bHnl&g2i_source=newsletter&lctg=0562042994036468E4DC95E5D9&active=no&utm_source=listrak&utm_medium=email&utm_term=https%3a%2f%2fwww.bostonherald.com%2f2022%2f04%2f14%2fbattenfeld-florida-gov-desantis-proposes-sending-illegal-immigrants-to-marthas-vineyard%2f&utm_campaign=boston-morning-memo&utm_content=curated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Boston Herald}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the scheme, undocumented aliens from the sunshine state will be taken by bus to Martha\u8217\'20\'19s Vineyard, the ultra-wealthy Massachusetts enclave where celebrities including Spike Lee, David Letterman, Carly Simon and James Taylor make their home, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/general-news/why-hollywood-hides-at-marthas-220053/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Hollywood Reporter.}}}\par \par \uc2 DeSantis is also reportedly planning on sending them to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s home state of Delaware and other perceivedly progressive states more amenable to taking in migrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Biden is dumping people, which he has dumped people, we now have money where we can reroute them to sanctuary states like Delaware,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said, according to the Herald.\par \par \uc2 The White House has dismissed Abbott and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s plans as \u8220\'20\'1Ca publicity stunt,\u8221\'20\'1D noting that states do not have authority over federal immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 The first bus from Texas contained only undocumented migrants who consented to the journey, Abbott\u8217\'20\'19s office confirmed.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CA bus carrying migrants from Texas arrived in Washington, D.C. this morning and a second bus is on the way, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovAbbott?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GovAbbott}}}\uc2 ...Congresswoman Sylvia Garcia echoed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @WhiteHouse}}}\uc2  response that Abbott is looking for publicity.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KHOU?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KHOU}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s story: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/abNUrzzH8Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/abNUrzzH8Q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Sylvia Garcia (@RepSylviaGarcia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepSylviaGarcia/status/1514393772787961856?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s testimony - if he is cooperative - will be almost without question some of the most valuable and compelling evidence the 6 January inquiry will have collated to date about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s involvement in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadly insurrection}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Miller was an ever-present at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s side throughout his administration, a supremely loyal and focused character credited as the mastermind of some of the most controversial and harshest policies it enacted.\par \par \uc2 An extremist known for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/24/stephen-miller-white-nationalist-trump-immigration-guru"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white nationalist and far-right views}}}\uc2 , Miller was central to almost every decision Trump made while in office, as well as ultra hardline immigration policies the former president would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/28/stephen-miller-trump-second-term-immigration-blitz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likely have enacted}}}\uc2  had he won a second term.\par \par \uc2 It is that loyalty to his old boss, and to Trumpism itself, that has analysts wondering if Miller will actually be forthcoming in his reported appearance before the House panel today, or whether he will clam up or plead the fifth amendment under questioning.\par \par \uc2 There is already speculation that Miller\u8217\'20\'19s agreement to appear - which neither he nor the panel has yet confirmed - was simply an exercise in avoiding the fate of other former Trump advisers Dan Scavino and \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/06/house-navarro-scavino-trump-advisers-contempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged with contempt}}}\uc2  of the House last week for ignoring their own subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 As for the panel itself, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard to escape the feeling that Trump, who has vociferously pushed the big lie that his 2020 election defeat was fraudulent, is now the main, if not sole focus of the final stages of its investigation.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s actions on the day of, and following the insurrection have been under scrutiny, most recently a revelation that calls he made on 6 January were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/30/trump-used-white-house-phone-call-capitol-attack-jan-6-not-official-log"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hidden from the official log}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The inquiry has also looked into an illegal scheme allegedly pushed by Trump and his supporters to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/28/january-6-capitol-attack-trump-electors-subpoenas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put forward fake electors}}}\uc2  to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the electoral college.\par \par \uc2 The panel has said it will likely hold public hearings this spring, and a report is expected before this year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, when Republicans are predicted to seize a majority in the House and shut the inquiry down, if it is still ongoing at that stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Miller 'to testify today to January 6 panel'\par \par \uc2 Big news from the House investigation into the Capitol riot: \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former top adviser, will give testimony to the panel today, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 The reported cooperation of Miller is further evidence that the inquiry is lapping at the doors of the Trump Oval Office, after the former president\u8217\'20\'19s daughter and son-in-law, \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Jared Kushner\uc2 , both former senior White House advisers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/05/ivanka-trump-capitol-attack-committee-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave their own testimony}}}\uc2  in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 According to two sources cited by the AP, it is unclear if Miller will appear in person or virtually before the nine-member bipartisan panel.\par \par \uc2 But the fact he is appearing at all is a significant development, and likely another major blow to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to shield information about his movements on the day of the insurrection and subsequent efforts to overturn the presidential election he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Miller, considered Trump\u8217\'20\'19s top aide through the entirety of his single term in office, has fiercely resisted previous efforts to get him to testify after receiving a subpoena in November, the AP says.\par \par \uc2 At the time, \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the Mississippi Democrat who chairs the panel, said Miller had \u8220\'20\'1Cparticipated in efforts to spread false information about alleged voter fraud\u8221\'20\'1D, the basis of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s big lie that his election defeat was fraudulent.\par \par \uc2 How cooperative Miller will be in terms of the testimony he has to offer remains to be seen. It is likely that Miller\u8217\'20\'19s decision to appear was prompted by last week\u8217\'20\'19s House vote to hold former Trump advisers \uc2 Peter Navarro\uc2  and Dan Scavino {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/06/house-navarro-scavino-trump-advisers-contempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in contempt}}}\uc2  for their refusal to comply with their own subpoenas.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/04/capitol-attack-panel-inches-closer-to-trump-inner-circle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Capitol attack panel scores two big wins as it inches closer to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 As promised, here\u8217\'20\'19s some more on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/ERP_2022_.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economic Report of the President}}}\uc2 , White House economists\u8217\'20\'19 annual assessment published today, and this year an apparent finger-pointing exercise too.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s no secret that the economy is weighing down the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s ambitions, with inflation this week reaching a four-decade high of 8.5% and little prospect of Democrats advancing recovery measures in a bitterly-divided Congress.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have been quick to label it the Biden inflation crisis, while the president himself says it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CPutin\u8217\'20\'19s price hike,\u8221\'20\'1D asserting that the Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine has sent the global economy haywire.\par \par \uc2 Biden, perhaps unsurprisingly, has the backing of the economists\u8217\'20\'19 report, which apportions blame to the Ukraine war, as well as other factors including the Covid-19 pandemic, the climate crisis and natural weather disasters, which have affected manufacturing and contributed to supply chain issues:\par \par \uc2 The fact that inflation has accelerated in so many countries underscores its common drivers. Pandemic-induced changes in behavior led to relatively more demand for goods than services.\par \par \uc2 This phenomenon of recovering demand for goods interacting with supply constraints can help to explain the relatively higher inflation in the United States, where the recovery was relatively stronger.\par \par \uc2 As for the supply chain disruption, the economists warn that could last much longer than the pandemic which helped to cause it:\par \par \uc2 Though modern supply chains have driven down consumer prices for many goods, they can also easily break.\par \par \uc2 The Covid-19 pandemic is not the first time that supply chains have been disrupted; the production and distribution of goods have been regularly snarled by natural disasters, cyberattacks, labor strikes, supplier bankruptcies, industrial accidents, and climate-induced weather emergencies.\par \par \uc2 The pandemic simply exposed just how complex and interconnected modern supply chains have become.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has launched an audacious bid to buy \uc2 Twitter\uc2  for more than $40bn, saying he wants to release its \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary potential\u8221\'20\'1D to boost free speech and democracy across the world.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Tesla\uc2  chief executive and world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person revealed in a regulatory filing on Thursday that he had launched a hostile takeover of \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . The news came just days after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/05/elon-musk-join-twitter-board-stake-tesla-spacex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he bought a 9.2% stake}}}\uc2  in the social media company and was subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/05/elon-musk-join-twitter-board-stake-tesla-spacex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered a seat on the board}}}\uc2 , but then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/11/elon-musk-will-not-join-twitter-board-after-all-companys-chief-executive-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to take up the position}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a letter to \uc2 Bret Taylor\uc2 , \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chair, Musk said the site was not thriving as a company or a tool for improving freedom of speech, and \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to be transformed as a private company\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk, who has more than 80 million followers on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , said if his offer was not accepted he would \u8220\'20\'1Creconsider my position as a shareholder\u8221\'20\'1D as he did not have \u8220\'20\'1Cconfidence in [\uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s current] management\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a threat,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s simply not a good investment without the changes that need to be made.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1418091/000110465922045641/tm2212748d1_sc13da.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) filing}}}\uc2  on Thursday, Musk said he had offered to buy all \uc2 Twitter\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares for $54.20 each \u8211\'20\'13 a total of $41.4bn (\u163\'00\'A331.5bn) based on 763.58m shares outstanding, according to data from the financial information provider Refinitiv.\par \par \uc2 enltrI made an offer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VvreuPMeLu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VvreuPMeLu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1514564966564651008?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/14/elon-musk-buy-twitter-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk offers to buy Twitter for more than $40bn}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 President to tout US innovation and leadership as approval rating falls\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is looking to sign off for the Easter break on an upbeat note with today\u8217\'20\'19s trip to an engineering research complex in North Carolina to plug his \u8220\'20\'1Cbuilding a better America\u8221\'20\'1D plans.\par \par \uc2 The president will tout the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/04/06/readout-of-congressional-briefing-on-national-security-impact-of-semiconductor-supply-chain-and-importance-of-passing-bipartisan-innovation-act/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bipartisan Innovation Act}}}\uc2 , a bill designed to boost American manufacturing and global technological leadership, but his remarks are sure to cover wider issues of the US economy and jobs growth.\par \par \uc2 Inflation, immigration and the Ukraine war are all weighing on his administration, and Biden is seeking to kickstart his stalled domestic agenda with the appearance in Greensboro before heading off to Camp David to spend the Easter holiday.\par \par \uc2 The president, however, will board Air Force One shortly with more bad news ringing in his ears \u8211\'20\'13 a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://poll.qu.edu/poll-release?releaseid=3843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quinnipiac poll}}}\uc2  puts Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval rating at only 33%, matching his previous low from January, with 54% disapproving of the job he\u8217\'20\'19s doing.\par \par \uc2 Biden has struggled with his domestic agenda: his flagship $2tn Build Back Better initiative boosting social spending and addressing the climate crisis was opposed by Republicans and ultimately {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2021/dec/19/joe-manchin-says-he-cannot-get-there-on-build-back-better-bill-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed by the moderate Democratic senator Joe Manchin}}}\uc2 , whose vote would have been crucial in the divided 50-50 chamber.\par \par \uc2 While progress at home has stalled, inflation has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/apr/12/us-inflation-rate-march-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soared to 8.5%}}}\uc2 , a 41-year high, with analysts saying the president is failing with his messaging. That\u8217\'20\'19s why he\u8217\'20\'19ll be talking up the bipartisan nature of the innovation act, which has Republican support in both the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 White House experts are shifting blame for the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic woes, including soaring inflation, away from Biden. The council of economic advisers\u8217\'20\'19 annual report published this morning says the Ukraine war and climate crisis are contributory. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have more on that shortly.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , the deputy White House press secretary, will conduct the final briefing of the week, a so-called gaggle aboard Air Force One as Biden heads for North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our Thursday US political blog.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will spend the final working day before the Easter break seeking a reset of his stalled domestic agenda, as inflation, immigration issues and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine weigh on his administration.\par \par \uc2 The president will head to North Carolina this morning, where he will tour an engineering research complex in Greensboro before delivering lunchtime remarks touting the Bipartisan Innovation Act, a bill designed to boost American manufacturing and global technological leadership.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s your daily reminder that every development in the Ukraine-Russia war can be found on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/14/russia-ukraine-war-latest-russia-says-warship-seriously-damaged-after-ammunition-explosion-us-to-send-800m-in-military-aid-to-ukraine-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re looking at in the US today:\par \par \uc2 * A new Quinnipiac poll has \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings in the tank. Only 33% approve of the job he\u8217\'20\'19s doing, and 54% disapprove, matching his previous low from January.\par \par \uc2 * White House economists warn in their annual report that supply chain issues will outlast the Covid-19 pandemic, and that the climate crisis and natural disasters are at least partly to blame.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Beto O\u8217\'20\'19Rourke\uc2 , Texas governor hopeful and a prominent rising figure in the Democratic party, is criticizing the Biden administration for ending the Title 42 immigration policy next month without a plan to deal with an expected surge of migrants.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration is unveiling its \u8220\'20\'1C equity action plans \u8221\'20\'1D today for dozens of federal agencies and all cabinet departments, seeking to make federal policies fairer for diverse communities.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220414ei4e001up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
