\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden arrives in Iowa to unveil plan to reduce gas prices amid soaring inflation \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 4,736 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2022\par 20:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President seeks lower gas prices with waiver for summer E15 salesUS inflation climbed to 8.5% in March, highest rate since 1981Russia-Ukraine war \u8211\'20\'13 follow the latest newsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re closing the US politics blog now, following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement in Iowa seeking to lower gas prices amid the nation\u8217\'20\'19s worst inflation crisis in more than 40 years.\par \par \uc2 The president said the move to allow sales of higher ethanol E15 gasoline this summer, following the relaxing of federal laws, could save families 10 cents a gallon, although the fuel will not be widely available nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today. Our live blog on the New York subway shooting will continue for a while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/apr/12/brooklyn-shooting-subway-platform-new-york-latest-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 , and you can follow developments in the Ukraine-Russia war on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/12/russia-ukraine-war-latest-mariupol-mayor-says-more-than-10000-civilians-killed-zelenskiy-taking-chemical-weapons-threat-seriously"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where else our day went:\par \par \uc2 * Biden and British prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  spoke by phone to assert their joint commitment to support Ukraine with humanitarian aid and military equipment.\par \par \uc2 * Biden was briefed on the New York subway shooting before he boarded Air Force One to Iowa, with press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  tweeting that senior administration officials are offering local authorities their support.\par \par \uc2 * The Oklahoma governor \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  signed a law outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Republican state.\par \par \uc2 * New York\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor \uc2 Brian Benjamin\uc2  was arrested for bribery and wire fraud.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden seeks lower gas prices with waiver for summer E15 sales\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is preparing to speak at a bioprocessing plant in Menlo, Iowa, to announce that he\u8217\'20\'19s waiving a federal rule banning summer sales of E15 gasoline - fuel with a higher blend of ethanol than regular gas - in an effort to bring down prices at the pump.\par \par \uc2 The president is pledging to lower energy costs after blaming the Ukraine war, and in particular the Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , for soaring prices affecting American families. Earlier today, it was announced US inflation reached 8.5% in March, its worst level in more than 40 years.\par \par \uc2 Biden will speak after touring the plant in the corn-rich state, where even Republicans seem to be on board with his plans. Biden insists the sale of plant-based E15 during the summer, during which it is usually banned because it creates denser levels of smog in higher temperatures, could save families 10 cents a gallon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHomegrown Iowa biofuels provide a quick and clean solution for lowering prices at the pump, and bolstering production would help us become energy independent once again,\u8221\'20\'1D the Iowa Republican senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  said, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/biden-business-iowa-campaigns-elections-227e09a39aed1680e1f4813334aeae64"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Grassley was among nine Republican and seven Democratic senators from midwestern states who sent Biden a letter last month urging him to allow year-round E15 sales, the AP said.\par \par \uc2 Industry groups, however, doubt the impact of the plan. E15, they say, will be available only at about 2,300 of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s more than 100,000 gas stations, concentrated in the Midwest and the South, including Texas.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three former Minneapolis police officers facing state charges over George Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death have rejected a plea deal with prosecutors, the Minnesota attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/12/us/george-floyd-officers-reject-plea-deal/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Tou Thao, J Alexander Kueng and Thomas Lane are scheduled to stand trial in June charged with aiding and abetting convicted murderer and fellow former Minneapolis officer Derek Chauvin while he knelt on Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s neck for nine minutes in May 2020.\par \par \uc2 Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s death sparked protests across the US and other countries through the summer of 2020, and contributed to the rise to prominence of the \uc2 Black Lives Matter movement\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chauvin was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/25/derek-chauvin-george-floyd-murder-sentencing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced to 22.5 years}}}\uc2  for second degree murder after his trial last summer, while Thao, Kueng and Lane are free on bail following their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/24/george-floyd-death-police-officers-guilty-civil-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conviction in February}}}\uc2  on federal charges of violating Floyd\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, the officers were offered the plea deals on 22 March, the Minnesota attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said. No details of the proposed plea deals have been made public, although they are expected to be revealed when the state trial gets under way.\par \par \uc2 CNN said it had contacted lawyers for all three former officers. Tom Plunkett, attorney for Kueng, declined to share details on why the offer was rejected. The network did not hear back from attorneys for the other two.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The South Dakota attorney general \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  has been suspended pending the outcome of a state senate trial, after he was impeached Tuesday by the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature over a fatal 2020 road accident in which he originally claimed he had hit a deer.\par \par \uc2 Ravnsborg was fined $1,000 plus court costs, but avoided jail time last year when he pleaded no contest to two misdemeanor traffic charges in the death of pedestrian Joseph Boever, 55, as he drove home from a political event.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota attorney general \uc2 Jason Ravnsborg\uc2  Photograph: Manuel Balce Ceneta/AP\par \par \uc2 Investigators said the attorney general was browsing political websites immediately before the collision, and that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/14/south-dakota-attorney-general-fatal-crash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called 911 to say he had struck a deer}}}\uc2 . Boever\u8217\'20\'19s body was found the next day, and his cellphone was discovered inside Ravnsborg\u8217\'20\'19s car.\par \par \uc2 On Monday night, Ravnsborg wrote to lawmakers urging them to vote against impeachment, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 But in a 36-31 vote, the House rejected the recommendation of a GOP-backed majority report from a special investigative committee and sided with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , who said Ravnsborg was guilty of lying to investigators.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also had pushed for impeachment, arguing that he was not \u8220\'20\'1Cforthcoming\u8221\'20\'1D to law enforcement officers and had abused the power of his office, the AP reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has set out some details of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming address in Iowa, where he will speak at a bioprocessing plant in rural Menlo later today about measures to combat soaring inflation and reduce the price of gas at the pump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration\u8217\'20\'19s strategy to spur the development of homegrown biofuels is critical to expanding Americans\u8217\'20\'19 options for affordable fuel in the short-term and to building real energy independence in the long-term by reducing our reliance on fossil fuels,\u8221\'20\'1D a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/04/12/fact-sheet-using-homegrown-biofuels-to-address-putins-price-hike-at-the-pump-and-lower-costs-for-american-families/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact sheet released by the White House}}}\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 To that end, Biden will announce that the environmental protection agency (\uc2 EPA\uc2 ) will issue an emergency waiver allowing E15 gasoline, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eia.gov/energyexplained/biofuels/ethanol-and-the-environment.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuel containing 15% ethanol}}}\uc2 , to be sold during the summer.\par \par \uc2 In ordinary times, sales of E15, which the White House says is on average 10 cents a gallon cheaper than regular gas, but which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2022/4/12/23021146/biden-administration-ethanol-e15-gas-prices"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some analysts say is more harmful to the environment}}}\uc2  because of its smog-producing ingredients, is not permitted in the summer months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn emergency waiver can help increase fuel supplies, give consumers more choice to get lower prices, and provide savings to many families,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House release says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAllowing higher levels of blending will also reduce our dependency on foreign fuels as we rely more heavily on home-grown biofuels. This will help us bridge towards real energy independence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president will also expand on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s financial investment in alternative energy, including more than $800m for the biofuel industry from pandemic assistance programs.\par \par \uc2 Biden has attracted criticism for expanding the fossil fuel industry, despite his investments in green energy. In this opinion piece for the Guardian last month, climate scientist and author Peter Kalmus took the administration to task:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/mar/31/why-is-biden-boasting-about-drilling-for-oil-our-planet-demands-we-stop-now"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is Biden boasting about drilling for oil? Our planet demands we stop now | Peter Kalmus}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  also spoke briefly about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/brooklyn-shooting-latest-new-york-sunset-park-subway-attack-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York subway attack}}}\uc2 , confirming that White House \u8220\'20\'1Csenior staff\u8221\'20\'1D were in contact with officials in Brooklyn, and that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was being kept informed of developments.\par \par \uc2 There was a possibility the president would speak later in Iowa about the situation, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve offered everything we can provide,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said, noting that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s senior aides had spoken directly with the New York mayor Eric Adams and city police commissioner \uc2 Keechant Sewell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just spoke with the president about it earlier on the plane and he reiterated his request\u8230\'20\'26 anything they need, anything they want, we are here to help them and provide that to them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Johnson 'commit to support Ukraine'\par \par \uc2 The White House has announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke by phone with the British prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  earlier today, affirming their \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitment\u8221\'20\'1D to support Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Few details were contained in the readout of the call, which the White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  announced during Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flight to Iowa, where he will later speak about inflation and reducing gasoline prices.\par \par \uc2 The statement said:\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joseph R. Biden\uc2 , Jr. spoke today with Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  of the United Kingdom about the Prime Minister\u8217\'20\'19s recent visit to Ukraine. The leaders affirmed their commitment to continue providing security and humanitarian assistance to Ukraine in the face of ongoing atrocities by Russia.\par \par \uc2 They also welcomed ongoing cooperation with allies and partners to impose severe costs on Russia for its unprovoked and unjustified war.\par \par \uc2 Psaki was asked about Ukraine during a press \u8220\'20\'1Cgaggle\u8221\'20\'1D aboard Air Force One, her answers barely decipherable on the extremely broken live audio feed.\par \par \uc2 She said there had been \u8220\'20\'1Cno confirmation\u8221\'20\'1D of earlier reports that Russia had used a chemical weapon in eastern Ukraine, but that the Biden administration expected the Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to step up his military\u8217\'20\'19s attacks in the east, following their withdrawal from around the capital Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect Russia will continue to launch air and missile strikes to the rest of the country to cause military and economic damage and cause terror, because Russia\u8217\'20\'19s goal in the end is to weaken Ukraine as much as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, pledging a continuation of US support in humanitarian aid and weapons systems.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe also expect that this stage of the conflict could last a long time. We should have no illusions that Russia will adjust tactics. So of course the focus is on continuing to provide a range of security assistance. We essentially look at and review requests made by Ukrainian leaders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 In one of the final acts in a 24-year political career, the Republican chief justice of the Ohio supreme court is defying her party and refusing to let them distort electoral districts to their advantage, a move that has some fellow Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/oh/columbus/news/2022/04/05/ohio-house-speaker-says--jury-is-still-out--on-if-ohio-s-supreme-court-chief-justice-violated-her-oath-in-redistricting-decisions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling for her impeachment}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/ohio-republican-judge-blocking-party-from-distorting-electoral-districts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Republican judge blocking her party from rigging electoral districts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy Tuesday so far. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand midway through the day:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is on his way to Iowa, where he will deliver remarks later this afternoon about how he plans to bring down raging inflation and reduce gas prices.\par \par \uc2 * US inflation climbed to 8.5% in March, the highest level for more than 40 years. The White House says the war in Ukraine is largely responsible for \u8220\'20\'1CPutin\u8217\'20\'19s price hike\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Biden was briefed on the New York subway shooting before he boarded Air Force One, with press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  tweeting that senior administration officials are offering local authorities their support.\par \par \uc2 * The Oklahoma governor \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  has signed a law outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Republican state.\par \par \uc2 * New York\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor \uc2 Brian Benjamin\uc2  has been arrested for bribery and wire fraud.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Russian people know little about \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s war on Ukraine because Putin has blocked their access to the truth, substituting propaganda and lies.\par \par \uc2 Years ago, pundits assumed the internet would open a new era of democracy, giving everyone access to the truth. But dictators like Putin and demagogues like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  have demonstrated how naive that assumption was.\par \par \uc2 At least the US responded to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies. Trump had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://socialblade.com/twitter/user/realdonaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 88 million}}}\uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers before \uc2 Twitter\uc2  took him off its platform \u8211\'20\'13 just two days after the attack on the Capitol, which he provoked, in part, with his tweets. (Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2021/1/10/22223356/every-platform-that-banned-trump-twitter-facebook-snapchat-twitch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media accounts were also suspended}}}\uc2  on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , \uc2 Snapchat\uc2 , Twitch and TikTok.)\par \par \uc2 These moves were necessary to protect American democracy. But \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the richest man in the world, with 80 million \uc2 Twitter\uc2  followers \u8211\'20\'13 wasn\u8217\'20\'19t pleased. Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/technology/elon-musks-arrival-stirs-fears-among-some-twitter-employees-2022-04-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2  that US tech companies shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be acting \u8220\'20\'1Cas the de facto arbiter of free speech\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk continues to tell his 80 million followers all sorts of things. I disagree with many of his positions, but ever since I posted a tweet two years ago criticizing him for how he treated his \uc2 Tesla\uc2  workers he has blocked me \u8211\'20\'13 so I can\u8217\'20\'19t view or post criticisms of his tweets to his followers.\par \par \uc2 Seems like an odd move for someone who describes himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech absolutist\u8221\'20\'1D. Musk advocates free speech but in reality it\u8217\'20\'19s just about power.\par \par \uc2 Read on:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/12/elon-musk-internet-twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s vision for the internet is dangerous nonsense | Robert Reich}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery intent on bringing my brother down\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sister said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only race I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enthusiastic about Joe getting involved in was the 2020 presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D Valerie Biden Owens {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/president-biden-sister-valerie-owens-donald-trump-intent/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CBS News}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I expected, and was not disappointed, that it would be ugly and mean, and it would be an attack on my brother, Joe, personally and professionally, because the former president is very intent on bringing my brother down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A year and a half into his presidency, Biden is battling crises at home including inflation and the coronavirus pandemic and abroad, over the Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Valerie Biden Owens Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 Trump dominates the Republican party, propagating the \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D about voter fraud in his defeat by Biden which fueled the January 6 attack on the US Capitol, continuing to attack Biden as incapable of the demands of office, flirting with a third White House run and dispensing endorsements to candidates in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, the Republican House minority leader, Kevin McCarthy, claimed Republicans would not swiftly impeach Biden \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/news/house/3263967-kevin-mccarthy-warns-against-impeaching-biden-for-political-purposes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for political purposes}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, should as expected the party take the House in November.\par \par \uc2 Biden Owens helped raise her brother\u8217\'20\'19s children after his first wife and daughter were killed in a car crash and has worked on all his campaigns. She has written a book called Growing Up Biden: A Memoir.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI assumed from the beginning that the former president and his entourage would attack my brother by going and attacking my family,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/trump-valerie-biden-owens-sister-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump \u8216\'20\'18very intent on bringing my brother down\u8217\'20\'19, Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s sister says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 A vast majority of Americans no longer consider the Covid-19 pandemic a \u8216\'20\'18crisis\u8217\'20\'19, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/axios-ipsos-poll-most-americans-say-covid-is-no-longer-a-crisis-6604f7d2-a476-48eb-8e2d-9cb94c425159.html?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios-Ipsos poll}}}\uc2  published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Instead, more than three-quarters of the population think coronavirus is a \u8220\'20\'1Cmanageable problem,\u8221\'20\'1D while one in six people do not consider it a problem at all, the poll found.\par \par \uc2 The news that fewer than one in 10 Americans thinks the pandemic is still a crisis comes as the Covid-19 subvariant BA.2 continues to spread across the nation, and Philadelphia became the first major city in the US to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/philadelphia-indoor-mask-mandate-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reimpose an indoor mask mandate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CDC figures show daily case numbers beginning to increase again after a massive fall following the Omicron variant peak at the beginning of this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople aren\u8217\'20\'19t following the Covid case numbers on a daily basis,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ipsos\uc2  pollster and senior vice president Chris Jackson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople see coverage and... assume the trend line is continuing even if it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/philadelphia-indoor-mask-mandate-covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Philadelphia becomes first major US city to reinstate indoor mask mandate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision illegal\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma governor \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2  has signed a law that makes it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , punishable by up to 10 years in prison, further advancing the push in numerous Republican states to curtail or eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Legal challenges are certain to follow as the law, approved by state legislators a week ago, is set to take effect 90 days after the state\u8217\'20\'19s legislature adjourns next month. That will likely be ahead of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2022/apr/08/oklahomas-move-to-ban-abortions-is-a-prelude-of-america-without-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected decision by the US supreme court}}}\uc2  this summer that could overturn the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that protected a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state of Oklahoma,\u8221\'20\'1D Stitt said during a signing ceremony for the bill, flanked by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers, clergy and students, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI promised Oklahomans that I would sign every pro-life bill that hits my desk, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing here today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under the bill, anyone convicted of performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would face up to 10 years in prison and a $100,000 fine. It does not authorize criminal charges against a woman for receiving an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the AP said.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/05/oklahoma-lawmakers-bill-makes-abortion-illegal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oklahoma lawmakers pass bill to make performing an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  illegal }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York's deputy governor indicted for fraud\par \par \uc2 New York\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor \uc2 Brian Benjamin\uc2  was arrested Tuesday for bribery and wire fraud, among other charges, as part of a federal corruption investigation.\par \par \uc2 The US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office in Manhattan unsealed an indictment accusing Benjamin, a Democratic former state senator, of conspiring to obtain campaign contributions from a real estate developer in exchange for helping guide a $50,000 grant to a nonprofit the developer controlled, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Benjamin turned himself in this morning, and is expected to appear in federal court in New York City later today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/new-york-lt-gov-brian-benjamin-arrested-campaign-finance-fraud-charges-rcna24022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The investigation by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and federal prosecutors in Manhattan has been ongoing since at least November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnewyork.com/news/local/crime-and-courts/harlem-mogul-with-ties-to-ny-lt-gov-benjamin-indicted-for-campaign-finance-fraud/3411494/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to WNBC New York}}}\uc2 , two months after he joined the administration of the incoming New York governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The channel said the inquiry was sparked by the indictment for fraud and identity theft of developer Gerald Migdol, Benjamin\u8217\'20\'19s long-term fundraiser, last year.\par \par \uc2 The Harlem state senator was, at that time, \u8220\'20\'1Cnot suspected\u8221\'20\'1D of any wrongdoing, prosecutors said.\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s indictment alleges that Benjamin and Migdol: \u8220\'20\'1Cfalsified campaign donor forms, misled municipal regulators and provided false information in vetting forms Benjamin submitted while he was being considered to be appointed as lieutenant governor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Benjamin has been approached for comment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/12/politics/brian-benjamin-new-york/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN said}}}\uc2 , adding that \uc2 Damian Williams\uc2 , US Attorney for the Southern District of New York, is expected to hold a press conference later.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been briefed on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/brooklyn-shooting-latest-new-york-sunset-park-subway-attack-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s subway shooting}}}\uc2  in New York city, the White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  has said.\par \par \uc2 According to her tweet, sent as the president prepares to travel to Iowa later this morning aboard Air Force One to give an address on inflation, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s aides have spoken with the New York mayor Eric Adams and police commissioner \uc2 Keechant Sewell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  has been briefed on the latest developments regarding the New York City subway shooting. White House senior staff are in touch with Mayor Adams and Police Commissioner Sewell to offer any assistance as needed.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1513885469876133899?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 12, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhite House senior staff are in touch with Mayor Adams and Police Commissioner Sewell to offer any assistance as needed,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki wrote.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/brooklyn-shooting-latest-new-york-sunset-park-subway-attack-news-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brooklyn shooting: several people shot at New York subway station}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t been in court for a few years, so excuse me if I\u8217\'20\'19m a bit rusty,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/administration/douglas-emhoff/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Doug Emhoff.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, not too much has changed in my life \u8211\'20\'13 except for the Secret Service, Air Force Two, the selfies, the cameras following me everywhere, and oh: my wife is the vice-president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  congratulates her husband after the mock trial. Photograph: David Smith\par \par \uc2 The theatre erupted in whoops and clapping. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , sitting in the fifth row with her sister Maya, blew kisses through a black face mask and applauded her husband.\par \par \uc2 It was one of those only-in-Washington moments. On Monday, the Shakespeare Theatre Company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shakespearetheatre.org/events/spring-mock-trial-2022/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hosted a \u8220\'20\'1Cmock trial\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  inspired by William Shakespeare\u8217\'20\'19s romantic comedy Much Ado About Nothing and presided over by retiring supreme court justice and good sport \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Much Ado is best known for Beatrice and Benedick, two proud intellects who only fall in love after others play Cupid. That seemed fitting for Harris and Emhoff, who were set up on a blind date by a mutual friend and married just shy of their 50th birthdays.\par \par \uc2 But the question before the not-so-serious court was: should Margaret be held liable for Don John\u8217\'20\'19s defamation of Hero? Emhoff, who was a prominent entertainment lawyer for nearly 30 years, was lead advocate on Margaret\u8217\'20\'19s behalf.\par \par \uc2 The event, full of inside-the-Beltway topical gags, had been due to take place last month but was postponed after the second gentleman came down with coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI thank your honours for granting my motion for a continuance due to plague,\u8221\'20\'1D began Emhoff, wearing a dark suit, blue shirt and blue tie, and standing at a lectern under bright stage lights. \u8220\'20\'1CThe White House apothecary told me my symptoms would be wild but \u8211\'20\'13 whew!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The mock trial is a longstanding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?430119-1/ruth-bader-ginsburg-presides-shakespeare-theatre-company-mock-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shakespeare Theatre Company tradition}}}\uc2  but had gone virtual for the past couple of years, due to the pandemic. Monday marked a return to an in-person audience at the Sidney Harman Hall but it was also livestreamed.\par \par \uc2 Emhoff, an amiable and slightly goofy presence, remarked: \u8220\'20\'1CMy parents tonight are watching the livestream but I might have told them that I was arguing in front of the United States supreme court so, cameraperson, can you just keep a very tight shot \u8230\'20\'26 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read David Smith\u8217\'20\'19s sketch here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/12/much-ado-doug-emhoff-shakespeare-debate-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Much ado about Doug: second gentleman takes spotlight at Shakespeare debate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is offering thoughts on the war in Ukraine, telling NBC in an interview to air Wednesday that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe danger was always there\u8221\'20\'1D in terms of Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crecklessness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The network launched {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/video/exclusive-obama-speaks-out-about-ukraine-war-dealing-with-putin-137544261773"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a teaser of the 44th president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks}}}\uc2  this morning, interviewer Al Roker noting that Obama was in the White House when Putin annexed Crimea in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 According to the former president:\par \par \uc2 Putin has always been ruthless, against his own people as well as others. He has always been somebody who\u8217\'20\'19s wrapped up in this twisted, distorted sense of grievance and ethnic nationalism. That part of Putin has always been there.\par \par \uc2 What we have seen, with the invasion of Ukraine, is him being reckless in a way that you might not have anticipated eight, 10 years ago, but you know, the danger was always there.\par \par \uc2 Obama\u8217\'20\'19s stance towards Putin over his two terms of office has long been the subject of discussion. An interesting analysis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/04/11/magazine/trump-putin-ukraine-fiona-hill.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by the New York Times magazine}}}\uc2  quotes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2021/nov/17/there-is-nothing-for-you-here-by-fiona-hill-review-more-than-a-white-house-memoir"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fiona Hill}}}\uc2 , a former Russia adviser for multiple presidents, as not being particularly complimentary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe either didn\u8217\'20\'19t understand the man or willfully ignored the advice,\u8221\'20\'1D Hill said after Obama described Putin as \u8220\'20\'1Clooking like the bored kid in the back of the classroom\u8221\'20\'1D at a 2013 news conference.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe said openly, \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t dis the guy - he\u8217\'20\'19s thin-skinned and quick to take insults\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Hill said.\par \par \uc2 In the NBC News interview, which will air tomorrow morning on the Today show, Obama likens events in Ukraine to attacks on democracy globally, including in the US:\par \par \uc2 What we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing consistently is a reminder of why it\u8217\'20\'19s so important for us not to take our own democracy for granted. Why it\u8217\'20\'19s so important to stand for and align ourselves with those who believe in freedom and independence. I think the current administration is doing what it needs to be doing.\par \par \uc2 Other topics that the interview will cover, according to Roker: Obama\u8217\'20\'19s recovery after he tested positive for Covid-19 last month, and the former president\u8217\'20\'19s advice on \u8220\'20\'1Cbecoming an empty nester\u8221\'20\'1D after daughters Malia and Sasha left home.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 US prices climb at highest rate in four decades, inflation at 8.5%\par \par \uc2 Prices in the US climbed at their highest rates since 1981, rising 8.5% over the year to the end of March as the war in Ukraine drove up energy costs for Americans, the labor department announced on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The latest Consumer Price Index (CPI) \u8211\'20\'13 which measures the prices of a basket of goods and services \u8211\'20\'13 comes after the index rose by 7.9% in the year through February, the fastest pace of annual inflation in 40 years.\par \par \uc2 Driven up by continuing supply chain issues, soaring demand and rising energy prices, inflation is now at levels unseen in the US since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  took the White House from \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The price increases are broad \u8211\'20\'13 with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/16/renters-rent-increases-us-lease"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the cost of rent}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/20/joe-biden-cursed-presidency-gas-prices-covid-inflation-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gas}}}\uc2  and food causing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/dec/23/america-got-more-expensive-in-2021-who-is-really-paying-the-price-a-visual-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particular hardship}}}\uc2  for lower income Americans and are a major blow to the Biden administration, already facing tough odds of retaining control of Congress in November\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Soaring gas prices were the main driver of the rise. The gasoline index rose 18.3% in March and accounted for over half of the all items monthly increase. Gas prices have begun to fall, in a sign that some economists have argued may suggest inflation has reached its peak.\par \par \uc2 The White House warned it was expecting a bad set of figures ahead of the report. On Monday White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , told reporters that the labor department\u8217\'20\'19s previous report had not included the majority of the jump in oil and gas costs caused by the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect March CPI headline inflation to be extraordinarily elevated due to Putin\u8217\'20\'19s price hike,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/apr/12/us-inflation-rate-march-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US inflation climbed to 8.5% in March, highest rate since 1981}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, welcome to the US politics blog, and happy Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not quite so happy for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , given the soaring inflation figures released this morning but, as they say, he has a plan. The president is traveling to rural Iowa today and will announce later \u8220\'20\'1Cactions to lower costs for working families, reduce the impact of \u8216\'20\'18Putin\u8217\'20\'19s Price Hike\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18Build a Better America\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D which is expected to include new measures to help reduce gas prices.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/12/russia-ukraine-war-latest-mariupol-mayor-says-more-than-10000-civilians-killed-zelenskiy-taking-chemical-weapons-threat-seriously"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 24-hour news blog is running here}}}\uc2  to bring you all the developments in the Russia-Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching in the US today:\par \par \uc2 * Philadelphia has become the first major city in the US to reinstate an indoor mask mandate as the Covid-19 subvariant BA.2 takes hold across the nation. Most Americans, however, no longer consider coronavirus a crisis, according to an Axios-Ipsos poll.\par \par \uc2 * White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will host her daily briefing to reporters aboard Air Force One as the president travels to Iowa.\par \par \uc2 * The 6 January House inquiry is edging closer towards the finish line as it continues its investigation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election, amid news that his daughter and former senior adviser \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  gave testimony to the panel for more than eight hours last week.\par \par \uc2 * A Virginia police officer, Thomas Robertson, has been found guilty of six charges related to the 6 January attack. His was only the second jury trial regarding the riot, hundreds more defendants await justice.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220412ei4c0020f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
