\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  vows to tackle \u8216\'20\'18grave threat\u8217\'20\'19 of untraceable \u8216\'20\'18ghost guns\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 5,948 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2022\par 21:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Modi meeting does not seem to have produced oil dealBiden announces measures to crack down on \u8216\'20\'18ghost guns\u8217\'20\'19Judge may rule on disqualification of Marjorie Taylor GreeneRussia-Ukraine war \u8211\'20\'13 follow the latest newsSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from the US politics blog for today, thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the White House to announce restrictions on \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns,\u8221\'20\'1D and to kick-off a new push for meaningful gun reforms, despite opposition in Congress. Among his first objectives will be to get his pick Steve Dettelbach confirmed as the new director of the bureau of alcohol, tobacco, firearms and explosives.\par \par \uc2 Developments in the Russia-Ukraine conflict can be found on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/11/russia-ukraine-war-latest-austrian-chancellor-to-meet-putin-ukraine-prepares-for-fresh-onslaught-in-east-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live 24-hour blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the US today:\par \par \uc2 * Biden had a \u8220\'20\'1Cconstructive and productive\u8221\'20\'1D video conference with India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , but failed to secure an assurance that India would stop buying Russian oil.\par \par \uc2 * A state judge knocked \uc2 Abby Finkenauer\uc2 , a Democrat seeking to unseat Republican \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  as Iowa senator, off the 7 June primary ballot on a technicality.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the Republican Wyoming congresswoman booted from her party leadership role for joining the House panel investigating the 6 January Capitol attack, has raised $2.94m for her reelection campaign in the year\u8217\'20\'19s first quarter.\par \par \uc2 * Maryland became the 15th US state to allow health professionals other than doctors to carry out abortions, as part of a bill expanding access to reproductive rights for women.\par \par \uc2 * The New York mayor Eric Adams announced that the Juneteeth holiday celebrating the end of slavery in the US would be a paid day-off for city employees for the first time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has announced she has now tested negative for coronavirus, days after she became one of the leading names in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/08/covid-19-spreads-democrats-biden-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flurry of Covid news}}}\uc2  last week involving Capitol Hill and White House figures.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  kisses House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  during an Affordable Care Act event in the East Room of the White House in Washington, Tuesday, April 5, 2022. At left is House Majority Whip James Clyburn, D-S.C., and right is Rep. Susan Wild, D-Pa. Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 So, look out, congressmen and women, Pelosi will be unleashed once again on Tuesday to bring her inimitable style to the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, happily I tested negative for COVID. Tomorrow, I will be exiting isolation at the direction of the Capitol\u8217\'20\'19s Attending Physician and consistent with CDC guidelines for asymptomatic individuals. Many thanks to everyone for their good wishes, chocolates and chicken soup.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1513574513178558471?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The picture at the top is one that got folks rattled, as those testing positive among Washington leaders got closer and closer to Biden himself. But the Speaker is back!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US president has taken to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to vent his frustration further at the proliferation of untraceable \u8216\'20\'18ghost\u8217\'20\'19 guns, calling them the \u8220\'20\'1Cweapon of choice for many criminals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  taking to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  is not a sentence often written, especially in comparison with his predecessor \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who would announce entire policy decisions, fire members of his cabinet and launch personal attacks all via the social media platform (from which he is banned).\par \par \uc2 Biden tweets seldom and mostly tamely. But he has posted a series of extra statements following his remarks earlier about new restrictions on ghost guns.\par \par \uc2 Having called ghost guns a weapon of choice for criminals he said his administration will do \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything we can to deprive them of that choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrLast year alone, law enforcement reported approximately 20,000 suspected ghost guns to ATF.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a ten-fold increase from 2016.\par \par \uc2 These guns are the weapon of choice for many criminals \u8212\'20\'14 and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything we can to deprive them of that choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1513598802447511554?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He lamented ghost guns being easy to assemble and use.\par \par \uc2 enltrA felon or domestic abuser can go from kit to gun in as little as 30 minutes. Buyers aren\u8217\'20\'19t required to pass a background check. And because the guns have no serial numbers, when they show up at crime scenes, they can\u8217\'20\'19t be traced.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1513598801034027017?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a drop in the ocean when it comes to new gun safety laws in the US.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the \uc2 United States Department of Justice\uc2  is banning the business of manufacturing one of these kits without a serial number and requiring sellers to run background checks \u8212\'20\'14 just as they must do with other firearms.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1513598803944816643?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 One more:\par \par \uc2 enltrIn addition to today\u8217\'20\'19s rule, we\u8217\'20\'19re working in four areas to reduce gun violence:\par \par \uc2 - Going after rogue gun dealers\par \par \uc2 - Disrupting illegal gun trafficking\par \par \uc2 - Funding community policing and community violence intervention\par \par \uc2 - Funding job training, drug treatment, mental health, and more\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1513612654488739843?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in Washington, DC has sentenced two men and a woman from Missouri to several weeks in jail for their roles in the January 6, 2021, insurrection at the US Capitol, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wreathed in tear gas as they attack the US Capitol in Washington, DC, during a clash with police officers defending the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  as it sought to certify \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential victory on January 6, 2021. Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Judge James Boasberg sentenced Emily Hernandez, of Sullivan, to 30 days in jail.\par \par \uc2 He also sentenced her uncle, William Merry, and another suburban St Louis man, Paul Scott Westover, to 45 days in jail each, the St Louis Post-Dispatch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stltoday.com/news/local/crime-and-courts/three-from-st-louis-area-get-jail-time-in-capitol-riot/article_247c096a-461f-5ca2-a0a2-d31f288bf240.html#tracking-source=home-top-story"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 All three also were ordered to pay $500 for damaging the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The trio entered the Capitol through a smashed door. A government sentencing memo says Merry goaded Hernandez into picking up a broken piece of Speaker of the House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nancy-pelosi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s sign. It also says Hernandez shot a video of herself stealing two other signs.\par \par \uc2 Westover pleaded guilty on December 6 to one count of parading, demonstrating or picketing in the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Merry pleaded guilty on January 5 to one count of theft of government property.\par \par \uc2 Hernandez pleaded guilty on January 10 to one count of entering and remaining in a restricted building.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The president closed his presentation on gun reform by introducing Steve Dettelbach, a former justice department prosecutor, as his nominee for director of the bureau of alcohol, tobacco, firearms and explosives (ATF).\par \par \uc2 It will be Biden\u8217\'20\'19s second attempt at getting a pick through Congress to head the agency after the confirmation of his previous choice, \uc2 David Chipman\uc2 , a 25-year ATF veteran, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/09/david-chipman-atf-biden-nomination-withdrawal-nra"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collapsed last year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSteve is immensely qualified,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe served the department of justice for two decades. He worked side by side to support the work of federal, state and local law enforcement including ATF agents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSteve\u8217\'20\'19s record makes him ready on day one to lead this agency and, by the way, in 2009 the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  unanimously confirmed him to serve as US attorney,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden added, presumably seeking to steer off any early congressional opposition to his choice for ATF director this time around.\par \par \uc2 Dettelbach\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation, Biden believes, will be a stride forward in what the president last year branded the US\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2021/apr/08/biden-condemns-us-gun-violence-as-international-embarrassment-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 international embarrassment}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D of gun violence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden was speaking after Mia Tretta, a teenage survivor of a 2019 shooting at Saugus high school in Santa Clarita, California, recounted her experience of seeing two of her closest friends killed by a fellow student, and suffering a serious stomach injury herself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI later learned that we had been shot by a 16-year-old student for reasons I will never know. He had brought his father\u8217\'20\'19s weapon to school. A firearm I would come to know as a ghost gun,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Tretta went on to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://everytownlaw.org/case/mia-tretta-represented-by-everytown-law-sues-ghost-gun-seller-for-contributing-to-saugus-high-school-shooting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sue the seller}}}\uc2  of the weapon used.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSchool shootings with ghost guns are on the rise. And the most lasting thing I have learned other than the loss of friends or the shattering of my youth is that nothing has relieved the pain in my heart like working to prevent more senseless shootings,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, praising Biden for \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding up for survivors\u8221\'20\'1D and taking \u8220\'20\'1Cbold, meaningful action to stop the spread of ghost guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden hugged Tretta after she spoke, then took the podium acknowledging the presence of so many survivors and victims\u8217\'20\'19 families, and activists working for gun law reforms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe loss in this crowd is incalculable. But so is the strength,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[You] represent individuals and families all across this country whose lives have been forever changed by a ghost gun. Some made national headlines, many others did not. We honor your strength and your action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA year ago this week I instructed the attorney general to write a regulation that would rein in the proliferation of ghost guns because I was having trouble getting past in the Congress, but I use what we call regulatory authority. A year later, we\u8217\'20\'19re here. We keep that promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That Biden is using executive authority to try to enact at least some reform is reflective of the current impasse he faces in Congress, despite Democrats controlling both houses and the White House.\par \par \uc2 As mass shootings and gun crimes, particularly those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/30/ghost-guns-ban-california-san-francisco-san-diego-los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committed using ghost guns}}}\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/27/us-murder-rate-increase-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proliferated}}}\uc2  across the nation, Republicans have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/02/republican-senator-blocks-gun-control-law-chuck-grassley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held up gun reforms}}}\uc2  in state houses across the country, as well as in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/apr/07/joe-biden-gun-violence-executive-actions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden to tackle gun violence with executive actions on \u8216\'20\'18ghost guns\u8217\'20\'19 and pistols}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden announces ghost gun restrictions, seeks to end 'terrible fellowship of loss'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cbasic common sense\u8221\'20\'1D to want untraceable, so-called ghost guns off the street, during a White House address to announce new firearms restrictions.\par \par \uc2 In an event at the Rose Garden attended by numerous survivors and families of victims of gun violence, the president said he was clamping down on the kit-form guns to try to prevent others joining the \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible fellowship of loss.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also took a swipe at Republicans in Congress, and the gun rights lobby, including the national rifle association (\uc2 NRA\uc2 ), that have opposed his efforts to enact reform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe gun lobby tried to tie up the regulations and paperwork for a long, long time. The \uc2 NRA\uc2  called this rule I\u8217\'20\'19m about to announce extreme,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  looks on as school shooting survivor Mia Tretta speaks in the Rose Garden Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut let me ask you, is it extreme to protect police officers? Extreme to protect our children? Extreme to keep guns out of the hands of people who couldn\u8217\'20\'19t even pass a background check?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that someone on a terrorist list can purchase one of these guns is extreme. Extreme? It\u8217\'20\'19s not extreme. It\u8217\'20\'19s just basic common sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s order will require ghost guns to be allocated serial numbers when they are sold, either in the first instance as kits, or if they are resold in assembled form.\par \par \uc2 But he acknowledged \u8220\'20\'1Cthis should be just the start\u8221\'20\'1D in terms of gun restrictions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to push Congress to act on sensible legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said announcing what he said would be a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomprehensive strategy to supercharge\u8221\'20\'1D such measures.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need Congress to pass universal background checks. And I know it\u8217\'20\'19s controversial, but I got it done once: ban assault weapons and high capacity magazines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden: Ghost guns pose 'especially grave threat'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration is announcing new firearms restrictions in a ceremony at the White House, at which the president is also unveiling his pick to head the bureau of alcohol, tobacco and firearms (ATF).\par \par \uc2 Biden, for once, is not making the initial presentation, instead standing by in his sunglasses in the Rose Garden sunshine, alongside the deputy attorney general Lisa Monaco, as the vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  announced the clampdown on untraceable \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Such weapons are cheaply and readily available in kit form on the internet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur nation continues to be plagued by an epidemic of gun violence,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTraditional guns are required to have serial numbers, which can help law enforcement identify firearms that have been stolen from its lawful owner, or found at the scene of a crime.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGhost guns have no serial numbers. They are practically untraceable making it more difficult for law enforcement to hold to account those who use weapons to do violence because of how easy they are to access and how difficult they are to trace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGhost guns pose an especially grave threat to the safety of our communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2 , Democratic congresswoman for Michigan, has announced she has tested positive for Covid-19, the first public acknowledgement of an infection by a prominent Washington figure this week, after a recent flurry.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib joins, among others, the House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , senators Joaquin Castro and Susan Collins, Biden administration officials Tom Vilsack and \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , the mayor of Washington DC Muriel Bowser, and the attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , who all announced they had received positive tests last week.\par \par \uc2 Tlaib, who says she is vaccinated and boosted, is experiencing symptoms, according to her tweet, and is currently isolating.\par \par \uc2 enltrOver the weekend, I began to experience COVID-19 symptoms & unfortunately have tested positive. This is a stark reminder that we are not out of this pandemic. Thankfully, I am vaccinated & boosted. I am currently isolating and following CDC guidelines. Please stay safe, everyone.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  (@RepRashida) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRashida/status/1513547475843526656?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has released more details of its soon-to-be-announced restrictions on \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/04/11/fact-sheet-the-biden-administration-cracks-down-on-ghost-guns-ensures-that-atf-has-the-leadership-it-needs-to-enforce-our-gun-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fact sheet}}}\uc2  issued to accompany \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s afternoon address from the Rose Garden says all such weapons put up for sale must be allocated a serial number so they can be traced in future.\par \par \uc2 Ghost guns are those assembled from kits, often purchased online, and without serial numbers, making it difficult, if not impossible to track them.\par \par \uc2 According to the fact sheet:\par \par \uc2 This final rule bans the business of manufacturing the most accessible ghost guns, such as unserialized \u8216\'20\'18buy build shoot\u8217\'20\'19 kits that individuals can buy online or at a store without a background check and can readily assemble into a working firearm in as little as 30 minutes with equipment they have at home,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House fact sheet states.\par \par \uc2 This rule clarifies that these kits qualify as \u8220\'20\'1Cfirearms\u8221\'20\'1D under the Gun Control Act, and that commercial manufacturers of such kits must therefore become licensed and include serial numbers on the kits\u8217\'20\'19 frame or receiver, and commercial sellers of these kits must become federally licensed and run background checks prior to a sale \u8211\'20\'13 just like they have to do with other commercially-made firearms.\par \par \uc2 The final rule will also help turn some ghost guns already in circulation into serialized firearms. Through this rule, the Justice Department is requiring federally licensed dealers and gunsmiths taking any unserialized firearm into inventory to serialize that weapon.\par \par \uc2 At her afternoon briefing, the White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked if she thought Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new rules would hold up in the face of expected stiff Republican opposition. Despite holding a majority in both houses of Congress, Democrats have been unable to progress gun control measures by way of legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president is confident in any executive order and the legal authority that he puts forward,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut what\u8217\'20\'19s important to note about the announcement he is making today is that this is a rule that is supported by law enforcement. It is a rule that will help address what we know is a rising component of gun crimes across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Modi call 'constructive', White House says, but no agreement over Russian oil\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  made efforts to dissuade India from continuing to purchase oil from Russia during his earlier call with the prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , the White House says, but did not appear to have secured a commitment that it would do so.\par \par \uc2 At her afternoon briefing to reporters \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the White House press secretary, characterised a \u8220\'20\'1Cconstructive, productive\u8221\'20\'1D video conference between the leaders, who discussed the conflict in Ukraine and India\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing reliance on Russian crude.\par \par \uc2 India purchased {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/31/india-defends-buying-discounted-russian-oil-despite-appeal-by-truss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 millions of barrels}}}\uc2  of Russian oil at a discount in February as other nations were ramping up sanctions on the country for its invasion of Ukraine, drawing criticism from the US and several allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the president did \u8230\'20\'26 was to make clear what the impact of course of our sanctions would be. We expect everybody to abide by those,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIndia only imports about 1-2% of its energy from Russia. We also made clear and the president made clear that we would be happy to help them in diversifying this as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president also made clear that he does not believe it\u8217\'20\'19s in India\u8217\'20\'19s interest to accelerate or increase imports of Russian energy, and other commodities as well,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, likely referring to India\u8217\'20\'19s investment in Russian S-400 military air defense systems.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Modi had given any commitment to reduce or eliminate purchases of Russian oil, Psaki said \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll let prime minister Modi and the Indians speak to that.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a constructive call, it was a productive call. It\u8217\'20\'19s a relationship that is vitally important to the United States and to the president. I would not see it as an adversarial call.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democrat with perhaps the best chance to unseat \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , the Republican senator from Iowa, in the midterm elections in November has been knocked off the 7 June primary ballot \u8211\'20\'13 for now.\par \par \uc2 As the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abby-finkenauer-kim-reynolds-congress-state-courts-a26d3d94937bb878827788956a6ece52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 , late on Sunday a state judge ruled that \uc2 Abby Finkenauer\uc2  cannot appear on the ballot for the Democratic primary, because of a technicality.\par \par \uc2 The ruling from the judge, Scott Beattie, an appointee of the Republican governor of Iowa, \uc2 Kim Reynolds\uc2 , overturned a decision from a panel of three state elected officials last week which found Finkenauer\u8217\'20\'19s campaign staff had mostly followed a law requiring candidates to obtain 3,500 signatures, including at least 100 from a minimum of 19 counties.\par \par \uc2 Two Republicans challenged Finkenauer\u8217\'20\'19s paperwork, saying signatures from at least two counties were missing the date required to accompany them, the AP said. Finkenauer can appeal the ruling to the Iowa supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Finkenauer is considered the Democratic frontrunner in the primary partly because of her past experience in Congress, having served in the US House from 2019 to 2021.\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats in the primary are Mike Franken, a retired admiral, and Glenn Hurst, a doctor and city council member. Whoever wins will advance to face Grassley, who at a sprightly 88 years old is in search of an eighth term in the Senate, having first been elected in 1980.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats for now hold a single-vote edge in the 50-50 Senate because vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can serve as a tiebreaker. As always, both parties are trying to retain seats while flipping others to secure a majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Watching {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  can be like entering an alternative universe. It\u8217\'20\'19s a world where \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t actually that bad but vaccines may be and where some unhinged rightwing figures are celebrated as heroes but \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , America\u8217\'20\'19s top public health official, is an unrivaled villain.\par \par \uc2 Given the steady stream of misinformation an avid Fox News consumer is subjected to, the viewers \u8211\'20\'13 predominantly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adweek.com/tvnewser/heres-the-median-age-of-the-typical-cable-news-viewer/355379/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elderly}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1027722947732144128?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1027722947732144128&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newsweek.com%2Ffox-news-white-audience-immigration-1067807"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -supporting \u8211\'20\'13 are sometimes written off as lost causes by Democrats and progressives, but according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://osf.io/jrw26/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new study}}}\uc2 , there is still hope.\par \par \uc2 In an unusual, and labor intensive, project, two political scientists paid a group of regular Fox News viewers to instead watch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  for a month. At the end of the period, the researchers found surprising results; some of the Fox News watchers had changed their minds on a range of key issues, including the US response to coronavirus and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 attitude to police.\par \par \uc2 Full article:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2022/apr/11/fox-news-viewers-watch-cnn-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What happens when a group of Fox News viewers watch CNN for a month?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interesting news from Wyoming \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2022/04/11/scoop-liz-cheneys-record-fundraising-haul-00024356"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 via Politico}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 about \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the defiantly anti-Trump conservative Republican.\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 . Photograph: J Scott Applewhite/AP\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that the daughter of former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cis prepared to announce that [she] raised an eye-popping $2.94m in Q1 of 2022, bringing her total haul for the cycle to more than $10m. With four months left to go in the primary campaign, Cheney has $6.8m on hand\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What that means is that Cheney is well placed for the fight to keep her seat, against a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -endorsed challenger and other Republican hopefuls, one of whom the website describes as \u8220\'20\'1Ceven Trumpier\u8221\'20\'1D than the one the former president has chosen to back.\par \par \uc2 Wyoming is deep-red Republican and as Politico says, \u8220\'20\'1Cin previous cycles it was common for Cheney to raise a few hundred thousand dollars in a quarter, mostly from Wyoming residents. With the national attention her race has received, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://go.politicoemail.com/?qs=c6cca71d8aeba76857149dc2f47513785627e117105d6d98ba34ee9d57c5e5fe0dacbf564013442c7cd24939ca866917"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 money has poured in from across the country}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheney was booted out of Republican House leadership over her membership, with \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois, of the January 6 committee. Unlike Kinzinger, one of four anti-Trump Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/05/fred-upton-house-republican-retirement-impeach-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to have announced retirements}}}\uc2  in November, Cheney is sticking around for the fight.\par \par \uc2 This has all raised her profile considerably. One more quote from Politico: \u8220\'20\'1CIf she beats Trumpism in Wyoming, [Cheney] will immediately be able to leverage her new national fundraising network into a potential 2024 [presidential] primary showdown against the man himself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter all, she said last May, \u8220\'20\'1CI will do everything I can to ensure that the former president never again gets anywhere near the Oval Office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Cheney and January 6:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/10/liz-cheney-disputes-report-january-6-panel-split-trump-criminal-referral"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney disputes report January 6 panel split over Trump criminal referral}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Modi pledge collaboration over Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  are talking now over a video link about the conflict in Ukraine and what Biden said is: \u8220\'20\'1COur close consultation on how to manage the destabilizing effects of this Russian war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US president and Indian prime minister are in a private session, at which Biden is expected to raise US concerns over India\u8217\'20\'19s perceived closeness to Moscow and its continuing investment in Russian oil and military systems.\par \par \uc2 But the mood was lighter as Biden and Modi presented a collaborative front in the public portion of their meeting, aired live on the White House website.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the root of our partnership is a deep connection between our people, a family of friendship and a shared value,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, as Modi appeared on a giant screen before him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people in Ukraine are suffering a horrific assault, including the tragic shelling in a train station last week that killed dozens of innocent children and women and civilians attempting to flee the violence. The United States and India are going to continue our close consultation on how to manage the destabilizing effects of this Russian war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Modi condemned Russian killings of Ukraine citizens and said India was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery worried\u8221\'20\'1D about the alleged atrocities in Bucha.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe condemn the killings and have called for an independent inquiry,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that India had contributed to the global effort to send help to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have also emphasized the importance of the security of civilians in Ukraine and the unhindered supply of humanitarian assistance to them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The press were asked to leave without the opportunity to ask questions, and the live feed went dark. It remains to be seen if Biden or Modi will make themselves available to reporters at the event\u8217\'20\'19s conclusion.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Maryland has become the 15th US state to allow health professionals other than doctors to carry out abortions, as part of a bill expanding access to reproductive rights for women.\par \par \uc2 Under the new law, midwives, senior nurses and trained doctor\u8217\'20\'19s assistants will be authorised to perform medical abortions from 1 July. The bill also directs the state to ring-fence $3.5m a year for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -care training.\par \par \uc2 The bill was vetoed by the Republican governor, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , but approved on Saturday with substantial majorities in the state house and senate.\par \par \uc2 Hogan claimed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.maryland.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/UPDATED-HB-937-Abortion-Care-Access-Act-Veto.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an open letter}}}\uc2  the bill would \u8220\'20\'1Cendanger the health and lives of women\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cset back standards for women\u8217\'20\'19s health care and safety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Maryland governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  Photograph: Brian Stukes/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence that allowing advanced clinicians to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aptoolkit.org/advancing-scope-of-practice-to-include-abortion-care/state-abortion-laws-and-their-relationship-to-scope-of-practice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states including }}}\uc2  California, New Mexico, Colorado, Illinois and New Hampshire has led to lower standards.\par \par \uc2 The law, which may face legal challenge from anti-choice groups, also requires most insurance companies to cover the cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at no cost to the patient. The average cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is $500 but costs vary widely across the US and can be much higher when accounting for travel and days off work.\par \par \uc2 The Maryland legislation comes amid a surge in bills in Republican-run states seeking to severely restrict or ban access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, a young woman was jailed in Texas after being accused of causing the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath of an individual by self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lizelle Herrera, 26 and from Starr county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/10/texas-woman-murder-charges-dropped-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was released on Sunday}}}\uc2  after charges were dropped amid widespread condemnation.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/maryland-abortion-republican-governor-larry-hogan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland expands \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access as lawmakers override Republican governor}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Juneteenth will be a paid holiday for city workers in New York for the first time this year, mayor Eric Adams has announced, further crystalizing recognition of the date commemorating the end of slavery in the US and fulfilling a promise made by his predecessor \uc2 Bill de Blasio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He made the announcement in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYCMayor/status/1513508783699501061"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Monday morning tweet}}}\uc2  citing the urgency of the declaration.\par \par \uc2 As the second Black mayor of New York City, I know that I stand on the shoulders of countless heroes and sheroes who put their lives on the line to secure a more perfect union. Now is the time for me to do a small part and recognize one of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s greatest wrongs.\par \par \uc2 Juneteenth is a time for reflection, assessment, and self-improvement. People across the country of all races, nationalities, and religions unite on this day to truthfully acknowledge the stain of slavery and celebrate the countless contributions of Black Americans. It\u8217\'20\'19s time for our city to finally do what\u8217\'20\'19s right and officially designate Juneteenth as a city holiday.\par \par \uc2 This decision is long overdue, which is why it will immediately take effect this year.\par \par \uc2 De Blasio promised to make 19 June, the official date of Juneteenth, a paid day off in 2020 as racial protests swept the nation, but was never able to agree a deal with union leaders.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  declared Juneteenth {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/19/us-juneteenth-mark-celebrations-federal-holiday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a federal holiday last year}}}\uc2 , the first new federal holiday since Martin Luther King Jr Day was first celebrated in 1986.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for our city to finally do what\u8217\'20\'19s right and officially designate Juneteenth as a city holiday. This decision is long overdue, which is why it will immediately take effect this year.\par \par \uc2 Read my full statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W0yPmKTl5q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W0yPmKTl5q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mayor Eric Adams (@NYCMayor) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYCMayor/status/1513508783699501061?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to announce restrictions on 'ghost guns'\par \par \uc2 Gun controls are back on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s radar, with the president set to announce this afternoon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/biden-ghost-guns-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restrictions on so-called ghost guns}}}\uc2 , those made from kits and without serial numbers, thus rendering them untraceable.\par \par \uc2 A number of gun law activists have been invited to attend the Rose Garden event at the White House, including victims\u8217\'20\'19 parents from the 2018 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjory Stoneman Douglas massacre}}}\uc2  in Parkland, Florida, the worst high school shooting in the US with 17 students and staff killed.\par \par \uc2 One of the activists, Manuel Oliver, whose 17-year-old son Joaquin was among the victims, has grown increasingly impatient in recent months over a perceived lack of action by Biden, who campaigned for the White House partly on a promise of gun reforms.\par \par \uc2 He and his wife Patricia, Joaquin\u8217\'20\'19s mother, have toured the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/17/manuel-oliver-guac-parkland-school-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 using drama and urban art}}}\uc2  to highlight gun deaths and promote their call for meaningful reforms.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe graphic evidence shows the social value of Guac\u8217\'20\'19s disruptive behavior. See you tomorrow, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  , and thanks for the invitation. Viva Guac! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChangeTheRef?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ChangeTheRef}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/patriciapadauy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @patriciapadauy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GunsDownAmerica?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GunsDownAmerica}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AMarch4OurLives?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AMarch4OurLives}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qzm7hachKh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qzm7hachKh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manuel Oliver (@manueloliver00) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/manueloliver00/status/1513238087320711173?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Oliver was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/14/parkland-victim-father-crane-protest-manuel-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested in Washington DC}}}\uc2  in February on the fourth anniversary of his son\u8217\'20\'19s death, climbing a crane and unfurling a banner directed at Biden reading: \u8220\'20\'1C45k died from gun violence on your watch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That figure is now above 54,000, according to the website {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.shockmarket.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shockmarket.org}}}\uc2 , which tallies gun deaths in the US since Biden took office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSee you tomorrow Potus, and thanks for the invitation,\u8221\'20\'1D Oliver {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/manueloliver00/status/1513238087320711173"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted on Sunday}}}\uc2 , crediting \u8220\'20\'1CGuac\u8221\'20\'1D, his son\u8217\'20\'19s nickname, for helping prompt Biden towards action.\par \par \uc2 The president will also introduce Steve Dettelbach, a former justice department prosecutor, as his nominee for director of the bureau of alcohol, tobacco, firearms and explosives (ATF)\par \par \uc2 Read more about today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/biden-ghost-guns-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden announces measures to crack down on \u8216\'20\'18ghost guns\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has indicated that an attempt to stop the far-right Republican congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  running for re-election will be allowed to proceed, with a ruling expected as early as today.\par \par \uc2 The challenge from a group of Georgia voters says Greene should be disqualified under the 14th amendment to the US constitution, because she supported insurrectionists who attacked the US Capitol on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://freespeechforpeople.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/nc-14.3-complaint-cawthorn-final-2022-01-10.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar challenge}}}\uc2  in North Carolina, against Madison Cawthorn, another prominent supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , was blocked.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  Photograph: Leah Millis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 But on Friday Amy Totenberg, a federal judge in Georgia, said she had \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant questions and concerns\u8221\'20\'1D about the ruling in the Cawthorn case, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/08/politics/marjorie-taylor-greene-candidacy-challenge-lawsuit/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Totenberg said she was likely to rule on Greene\u8217\'20\'19s attempt to have her case dismissed on Monday, two days before a scheduled hearing before a state judge.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://constitutioncenter.org/interactive-constitution/amendment/amendment-xiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 14th amendment}}}\uc2  was passed by Congress in 1866, a year after the end of the civil war, and ratified in 1868.\par \par \uc2 It says: \u8220\'20\'1CNo person shall be a Senator or Representative in Congress, or elector of President and Vice-President, or hold any office, civil or military, under the United States, or under any state, who, having previously taken an oath \u8230\'20\'26 to support the Constitution of the United States, shall have engaged in insurrection or rebellion against the same, or given aid or comfort to the enemies thereof.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congress can reverse any such prohibition.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/11/marjorie-taylor-greene-judge-ruling-far-right-republican-reelection"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene: judge mulls move to bar Republican from Congress}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 A plain-talking \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is likely to greet the Indian prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 , on their video call this morning, the president expected to seek a harder line from New Delhi towards Russia over the Ukraine war.\par \par \uc2 The US and allies are concerned by recent Indian actions, including abstaining from last week\u8217\'20\'19s vote that saw Russia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/apr/07/russia-suspended-un-human-rights-council-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  from the United Nations human rights council, buying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/31/india-defends-buying-discounted-russian-oil-despite-appeal-by-truss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3bn barrels of Russian crude}}}\uc2  while other nations were ramping up oil sanctions, and acquisition of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s S-400 air defense systems.\par \par \uc2 According to the White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , in a statement on Sunday, the Biden-Modi call will discuss: \u8220\'20\'1CStrengthening the global economy, and upholding a free, open, rules-based international order to bolster security, democracy, and prosperity in the Indo-Pacific.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To many analysts, the softer language conceals what is expected to be a resolute US president setting out some hard truths to his Indian counterpart, and that consequences await if Modi\u8217\'20\'19s government continues to court Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Vivian Salama, the Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s national security reporter, characterizes ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vmsalama/status/1513325494267269121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in this tweet}}}\uc2  ) talk of deepening \u8220\'20\'1Cties between our governments, economies and people,\u8221\'20\'1D per Biden\u8217\'20\'19s schedule announcing the meeting, thus: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is White House speak for: \u8216\'20\'18Potus to express deep disappointment in India\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing ties with Moscow and will warn Modi about repercussions should he choose to accelerate energy imports from Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll get the chance to assess the mood in the room when Biden and Modi appear briefly for reporters as they make the call, which is scheduled for 11am.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is White House speak for: POTUS to express deep disappointment in India\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing ties with Moscow and will warn Modi about repercussions should he choose to accelerate energy imports from Russia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pK3Nt36sEr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pK3Nt36sEr}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vivian Salama (@vmsalama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vmsalama/status/1513325494267269121?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, happy Monday, and thanks for joining the blog for what promises to be another intriguing week in US politics.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host a video call with the Indian prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  this morning, ostensibly billed as a meeting to \u8220\'20\'1Cdeepen ties between our governments, economy and people,\u8221\'20\'1D which the Wall Street Journal\u8217\'20\'19s national security reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/vmsalama/status/1513325494267269121"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vivian Salama sees}}}\uc2  as White House speak for: \u8220\'20\'1CPotus to express deep disappointment in India\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing ties with Moscow and will warn Modi about repercussions should he choose to accelerate energy imports from Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Russian war continues to escalate in eastern Ukraine in particular, and you can follow developments in our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/apr/11/russia-ukraine-war-latest-austrian-chancellor-to-meet-putin-ukraine-prepares-for-fresh-onslaught-in-east-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live 24-hour blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching in the US today:\par \par \uc2 * Biden will announce measures to restrict \u8220\'20\'1Cghost guns\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 made from kits and without serial numbers \u8211\'20\'13 in an address at the White House at 2.15pm. The president will also introduce Steve Dettelbach, a former justice department prosecutor, as his nominee for director of the bureau of alcohol, tobacco, firearms and explosives (ATF).\par \par \uc2 * A federal judge in Georgia could rule as early as today on a motion that could allow the progression of a lawsuit to disqualify the far-right Republican \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  from Congress as an insurrectionist.\par \par \uc2 * The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , will deliver her first briefing of the week at 1pm.\par \par \uc2 * The vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , will announce new action on relieving medical debt later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220411ei4b001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
