\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Murder charges dropped against Texas woman for \u8216\'20\'18self-induced  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 622 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2022\par 15:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lizelle Herrera has been released after being thrown in jail last week, while district attorney says this is \u8216\'20\'18not a criminal matter\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The woman who was thrown in jail on a murder charge in Texas for allegedly having caused the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath of an individual by self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D has been released after the local district attorney dropped the case.\par \par \uc2 Lizelle Herrera, 26, was reported to be back with her family on Sunday after the district attorney in Rio Grande City, on the US-Mexico border, put out {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=387792383351845&set=a.293809186083499"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a statement }}}\uc2  saying he was immediately dismissing the case. Herrera had been arrested last Thursday and placed in the Starr county jail on the back of a grand jury indictment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe issues surrounding this matter are clearly contentious,\u8221\'20\'1D the DA, Gocha Allen Ramirez, said. \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, based on Texas law and the facts presented, it is not a criminal matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prosecutor added: \u8220\'20\'1CMs Herrera did not commit a criminal act under the laws of the state of Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramirez\u8217\'20\'19s statement correlates with the view of legal experts and women\u8217\'20\'19s rights advocates who say that Herrera\u8217\'20\'19s arrest should never have happened in the first place. Texas authorities are now likely to face accusations that by putting the woman behind bars they committed an act of gross overreach.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no law in Texas that authorizes treating people who have miscarriages, still births or abortions as murderers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lynn Paltrow, executive director of National Advocates for Pregnant Women.\par \par \uc2 The current law in Texas explicitly exempts women from being policed for any self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The state has attracted considerable attention in recent months after it passed SB 8, legislation that allows private citizens to sue anyone who helps a woman get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as early as six weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 But SB 8 is a civil \u8211\'20\'13 not a criminal \u8211\'20\'13 provision, and it cannot be applied to the woman receiving the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  herself.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which passed all the way up to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , has put a chill over Texas. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2022/03/TxPEP-out-of-state-SB8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent study}}}\uc2  from the policy evaluation project of the \uc2 University of Texas at Austin\uc2  found that between August and December last year, 1,400 women had been forced out of Texas to seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in other states.\par \par \uc2 The precise details of what happened to Herrera are still unclear, but it appears that the hospital she attended reported her to authorities. In his statement, Ramirez said the Starr county sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s department investigated Herrera after the hospital brought \u8220\'20\'1Cthe incident\u8221\'20\'1D to the officers\u8217\'20\'19 attention.\par \par \uc2 Local advocacy groups in southern Texas expressed joy at Herrera\u8217\'20\'19s release, coupled with anger that she had been detained in the first place. South Texans for Reproductive Justice called the dismissal of charges a \u8220\'20\'1Cbittersweet victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sotx4rj/status/1513209098518601736"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 group said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt should not have taken national attention for these charges to be dismissed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The confusion over Herrera\u8217\'20\'19s wrongful arrest is an indication of the tensions that are rising in states across the country ahead of a critical ruling by the supreme court on the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  framed in Roe v Wade. The court is expected to give its decision in June, and all indications suggest it is likely to rein back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at least to some degree.\par \par \uc2 Paltrow warned that any move by the supreme court to hand more control over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to the states would inevitably lead to increased rates of surveillance, reporting and arrests of women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the past 50 years, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have been trying to groom people in the US to view pregnant women as criminals,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220410ei4a002e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
