\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Maryland expands  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access as lawmakers override Republican governor\b0\par\par\uc2 Nina Lakhani in New York \par \uc2 461 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2022\par 14:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Midwives, nurses and physician assistants authorised to perform abortions after lawmakers approve bill vetoed by \uc2 Larry Hogan\par \par \uc2 Maryland has become the 15th US state to allow health professionals other than doctors to carry out abortions, as part of a bill expanding access to reproductive rights for women.\par \par \uc2 Under the new law, midwives, senior nurses and trained doctor\u8217\'20\'19s assistants will be authorised to perform medical abortions from 1 July. The bill also directs the state to ring-fence $3.5m a year for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -care training.\par \par \uc2 The bill was vetoed by the Republican governor, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 , but approved on Saturday with substantial majorities in the state house and senate.\par \par \uc2 Hogan claimed in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.maryland.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/UPDATED-HB-937-Abortion-Care-Access-Act-Veto.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an open letter}}}\uc2  the bill would \u8220\'20\'1Cendanger the health and lives of women\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cset back standards for women\u8217\'20\'19s health care and safety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence that allowing advanced clinicians to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aptoolkit.org/advancing-scope-of-practice-to-include-abortion-care/state-abortion-laws-and-their-relationship-to-scope-of-practice/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states including }}}\uc2  California, New Mexico, Colorado, Illinois and New Hampshire has led to lower standards.\par \par \uc2 The law, which may face legal challenge from anti-choice groups, also requires most insurance companies to cover the cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at no cost to the patient. The average cost of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is $500 but costs vary widely across the US and can be much higher when accounting for travel and days off work.\par \par \uc2 The Maryland legislation comes amid a surge in bills in Republican-run states seeking to severely restrict or ban access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, a young woman was jailed in Texas after being accused of causing the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath of an individual by self-induced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lizelle Herrera, 26 and from Starr county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/10/texas-woman-murder-charges-dropped-self-induced-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was released on Sunday}}}\uc2  after charges were dropped amid widespread condemnation.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers and rights groups warned that the incident would have a chilling effect for women, even though the current law in Texas explicitly exempts women from being criminalised for any self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Research suggests that hundreds if not thousands of women in Texas have been forced to cross state lines to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care since the state enacted an almost total ban last year.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2022/03/2022-state-legislative-sessions-abortion-bans-and-restrictions-medication-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , a reproductive health research group, lawmakers in 19 states approved a record-breaking 108 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in 2021 \u8211\'20\'13 more than any other year since the 1973 Roe v Wade supreme court ruling which established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By the end of March 2022, 529 restrictions had been introduced across 41 states. The supreme court is poised to severely weaken or overturn Roe later this year.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, Maryland became the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/state-watch/327653-maryland-becomes-first-state-to-mitigate-planned-parenthood-funding-cuts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first state}}}\uc2  to pass legislation guaranteeing funding for Planned Parenthood, the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, regardless of federal cuts.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220411ei4b00209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
