\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 We are witnessing the final days of reproductive freedom in America\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,072 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2022\par 13:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The bill \u8211\'20\'13 which makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony \u8211\'20\'13 indicates that the state, like most legal observers, expects the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to overturn Roe\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma state legislature has been busy. This week, in a surprise move, the state house passed a bill criminalizing all abortions. The bill had been passed by the state senate last year but had been largely abandoned as Oklahoma conservatives sought other, more promising, ways to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state. As an outright ban on abortions, enforced by the state, the Oklahoma bill that now heads to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s desk for signature would be in plain violation of Roe v Wade, and unlikely to survive a court challenge while that precedent stands.\par \par \uc2 The passage of the bill \u8211\'20\'13 which makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony and would imprison doctors for up to 10 years per procedure \u8211\'20\'13 indicates that the state, like most legal observers, expects the supreme court to overturn Roe soon. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://webserver1.lsb.state.ok.us/cf_pdf/2021-22%20ENR/SB/SB612%20ENR.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The bill}}}\uc2 , which Oklahoma Republicans voted on while many of their Democratic colleagues were away participating in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tulsaworld.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/house-sends-near-total-abortion-ban-to-oklahoma-gov-kevin-stitt/article_9f583b12-b4ea-11ec-a6bf-fbd33a11cff1.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  and civil rights rally}}}\uc2 , provides no exceptions for rape or incest. Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Republican \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tulsaworld.com/news/state-and-regional/govt-and-politics/house-sends-near-total-abortion-ban-to-oklahoma-gov-kevin-stitt/article_9f583b12-b4ea-11ec-a6bf-fbd33a11cff1.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously stated}}}\uc2  that he will sign any anti-choice bill that is sent to him. If he signs this one, it will go into effect this summer.\par \par \uc2 The day after the Oklahoma legislature sent the outright ban to Stitt\u8217\'20\'19s desk, Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s House Committee on Public Health approved another bill, this one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/pressroom/oklahoma-house-committee-approves-six-week-abortion-ban-sending-it-for-final-floor-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  at six weeks}}}\uc2 . That bill is modeled after Texas\u8217\'20\'19 SB8, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that the supreme court allowed to go into effect in September, which bypasses Roe by having the ban on abortions be enforced by private lawsuits instead of state prosecution. Instead of imprisoning doctors, as the outright ban would do, this law aims to bankrupt them. The Texas-style bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://webserver1.lsb.state.ok.us/cf_pdf/2021-22%20ENGR/SB/SB1503%20ENGR.PDF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SB1503}}}\uc2 , now heads to the full Oklahoma house for approval. If it becomes law, it will take effect immediately.\par \par \uc2 The moves by Oklahoma come as the state has been playing host to reproductive refugees fleeing neighboring Texas for the past seven months. Ever since the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/04/america-abortion-crisis-roe-v-wade-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed SB8 to go into effect}}}\uc2  on 1 September, Texas women in need have been flocking to Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s four clinics, enduring the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/rcna23044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labyrinthine restrictions}}}\uc2  that Oklahoma already has in place \u8211\'20\'13 including an ultrasound, a 72-hour waiting period, and mandatory anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  counseling \u8211\'20\'13 at great expense, in order to end their pregnancies. Texans fleeing the state for care have wound up in clinics from California to New York, but more of them have gone to Oklahoma than to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/04/05/oklahoma-abortion-texas-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 any other state}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2022/03/TxPEP-out-of-state-SB8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than half}}}\uc2  of Texas women who have fled the state for abortions since SB8 went into effect have gotten their care in Oklahoma. The state\u8217\'20\'19s clinics \u8211\'20\'13 two in Tulsa, and two in Oklahoma City \u8211\'20\'13 have been slammed with these out-of-state visitors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we saw very immediately after SB8 is, we doubled our volume,\u8221\'20\'1D Kailey Voellinger, the director of a clinic in Oklahoma City, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/rcna23044"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  NBC News. \u8220\'20\'1CWe went from seeing about 100 to 150 patients to almost 300 in a month.\u8221\'20\'1D She says the demand is so great that her clinic has had to turn women away. Now, these new laws might stop her from treating anyone at all.\par \par \uc2 The human tragedy of this \u8211\'20\'13 the dreams that will be denied, the pain that will be endured, the humiliation and the enforced poverty that will inflicted on women forced to become mothers against their interests and against their will \u8211\'20\'13 is incalculable\par \par \uc2 These are the final days of reproductive freedom in America. The supreme court will almost certainly overturn Roe in Dobbs v Jackson this spring. Once it does, 21 states have laws or amendments already in place that would make them certain to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as quickly as possible, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , a reproductive rights research group. Twelve states have so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger bans\u8221\'20\'1D, laws that declare \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal as soon as Roe is overturned. Nine have pre-Roe bans that are still on the books, which could go back into effect once Roe is gone.\par \par \uc2 The result is that in the span of a few short weeks, women\u8217\'20\'19s rights are likely to be snuffed out in vast swaths of the country \u8211\'20\'13 from the deep south, across the great plains, and into the mountain west, women will lose the freedom, and the dignity, that comes with the right to choose. The human tragedy of this \u8211\'20\'13 the dreams that will be denied, the pain that will be endured, the humiliation and the enforced poverty that will inflicted on women forced to become mothers against their interests and against their will \u8211\'20\'13 is incalculable.\par \par \uc2 What has the White House done to help mitigate this catastrophe? Very little. When the supreme court allowed SB8 to go into effect, nullifying Roe, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/amp/ncna1278380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cwhole-of-government response\u8221\'20\'1D to safeguard \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. But that whole-of-government response has not materialized. The administration\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to the end of reproductive rights has been tepid and underwhelming. The Department of Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/statement-attorney-general-merrick-b-garland-regarding-texas-sb8-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  to step up its enforcement of the Face Act, a law that aims to stop anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protestors from blocking the entrances to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics \u8211\'20\'13 a nice thought, but one that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go very far if all those clinics are forced to close. The justice department also sued to block SB8 in the courts, but the supreme court, predictably, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/11/supreme-court-abortion-ruling-unsettling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw that out}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/texas-abortion-fight/tnamp/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal experts on the left}}}\uc2  offered ideas for inventive ways that the Biden administration could step in to protect the rights of Texas women \u8211\'20\'13 provided that they were willing to bend some norms, and ruffle some feathers, in doing so. The Biden administration declined.\par \par \uc2 Even Biden\u8217\'20\'19s public statements are not especially strongly worded. Throughout his presidency, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists have been frustrated with the president\u8217\'20\'19s unwillingness to say the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. He prefers euphemisms such as \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutional rights\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s rights\u8221\'20\'1D, and the avoidance, according to some activists, suggests a stigmatizing disdain for the issue. At any rate, as the sun goes down on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in America, one does not get the impression that Biden will be willing to fight for a right that he is not even willing to name.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220408ei48001jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
