\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Oklahoma lawmakers pass bill to make performing an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  illegal\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and agencies \par \uc2 675 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 April 2022\par 11:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State house approves bill that would make performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony and punishable by 10 years in prison\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma lawmakers overwhelmingly passed a bill to make performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a felony punishable by 10 years in prison and a $100,000 fine. That is likely to land the bill on the desk of the Republican governor, \uc2 Kevin Stitt\uc2 , who has promised to sign all anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s bill is just one in a raft of Republican bills to severely restrict or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , all timed before a widely anticipated supreme court case that disrupts nearly 50 years of established protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. If Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s bill passes into law, it will take effect this summer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen [patients] hear this is happening, and probably will happen soon, they are in shock,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dr Iman Alsaden, medical director of Planned Parenthood Great Plains.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe implications of all of this is there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a few states that are relied on to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care to people, and those people who do not live in those states will have to wait enormously long wait times,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alsaden. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re just looking at really making people jump through extraordinary hoops.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 781,000 women of reproductive age live in Oklahoma. However, the bill is also expected to have an outsized impact on the nearly 7 million women of reproductive age who live in Texas. Thousands of pregnant Texans have relied on legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Oklahoma since Texas outlawed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks gestation in September 2021.\par \par \uc2 Since Texas outlawed most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, Planned Parenthood Great Plains\u8217\'20\'19s caseload of Texas patients has gone from about four dozen from September to December 2020, to more than 1,100 in the same three-month period in 2021. Demand from patients in Texas has been so great it has already displaced some Oklahoma patients, Alsaden said, who she has seen travel to Kansas for care.\par \par \uc2 Alsaden said Planned Parenthood Great Plains intended to challenge any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in court. However, the fate of any such challenge and others like it are uncertain.\par \par \uc2 Before former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took office, federal courts routinely blocked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. However, Trump was able to confirm three conservative justices, which tipped the balance of the supreme court to the right.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the supreme court has shown a willingness to severely restrict or perhaps overturn the right to terminate a pregnancy, even though the majority of Americans support legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A supreme court decision in a crucial \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case is expected in June.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese legislators have continued their relentless attacks on our freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D said Emily Wales, interim president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Great Plains Votes, a related reproductive rights advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese restrictions are not about improving the safety of the work that we do. They are about shaming and stigmatizing people who need and deserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republican legislators who sponsored the bill emphasized that the punishments outlined were for doctors, \u8220\'20\'1Cnot for the woman\u8221\'20\'1D, said the Oklahoma state representative Jim Olsen.\par \par \uc2 Notably, the bill was also unusual for being revived from the 2021 legislative session. During hearings in 2021, Olsen said he felt ending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a moral duty and compared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2021/04/16/abortion-restrictions-unconstitutional-bills-oklahoma/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminating a pregnancy to slavery}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also Tuesday, the Oklahoma house adopted a resolution to recognize aborted fetuses as lives lost and urged citizens to fly flags at half-staff on 22 January, the day the supreme court established a legal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the landmark 1973 case Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of these laws are rooted in paternalism and racism and white supremacy, and they disproportionately affect people who are Black and brown and low-income, and they do that under the guise of quote-unquote helping people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alsaden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you wanted to help someone, there is something basic you need to do when you are helping them \u8211\'20\'13 which is listen to what they need,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220406ei46001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
