\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Five sets of fetal remains found in anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  activist\u8217\'20\'19s home, DC police say\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and Stephanie Kirchgaessner \par \uc2 510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 March 2022\par 22:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lauren Handy claims she gained access to organ bank at university in Seattle but authorities have not disclosed source of fetuses\par \par \uc2 Five sets of human fetal remains were recovered from the Washington DC home of an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist after a raid, the capital\u8217\'20\'19s Metropolitan police department confirmed to the Guardian on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The activist, a woman named Lauren Handy, 28, is a leader of the group Progressive Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  uprising (PAAU) and has described herself as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rewirenewsgroup.com/article/2018/03/01/trespassing-trial-march-caught-attention-activists-sides-abortion-movement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catholic anarchist}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in the past.\par \par \uc2 Local television station {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wusa9.com/article/news/local/dc/dc-homicide-detectives-pull-biohazard-evidence-from-home-connected-to-anti-abortion-activist-arrests/65-b15087a9-c3d7-45ba-b3f3-7a72a918f959"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WUSA9}}}\uc2  reported remains were carried out in red biohazard bags on Wednesday. Handy\u8217\'20\'19s only comment at the time was: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople will freak out when they hear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Authorities have not disclosed the source of the fetal remains. Handy also claimed on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/repreaux/status/1096775572544516096?s=21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter}}}\uc2  to be inspired to \u8220\'20\'1Cliberate\u8221\'20\'1D fetal remains \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom med [sic] waste companies and give them a proper burial\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Although Handy recently claimed to have \u8220\'20\'1Cgained access\u8221\'20\'1D to a fetal tissue and organ bank at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2  in Seattle, the university said its cold storage area was locked and nothing was taken. Handy was separately indicted on Wednesday for forcing entry into a Washington DC \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in 2020 October.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn March 9th myself & [sic] fellow activists gained access to \uc2 University of Washington\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s fetal organ labs & freezers,\u8221\'20\'1D Handy claimed on \uc2 Twitter{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/repreaux/status/1506802276215709699"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on 23 March}}}\uc2 . She also retweeted pictures posted by PAAU that show the contents of a cold room at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The university cold room contained brown bags, in which donated fetal remains dating back to the 1960s were stored inside new containers. The university said the remains were there as they were in the process of completing regulatory steps, \u8220\'20\'1Cso that the respectful cremation can occur\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis process is common when an institution considers the continuing educational or scientific value of its historical collections,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tina Mankowski, senior director of communications at the \uc2 University of Washington\uc2  school of medicine.\par \par \uc2 Researchers at the university use remains to study birth defects and other conditions, \u8220\'20\'1Call with the goal of improving the health and well-being of babies and their mothers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/nine-defendants-indicted-federal-civil-rights-conspiracy-and-freedom-access-clinic-entrances"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal prosecutors}}}\uc2  indicted Handy on charges of blockading a Washington DC \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, where she allegedly claimed to be a patient to gain entry. She and eight co-defendants {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/nine-anti-abortion-protesters-indicted-allegedly-blocking-dc-clinic-rcna22257"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could face}}}\uc2  up to 11 years in prison and $350,000 in fines if found guilty.\par \par \uc2 The news comes as conservative states across the country rush to limit women\u8217\'20\'19s access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in anticipation of a forthcoming supreme court decision expected to severely curtail women\u8217\'20\'19s right to terminate a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, some Democratic-led states have worked to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in state law.\par \par \uc2 Current federal law requires states to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until a fetus can survive outside the womb, generally regarded as 24 weeks gestation, because of a decision in the 1973 landmark supreme court case Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220331ei3v0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
