\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 midterms pitch: never mind the policy, here\u8217\'20\'19s the culture war\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,709 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 March 2022\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, anti-LGBTQ laws, book bans \u8211\'20\'13 the party sees hot button issues as a tried and test path to victory. Democrats ignore it at their peril, experts say\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSue-thy-neighbour\u8221\'20\'1D laws that ban abortions after six weeks of pregnancy in Texas and now Idaho. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/mar/21/disney-faces-backlash-lgbtq-controversy-dont-say-gay-bill-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2  censoring discussion of sexual orientation in schools in Florida. A ban on Maus, a graphic novel about the Holocaust, by a school board in Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s national government might be under Democratic control but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/02/22/politics/republicans-civil-liberties-abortion-voting-race/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its red states}}}\uc2  are on the march with sweeping laws targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , LGBTQ+ people and the teaching of race in schools that threaten to turn back the clock to an era when a citizen\u8217\'20\'19s rights depended on where they lived.\par \par \uc2 The offensive on cultural hot button issues also appears calculated to ensure that November\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/schoolhouse-culture-wars-factor-2022-midterms/story?id=83343766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections}}}\uc2  will be contested on a playing field of rightwing outrage. Democrats argue that Republicans resort to such territory in lieu of policy substance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no serious agenda on the Republican side,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://donnabrazile.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donna Brazile,}}}\uc2  a former acting chairperson of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1C It\u8217\'20\'19s the same choir that had the same anthem from the 60s through the last election cycle. Without an agenda, without a leader, without a way forward, you have to rely on the old hits. It\u8217\'20\'19s no longer on vinyl; it\u8217\'20\'19s digital.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the White House and Republicans lost both chambers of Congress in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/29/us/state-legislatures-voting-gridlock.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trumpism is thriving}}}\uc2  in the 30 states where Republicans have legislative control. Under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s continued influence, they are exploiting wedge issues as never before.\par \par \uc2 Last year seven states imposed new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/12/state-policy-trends-2021-worst-year-abortion-rights-almost-half-century?gclid=CjwKCAiA6seQBhAfEiwAvPqu13LZ-v20J_JEUQHxm_zv9X8pvqOTK-4YUDszmq-u20XM5KL8K7A5YxoCnIUQAvD_BwE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 , the biggest such wave of legislation since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s landmark Roe v Wade decision in 1973.\par \par \uc2 A law in Texas bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a doctor detects an embryonic heartbeat \u8211\'20\'13 usually around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 and allows private citizens to sue clinics, doctors and anyone else accused of helping provide such abortions in the state. In the month after it took effect the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/abortions-in-texas-drop-by-60-in-1st-month-under-new-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number of abortions}}}\uc2  reported in Texas fell by 60%, with many women travelling to neighbouring states.\par \par \uc2 Deep red Idaho this week passed a similar measure, a six-week restriction again relying on private citizens to enforce the law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Sabato,}}}\uc2  director of the Center for Politics at the \uc2 University of Virginia\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re right back in the Soviet era with neighbours and family members snitching on neighbours and family members. That\u8217\'20\'19s unbelievable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Missouri, Oklahoma and Tennessee are considering similar proposals, while earlier this month Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Republican-led legislature sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/04/florida-republicans-abortion-15-weeks-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  to Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  for signature.\par \par \uc2 Republican state legislatures have also launched what the \uc2 Human Rights Campaign\uc2 , America\u8217\'20\'19s biggest LGBTQ advocacy group, describes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2022/03/25/lgbtq-rights-gop-bills-dont-say-gay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the worst attack on LGBTQ+ rights}}}\uc2  in decades. A record of more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://u7061146.ct.sendgrid.net/ls/click?upn=4tNED-2FM8iDZJQyQ53jATUSXiX0WnG9yshlQuGZSAchmTZJ-2F5mYZI1vl0-2F5JegV4WSJPgqjjCYuRr39GcwH3BbvRJAX41KYJKgaD-2FS9ohW1-2Fnth7grPWktxYP6j5dbUSPj5qm_YxCxpoge33FNHhRVcK23d8GzaVst5uoX5tUlACB4zqTg22-2B36wZNVHJzoGBt3AIr-2BaBYn6bCBI2lfSuNi8yu7yEu4BIhdNWqgtTkFody3r2XabIO20WmaFjErUgtEjT-2BWgom4JPTrp-2Brum6PJUUPKWlIlB-2BMzyLDSBwoxAfEMB9cCD7iOU6omF9IPsGk4SQmgKVou4iYpv5frE4F2WkFTj1anwbd4Hu-2FzL-2FmG958n9kFWJcagPnE2qpjuBw7JHfORyOTZTYcP4Cusz-2FrZcpfAv5hA1-2B6YTeHtwS3A7Nucs9JOQw7OcigXkzpeu7QaE9KOTuDM4h7YW1neN5ooXxWc2zWyTlDNZQV3rv3RQP-2B8aU-3D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 300 anti-LGBTQ+ bills}}}\uc2  have been introduced this year, it says, with 130-plus specifically targeting transgender people.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HRC\uc2  describes the legislation as part of a coordinated effort by powerful interests promoted by rightwing entities such as \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThese groups peddle in fear and pit people against each other to marginalize and punish LGBTQ+ people \u8211\'20\'13 and especially transgender children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the most egregious examples is Florida legislation dubbed \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D that would bar instruction on \u8220\'20\'1Csexual orientation or gender identity\u8221\'20\'1D in schools from kindergarten through grade 3. Its dog-whistling impulse was evident when \uc2 Christina Pushaw\uc2 , press secretary for DeSantis, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChristinaPushaw/status/1499886619259777029?s=20&t=lzboLMrhqkP7tf0oRhEskg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted:}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThe bill that liberals inaccurately call \u8216\'20\'18don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8217\'20\'19 would be more accurately described as an anti-grooming bill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/about/staff/cathryn-oakley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cathryn Oakley,}}}\uc2  state legislative director and senior counsel for the \uc2 Human Rights Campaign\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re looking at one of the worst legislative sessions for LGBTQ issues ever in terms of volume of bills introduced.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlmost all of them are targeting transgender youth, whether that\u8217\'20\'19s through bans on trans students being able to play school sports consistent with their gender identity, bans on trans youth being able to access gender-affirming medical care, bans on trans students being able to use the correct restroom in school.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oakley added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8216\'20\'18don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay or trans\u8217\'20\'19 bill lives at the intersection of this huge effort to attack LGBTQ but particularly trans youth and the movement that we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen resurrected in the recent years that\u8217\'20\'19s about surveilling teachers and censoring curriculum, whether that\u8217\'20\'19s talking about critical race theory, about what\u8217\'20\'19s in the sex ed class or about banning books.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Tennessee, the McMinn county school board removed Maus, a Pulitzer prize-winning graphic novel about the Holocaust, from its curriculum because of \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate language\u8221\'20\'1D and an illustration of a nude woman (actually a cartoon mouse). The state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Bill Lee\uc2 , then proposed a law for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/entertainment-education-race-and-ethnicity-racial-injustice-legislature-9c5434dfe55f31ac45b3b0b0d890bf49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closer scrutiny of school libraries}}}\uc2  so students consume \u8220\'20\'1Cage appropriate\u8221\'20\'1D content.\par \par \uc2 Tennessee also banned the teaching of a critical race theory (CRT), an academic discipline that examines how racism becomes embedded in legal systems but has been caricatured by Republicans as a divisive anti-white ideology.\par \par \uc2 Eight other Republican-led states \u8211\'20\'13 Idaho, Oklahoma, Texas, Iowa, New Hampshire, South Carolina, Arizona and North Dakota \u8211\'20\'13 had also passed legislation against the teaching of CRT as of last November, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/fixgov/2021/07/02/why-are-states-banning-critical-race-theory/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Brookings Institution}}}\uc2  thinktank in Washington, with nearly 20 states introducing or planning to introduce similar legislation.\par \par \uc2 Brookings also noted that the conservative Fox News channel had mentioned \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical race theory\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediamatters.org/fox-news/fox-has-mentioned-critical-race-theory-nearly-1300-times-past-35-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,300 times}}}\uc2  in less than four months. CRT was a frequently cited bogeyman at the recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/24/ron-desantis-cpac-speech-florida-joe-biden-media"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conservative Political Action Conference}}}\uc2  in Orlando, Florida, which was themed \u8220\'20\'1CAwake not woke\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a sure sign of its potential to energise and rile up the base for electoral purposes.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/experts/elaine-kamarck/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elaine Kamarck}}}\uc2 , a senior fellow at Brookings and former Bill Clinton administration official, said: \u8220\'20\'1C There were some very good things about the old Republican party. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s a party of racists and homophobes and people pursuing bizarre cultural things. It\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re a bankrupt party and yet they manage to do well on these kinds of issues because people get emotional about them and don\u8217\'20\'19t really understand or in fact care about the economic issues. Democrats have been tone deaf thinking that the economic issues will always trump the cultural issues. They don\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For Republicans, this week\u8217\'20\'19s Senate judiciary committee hearing for Judge \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  seemed to be as much as about campaigning for the 2022 midterms, which will decide control of the House of Representatives and Senate, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/05/ketanji-brown-jackson-supreme-court-republicans-mitch-mcconnell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first Black woman}}}\uc2  nominated to the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 Dwelling on CRT, Senator Ted Cruz of Texas held up the book Antiracist Baby by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/12/ibram-x-kendi-antiracism-backlash-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ibram X Kendi}}}\uc2  and demanded: \u8220\'20\'1C Do you agree\u8230\'20\'26 that babies are racist?\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2  of Tennessee asked: \u8220\'20\'1CCan you provide a definition for the word \u8216\'20\'18woman\u8217\'20\'19?\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/health-wellness/2022/03/24/marsha-blackburn-asked-ketanji-jackson-define-woman-science/7152439001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 replied}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m not a biologist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tarasetmayer.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tara Setmayer,}}}\uc2  a senior adviser to the anti-Trump group Lincoln Project, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Scotus [supreme court] nomination hearings this week were a window into the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s strategy going into midterms and 2024. They have no policy agenda. They are strictly focused on culture war wedge issues because they\u8217\'20\'19ve had success energising their base with them and the people who are leading the charge are fundamentally unserious people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenator \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has already said that he\u8217\'20\'19s not releasing a policy agenda. There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason for that. Culture war politics can work and Democrats run the risk of underestimating how powerful and energising this tactic of politicking can be. They underestimate it at their own peril .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 What links many hot button issues is children. Whether unborn or at school, they are portrayed by Republicans as vulnerable to sinister forces aligned with Democrats and leftwing militants. Glenn Youngkin, the governor of Virginia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/02/04/glenn-youngkin-virginia-education-tip-line-stokes-tribal-wars-race/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 set up a tip line}}}\uc2  so parents could send \u8220\'20\'1Creports and observations\u8221\'20\'1D about perceived objectionable conduct by teachers and school staff.\par \par \uc2 The appeal to parental instincts rather than to policy judgments was accelerated by frustrations over mask mandates and school closures during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Setmayer, a political commentator and former Republican communications director on Capitol Hill, said: \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the issues speak to the fundamental desire to protect your children. There\u8217\'20\'19s a reason why Republicans for decades have always included getting involved at the school board level as part of their grassroots playbook.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny time you frame a political issue around children, you can activate voters who may not have been activated before because they want to make sure that their children are safe. It becomes a more righteous issue; it\u8217\'20\'19s not just about them in their minds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Not all Republicans are on board. This week Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2 , and Governor \uc2 Spencer Cox\uc2  of Utah vetoed legislation that would bar transgender girls from taking part in girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports at school. But such voices remain in the minority, with the Trump-dominated party only likely to become more aggressive on hot button issues as the polls draw closer.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fordham.edu/info/24277/ma_in_elections_and_campaign_management_faculty/6866/monika_l_mcdermott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Monika McDermott,}}}\uc2  a political science professor at \uc2 Fordham University\uc2  in New York, said: \u8220\'20\'1CAt this point Democrats are in some ways dismissing it as well as though they think people will see through it and I think that\u8217\'20\'19s a big mistake.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to fight this head on, counter these arguments, make things clear, try to redefine things like so-called critical race theory and explain the reasons why they support teaching this kind of historical perspective in schools and why it\u8217\'20\'19s necessary, and why \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been legal for so long and what\u8217\'20\'19s happening to it now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to do the same kind of call to arms that Republicans are doing but on the liberal side, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t see them doing that at this point. I see them resting on their laurels to a certain extent, targeting specific districts. It\u8217\'20\'19s all about strategy but they\u8217\'20\'19re not getting at the heart of the matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220326ei3q000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
