\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  ban modeled on Texas law advances in Tennessee\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 454 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 March 2022\par 14:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bill allows anyone \u8211\'20\'13 even relatives of rapists \u8211\'20\'13 to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and empowers investigators to question any woman who loses a pregnancy\par \par \uc2 The Tennessee state house is considering a \u8220\'20\'1CTexas-style\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that would allow relatives, friends, neighbors and the spouse of a rapist to sue anyone who provides or assists in the provision of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to his victim.\par \par \uc2 The bill, which would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely with no exceptions for rape or incest, cleared one hurdle last week, when a health subcommittee passed it.\par \par \uc2 The bill is modeled after the Texas six-week ban, which the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 let stand}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas bill deputizes private citizens to enforce the law by giving them the right to sue any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider they believe has violated the law or anyone aiding provision. As in Texas, the government will not be the enforcer under the Tennessee bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill is modeled directly after the legislation passed in Texas last year,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/tennessee-republicans-introduce-texas-styled-abortion-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the Republican Rebecca Alexander, the legislation sponsor, in a committee session. \u8220\'20\'1CAbortions since that bill has been passed have dropped 60% in Texas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/parents/pregnancy/tennessee-bill-rapists-sue-abortion-rcna20581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 added}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis is my bill. My intent is to bring a bill that protects the unborn life in this state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill would allow people to sue anyone who helps someone obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cregardless of any standing they have in the case\u8221\'20\'1D. Lawsuits filed against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and assistants would come with a minimum fine of $10,000.\par \par \uc2 A state Democrat, Bob Freeman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/parents/pregnancy/tennessee-bill-rapists-sue-abortion-rcna20581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked}}}\uc2  Alexander if the bill would allow a rapist\u8217\'20\'19s relatives, friends, spouse and neighbors to sue a victim.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy assumption is that they could, other than the rapist,\u8221\'20\'1D said Alexander.\par \par \uc2 Although rape victims could not be sued under the bill, the bill would \u8220\'20\'1Callow investigators to ask people who lose a pregnancy how it was lost\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/parents/pregnancy/tennessee-bill-rapists-sue-abortion-rcna20581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Rejul Bejoy, a legislative attorney.\par \par \uc2 In 2019, nearly 6,000 cases of sexual assault were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/tn/health/program-areas/rwh/2019-SAReport.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2  to Tennessee law enforcement agencies. According to the state department of health, children between 14 and 17 had the highest rate of sexual assault victimization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill, while it\u8217\'20\'19s being framed as an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill, is really not doing anything to further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Freeman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.today.com/parents/pregnancy/tennessee-bill-rapists-sue-abortion-rcna20581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Today. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really just going to bring all sorts of lawsuits and force people to have to potentially answer questions about a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt never ceases to amaze me, the bills that pass. I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how it will fare in the full committee. But let me say this: if it passes through the senate and the house, the governor will sign it into law. Guaranteed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220321ei3l0028r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
