\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Idaho copies extreme Texas law and bans  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after six weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 Gloria Oladipo \par \uc2 532 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 March 2022\par 15:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Outrage as state becomes first in US to pass ban modelled on Texas law that allows family members to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers\par \par \uc2 Idaho has become the first US state to pass an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban modeled after a controversial {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law }}}\uc2  that prohibits abortions after about six weeks or when a heartbeat is detected.\par \par \uc2 The news comes with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights under assault across the US \u8211\'20\'13 despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewforum.org/fact-sheet/public-opinion-on-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clear majority support}}}\uc2  for such rights. The conservative-dominated \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is thought likely to overturn Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling which established the right, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/04/blue-states-abortion-rights-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 later this year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Idaho house members {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2022/03/14/idaho-abortion-ban-texas-brad-little/7043235001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed the ban 51-14}}}\uc2 . No Democrats supported the legislation. The Senate has approved the bill and the Republican governor, \uc2 Brad Little\uc2 , is expected to sign it.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups called on Little to use his veto.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood called the bill a copycat of the Texas bill that became {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law last May}}}\uc2  and was controversially left in place by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/22/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the supreme court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIdaho\u8217\'20\'19s anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lawmakers ignored public opinion and rushed through this legislation, looking to capitalize on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19s ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.plannedparenthoodaction.org/pressroom/idaho-becomes-first-state-to-pass-copycat-texas-style-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/03/14/politics/idaho-abortion-bill-six-weeks/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adding}}}\uc2  that the bill\u8217\'20\'19s proponents have been open about wanting Idaho to become \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next Texas\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer M Allen, chief executive of Planned Parenthood Alliance Advocates, an Idaho nonprofit, said: \u8220\'20\'1CLittle must do the right thing, listen to the medical community and veto this legislation before it forces Idaho patients to leave the state for critical, time-sensitive care or remain pregnant against their will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Idaho bill would also allow family members to sue doctors who perform procedures after six weeks of pregnancy, before most people know they are pregnant. The bill provides a minimum reward of $20,000 plus legal fees within four years of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for successful suits, compared to minimum $10,000 and legal costs under the Texas law.\par \par \uc2 Unlike the Texas law, the Idaho bill provides some exceptions in cases of rape or incest. While a rapist could not sue practitioners under Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s new bill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/14/us/idaho-abortion-bill-texas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 family members could}}}\uc2 . Victims would have to file a police report and provide it to a doctor before they could get the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill is not clever, it\u8217\'20\'19s absurd,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/14/us/idaho-abortion-bill-texas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Democratic representative Lauren Necochea, adding that the rape and incest exemptions were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot meaningful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Last year, Little signed a \u8220\'20\'1Cheartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D bill into law, but it included a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger provision\u8221\'20\'1D that stopped it being in effect until a federal court approved it, which has not happened.\par \par \uc2 Several Republican-run states have taken steps to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Among them, bills in Missouri {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2022/03/11/missouri-house-anti-abortion-bills-take-aim-crossing-state-lines-ectopic-pregnancies/7003993001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 would permit lawsuits }}}\uc2  against those who help someone cross state lines to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Terminating non-viable pregnancies would be a criminal offense.\par \par \uc2 The Oklahoma senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-oklahoma-texas-oklahoma-city-legislature-c925f7ad01c7082509e64ba778a9b783"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently passed six anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  measures}}}\uc2 , including a copycat of the Texas ban. In February, the Arizona senate passed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that would prohibit the procedure after 15 weeks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/audio/2021/dec/01/the-mississippi-and-texas-laws-threatening-abortion-rights-us-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  similar to the law passed in Mississippi}}}\uc2 , which is expected to lead the supreme court to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220315ei3f002jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
