\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US and allies set to revoke normal trade relations with Russia over Ukraine war, says Biden \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 6,845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 March 2022\par 22:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US \u8216\'20\'18taking first steps\u8217\'20\'19 to ban imports of Russian vodka and diamonds\u8216\'20\'18We are not ready\u8217\'20\'19: a cyber expert on US vulnerability to a Russian attackLive updates: Russia-Ukraine warFull report: Russia widens attack to more citiesSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 End of day summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively day in Washington. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is headed to Camp David after a busy day that began at the White House, where he announced that the US would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1#block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1#block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to revoke }}}\uc2  Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmost favored nation\u8221\'20\'1D trading status, in coordination with allies. Ending normal trade relations will \u8220\'20\'1Cmake it harder for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia }}}\uc2  to business with the United States\u8221\'20\'1D. The US also banned the import of Russian seafood, alcohol and diamonds.\par \par \uc2 * In Philadelphia, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b8a4b8f08d38fbc42c1c4#block-622b8a4b8f08d38fbc42c1c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  House Democrats that this November\u8217\'20\'19s mid-term elections are the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost important in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D, and urged them to make the economic case to voters in plain, simple language. He then visited an elementary school to mark the one-year anniversary of the American Rescue Plan.\par \par \uc2 * The president also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b723f8f08d64fa95ea615#block-622b723f8f08d64fa95ea615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned }}}\uc2  that Russia would \u8220\'20\'1Cpay a severe price\u8221\'20\'1D if it used chemical weapons against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2 . The White House declined to elaborate on what such a response might look like.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Treasury Department\uc2  has unveiled new sanctions targeting \u8220\'20\'1CKremlin elites, oligarchs, and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s political and national security leaders\u8221\'20\'1D as part of its coordinated effort to punish Moscow for its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-622b5afa8f08d38fbc42bfc2#block-622b5afa8f08d38fbc42bfc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking }}}\uc2  in Romania at the end of her high-profile trip there and to Poland, both fellow Nato members, said the military alliance is \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D in its commitment to defend its territory.\par \par \uc2 Thank you for following along with us. Please follow our in-depth, around the clock global liveblog for all the latest on the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/11/russia-ukraine-war-latest-news-we-are-dealing-with-a-terrorist-state-says-zelenskiy-biden-plans-fresh-russian-trade-crackdown-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war latest news: Russia may be planning to use biological weapons, US says, as Russia warns of \u8216\'20\'18uncontrolled spread of bio agents\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Treasury Department{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0650"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  a new round of sanctions targeting \u8220\'20\'1CKremlin elites, oligarchs, and Russia\u8217\'20\'19s political and national security leaders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new sanctions target the wife and adult children of Putin\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman, Dmitriy Sergeevich Peskov; Russian tycoon and \u8220\'20\'1CKremlin insider\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Viktor Vekselberg\uc2 ; and 10 members of the management board of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s second largest bank, \uc2 VTB Bank\uc2 . The list also includes 12 members of the Russian state Duma, including Vyacheslav Victorovich Volodin, who is also a permanent member of \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s Security Council\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTreasury continues to hold Russian officials to account for enabling Putin\u8217\'20\'19s unjustified and unprovoked war,\u8221\'20\'1D Treasury secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s actions also further isolates the severely damaged Russian economy by prohibiting trade in products that are key to the economic and financial interests of all Russian elites.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 State department spokesman \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  denounced Russia\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , \uc2 Vasily Nebenzya\uc2 , for downplaying the strike on a maternity hospital during a security council meeting convened by Moscow earlier today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a brutal strike against a maternity hospital that killed innocent Ukrainians,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrState Deptartment spokesperson \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  calls out Russian Ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 Vasily Nebenzya\uc2  for peddling misinformation at the Security Council:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a brutal strike against a maternity hospital that killed innocent Ukrainians.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/W38FHUNxNV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/W38FHUNxNV }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1502380178651164676?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 11, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Senate confirmed George Tsunis to be the US ambassador to Greece on Friday.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Senate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Senate }}}\uc2  confirmed by voice vote: Executive Calendar #782 George J. Tsunis to be Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the United States of America to Greece.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Press Gallery (@SenatePress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatePress/status/1502135128797192192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 11, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith wrote about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nomination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://arbor.com/our-team/george-tsunis/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tsunis, }}}\uc2  a hotel developer and Democratic donor with no diplomatic experience. Tsunis was previously nominated by Obama to be the ambassador to Norway. It did not go well, per Smith\u8217\'20\'19s report.\par \par \uc2 On that occasion Tsunis was \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominee for ambassador to Norway. Bumbling and ill-prepared, he admitted that he had never been to Norway and referred to the country as having a president when, as a constitutional monarchy, it does not.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/11/joe-biden-george-tsunis-greece-ambassador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He\u8217\'20\'19s a punchline\u8217\'20\'19: \u8216\'20\'18laughable\u8217\'20\'19 pick for Greece envoy puts pressure on Biden }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At an Oval Office meeting with the then Ukrainian president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/petro-poroshenko"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Petro Poroshenko }}}\uc2 , in 2017, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  asked his national security adviser if US troops were in Donbas, territory claimed by Russian-backed separatists, which \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  last month used as pretext for a full and bloody invasion.\par \par \uc2 Marie Yovanovitch\uc2 . Photograph: Andrew Harnik/AP\par \par \uc2 Describing the meeting in a new book, the then US ambassador to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2 , \uc2 Marie Yovanovitch\uc2 , writes: \u8220\'20\'1CAn affirmative answer to that question would have meant that the United States was in a shooting war with Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yovanovitch adds: \u8220\'20\'1CI pondered whether it was better to interpret Trump\u8217\'20\'19s question as suggesting that the commander-in-chief thought it possible that US troops were fighting Russia-led forces, or instead as an indicator that the president wasn\u8217\'20\'19t clear which country was on the other side of the war against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEither way, it was disconcerting that he did not seem to know where we had our troops \u8211\'20\'13 his troops \u8211\'20\'13 deployed. I could only imagine what the Ukrainians were thinking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/nov/15/marie-yovanovitch-state-department-fails-fight-corrupt-interests-impeachment-testimony"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired Yovanovitch }}}\uc2  in 2019, amid attempts to withhold military aid to Ukraine in return for political dirt on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and other rivals, an affair which fueled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment.\par \par \uc2 Yovanovitch describes the Trump-Poroshenko meeting in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Lessons-Edge-Memoir-Marie-Yovanovitch/dp/0358457548"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lessons from the Edge: A Memoir }}}\uc2 , which will be published on Tuesday. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  obtained a copy.\par \par \uc2 Full story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/mar/11/donald-trump-ukraine-crimea-russia-poroshenko-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump thought US troops were in Ukraine in 2017, ex-ambassador says in book }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The justice department is sifting through a mountain of evidence from social media and body cameras as officials prosecute cases involving the January 6 attack on the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 The expansive scope of potential evidence has caused January 6 cases to move significantly slower than many expected, and it has created an opening for Republicans to criticize federal prosecutors\u8217\'20\'19 handling of the situation.\par \par \uc2 The LA Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-03-11/hundreds-of-jan-6-defendants-wait-day-in-court-as-justice-department-processes-mountain-of-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Some judges are getting antsy about how slow the cases are moving. And some Republican politicians have used the delays to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/dc-politics/dc-jail-gop/2021/07/29/8362d17e-f096-11eb-bf80-e3877d9c5f06_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticize the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the  }}}\uc2  cases, saying it is time to wrap up the investigations and move on, an argument that could get louder if the party regains control of Congress next year.\par \par \uc2 U.S. attorneys are under immense pressure to successfully prosecute as many of these cases as possible and don\u8217\'20\'19t want to risk defendants getting off on a technicality because they weren\u8217\'20\'19t given all the evidence against them, or worse, evidence that could clear them.\par \par \uc2 At this rate it may take years to prosecute all the cases. The Justice Department continues to announce indictments nearly weekly. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/wanted/capitol-violence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is still trying to identify  }}}\uc2  at least 350 more people.\par \par \uc2 As a result, 14 months after rioters brawled with police, resulting in several deaths and scores of injuries, caused millions of dollars of damage and disrupted the certification of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory, only one Jan. 6 defendant, Guy Reffitt, has faced a jury. Reffitt, a member of the Texas Three Percenter militia group, was found guilty on all counts Tuesday, including obstruction of an official proceeding and carrying a firearm while being unlawfully on Capitol grounds.\par \par \uc2 Read the LA Times\u8217\'20\'19 full report on the collection of evidence in January 6 cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/politics/story/2022-03-11/hundreds-of-jan-6-defendants-wait-day-in-court-as-justice-department-processes-mountain-of-information"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A Capitol rioter who pushed a police officer off a ledge during the deadly January 6 riots has been arrested by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  after authorities identified him through a photo from a sea turtle fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 Authorities arrested Ralph Joseph Celentano III, 54, in Broad Channel, Queens on Wednesday and charged him with assaulting, resisting, or impeding officers, civil disorder, engaging in physical violence in a restricted building or grounds, and related offenses, the Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/03/10/ralph-celentano-capitol-riot-turtle/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/usao-dc/pr/new-york-man-arrested-charges-actions-during-jan-6-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to }}}\uc2  court documents, Celentano was captured by security cameras wearing a backpack with a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  flag and a folding chair affixed to it. He approached a \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officer from behind and launched at him in a \u8220\'20\'1Cfootball-type tackle,\u8221\'20\'1D causing the officer to fall over a ledge and onto a terrace below.\par \par \uc2 The officer, an Iraq war veteran, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cblind-sided\u8221\'20\'1D and recalled thinking, \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t survive a war to go out like this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Investigators were able to identify Celentano after they received a tip with a picture of him and a group of people that was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2022/03/10/ralph-celentano-capitol-riot-turtle/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  posted }}}\uc2  on the Jenny Albert Sea Turtle Foundation Facebook page.\par \par \uc2 A volunteer at the foundation confirmed Celentano\u8217\'20\'19s identity and another person, who has been friends with Celentano for more than 13 years, also confirmed his identity.\par \par \uc2 Since the riots, over 775 individuals have been arrested across the country for crimes related to the break of the US Capitol, with over 245 being charged with assaulting or impeding law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  traveled to Philadelphia today to speak with House Democrats, who are wrapping up a two-day retreat in the city.\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://punchbowl.news/archive/punchbowl-news-midday-inside-bidens-meeting-with-house-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has details }}}\uc2  on what Biden told lawmakers behind closed doors:\par \par \uc2 Biden said Covid has interrupted politicians\u8217\'20\'19 ability to communicate. He said constituents want to look you in the eye. Biden called himself a \u8216\'20\'18rope line guy\u8217\'20\'19 and told lawmakers that people want to get a feel for you.\par \par \uc2 Biden also said that, when he travels, he sees signs that say \u8216\'20\'18Fuck you Biden\u8217\'20\'19 and kids give him the finger. He said \u8216\'20\'18you guys probably don\u8217\'20\'19t get that kind of response.\u8217\'20\'19 Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said \u8216\'20\'18I do\u8217\'20\'19 to laughter.\par \par \uc2 Biden also told House Democrats that he has spoken to the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , almost every day since the start of the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke to Zelenskiy today to update him on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe actions the United States is taking today in coordination with the \uc2 G7\uc2  and the \uc2 EU\uc2  to further raise the costs on Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the White House\u8217\'20\'19s readout of the conversation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with students at Honorable Luis Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz-Mar\u237\'00\'EDn Elementary School in Philadelphia as he promoted the benefits of the American Rescue Plan.\par \par \uc2 The elementary school students constructed a sign saying \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome Mr President!\u8221\'20\'1D to greet Biden upon his arrival this afternoon:\par \par \uc2 enltr.? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS }}}\uc2  ? meets with students in Philadelphia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xtj7IwUXHX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xtj7IwUXHX }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeff Mason (@jeffmason1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeffmason1/status/1502370707120005127?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 11, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 According to the press pool, the president is hearing from school officials about the afterschool arts programs that have been launched using funds from the coronavirus relief package.\par \par \uc2 Biden is joined at the school by \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2 , the secretary of education, and \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2 , the governor of Pennsylvania, among others.\par \par \uc2 Bien at Luis Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz Marin elementary school in Philadelphia on Friday. Photograph: Patrick Semansky/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has now arrived at Honorable Luis Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz-Mar\u237\'00\'EDn Elementary School in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, as the president marks one year since he signed the coronavirus relief bill into law.\par \par \uc2 In a memo shared with the press pool, the White House noted that the elementary school is a Title I, dual-language (English and Spanish) school with about 600 students enrolled from prekindergarten through eighth grade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Hon. Luis Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz-Mar\u237\'00\'EDn Elementary School has deployed American Rescue Plan funding for a number of purposes aligned with the President\u8217\'20\'19s call to action in his State of the Union address and Unity Agenda to hire more school staff, provide tutoring, and address student mental health,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result of additional funds provided through the American Rescue Plan, the school has been able to launch afterschool enrichment programs that it says have improved the school\u8217\'20\'19s culture and supported student mental health, paid teachers to provide reading interventions after school for students that have experienced the most learning loss as a result of the pandemic, and hired coaches for their teachers, which the school has said resulted in teachers improving their instruction more quickly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 News is coming through that the \uc2 Walt Disney Co\uc2  is pausing all political donations in Florida.\par \par \uc2 And, starting immediately, Reuters notes, the company said it is increasing support for advocacy groups to combat legislation in other states that is discriminatory to LGBTQ+ people.\par \par \uc2 Walt Disney Co\uc2  logo at the New York stock exchange - file pic. Photograph: Richard Drew/AP\par \par \uc2 The Republican-dominated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida }}}\uc2  legislature {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/dont-say-gay-bill-florida-senate-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a bill }}}\uc2  on Tuesday which would forbid instruction on sexual orientation and gender identity in kindergarten through third grade, rejecting a wave of criticism from Democrats that it marginalizes LGBTQ+ people.\par \par \uc2 The proposal, which opponents have dubbed the \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill, now moves to the desk of the Republican governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ron-desantis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis }}}\uc2 , who is expected to sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 Anasofia Pelaez and Kimberly Blandon (L-R) protest in front of Florida State Senator Ileana Garcia\u8217\'20\'19s (R-FL) office the passage of the Parental Rights in Education bill, dubbed the \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill by LGBTQ activists on March 09, 2022 in Miami, Florida. The bill passed by the Florida Senate and House would limit what classrooms can teach about sexual orientation and gender identity. Photograph: Joe Raedle/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Since its inception, the measure has drawn intense opposition from LGBTQ+ advocates, students, Democrats, the White House and the entertainment industry, amid increased attention on Florida as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2  push culture war legislation and DeSantis ascends in the GOP as a potential presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 Of course, \uc2 Disney\uc2  has its humungous business Disney World in Orlando, Florida, a destination for millions of tourists - including a gazillion gay ones - from the US and the whole world.\par \par \uc2 Toxic. Ron de Santis is expected to sign a bill banning education on sexual orientation in Florida schools, prompting protests. Photograph: Joe Raedle/\uc2 Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Georgia lawmakers are trying to pass a similar bill that would ban discussions of gender identity and sexual orientation in private schools, introducing the measure. As are some other states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/11/georgia-florida-dont-say-gill-bill-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Outcry as Georgia lawmakers aim to pass Florida-style \u8216\'20\'18don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8217\'20\'19 bill  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Texas court deals fresh blow to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  providers conceded a final blow to their best hope of stopping the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law after a new ruling ended what little path forward the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  had left for clinics.\par \par \uc2 The decision by the Texas Supreme Court, which is entirely controlled by Republicans, spelled the coming end to a federal lawsuit that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics filed even before the restrictions took effect in September, but were then rejected at nearly every turn afterward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing left, this case is effectively over with respect to our challenge to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marc Hearron, attorney for the Center for Reproductive Rights, which led the challenge against the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas }}}\uc2  law known as Senate Bill 8 (SB8), the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Cindy Gomez, of Austin, attends the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March ATX rally, at the Texas State Capitol in Austin, Texas, last fall. Photograph: Stephen Spillman/AP\par \par \uc2 The AP continues:\par \par \uc2 Although Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics are not dropping the lawsuit, they now expect it will be dismissed in the coming weeks or months.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after roughly six weeks of pregnancy and makes no exceptions in cases of rape or incest. Abortions in Texas have plummeted by more than 50% since the law took effect.\par \par \uc2 It is likely to further embolden other Republican-controlled states that are now pressing forward with similar laws, including neighboring Oklahoma, where many Texas women have crossed state lines to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the past six months.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-controlled Oklahoma Senate on Thursday approved a half-dozen anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures, including a Texas-style ban.\par \par \uc2 The decision by the Texas Supreme Court turned on whether medical licensing officials had an enforcement role under the law known as Senate Bill 8, and therefore, could be sued by clinics that are reaching for any possible way to halt the restrictions.\par \par \uc2 But writing for the court, Justice Jeffrey Boyd said those state officials have no enforcement authority, \u8220\'20\'1Ceither directly or indirectly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers did not immediately comment on the ruling but had already acknowledged they were running out of options and that the law would stay in place for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  has signaled in a separate case out of Mississippi that it would roll back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and possibly overturn its landmark Roe v. Wade decision, in a ruling that is expected later this year.\par \par \uc2 Texas\u8217\'20\'19s highly restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law has forced thousands of women to cross state lines to seek the procedure, according to new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2022/03/TxPEP-out-of-state-SB8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  research }}}\uc2  by the University of Texas, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/09/texas-abortion-ban-cross-state-lines-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/09/texas-abortion-ban-cross-state-lines-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban forcing thousands to cross state lines for procedure \u8211\'20\'13 study }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello again to all our US politics live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s been a busy day so far and more to come.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just wrapped up an address to a gathering of the House Democrats, in Philadelphia, with much talk of Ukraine but also of coming elections.\par \par \uc2 If you would like to follow our global, in-depth, round-the-clock live blog on the Ukraine crisis, please click {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/11/russia-ukraine-war-latest-news-we-are-dealing-with-a-terrorist-state-says-zelenskiy-biden-plans-fresh-russian-trade-crackdown-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ll also continue to bring you Ukraine-related US news in this blog, too.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b8a4b8f08d38fbc42c1c4#block-622b8a4b8f08d38fbc42c1c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  House Democrats that this November\u8217\'20\'19s mid-term elections are the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost important in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D, as the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 triumvirate of control of the House, Senate and White House is under threat on Capitol Hill.\par \par \uc2 * The president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b723f8f08d64fa95ea615#block-622b723f8f08d64fa95ea615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned }}}\uc2  that Russia would \u8220\'20\'1Cpay a severe price\u8221\'20\'1D if it used chemical weapons against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The USis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1#block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moving }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1#block-622b6b8f8f08d64fa95ea5d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to revoke }}}\uc2  Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmost favored nation\u8221\'20\'1D trading status, in coordination with allies. Ending normal trade relations will \u8220\'20\'1Cmake it harder for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia }}}\uc2  to business with the United States\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden said.\par \par \uc2 * House Speaker Nancy Pelosi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-622b63238f08ec6557dfb8ad#block-622b63238f08ec6557dfb8ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered }}}\uc2  all assistance from Congress to pass legislation codifying the revocation of normal trade status for Russia.\par \par \uc2 * Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/11/joe-biden-suspension-normal-trade-russia-ukraine-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-622b5afa8f08d38fbc42bfc2#block-622b5afa8f08d38fbc42bfc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking }}}\uc2  in Romania at the end of her high-profile trip there and to Poland, both fellow Nato members, said the military alliance is \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D in its commitment to defend its territory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato }}}\uc2 , Julianne Smith, has been talking at a Washington Post Live event about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s allegations of Ukrainian biological weapons.\par \par \uc2 She made counter-claims about Russia\u8217\'20\'19s biological weapons, but in mentioning \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2  and Syria, she appears to be referring to chemical weapons rather than biological agents.\par \par \uc2 This is what she said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen over the years is that Russia is actually the country that is the one that relies on biological weapons. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen them rely on biological weapons as it relates to attempted assassinations. You could think of Navalny, in particular, but others. You could look at what they did and how they operated in Syria, which was horrifying- their reliance on these types of weapons are in direct violation of international law. So yes, we are worried when we hear them making these accusations. Sometimes what they do is they accuse us of something that they\u8217\'20\'19re about to do themselves- and to use that as a pretext for some sort of other attack on their part.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden is now offering a lengthy explanation for rising gas prices, an issue that Republicans have used to hammer Democrats ahead of the midterms. The culprits, he said, were the coronavirus and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , not Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 spending.\par \par \uc2 He highlighted fact-checks and an op-ed accusing Republicans of hypocrisy for pushing Biden to ban Russian oil imports while attacking him for rising fuel costs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats didn\u8217\'20\'19t cause this problem, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  did,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While fighting to bring down the cost of gas, Biden said Democrats can \u8220\'20\'1Csave people a lot of money\u8221\'20\'1D by bringing down the costs of childcare, prescription drugs and senior care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no one way to increase the standard of living,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden is now sharpening his attacks on Republicans, a rhetorical pivot many Democrats have been waiting for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn this anniversary of the American Rescue Plan, let\u8217\'20\'19s be clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe did it alone \u8211\'20\'13 without one single, solitary Republican vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American economy was flat on its back, it was the Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 it was you that \u8211\'20\'13 brought us back,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, drawing a big applause.\par \par \uc2 Biden then praised passage of the Infrastructure law. In a notable shift, Biden, who has long touted the bipartisan support for the law, joked with Democrats that only a handful of Republicans in the House supported the measure but many more are eager to take credit for the public works projects in their districts.\par \par \uc2 How many House Republicans backed the infrastructure bill, Biden asked. \u8220\'20\'1C13, 14 or something? I mean c\u8217\'20\'19mon, I was happy for them, don\u8217\'20\'19t get me wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, as members shouted 13.\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CHave you noticed that every new bridge, every trench dug to take out lead pipes... there\u8217\'20\'19s a Republican standing there saying, \u8216\'20\'18This is a great thing. Wonderful. We did it!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to House Democrats: November midterms are the 'most important in modern history'\par \par \uc2 Biden opened his remarks to House Democrats with a joke about having attending many such retreats himself and knows that when the \u8220\'20\'1Clast speaker\u8217\'20\'19s up you want to get the hell out of here no matter who it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Getting serious, Biden sought to lay out the stakes this November, saying that the midterm elections may be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most important in modern history.\u8221\'20\'1D He said the stakes were high and Democrats had much left to do.\par \par \uc2 If Democrats lose their majorities,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only thing i\u8217\'20\'19ll have then is the veto pen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Acknowledging tensions between House Democratic leaders and the White House over the response to Russia, Biden thanked members for their patience and said it gave him time to unify the US allies behind the latest efforts to punish Putin. Biden told them that he had just spoken to Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  for nearly an hour, as he does almost daily.\par \par \uc2 He covered familiar territory \u8211\'20\'13 vowing to support Ukraine with weapons and humanitarian aid. He said the US would welcome refugees and that the US would not fight a war with Russia in Ukraine, but would defend Nato territory.\par \par \uc2 Then he moved to more domestic matters, touting the administration\u8217\'20\'19s achievements combatting the pandemic and the impact of the American Rescue Plan, which Congress passed exactly one year ago today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt didn\u8217\'20\'19t cause the inflation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, rejecting a Republican attack line. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, there\u8217\'20\'19s more to the story than that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on Pamela Moses, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s own Sam Levine, whose incredible and dogged reporting that uncovered new information in a case that helped draw attention to the racial disparity between white and Black defendants when it comes to election crimes.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys for Pamela Moses, the Memphis woman who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/25/pamela-moses-new-trial-voting-memphis-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted a retrial }}}\uc2  after being sentenced to six years in prison for trying to register to vote, demanded that a local prosecutor drop the case against her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMs Moses should not have to sit for another trial at all. You have the evidence that was there to show you there was no fraud done,\u8221\'20\'1D Rodney Diggs, one of her attorneys, said at a press conference in Memphis on Friday. If the local district attorney, Amy Weirich, decides to move forward with the case, Moses\u8217\'20\'19 lawyers said she should recuse herself and appoint a special prosecutor.\par \par \uc2 Moses was sentenced to six years in prison in January after she tried to register to vote in 2019 while on probation for a felony. Even though Moses said she believed she had completed probation, prosecutors said she knew she had not and convinced a probation officer to sign off on a form saying she was eligible to vote.\par \par \uc2 A new document, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/24/fight-to-vote-newsletter-black-woman-jailed-voting-error-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 obtained by the Guardian last month }}}\uc2 , significantly undermined that argument. It showed an internal investigation from the probation office concluded that the probation officer made a good-faith mistake in signing off on Moses\u8217\'20\'19 voting eligibility and was negligent. The judge overseeing the case said the document should have been turned over to Moses\u8217\'20\'19 legal team during the trial, which was part of why he ordered a retrial.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/11/pamela-moses-black-woman-jailed-over-voting-error-speaks-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s a scare tactic\u8217\'20\'19: Pamela Moses, the Black woman jailed over voting error, speaks out }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Russian ambassador to \uc2 UN\uc2 , \uc2 Vasily Nebenzya\uc2 , has been presenting the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s allegations that Ukraine and the US had a plot to spread biological weapons with migratory birds, bats and insects. Nebenzya issued a chilling warning to Eastern Europe that biological agents could spread across Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s borders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe call upon you to think about a very real biological danger to the people in European countries, which can result from an uncontrolled spread of bio agents from Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D the Russian ambassador said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd if there is a such a scenario then all Europe will be covered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe risk of this is very real given the interests of the radical nationalist groups in Ukraine are showing towards the work with dangerous pathogens conducted together with the ministry of defence of the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 After Nebenzya spoke, Albania, the US and France have voiced alarm that the allegations may be an advance cover story for Russian plans to unleash chemical or biological weapons.\par \par \uc2 US ambassador, \uc2 Linda Thomas-Greenfield\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1C The intent behind these lies seem clear and it is deeply troubling. We believe Russia could use chemical or biological agents for assassinations as part of a false flag incident or to support tactical military operations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  security council hearing is underway. We have this dispatch from our world affairs editor, Julian Borger.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  security council is holding a hearing called for by Russia to make its allegations about a Ukrainian biological weapons lab.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  high commissioner for disarmament , \uc2 Izumi Nakamitsu\uc2 , has been speaking before the Russians: \u8220\'20\'1C The \uc2 United Nations\uc2  is not aware of any biological weapons programs. That is largely thanks to the 1972 Biological Weapons Convention, which prohibits the development, production, acquisition, transfer, stockpiling, and use of biological and toxin weapons.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nakamitsu said that unlike chemical weapons, there is no independent verification regime for biological weapons, and monitoring is left to state parties, but she said there was a mechanism for those state parties to raise their concerns.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bates only took one question before he was interrupted by the pilot asking passengers to take their seats. Shortly thereafter the feed your live-blogger was using to follow the mid-flight briefing cut out.\par \par \uc2 Asked to elaborate on what consequences Russia could face if it used chemical weapons against Ukraine, Bates deferred to the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks and said the \u8220\'20\'1Cmeaning was unmistakable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said the US was taking part in today\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  session so that it could \u8220\'20\'1Cforcefully debunk\u8221\'20\'1D Russia\u8217\'20\'19s claims that Ukraine was operating a biological weapons program and to \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther call Putin out, as we have during this entire episode successfully at each juncture, where we have reason to believe they are trying to fabricate another false justification for more violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is,\u8221\'20\'1D Bates said, \u8220\'20\'1CRussia is the only country in this equation with a chemical and biological weapons program in violation of international law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said there were \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong indications\u8221\'20\'1D that Russia was committing war crimes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Russia is intentionally targeting civilians, that would be a war crime,\u8221\'20\'1D Bates said, noting that the attacks on apartment complexes, a maternity hospital and evacuation corridors have resulted in rising civilian deaths. \u8220\'20\'1CEvidence is mounting, and we are documenting it as as it takes place. There are strong indications that this is occurring and that the heinous way Russia is prosecuting this war will result in war crimes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This afternoon, after Biden addresses House Democrats at their retreat in Philadelphia, he will visit a majority-Hispanic elementary school to mark the one-year anniversary of the American Rescue Plan. There he will discuss how the pandemic aid helped schools across the country re-open and to help address the long-term impact the pandemic has had on students in terms of both learning and mental health.\par \par \uc2 Biden will also speak directly from the students, White House deputy press secretary Andrew Bates told reporters aboard Air Force One, previewing the visit to Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 He also highlighted bipartisan praise for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court nominee, \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2 , who completed a second week of meetings with senators ahead of her confirmation hearings later this month.\par \par \uc2 Bates said Biden would sign a short-term continuing resolution to keep the government open until the bipartisan funding bill is ready to be signed next week.\par \par \uc2 He added that the White House intends to hold an event next week commemorating women\u8217\'20\'19s history month and that there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdecent bet\u8221\'20\'1D it would celebrate St. Patrick\u8217\'20\'19s day on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is largely focused on US-related Ukraine news and general US politics. If you\u8217\'20\'19d like to read more about the war in Ukraine, I would invite you to follow the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s global liveblog, which is providing around the clock coverage sourced from our reporters around the world.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/11/russia-ukraine-war-latest-news-we-are-dealing-with-a-terrorist-state-says-zelenskiy-biden-plans-fresh-russian-trade-crackdown-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war latest news: Ukraine at \u8216\'20\'18strategic turning point\u8217\'20\'19, claims Zelenskiy, as Russian airstrikes hit three cities }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: Russia would pay a 'severe price' for use of chemical weapons\par \par \uc2 At the end of his remarks, Biden took one question from a reporter who asked about the intelligence underpinning the US\u8217\'20\'19 claims that Russia may be preparing to use chemical weapons and whether that would warrant a military response.\par \par \uc2 Biden declined to comment on the intelligence, and said only that Russia would \u8220\'20\'1Cpay a severe price\u8221\'20\'1D if it used chemical weapons against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The US and Britain have warned that Russia may be creating a pretext to use chemical weapons by making \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse flag claims\u8221\'20\'1D about a biological weapons program operating inside Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The assertion by Russia that the US is conducting \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological activities\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 a claim presented without evidence and which Ukraine has vehemently denied and the US has called gaslighting \u8211\'20\'13 is the subject of today\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  meeting, due to convene shortly at Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s request.\par \par \uc2 The development, production, stockpiling and use of chemical weapons is banned by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opcw.org/chemical-weapons-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an international treaty }}}\uc2  signed by 193 countries, explain the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Dan Sabbagh\uc2  and Julian Borger. Direct attacks on civilians or civilian infrastructure are considered war crimes.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, chemical weapons have nevertheless been used on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opcw.org/sites/default/files/documents/2021/06/210604_DG%20Statement_UNSC%20Meeting_3%20June%202021_WEB.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 17 occasions }}}\uc2  during Syria\u8217\'20\'19s civil war, according to the \uc2 Organisation for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons (OPCW)\uc2 Organisation for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons\uc2  (OPCW), which has accused the Russian-backed regime of Bashar al-Assad of being behind several high-profile attacks.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/britain-fears-russia-could-be-setting-stage-to-use-chemical-weapons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Britain and US fear Russia could be setting stage to use chemical weapons }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his remarks, Biden said the US would welcome Ukrainian refugees with \u8220\'20\'1Copen arms\u8221\'20\'1D and vowed to provide additional support to the besieged nation. Repeating the message Harris just delivered in Romania, Biden, speaking from the White House\u8217\'20\'19s Roosevelt Room, pledged again that the US was prepared to defend \u8220\'20\'1Cevery single inch of Nato territory with the full might of a united and galvanized\u8221\'20\'1D security alliance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not fight a war against Russia in Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CDirect confrontation between \uc2 Nato\uc2  and Russia is world war three, something we must strive to prevent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden declared that Putin\u8217\'20\'19s war against Ukraine had already failed.\par \par \uc2 [Putin] hoped to dominate Ukraine without a fight. He failed. He hoped to fracture European resolve. He failed. He hoped to weaken the Transatlantic alliance. He failed. He hoped to split apart American democracy, in terms of our positions. He failed.\par \par \uc2 The American people are united. The world is united and we stand with the people of Ukraine. We will not let autocrats and would-be emperors dictate the direction of the world. Democracies are rising to meet this moment, rallying the world to the side of peace and the side of security. We are showing our strength and we will not falter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden: US and allies to deny 'most favored nation' status to Russia\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has announced that the US was moving to revoke Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmost favored nation status\u8221\'20\'1D in coordination with allies.\par \par \uc2 Revoking Russia\u8217\'20\'19s permanent normal trade relations will \u8220\'20\'1Cmake it harder for Russia to business with the United States\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the US was \u8220\'20\'1Ctaking the first steps\u8221\'20\'1D to ban imports of Russian vodka, seafood and diamonds.\par \par \uc2 Biden thanked Pelosi for pushing the US to take this action, and for holding off on a measure in Congress until he \u8220\'20\'1Ccould line up all of our key allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPutin is the aggressor and Putin must pay a price,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He also detailed other economic sanctions the US has taken to destabilize the Russian economy and squeeze Putin and those around him.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the US and its allies were targeting an expanded list of Russian oligarchs,and ramping up efforts to capture their \u8220\'20\'1C ill-begotten gains.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey support Putin. They steal from the Russian people and they seek to hide their money in our countries,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, emphasizing one of the most popular aspects of the west\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on Russia. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re part of that kleptocracy that exists in Moscow and they must share in the pain of these sanctions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In addition to seizing their \u8220\'20\'1Csuperyachts\u8221\'20\'1D and vacation homes, Biden said the US was also banning the export of luxury luxury goods to Russia, calling it the latest, but \u8220\'20\'1Cnot the last step we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pelosi: US will seek to end normal trade relations with Russia\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters at the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 retreat-that-is- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JakeSherman/status/1502293392448970754"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not }}}\uc2  -a- retreat in Philadelphia, House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said the US would revoke Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmost favored nation\u8221\'20\'1D trade status over its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 enltrBefore Biden speaks in Philly, PELOSI says she is pleased ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS }}}\uc2  ? today will announce the end of normal trade relations with Russia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n6p9rSSyRG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n6p9rSSyRG }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott Wong (@scottwongDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/scottwongDC/status/1502287399686180870?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 11, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 Biden is set to speak shortly about ending Russia\u8217\'20\'19s special trade status in coordination with the \uc2 EU\uc2  and \uc2 G7\uc2  nations, a move that will allow the countries to raise tariffs on Russian imports. It is the latest step in a series of escalating economic sanctions and actions taken to punish Russia for its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The US currently only excludes two countries from this designation: Cuba and North Korea, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s economic correspondent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richard-partington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Partington }}}\uc2  explains. Removing Russia\u8217\'20\'19s status would would increase its border tax on Russian goods in the US to more than 10 times the current applied rate of about 3% on average.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/11/g7-nations-drawing-up-plans-impose-heavy-tariffs-russia-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 G7 nations draw up plans to impose heavy tariffs on Russia }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Long after the sun set over the US capitol on Thursday, US senators, loathe to work on a Friday, gave final approval to a $1.5tn funding bill.\par \par \uc2 The sweeping omnibus bill belatedly funds the federal government through the fiscal year, ending a cycle of stop-gap measures and shutdown threats. The package, which was passed with bipartisan support in both chambers, includes $13.6bn of military and humanitarian assistance for Ukraine and its European allies. The bill now goes to Biden for his signature.\par \par \uc2 In a statement , White House Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , said the bipartisan support for the bill \u8220\'20\'1Cproves once more that members of both parties can come together to deliver results for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It will reduce costs for families and businesses, support our economic recovery, and advance American leadership abroad. With these resources, we will be able to deliver historic support for the Ukrainian people as they defend their country and democracy, launch a bold new initiative to drive unprecedented progress in curing cancer and other diseases, and provide additional support to our law enforcement so they can protect our communities.\par \par \uc2 Psaki also urged Congress to re-start negotiations over \u8220\'20\'1Cthe funds urgently needed to prevent severe disruptions to our Covid response\u8221\'20\'1D. In a blow to Democrats and the White House, the House dropped a provision providing $15.6bn in funding for bolstering efforts to combat the coronavirus pandemic after lawmakers balked at the proposed offsets for the relief money, which would have resulted in cuts to aid states were relying on.\par \par \uc2 Everett Kelley\uc2 , the national president of the \uc2 American Federation of Government Employees\uc2 , the largest federal employee union, welcomed the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage but said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cno cause to celebrate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Because of continued threats of government shutdowns from political obstructionists and uncertainty caused by stopgap continuing resolutions, federal agencies for a year and a half have been forced to operate under the budget priorities of the previous administration,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the future, ideally beginning with the 2023 fiscal year approaching in just six months, Congress must pass agency operating budgets on time so government agencies avoid unnecessary obstacles to delivering for the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris: US commitment to \uc2 Nato\uc2 's article 5 'ironclad'\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Bucharest, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  reaffirmed the US\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s article five, that an attack on one member is an attack on all. Echoing the president, she said the US was prepared to defend \u8220\'20\'1Cevery inch\u8221\'20\'1D of Nato territory, declaring the alliance \u8220\'20\'1Cbigger and stronger than ever\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cironclad\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The message, delivered from a former Soviet satellite state, was intended to calm nerves in eastern Europe and to send a clear message to the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , should he escalate the war beyond Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s borders.\par \par \uc2 Turning to Iohannis, Harris said she was moved by his stories of refugees fleeing Ukraine. She thanked Romania for welcoming tens of thousands of refugees with \u8220\'20\'1Csuch compassion and such grace\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our live coverage of the news in Washington and around the country.\par \par \uc2 Shortly we will hear from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , where he is expected to announce that the US will join \uc2 G7\uc2  nations and the \uc2 European Union\uc2  in calling for a suspension of normal trade relations with Russia to punish Moscow for what the White House calls its \u8220\'20\'1Cunprovoked and unjustified war on Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Then he will travel to Philadelphia, where House Democrats are cooped up for a three-day retreat that began inauspiciously, with members angry and upset over the machinations that delayed and almost derailed passage of a $1.5tn omnibus funding bill. The president will deliver remarks at the conference, rallying his party ahead of what is expected to be a bruising midterm for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 That measure, which includes aid to Ukraine and funds the federal government through September, passed the Senate late Thursday night. It now goes to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s desk for signature.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is concluding her trip to Poland and Romania. Any minute, she will appear with the Romanian president \uc2 Klaus Iohannis\uc2  for a press conference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220311ei3b001xm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
