\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida Republicans pass bill to ban  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza and agencies \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2022\par 15:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  expected to sign bill into lawAbortion rights under increasing threat in many US states\par \par \uc2 Republican lawmakers in Florida passed a bill on Thursday evening to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks, nine weeks earlier than is currently allowed in the state.\par \par \uc2 The governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , is expected to sign the bill, which is modeled on a Mississippi law that has become the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subject of a supreme court case}}}\uc2  that could severely curtail or perhaps overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me be clear: there is no such thing as a reasonable ban,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democratic representative Anna Eskamani, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnnaForFlorida/status/1499581054214098969"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in response to the bill\u8217\'20\'19s passage}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDespite impassioned pleas by Democrats to include exceptions for rape, incest and human trafficking, none were accepted by the Republican majority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new bill also drew rebuke from the Biden administration, which called it \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme by any standard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe right of women to make decisions about their own bodies is non-negotiable,\u8221\'20\'1D Vice-President Kamala Harris said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIf signed into law, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s bill would violate the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the supreme court has recognized for nearly 50 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under current federal law, women have a constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy until a fetus can survive outside the womb, generally regarded as 24 weeks. That right was established in a landmark 1973 supreme court case, Roe v Wade, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/22/us-abortion-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-49-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 invalidated dozens of state \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 . Until recently this meant Florida\u8217\'20\'19s bill would have been almost certain to be permanently blocked by federal courts, if DeSantis did sign it.\par \par \uc2 However, in December the supreme court heard oral arguments in a case that centers on a 15-week ban in Mississippi. During arguments in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Clinic, the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared open}}}\uc2  to severely curtailing or perhaps reversing the rights found in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 If \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law were returned to the states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  would be expected to rapidly outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A decision in Dobbs is expected in June.\par \par \uc2 Southern states have been emboldened to pass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/03/texas-abortion-ban-six-months-grave-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly draconian \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\uc2 . Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban, for example, is scheduled to go into effect on 1 July.\par \par \uc2 It is also notable given Florida has long been considered \u8220\'20\'1Cpurple\u8221\'20\'1D: though it has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 controlled by Republicans}}}\uc2  for two decades, the state\u8217\'20\'19s evenly split electorate meant it has been a presidential battleground for just as long.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban joins a slate of other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/desantis-gops-rising-star-2024-hopefuls-drill-anti/story?id=83143776"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Canti-woke\u8221\'20\'1D conservative bills}}}\uc2  Republicans pushed in a contentious legislative session this year, powered in part by DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s apparent presidential ambitions.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in the US come as nations around the world have continued to liberalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, including in Latin America countries {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2022/feb/22/this-is-historic-pro-choice-campaigners-celebrate-legal-abortion-in-colombia-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historically hostile to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abortions after 15 weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/24/medication-abortion-majority-2020-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are not common}}}\uc2 , and are more expensive and logistically complicated than earlier abortions. Only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/evidence-you-can-use/later-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11% of women}}}\uc2  who terminate a pregnancy do so in the second trimester (after 13 weeks). Slightly more than 1% of people who obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  do so after 21 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Fetal anomalies are one reason pregnant people may seek to terminate a second trimester pregnancy. Although anomalies can be detected at any time, some may not be found until after 20 weeks, when pregnant people undergo a lengthy sonogram focused on fetal anatomy.\par \par \uc2 In hearings, the Republican representative Dana Trabulsy said she had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and regretted it. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the right to life, and to give up life is unconscionable to me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ucsf.edu/news/2020/01/416421/five-years-after-abortion-nearly-all-women-say-it-was-right-decision-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 peer-reviewed survey}}}\uc2  of nearly 1,000 US women showed 95% of women felt their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the right decision for them.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220307ei37002pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
