\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A grave warning\u8217\'20\'19: six months of Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban sow fear and anguish\b0\par\par\uc2 Mary Tuma \par \uc2 1,049 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 March 2022\par 07:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban has had \u8216\'20\'18devastating\u8217\'20\'19 effects, providers say, and offers a glimpse of the future if Roe v Wade is overturned\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  most restrictive}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the US has inflicted \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating\u8221\'20\'1D consequences in Texas since it was introduced six months ago, according to healthcare providers and pro-choice groups.\par \par \uc2 Senate Bill 8 (SB 8) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  bars the procedure}}}\uc2  once embryonic cardiac activity is detected, typically at six weeks of pregnancy or earlier, with no exception for rape or incest. As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://sites.utexas.edu/txpep/files/2021/07/TxPEP-research-brief-senate-bill-8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most people}}}\uc2  are not aware they are pregnant this early on, the unprecedented law amounts to a near-total ban.\par \par \uc2 It also delegates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/10/texas-abortion-law-jonathan-f-mitchell-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enforcement to private citizens}}}\uc2 , in lieu of the state, encouraging anti-choice vigilantes to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers as well as anyone who \u8220\'20\'1Caids or abets\u8221\'20\'1D care for damages of at least $10,000, creating a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/15/no-one-wants-to-get-sued-some-abortion-providers-have-stopped-working-in-texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chilling effect}}}\uc2  among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters.\par \par \uc2 Amy Hagstrom Miller\uc2 , president and CEO of Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health, which operates four \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Texas, described the panic, fear and anguish of patients unable to obtain constitutionally protected healthcare in their home state. She said her clinic staff had transformed counseling sessions into trauma and grief support, coupled with travel logistics advice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor six months we have heard the cries and pleas of Texans who have had their healthcare freedoms stripped away,\u8221\'20\'1D Hagstrom Miller said in a recent press briefing. \u8220\'20\'1CIn many cases, there is nothing we can do for them other than listen, hold their hands and dry their tears.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under SB 8, abortions in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://liberalarts.utexas.edu/txpep/research-briefs/sb8-initial-impact-brief.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  have fallen by almost 50%}}}\uc2 . Texans have been forced to travel hundreds \u8211\'20\'13 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/11/new-evidence-texas-residents-have-obtained-abortions-least-12-states-do-not-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  even thousands}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 of miles for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, with an average distance that is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/08/impact-texas-abortion-ban-14-fold-increase-driving-distance-get-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  14 times}}}\uc2  greater than before, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is only if they can find the necessary resources including time off work, childcare, lodging, transportation and others necessary to cross state lines. Some Texans are being forced to carry pregnancies against their will, providers say. They stress the impact of SB 8 falls hardest on low-income people and black and brown communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSenate Bill 8 has been absolutely devastating for Texas communities, especially for people who call on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds for support,\u8221\'20\'1D says Amanda Williams, executive director of the Lilith Fund.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds that offer financial assistance to low-income patients and people of color said they were now spending \u8220\'20\'1Csix times more\u8221\'20\'1D on travel expenses under SB 8 in a video {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lawyeringproject.org/six-months-of-sb8/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  detailing the impact}}}\uc2  of the law.\par \par \uc2 Anna Rupani of Fund Texas Choice says the number of people leaving Texas for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care has risen fivefold among those they help. Similarly, Kamyon Conner of Texas Equal Access Fund reports 91% of those who call the non-profit are in need of out-of-state care.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in this state are being forced to travel for healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D Conner said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need the support of everyone in the country right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  recently released new data showing a nearly 800% increase in Texas patients at their health centers in nearby states, including New Mexico, Kansas, Colorado and Missouri in the first four months of SB 8 compared with last year. \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  clinics in Oklahoma alone saw a nearly 2,500% increase in patients from Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese numbers are staggering and just one part of the devastating picture on the ground in Texas and the surrounding states,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[T]he country\u8217\'20\'19s most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has led to continued chaos and a sustained crisis for patients and providers in Texas and beyond. This reality is heartbreaking and a glimpse of what\u8217\'20\'19s to come should the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/abortion-rights-supreme-court-states-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court restrict}}}\uc2  the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even further.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clinics in neighboring states have become overburdened with an influx of patients, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texasobserver.org/texas-abortion-ban-is-having-a-domino-effect-on-clinics-across-the-u-s/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 causing a ripple effect}}}\uc2  across the US reproductive health network.\par \par \uc2 Kathaleen Pittman, clinic administrator at Hope Medical Group for Women in Shreveport, Louisiana, said in her 30 years as a provider she had \u8220\'20\'1Cnever been so afraid\u8221\'20\'1D for her patients, most of whom live at or below the poverty level. With a nearly 50% jump in Texas patients, the clinic is \u8220\'20\'1Coverloaded\u8221\'20\'1D and cannot schedule appointments until one month out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur staff is exhausted and the phone calls are nonstop,\u8221\'20\'1D says Pittman. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are crying because they can\u8217\'20\'19t understand how a state can have so much control over their lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/14/texas-abortion-ban-lawsuit-planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  legal efforts}}}\uc2  from Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/12/28/politics/the-year-supreme-court-conservatives-made-their-mark/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stacked with conservative}}}\uc2  anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  justices \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to halt}}}\uc2  the extreme measure on more than one occasion and has largely stripped providers of their power to challenge the law. In January, the conservative fifth circuit court of appeals asked the Texas supreme court to determine if narrow challenges against state medical licensing officials can proceed, and providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2022/02/24/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  await that decision}}}\uc2 . However, they consider the move by the conservative fifth circuit an attempt to \u8220\'20\'1Cfurther slow-walk the case\u8221\'20\'1D and allow SB 8 to remain in place indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court greenlit this law\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented vigilante scheme and essentially said that federal courts are powerless to stop it. There is no end in sight to this nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marc Hearron, senior counsel at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2  and arguing attorney for the plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is happening in Texas should be a grave warning for the rest of the country. This is a preview of what will happen on a much larger scale if Roe falls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overturn or undermine the pivotal 1973 Roe v Wade ruling that guarantees the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upcoming decision}}}\uc2 , in response to a 15-week Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, is expected in June. In addition to SB 8, Texas passed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://capitol.texas.gov/BillLookup/History.aspx?LegSess=87R&Bill=HB1280"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that would automatically bar all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care if Roe falls.\par \par \uc2 The Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, a measure that would codify Roe into federal law \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially help Texans \u8211\'20\'13 was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  blocked}}}\uc2  by Senate Republicans on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a tragedy. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers alone cannot fix this,\u8221\'20\'1D Hagstrom Miller said of SB 8. \u8220\'20\'1CThis should not be the reality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220303ei33000up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
