\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Biden warns Putin \u8216\'20\'18will pay\u8217\'20\'19 for invasion\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2022\par 11:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President bans Russian aircraft in US airspace as bombardment of Ukraine intensifies. Plus, the teen tracking oligarchsDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced last night that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/01/us-russia-aircraft-joe-biden-state-of-the-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US was banning Russian aircraft from its airspace}}}\uc2  and promised to go after Russian oligarchs in retaliation for the invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In his State of the Union address, Biden said this would further isolate \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . The announcements are the latest in a series of sanctions against Russia and come after similar actions by Canada and the EU this week.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/02/ukraine-cities-bombardment-russia-attack-kyiv-kharkiv-russian-war-invasion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s besieged cities have come under more heavy bombardment}}}\uc2  after Russian commanders facing fierce resistance intensified their shelling of urban areas.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian security heads said this morning that Russian paratroopers had landed in Kharkiv and engaged in heavy fighting with Ukrainian forces.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What do we know on day seven of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion? Several cities are under heavy bombardment again and thousands of Ukrainians are trying to leave Kyiv , our correspondent in Kyiv reported, as \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  warned it plans to strike targets there. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/02/ukraine-russia-invasion-war-what-we-know-on-day-seven"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s everything we know so far}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else is happening? Researchers are gathering mounting evidence that the Russian military is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/02/researchers-gather-evidence-of-possible-russian-war-crimes-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committing war crimes}}}\uc2  with deadly attacks on civilians and the use of cluster munitions.\par \par \uc2 State of the Union:\par \par \uc2 Biden seeks to reassure Americans exhausted by the pandemic and anxious about Ukraine\par \par \uc2 In his address, traditionally one of the most widely viewed speeches a president makes, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/01/joe-biden-ukraine-state-of-the-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden sought to assure Americans}}}\uc2  demoralized after two years of a global pandemic that transformed American life, and, now, rattled by a land war in Europe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want you to know that we are going to be OK,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast year Covid-19 kept us apart,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, surveying the chamber filled with lawmakers, cabinet officials and the justices of the supreme court as he opened his prime-time address. \u8220\'20\'1CThis year we are finally together again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was the war in Ukraine, however, that brought rare bipartisanship to the house chamber, where members of both parties rose to applaud Biden when he disparaged Putin. Hailing the \u8220\'20\'1Cfearlessness\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Ciron will\u8221\'20\'1D of the Ukrainian people, Biden introduced the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/ukraine-ambassador-standing-ovation-state-of-the-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visibly emotional Ukrainian ambassador to the US}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Oksana Markarova\uc2 . He asked the chamber to stand with him and send an \u8220\'20\'1Cunmistakable signal\u8221\'20\'1D, a message of solidarity with the Ukrainian people.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What else did he talk about? Biden outlined a \u8220\'20\'1Cunity agenda\u8221\'20\'1D that he said could find bipartisan support. The list included combatting the opioid epidemic, expanding mental health resources, supporting US veterans and supercharging the \u8220\'20\'1Cmoonshot\u8221\'20\'1D effort to fight cancer.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Was it a speech for the ages, with a ringing phrase that will define this moment of global peril? Perhaps not, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/01/state-of-the-union-ukraine-biden-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes David Smith}}}\uc2 . But it will have made millions of people in America and around the world grateful that the man at the podium was not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans and Joe Manchin block Senate bill to secure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 A bill to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in federal law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/republicans-joe-manchin-us-senate-block-bill-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was blocked by Senate Republicans yesterday}}}\uc2 . Although Democrats expected it to fail, they brought the measure forward at a perilous moment for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, to ensure votes were recorded.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected in June to decide a Mississippi case that could severely curtail or damage \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Democrats were 14 votes shy of the 60 needed to bring the bill to the floor for debate. Manchin, of West Virginia, was the only Democrat to join Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a fundamental right and women\u8217\'20\'19s decisions over women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare belong to women, not to extremist rightwing legislators,\u8221\'20\'1D the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , told reporters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What would the bill have meant if it had passed? The bill brought before the Senate, the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, would codify the rights provided by Roe in federal law. Last September, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  by the Democrat-controlled house.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Astronomers who thought they had discovered a black hole on our cosmic doorstep have said they were mistaken, instead revealing they have found a two-star system involving a stellar \u8220\'20\'1Cvampire\u8221\'20\'1D. At just 1,000 light years from Earth, it was thought to be the closest yet found to our planet.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Texas voters\par \par \uc2 went to the polls on Tuesday in the first primary contest of the US 2022 midterm elections. The state attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 , a staunch Trump ally who has the former president\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, is seeking the Republican nomination for a third term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The\par \par \uc2 house select committee investigating the 6 January\par \par \uc2 Capitol attack has issued new subpoenas to lawyers for\par \par \uc2 Trump suspected to be involved in efforts to stop the certification of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election victory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As fighting continues in Ukraine after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion, people have been fleeing to neighbouring countries. But people in Lithuania, Slovakia, Latvia, Estonia, Romania and Poland fear Nato membership {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/01/ukraine-neighbours-nato-lithuania-poland-slovakia-latvia-estonia-romania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may not stop Russia invading them next}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day:\par \par \uc2 more rights defenders murdered in 2021, with 138 activists killed just in Colombia\par \par \uc2 A Colombian conservationist who saved a rare species of parrot from extinction, a young feminist activist in Afghanistan, and two poets in Myanmar who used words to protest against the military coup, were among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2022/mar/02/more-human-rights-defenders-murdered-2021-environmental-indigenous-rights-activists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 358 human rights defenders murdered in 35 countries last year}}}\uc2 , analysis has found. Many of the killings could have been prevented, as they were preceded by threats and calls for protection, according to FLD, which tries to protect activists at risk.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: how a 21-year-old millionaire started a media frenzy\par \par \uc2 In 1970, Michael Brody Jr announced he would give away $25m, inspiring hundreds of thousands of letters. But, as a new documentary shows, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/mar/02/dear-mr-brody-millionaire-media-frenzy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the story took an unlikely turn}}}\uc2 . The director Keith Maitland and the veteran film producer Ed Pressman have centred their new documentary, Dear Mr Brody, on a trove of unread letters that came into Pressman\u8217\'20\'19s possession. \u8220\'20\'1CEach letter is a life,\u8221\'20\'1D the producer said. \u8220\'20\'1COpening them is like peeking behind a curtain into somebody\u8217\'20\'19s private story,\u8221\'20\'1D Maitland added.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: how women reshaped the history of the Beatles\par \par \uc2 My Ticket to Ride is far from the only Beatles book released last year. But Janice Mitchell\u8217\'20\'19s memoir is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2022/mar/01/its-a-more-expansive-inclusive-version-how-women-reshaped-the-history-of-the-beatles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of the few Beatles books written by a woman}}}\uc2  in the 60 years since they released their debut single. The Beatles have profoundly shaped and enriched the lives of women, but the literature, journalism and critical scholarship \u8211\'20\'13 with a few notable exceptions \u8211\'20\'13 tends to focus disproportionately on how men experience and appreciate the band and its music.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: how one of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s most beloved animals may be close to climate extinction\par \par \uc2 When Hurricane Irma ravaged south Florida in September 2017 it inundated homes, knocked out electricity for millions of homes and killed more than 30 people. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/mar/01/florida-key-deer-endangered-climate-extinction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The devastation was not confined to humans}}}\uc2 , however. In the Florida Keys, one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s most beloved animals also took a beating: the Key deer, a small subspecies of white-tailed deer that evolved in peaceful isolation on the islands and is now protected under the Endangered Species Act, writes Jimmy Tobias for Type Investigations.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: teen who tracked \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s jet turns his attention to Russian oligarchs\par \par \uc2 The teenager known for tracking \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s jet has started to monitor the flight paths of Russian oligarchs as their movements come under increasing scrutiny following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine. In a new \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account created over the weekend, 19-year-old Jack Sweeney from Florida {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/mar/01/teen-tracks-russian-oligarchs-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has already amassed more than 230,000 followers}}}\uc2 . He said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just been crazy. I just figured some people would be interested in it. I just didn\u8217\'20\'19t think all kinds of people would be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220302ei32001p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
