\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Republicans and Joe Manchin block Senate bill to secure  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 511 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 March 2022\par 14:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats knew it would not pass but wanted the votes recorded nonetheless\par \par \uc2 A bill to enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in federal law was blocked by Senate Republicans on Monday. Although Democrats expected the bill to fail, they brought the measure forward at a perilous moment for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, to ensure votes were recorded.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected in June to decide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Mississippi case}}}\uc2  which could severely curtail or gut \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights nationally.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Democrats were 14 votes shy of the 60 needed to bring the bill to the floor for debate. Joe Manchin, of West Virginia, was the only Democrat to join Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a fundamental right and women\u8217\'20\'19s decisions over women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare belong to women, not to extremist rightwing legislators,\u8221\'20\'1D the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery American deserves to know where their senator stands on an issue as important as the right to choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In 1973, the supreme court invalidated dozens of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in its landmark Roe v Wade ruling, which found a constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy. Since then, Roe has protected women\u8217\'20\'19s right to abort a pregnancy to the point a fetus can survive outside the womb, generally regarded as 22 to 24 weeks gestation.\par \par \uc2 The bill brought before the Senate on Monday, the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act (WHPA), would codify the rights provided by Roe in federal law. Last September, it was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  by the Democrat-controlled House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight we voted in the Senate to say that Roe v Wade is the law of the land,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  of Washington state, a lead sponsor of the bill, after it failed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats stood up and said women should make their own healthcare decisions. We trust women. We trust patients. We trust their doctors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In oral arguments in the Mississippi case, justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showed an interest}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/11/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-gay-rights-contraceptives-fertility-treatments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 undermining or overturning Roe}}}\uc2 . If the conservative majority were to reverse Roe, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would effectively become a state issue. In that scenario, 26 states are expected to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately or as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 The 6-3 conservative court has already permitted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/10/texas-law-abortion-drops-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 severe restrictions}}}\uc2  in Texas, which it allowed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/sep/02/sonia-sotomayor-dissent-texas-abortion-ban-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enact a ban}}}\uc2  at six weeks, before most women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The WHPA would codify a right American women have had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for generations}}}\uc2  and block medically unnecessary restrictions. That would undo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of laws passed by right-leaning states}}}\uc2  that have sought to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more expensive and difficult to obtain, often without any medical benefit to women.\par \par \uc2 Steve Daines, a Montana Republican, called the WHPA \u8220\'20\'1Cextreme\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an egregious violation of the most fundamental of all human rights, and that is the right to life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Young women, poor women and women of color disproportionately seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans would fall heavily on such populations, forcing millions to travel hundreds of miles to seek \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and leaving others with few options except clandestine providers or unwanted pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220301ei310020b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
