\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 White nationalists are flocking to the US anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  movement\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,106 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2022\par 16:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The white supremacist and anti-choice movements have always been closely linked. But more and more, they are becoming difficult to tell apart\par \par \uc2 This weekend\u8217\'20\'19s March for Life rally, the large anti-choice demonstration held annually in Washington DC to mark the anniversary of the Roe v Wade decision, has the exuberant quality of a victory lap. This, the 49th anniversary of Roe, is likely to be its last. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  is poised to overturn Roe in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health, which is set to be decided this spring. For women in Texas, Roe has already been nullified: the court went out of its way to allow what Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  called a \u8220\'20\'1Cflagrantly unconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go into effect there, depriving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the one in 10 American women of reproductive age who live in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s second largest state.\par \par \uc2 These victories have made visible a growing cohort within the anti-choice movement: the militias and explicitly white supremacist groups of the organized far right. Like last year, this year\u8217\'20\'19s March for Life featured an appearance by Patriot Front, a white nationalist group that wears a uniform of balaclavas and khakis. The group, which also marched at a Chicago March for Life demonstration earlier this month, silently handed out cards to members of the press who tried to ask them questions. \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica belongs to its fathers, and it is owed to its sons,\u8221\'20\'1D the cards read. \u8220\'20\'1CThe restoration of American sovereignty must follow the restoration of the American Family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Explicit white nationalism, and an emphasis on conscripting white women into reproduction, is not a fringe element of the anti-choice movement. Associations between white supremacist groups and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  forces are robust and longstanding. In addition to Patriot Front, groups like the white nationalist Aryan Nations and the neo-Nazi Traditionalist Worker party have also lent support to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. These groups see stopping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of a broader project to ensure white hegemony in addition to women\u8217\'20\'19s subordination. Tim Bishop, of the Aryan Nations, noted that \u8220\'20\'1CLots of our people join [anti-choice organizations] \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s part of our Holy War for the pure Aryan race.\u8221\'20\'1D That the growing white nationalist movement would be focused on attacking women\u8217\'20\'19s rights is maybe to be expected: research has long established that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/culture/2016/12/14/13576192/alt-right-sexism-recruitment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recruitment to the alt-right}}}\uc2  happens largely among men with grievances against feminism, and that misogyny is usually the first form of rightwing radicalization.\par \par \uc2 But the affinity goes both ways: just as the alt-right loves the anti-choice movement, the anti-choice movement loves the alt-right. In 2019, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/kristen-hatten-white-nationalist_n_5acd0d5be4b0259339de14f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristen Hatten}}}\uc2 , a vice-president at the anti-choice group New Wave Feminists, shared racist content online and publicly identified herself as an \u8220\'20\'1Cethnonationalist\u8221\'20\'1D. In addition to sharing personnel, the groups share tactics. In 1985, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/anti-abortion-white-supremacy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the KKK began circulating \u8220\'20\'1CWanted\u8221\'20\'1D posters}}}\uc2  featuring the photos and personal information of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. The posters were picked up by the anti-choice terrorist group Operation Rescue in the early 90s. Now, sharing names, photos and addresses of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and clinic staff is standard practice in the mainline anti-choice movement, and the stalking and doxing of providers has become routine. More recently, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have escalated their violence, returning to the murderous extremism that characterized the movement in the 1990s: in Knoxville, a fire that burned down a planned parenthood clinic on New Year\u8217\'20\'19s Eve was ruled an arson. Maybe the anti-choice crowd is taking tips from their friends in the alt-right.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not that the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s embrace of white nationalism is totally uncomplicated. When the Traditionalist Worker party showed up at a Tennessee Right to Life march in 2018, the organizers shooed them off, and later issued a statement saying they condemned violence both from the right, and from leftwing groups like \u8220\'20\'1Cantifa\u8221\'20\'1D. Hatten was fired from her anti-choice job after a public outcry. The anti-choice movement has even started trying to appropriate the language of social justice. They posit \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/2021/10/27/abortion-equality-must-include-unborn-children/6136660001/?gnt-cfr=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 equality}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D between embryos and women, try to brand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/11/pro-life-feminists-supreme-court/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 feminist}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, incessantly compare \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.asanet.org/sites/default/files/savvy/sectionchs/documents/beisel.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Holocaust}}}\uc2 , and claim that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Can act rife with the potential for eugenic manipulation\u8221\'20\'1D, in the words of the supreme court justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2019/05/31/clarence-thomas-tried-link-abortion-eugenics-seven-historians-told-post-hes-wrong/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 . Anti-choice groups are eager to claim the moral authority of historical struggles against oppression, even as they work to further the oppression of women.\par \par \uc2 But the link between the anti-choice movement and white supremacy is much older and more fundamental than this recent, superficial social justice branding effort. Before an influx of southern and eastern European immigrants to the United States in the latter half of the 19th century, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception had only been partially and sporadically criminalized. This changed in the early 20th century, when an additional surge of migrants from Asia and Latin America calcified white American racial anxieties and led to white elites decrying the falling white birth rate as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/outlook/2019/08/27/how-white-nationalists-aligned-themselves-with-antiabortion-movement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 race suicide}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans were quickly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/outlook/2019/08/27/how-white-nationalists-aligned-themselves-with-antiabortion-movement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced nationwide}}}\uc2 . As the historian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/outlook/2019/08/27/how-white-nationalists-aligned-themselves-with-antiabortion-movement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Leslie Raegan put it}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWhite male patriotism demanded that maternity be enforced among white Protestant women.\u8221\'20\'1D The emerging popular eugenics movement supported this campaign of forced birth for \u8220\'20\'1Cfit\u8221\'20\'1D mothers, while at the same time implementing a widespread campaign of involuntary sterilization among the poor, particularly Black women and incarcerated women. Meanwhile, white women who sought out voluntary sterilization were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://books.google.com/books?id=KOuRDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT21&dq=homeland+maternity&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjX2IHE-ZTkAhW6HTQIHUiYC_kQ6AEIKjAA#v=onepage&q=husbands%E2%80%99%20consent&f=false"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discouraged}}}\uc2  or outright denied the procedure, a practice that is still mainstream in the medical field today.\par \par \uc2 In the current anti-choice and white supremacist alliance, the language of \u8220\'20\'1Crace suicide\u8221\'20\'1D has been supplanted by a similar fear: the so-called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.adl.org/resources/backgrounders/the-great-replacement-an-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Great Replacement}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, a racist conspiracy theory that posits that white Americans are being \u8220\'20\'1Creplaced\u8221\'20\'1D by people of color. (Some antisemitic variations posit that this \u8220\'20\'1Creplacement\u8221\'20\'1D is somehow being orchestrated by Jewish people.)\par \par \uc2 The way to combat this, the right says, is to force childbearing among white people, to severely restrict immigration, and to punish, via criminalization and enforced poverty, women of color. These anxieties have always animated the anti-choice movement, and they have only become more fervent among the March for Life\u8217\'20\'19s rank and file as conservatives become increasingly fixated on the demographic changes that will make America a minority-white country sometime in the coming decades. The white supremacist and anti-choice movements have always been closely linked. But more and more, they are becoming difficult to tell apart.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220124ei1o001ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
