\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden emphasizes need for Build Back Better, citing a more just tax system \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton and Joan E Greve \par \uc2 6,325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 January 2022\par 01:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President: \u8216\'20\'18Raise your hand if you think the present tax structure is fair\u8217\'20\'19Democrats seek to revive parts of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better programSenator Joe Manchin doomed the legislation last monthSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today in summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me on the west coast, here are some of the notable moments from throughout the day:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visited southern California to spotlight a bevy of investments at the federal and state levels in wildfire preparedness, response, and recovery.\par \par \uc2 * Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Black senators walked out of legislature and withheld their vote in protest of a bill that would would ban schools from teaching critical race theory.\par \par \uc2 * People are bracing for an anti-vaccine rally in Washington DC that has been largely organized on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and is expected to draw tens of thousands of people.\par \par \uc2 * Biden emphasized the need to pass Build Back Better, arguing it will help create a fairer tax system in the US. Speaking at the US Conference of Mayors\u8217\'20\'19 meeting in Washington today, Biden said it was vital that the wealthiest Americans pay their \u8220\'20\'1Cfair share\u8221\'20\'1D in taxes.\par \par \uc2 * Democrats are attempting to revive their Build Back Better Act, a month after Senator Joe Manchin announced he would oppose the legislation. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Wednesday, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident we can get pieces, big chunks of the Build Back Better law signed into law.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin has indicated Democrats will be \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting from scratch\u8221\'20\'1D in their negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Have a great weekend.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Anti-vaccine rally planned for this weekend in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 Thousands of protesters, including prolific anti-vaccine figures are expected to flood the streets of DC to protest vaccine mandates.\par \par \uc2 The event was primarily organized on the \u8220\'20\'1CDefeat the Mandates DC\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Facebook\uc2  group and on smaller far-right internet platforms. According to NBC News, hotels in Virginia are already fully booked and organizers have crowdfunded at least $200,000 ahead of the planned demonstration.\par \par \uc2 The permit for the rally was filed by the Children\u8217\'20\'19s Health Defense an anti-vaccine nonprofit founded by \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 . Dr Robert Malone, a virologist who has become a leading anti-vaccine voice is also slated to speak.\par \par \uc2 Read more ahead of the planned demonstration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/tech/internet/organized-facebook-s-anti-vaccine-activists-head-dc-rcna12806"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 A Texas man has been arrested and federally charged for allegedly threatening to kill Georgia election workers and other state officials. This is the first case brought by the Department of Justice\u8217\'20\'19s election threats task force.\par \par \uc2 According to the indictment, Chad Christopher Stark, 54, posted a message on \uc2 Craigslist\uc2  on 5 January, 2021, with the title \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia Patriots it\u8217\'20\'19s time to kill [Official A] the Chinese agent - $10,000,\u8221\'20\'1D according to an NPR report on the arrest.\par \par \uc2 These types of threats have been happening across the US since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the the 2020 election and began pushing false claims that he was cheated out of a second term due to widespread election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Read the rest of NPR\u8217\'20\'19s writeup of Stark\u8217\'20\'19s case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/01/21/1074764509/texas-man-faces-federal-charges-for-allegedly-threatening-georgia-election-offic?utm_source=twitter.com&utm_campaign=politics&utm_medium=social&utm_term=nprnews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s Black senators walked out of legislature and withheld their vote in protest of a bill that would would ban schools from teaching critical race theory.\par \par \uc2 The bill\u8217\'20\'19s chief sponsor, Michael McLendon, a Republican senator says that constituents have heard about the theory in the news and don\u8217\'20\'19t want it taught in schools, according to a Washington Post write-up of the Black senators\u8217\'20\'19 walkout. But, the state superintendent has said that critical race theory is not being taught in public schools and no one has presented evidence indicating that it has been previously.\par \par \uc2 Still, Senate bill 2113 passed by a vote of 32-2. Watch footage of the senators\u8217\'20\'19 walk out below.\par \par \uc2 enltrWALKING OUT: Mississippi's Black Senators walked out of legislature to protest a bill that would ban critical race theory. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BgRYSlTEPz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BgRYSlTEPz }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ulRck3UtRy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ulRck3UtRy }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 WLBT 3 On Your Side (@WLBT) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WLBT/status/1484607927684059142?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just wrapped up her remarks on the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s investment in wildfire preparedness and recovery in California and throughout the west.\par \par \uc2 In addition to highlighting the promise of satellites to understand and respond to blazes, and increasing pay for federal firefighters, the vice-president underscored the following:\par \par \uc2 * $600m of a $1.3bn federal grant for disaster relief will go to California\par \par \uc2 * $1bn in wildfire prevention grants that were recently approved by state lawmakers\par \par \uc2 * $5bn in wildfire preparation and response earmarked in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure bill\par \par \uc2 Harris also emphasized the need for federal, state and local collaboration to deal with fires that are increasing in frequency and intensity each season.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot respond only in reaction to a moment of harm or danger... we are our best when local, state and federal work together, hand in hand, unencumbered by partisanship or politics,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ahead of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 statements, Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  expressed his gratitude for the current administration\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to support California\u8217\'20\'19s wildfire mitigation and recovery efforts.\par \par \uc2 This is a profound, existential moment... but it\u8217\'20\'19s also a moment of optimism... These efforts means nothing without the support \u8211\'20\'13 not just financial \u8211\'20\'13 from the Biden-Harris administration,\u8221\'20\'1D Newsom said at San Bernardino county\u8217\'20\'19s Del Rosa fire station.\par \par \uc2 He also acknowledged Greenville and Paradise, two California cities that were all but obliterated by wildfires in 2021 and 2018 respectively.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Dani Anguiano recently wrote about where things stand in Greenville. Read her coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/05/greenville-california-mountain-town-destroyed-dixie-fire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/05/greenville-california-mountain-town-destroyed-dixie-fire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revisiting Greenville: the mountain town destroyed by California\u8217\'20\'19s largest wildfire }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we await \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 remarks here is some background on the setting she is in:\par \par \uc2 San Bernardino County in California\u8217\'20\'19s Inland Empire is notoriously fire-prone and has been especially hard hit by blazes including the 2020 El Dorado fire that was sparked by a pyrotechnic device used during a gender-reveal party and burned for more than three weeks.\par \par \uc2 Read my west coast colleague Gabrielle Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of that incident here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/21/couple-gender-reveal-party-wildfire-charged"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California couple whose gender-reveal party sparked a wildfire charged with 30 crimes }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  goes to San Bernardino to promote Biden administration wildfire response efforts\par \par \uc2 The vice-president came to southern California to give remarks on a $600m federal investment meant to help the state recover from unprecedentedly devastating wildfires over recent years.\par \par \uc2 Harris joined California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2  and secretary of agriculture Tom Vilsack.\par \par \uc2 Watch the livestream here:\par \par \uc2 enltrLIVE NOW: Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in San Bernardino, California, to deliver remarks on the administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to combat wildfires {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7nwP9qLw2r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7nwP9qLw2r }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1484649175706963969?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good afternoon, this is Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton blogging from sunny Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in Southern California today with Agriculture Secretary Tom Vilsack to promote the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s $3 billion investment in wildfire preparedness and response.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll have more on the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks later in the day.\par \par \uc2 A live stream of the event can be found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/watch-live-vice-president-harris-and-secretary-vilsack-speak-on-wildfire-preparedness-in-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats are attempting to revive their Build Back Better Act, a month after Senator Joe Manchin announced he would oppose the legislation. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Wednesday, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident we can get pieces, big chunks of the Build Back Better law signed into law.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin has indicated Democrats will be \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting from scratch\u8221\'20\'1D in their negotiations.\par \par \uc2 * Biden emphasized the need to pass Build Back Better, arguing it will help create a fairer tax system in the US. Speaking at the US Conference of Mayors\u8217\'20\'19 meeting in Washington today, Biden said it was vital that the wealthiest Americans pay their \u8220\'20\'1Cfair share\u8221\'20\'1D in taxes.\par \par \uc2 * Politico published a draft executive order from the Trump administration that outlines a plan to seize voting machines in battleground states. The order, which was never sent, was part of a collection of documents turned over to the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection after the supreme court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to block the documents\u8217\'20\'19 release.\par \par \uc2 * The US said Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully prepared\u8221\'20\'1D to hold a summit with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , as fears intensify over a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine. US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  met with his Russian counterpart, Sergei Lavrov, in Geneva today to continue the two countries\u8217\'20\'19 discussions over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * Biden delivered remarks on the need to boost US production of semiconductors, which power everything from cell phones to electrical grids. During the event, the CEO of Intel announced his company would invest more than $20bn to build a semiconductor production facility in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 And the Manhattan US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office, which is investigating \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s dealings in Ukraine, has now received thousands of documents from the Trump lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s devices, which were seized by investigators last April.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/giuliani-privilege-fruman-sentence/2022/01/21/1a74ecc2-7ad6-11ec-bf97-6eac6f77fba2_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The retired federal judge assigned to review the contents of 18 electronic devices seized from \uc2 Rudolph W. Giuliani\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s home and offices in Manhattan last spring has withheld about half of what former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s personal lawyer argued should be kept out of the hands of investigators because it was privileged.\par \par \uc2 More than 3,000 communications were released to prosecutors on Wednesday, an action reflected in a four-page report submitted to a judge overseeing litigation on the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s April 28 seizure of Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s phones and computers. The contents of the devices were not disclosed.\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan U.S. attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office has been investigating Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s dealings in Ukraine while he was representing Trump. Prosecutors have said Giuliani might have acted as an unregistered foreign agent, which was the basis for the agents\u8217\'20\'19 search. Giuliani, a former mayor of New York who also once headed the prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s office that now has him under a microscope, has denied any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani has also attracted the attention of the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, which issued a subpoena to the Trump ally this week.\par \par \uc2 In his statement announcing the subpoena of Giuliani and three other Trump lawyers, committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  said each person had \u8220\'20\'1Cadvanced unsupported theories about election fraud, pushed efforts to overturn the election results, or were in direct contact with the former President about attempts to stop the counting of electoral votes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/18/us-capitol-attack-committee-subpoenas-rudy-giuliani-and-other-trump-lawyers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Capitol attack committee subpoenas Rudy Giuliani and other Trump lawyers }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the National Archives has turned over hundreds of pages of documents from the Trump administration to the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, per Guardian contributor Hugo Lowell.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust in: National Archives confirms they released hundreds of pages of Trump White House documents to the Jan. 6 committee yesterday evening after the Supreme Court rejected Trump\u8217\'20\'19s executive privilege claim\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1484559027547824136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 The news comes two days after the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/19/us-capitol-riot-trump-documents-national-archives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected }}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s request to block the release of the documents based off claims of executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 The newly released documents are expected to include call logs, daily presidential diaries, handwritten notes and memos from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s top aides.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/19/us-capitol-riot-trump-documents-national-archives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court rejects Trump bid to shield documents from January 6 panel }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Draft Trump order told defense chief to seize voting machines\par \par \uc2 In the heady days between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defeat in November 2020 and the 6 January insurrection at the US Capitol, an executive order was prepared. It commanded the defense secretary to seize voting machines in battleground states, as part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D that the vote was rigged.\par \par \uc2 The draft executive order, obtained and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/01/21/read-the-never-issued-trump-order-that-would-have-seized-voting-machines-527572"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published }}}\uc2  by Politico, was never sent and its author is unknown.\par \par \uc2 It was part of a cache of documents handed over to the House committee investigating the 6 January violence, after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/19/us-capitol-riot-trump-documents-national-archives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supreme court ruled }}}\uc2  this week that Trump could not shield himself from oversight on grounds of executive privilege.\par \par \uc2 The disclosure of the draft order adds to evidence of the lengths to which Trump and his close advisers were prepared to go to keep him in the White House, against the will of the American people.\par \par \uc2 Under the draft order, the defense secretary would have been required to carry out an assessment of the voting machines \u8220\'20\'1Cno later than 60 days from commencement of operations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/21/donald-trump-voting-machines-draft-executive-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Draft Trump order told defense chief to seize swing-state voting machines }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In case you missed it yesterday: the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  declined to expedite the case over Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which bans the procedure as early as six weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/texas-53d084f9c8b2b9e3ee50df06224aaaa4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Over dissents from the three liberal justices, the court declined to order a federal appeals court to return the case to a federal judge who had temporarily blocked the law\u8217\'20\'19s enforcement. The court offered no explanation for its action.\par \par \uc2 The Texas ban is thus likely to remain in effect for the foreseeable future, following a decision by the 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals in New Orleans to send the case to the Texas Supreme Court, which is entirely controlled by Republican justices and does not have to act immediately.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/21/supreme-court-declines-to-speed-challenge-texas-abortion-limits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court declines to speed challenge to Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  limits }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , also marked the 49th anniversary of Roe v Wade during her daily briefing this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReproductive health care has been under extreme and relentless assault ever since [Roe was decided], especially in recent months,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec }}}\uc2  on 49th anniversary of Roe v. Wade ruling: "Reproductive health care has been under extreme & relentless assault ever since, especially in recent months...We're deeply committed to making sure everyone has access to care and we will defend it with every tool we have." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hQ3m8pL6wG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hQ3m8pL6wG }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1484582153526685704?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 The press secretary noted it had been nearly 150 days since the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, which bans the procedure as early as six weeks into pregnancy, went into effect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re deeply committed to making sure everyone has access to care and we will defend it with every tool we have,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 Psaki added that the Biden administration is continuing its efforts with Congress to codify Roe v Wade into law, but that goal will be extremely difficult (if not impossible) to achieve with Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 current narrow majorities in the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The theme of this year\u8217\'20\'19s March for Life was \u8220\'20\'1Cequality begins in the womb.\u8221\'20\'1D Organizers wrapped their speeches in the rhetoric of the social justice movement, arguing that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was anathema to racial and gender equality.\par \par \uc2 Jeanne Mancini, president of the March for Life Education and Defense Fund, decried Roe v Wade decision handed down by an all-male majority on the supreme court in 1973.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMurder is not a women\u8217\'20\'19s right,\u8221\'20\'1D read one sign carried by a young man in a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  beanie. Another popular sign read \u8220\'20\'1CBLM = Babies Lives Matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prochoiceamerica.org/report/new-anti-choice-feminist-branding-has-been-years-in-the-making/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo }}}\uc2  by reproductive rights organization Naral accused the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement of \u8220\'20\'1Cco-opting social justice rhetoric in order to make its extreme agenda appear more palatable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this critical moment for the future of reproductive freedom, we must call out the anti-choice movement\u8217\'20\'19s fake \u8216\'20\'18feminism\u8217\'20\'19 for what it is: a tactic for maintaining white, patriarchal control,\u8221\'20\'1D it read.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 March for Life speakers dream of post-Roe future\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Roe\u8217\'20\'19s 49th anniversary this weekend. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are hopeful it\u8217\'20\'19ll be the last.\par \par \uc2 At the annual March for Life demonstration in D.C., anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists were optimistic the Supreme Court will soon overturn Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that established a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 enltrMarch for life organizer Jeanne Mancini tells activists on the national mall that \u8220\'20\'1CRoe is not settled law.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9ujy2ZjVXH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9ujy2ZjVXH }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1484576099879247872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are hoping and praying that this year, 2022, will bring a historic change for life,\u8221\'20\'1D Jeanne Mancini, president of the March for Life Education and Defense Fund, said.\par \par \uc2 The crowd for the march was tens of thousands strong, and attendees waved signs that read: \u8220\'20\'1CI am the post-Roe generation\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe future is anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the rally, Congressman Chris Smith, a Republican from New Jersey, said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cfresh hope and heightened expectations\u8221\'20\'1D that a new conservative-supermajority on the Supreme Court would reverse Roe, overturning nearly half a century of precedent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In his speech at the US Conference of Mayors\u8217\'20\'19 meeting, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also announced a new partnership with state and local governments aimed at lowering greenhouse gas emissions from buildings.\par \par \uc2 The Hill has more details on the initiative:\par \par \uc2 According to a White House fact sheet first shared with The Hill, the partnership will include 33 state and local governments that encompass 20 percent of the country\u8217\'20\'19s building footprint and 22 percent of its population.\par \par \uc2 The fact sheet said that the initiative will \u8216\'20\'18unlock energy efficiency and electrification across the buildings sector as an engine for job creation all while lowering energy bills for consumers.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The goal of the coalition is to advance legislation or regulation in each local or state jurisdiction by Earth Day 2024.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden calls for passage of Build Back Better, citing need for fairer tax system\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  once again emphasized the need to pass the Build Back Better Act, Democrats $1.75tn spending package that includes significant investments in childcare, healthcare and climate initiatives.\par \par \uc2 The president said the bill would also establish a more just tax system in the US, arguing it was time for the wealthiest Americans to pay their \u8220\'20\'1Cfair share\u8221\'20\'1D in taxes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRaise your hand if you think the present tax structure is fair. And we\u8217\'20\'19ll take a picture of you and send it home,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden joked, prompting laughs from the crowd at the US Conference of Mayors\u8217\'20\'19 meeting.\par \par \uc2 The Build Back Better Act has stalled in the Senate due to opposition from Democrat Joe Manchin, but there were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/21/joe-biden-build-back-better-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61eac0a68f082f7fb30cd378#block-61eac0a68f082f7fb30cd378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signs of renewed energy }}}\uc2  to restart negotiations this week.\par \par \uc2 The president closed his remarks with his standard pitch about American resilience, and he applauded the mayors\u8217\'20\'19 work for their cities and towns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKeep it going, folks. We need you badly,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told the mayors.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden addresses US Conferences of Mayors\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now speaking at the US Conference of Mayors\u8217\'20\'19 90th annual winter meeting in Washington, touting the accomplishments of his first year in office.\par \par \uc2 The president specifically celebrated the passage of the bipartisan infrastructure bill, which he signed into law in November.\par \par \uc2 Biden also addressed reiterated his position on the need to increase funding for police departments, a stance that is at odds with many progressives in his party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be cutting funding for police departments,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CI proposed increasing funding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New DOJ elections threat taskforce makes first arrest after Texas man makes alleged death threats\par \par \uc2 A special Justice Department unit created to combat threats against election officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/texas-man-arrested-making-election-related-threats-government-officials#:~:text=A%20Texas%20man%20was%20arrested,carried%20out%20by%20the%20FBI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made its first arrest }}}\uc2  on Friday after a man allegedly posted threats online against Georgia election workers.\par \par \uc2 Chad Stark, a 54 year-old resident of Texas, was arrested by law enforcement after officials allege he posted a message on \uc2 Craigslist\uc2  on 5 January 2021 saying that he wanted \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia Patriots\u8221\'20\'1D to kill several election officials.\par \par \uc2 Stark was charged with one count of communicating interstate threats, which has a maximum sentence of five years in prison. He is expected to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/regulation/court-battles/590794-texas-man-arrested-for-death-threats-to-election-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his first appearance }}}\uc2  in an Austin, Texas court on Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Stark\u8217\'20\'19s arrest marks the first criminal case brought by this interagency election threats taskforce. The unit was created in June 2021 under the Biden administration to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/texas-man-arrested-making-election-related-threats-government-officials#:~:text=A%20Texas%20man%20was%20arrested,carried%20out%20by%20the%20FBI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 help address a rise in threats to election workers }}}\uc2  following the 2020 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Justice Department has a responsibility not only to protect the right to vote, but also to protect those who administer our voting systems from violence and illegal threats of violence,\u8221\'20\'1D said Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2  allies allegedly plotted to lean on Republicans to back vote audits\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/peter-stone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Stone }}}\uc2  reports for \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  agents and the House panel investigating the January 6 attack on the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  have both learned of an alleged plan by allies of retired army Lt Gen Michael Flynn to gather \u8220\'20\'1Cintelligence\u8221\'20\'1D on top {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cmove\u8221\'20\'1D them to back election audits in key states Trump lost, said ex-whistleblower Everett Stern who talked to the panel and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michael Flynn\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former national security advise Photograph: Carolyn Kaster/AP\par \par \uc2 Stern, who runs the intelligence firm Tactical Rabbit and is a Republican vying for a Senate seat in Pennsylvania, in multiple interviews with \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  said two Flynn associates with the rightwing Patriot Caucus group enlisted his help in April in a scheme to seek potentially damaging information on two Republican members of Congress to prod them to back an audit of the 2020 vote that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won.\par \par \uc2 Stern told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  he spent several hours in November telling House panel investigators about the alleged drive by Flynn associates who sought campaign finance and other dirt on Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Senator \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  and Congressman \uc2 Brian Fitzpatrick\uc2  to win their support for an audit to bolster Trump\u8217\'20\'19s debunked charges that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win was fraudulent.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 See the full story below...\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/21/michael-flynn-allies-allegedly-targeted-republicans-back-election-audits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Flynn allies allegedly plotted to lean on Republicans to back vote audits }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Democrats are attempting to revive their Build Back Better Act, a month after Senator Joe Manchin announced he would oppose the legislation. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Wednesday, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident we can get pieces, big chunks of the Build Back Better law signed into law.\u8221\'20\'1D Manchin has said Democrats will be \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting from scratch\u8221\'20\'1D in their negotiations.\par \par \uc2 * The US said Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully prepared\u8221\'20\'1D to hold a summit with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , as fears intensify over a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine. US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  met with his Russian counterpart, Sergei Lavrov, in Geneva today to continue the two countries\u8217\'20\'19 discussions over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * Biden delivered remarks on the need to boost US production of semiconductors, which power everything from cell phones to electrical grids. During the event, the CEO of Intel announced his company would invest more than $20bn in a semiconductor production facility in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  whether the White House believes certain provisions of the Build Back Better Act could attract the support of 10 Senate Republicans to overcome a potential filibuster.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou tell me,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki replied. \u8220\'20\'1CIs there a proposal where there are 10 Republicans? I\u8217\'20\'19m not aware of one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The question comes two days after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed confidence that \u8220\'20\'1Cbig chunks\u8221\'20\'1D of the Build Back Better Act could still get enacted.\par \par \uc2 That sparked questions about whether the bill would be split into several components, but that would likely mean those proposals would not be eligible for passage via reconciliation, which allows Democrats to circumvent the Senate filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Psaki seemed to indicate Democrats were still focused on passing a package via reconciliation, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the president was talking about is, we have 50 votes in the Senate. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get as much -- a big, mountain-sized chunk, whatever you want to call it -- as much as we can of the Build Back Better agenda that we can get 50 votes for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters, and she is answering questions about the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s talks with Russia amid concerns of a potential invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  met with Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Sergei Lavrov, in Geneva today to continue the discussions over Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Psaki said that Blinken communicated Russia would suffer \u8220\'20\'1Cswift and severe consequences\u8221\'20\'1D if President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  launches an invasion.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary added that, while there were no major breakthroughs in the talks today, the US is still urging Russia to pursue a path of \u8220\'20\'1Cdialogue and diplomacy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is up to them to decide which path they are going to choose,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on a clearer path to understanding each other\u8217\'20\'19s concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  discussed the importance of the US-Japanese alliance and potential responses to Russian aggression during their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/21/joe-biden-build-back-better-democrats-us-politics-live-updates?page=with:block-61eadae98f082f7fb30cd57a#block-61eadae98f082f7fb30cd57a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtual meeting this morning }}}\uc2 , the White House said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe President commended Prime Minister Kishida\u8217\'20\'19s strong commitment to the U.S.-Japan Alliance, and his determination to fundamentally strengthen Japan\u8217\'20\'19s defense capabilities to reinforce deterrence against common threats,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in its readout of the meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe leaders committed to work closely together to deter Russian aggression against Ukraine, and Prime Minister Kishida pledged to continue close coordination with the United States, other Allies and partners, and the international community on taking strong action in response to any attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The White House also noted that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cwelcomed Prime Minister Kishida\u8217\'20\'19s invitation to visit Japan for the next Quad Leaders Meeting in the first half of 2022\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  initially indicated he would not take any questions from reporters, out of concern that it would shift focus away from \uc2 Intel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement about its new semiconductor facility in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou guys will ask me all about Russia and not about anything having to do with chips,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 But one reporter was able to ask the president a question regarding today\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, specifically about how the US will source raw materials to produce semiconductor chips when much of those materials come from countries like Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot not in Afghanistan,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. He added that the US is pursuing research to identify new sources of raw materials, including some potential locations within the country.\par \par \uc2 With that, Biden walked away from the podium without taking any additional questions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  celebrated \uc2 Intel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it will invest more than $20bn to build a semiconductor production facility in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo be able to say \u8216\'20\'18made in Ohio,\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18made in America,\u8217\'20\'19 what we used to always be able to say 25, 30 years ago -- that\u8217\'20\'19s what this is about,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 The president noted that semiconductors power \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually everything in our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D including cell phones, cars and electrical grids.\par \par \uc2 Biden argued investments like \uc2 Intel\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s will allow the US to pursue a \u8220\'20\'1Cstiff economic and technological competition\u8221\'20\'1D with China, which has dedicated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/techstream/lagging-but-motivated-the-state-of-chinas-semiconductor-industry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant resources }}}\uc2  to building up its domestic semiconductor industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re better positioned than any nation -- any nation -- to seize these opportunities,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think our best days are ahead of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Intel\uc2  announces $20bn investment in Ohio semiconductor facility at White House\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now hosting an event on the need to boost US production of semiconductors, and he is joined by Intel CEO \uc2 Pat Gelsinger\uc2  and commerce secretary \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gelsinger announced that \uc2 Intel\uc2  will invest more than $20bn to build a \u8220\'20\'1Cmegasite\u8221\'20\'1D in Ohio dedicated to producing semiconductor chips.\par \par \uc2 Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s two senators, Democrat \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  and Republican Rob Portman, are present for the event as well, and Gelsinger thanked them for their support.\par \par \uc2 Gelsinger said a semiconductor factory is really more like a \u8220\'20\'1Csmall city\u8221\'20\'1D that will serve as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmagnet for the entire tech industry\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd all of this is creating new jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D Gelsinger said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2  this morning to \u8220\'20\'1Cadvance our shared vision for a free and open Indo-Pacific,\u8221\'20\'1D per the president\u8217\'20\'19s official schedule.\par \par \uc2 Biden shared a picture of the meeting on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying, \u8220\'20\'1CIt was an honor to meet with Prime Minister Kishida to further strengthen the U.S.-Japan Alliance \u8212\'20\'14 the cornerstone of peace and security in the Indo-Pacific and around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIt was an honor to meet with Prime Minister Kishida to further strengthen the U.S.-Japan Alliance \u8212\'20\'14 the cornerstone of peace and security in the Indo-Pacific and around the world. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZItwL1fvY0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZItwL1fvY0 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1484541316403023879?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During the talks in Geneva, US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  told Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Sergei Lavrov, that the White House still hopes to deescalate tensions along Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s border before an invasion occurs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my meeting with Foreign Minister Lavrov today, I stressed that Russia has two choices: Diplomacy and de-escalation or massive costs to Russia. Our strong preference is to pursue the path of diplomacy,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrIn my meeting with Foreign Minister Lavrov today, I stressed that Russia has two choices: Diplomacy and de-escalation or massive costs to Russia. Our strong preference is to pursue the path of diplomacy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/k7RT5qLzXJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/k7RT5qLzXJ }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Secretary \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  (@SecBlinken) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken/status/1484547579299966978?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 21, 2022 }}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sent a similar message yesterday, saying he has warned Putin that his country will suffer massive economic consequences if he approves an invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been absolutely clear with President Putin. He has no misunderstanding. If any -- any -- assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet there be no doubt at all that if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18fully prepared\u8217\'20\'19 to hold summit with Putin over Ukraine tensions\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger and Patrick Wintour report:\par \par \uc2 The US has said that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully prepared\u8221\'20\'1D to hold a summit with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  if it would be useful in lessening the threat to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2  posed by a continuing Russian build up of troops.\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Tony Blinken\uc2 , also said Washington and its allies were ready to respond in writing next week to Russian demands on the future of Nato and European security, which Moscow has said must be addressed to avoid it taking \u8220\'20\'1Cmilitary measures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Blinken repeated the US and Nato position there could still be no compromise on the central issue of the right of Ukraine and other countries to join Nato in the future.\par \par \uc2 The offer of a summit came after talks between Blinken and his Russian counterpart, Sergei Lavrov in Geneva, as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/19/ukraine-frontline-fear-and-defiance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weeks-long standoff over Ukraine }}}\uc2  teeters on the cusp of a pivotal and potentially violent phase, with rising concerns that Europe may again be beset by war.\par \par \uc2 In his remarks to the press afterwards, Blinken stressed it had not been a negotiation but a \u8220\'20\'1Ccandid exchange of concerns and ideas\u8221\'20\'1D, which had been \u8220\'20\'1Cfrank and substantive\u8221\'20\'1D and should lead to further talks.\par \par \uc2 Read \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/21/russia-and-us-to-meet-in-geneva-as-ukraine-war-fears-grow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18fully prepared\u8217\'20\'19 to hold summit with Putin over Ukraine tensions  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite the hurdles that a revamped Build Back Better Act would face, there seems to be some growing consensus among Democrats that the bill should focus on addressing climate change, extending Obamacare subsidies and establishing free prekindergarten.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI remain very optimistic that we can get big pieces of the plan over the finish line, including reducing the price of prescription drugs, expanding opportunity with early education, making child care more affordable [and] addressing the climate crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic Senator \uc2 Chris Van Hollen{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2022/01/20/biden-build-back-better-chunks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Washington Post }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At this point, it seems unlikely that Democrats will be able to resurrect the expanded Child Tax Credit program, which expired at the end of 2021.\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin has expressed concern about the price tag of the Build Back Better Act, and the expanded Child Tax Credit program would cost {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2021-12/57673-BBBA-GrahamSmith-Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about $1.6tn }}}\uc2  for the next ten years if it were made permanent. (The House-passed version of the Build Back Better Act only calls for extending the program for one year.)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked one year in office yesterday, and the president is struggling to enact his legislative agenda with narrow majorities in the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Senate Republicans were able to block Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill by using the filibuster, which requires 60 votes for most proposals to advance.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats then tried to amend the filibuster to create a carveout for voting rights bills, but that effort failed because two of their own members, Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 , joined Republicans in opposing the suggested change.\par \par \uc2 The failures have sparked questions over whether Biden should revamp his White House staff as he enters his second year in office.\par \par \uc2 NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/klain-under-scrutiny-biden-struggles-n1287801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 From inside the administration, some officials express concern that [White House chief of staff \uc2 Ron Klain\uc2  ] \u8216\'20\'18micromanages\u8217\'20\'19 the West Wing and gives outsize credence to cable news and social media. Some former colleagues and longtime Biden allies fret that advice they used to offer Biden directly isn\u8217\'20\'19t getting through. And on Capitol Hill, Klain has been a favorite target for Democrats, and especially Republicans, who say Biden has drifted too far to the left....\par \par \uc2 The main criticisms of Klain, whether from current or former Biden staff members or those who consider themselves allies of the president, flow from a single idea: that Biden has strayed from his core brand as a pragmatic, empathetic politician who won the Democratic nomination as a moderate willing to compromise. They see Klain as the person responsible for that. His ubiquitous presence on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  has solidified that view, particularly for those who see it as being out of step with a 2020 campaign that deliberately tuned out cable news pundits and \u8216\'20\'18blue checks\u8217\'20\'19 on social media.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At her press conference yesterday, a reporter asked House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment that Democrats will be able to pass \u8220\'20\'1Cbig chunks\u8221\'20\'1D of the Build Back Better Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, let me just say, \u8216\'20\'18chunks\u8217\'20\'19 is an interesting word,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi replied.\par \par \uc2 She added, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure that we can agree upon something significant. Call it a chunk if you want. But, whatever you call it, we want it to be able to make a difference in transforming the workplace by honoring work, by respecting the fact that there are families that have to make decisions between home and work, and, again, protecting the planet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Pelosi emphasized that the bill will still need to be passed via reconciliation in order to avoid a filibuster in the Senate, which may make it more difficult to split it up into multiple components.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are big chunks of the bill that have to be contained in the bill,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut remember this. This is a reconciliation bill. So when people say let\u8217\'20\'19s divide it up \u8211\'20\'13 nah. No, they don\u8217\'20\'19t understand the process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats attempt to revive 'chunks' of Build Back Better\par \par \uc2 Greetings, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are attempting to revive components of their Build Back Better Act, the $1.75tn spending package that includes massive investments in childcare, healthcare and climate initiatives.\par \par \uc2 A version of the bill passed the House, but the legislation stalled in the Senate after Joe Manchin announced his opposition last month.\par \par \uc2 Now, Manchin seems open to the idea of restarting the negotiations over the bill, telling reporters yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll just be starting from scratch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Manchin speaks to reporters after voting at the US Capitol. Photograph: Elizabeth Frantz/Reuters\par \par \uc2 Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s comments came after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  voiced confidence that Democrats will be able to get some of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s most significant provisions signed into law.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m confident we can get pieces, big chunks of the Build Back Better law signed into law,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said at his press conference on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 However, the changes that Manchin will likely demand may spark criticism among progressives in Congress, and Democrats can afford very few defections if they want to get a bill across the finish line.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220121ei1l0028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
