\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden warns Russia will \u8216\'20\'18pay a heavy price\u8217\'20\'19 if Putin launches Ukraine invasion \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 7,164 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 January 2022\par 00:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President clarifies comments from Wednesday on Ukraine-RussiaVolodymyr Zelenskiy criticizes Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18minor incursions\u8217\'20\'19 remarkMitch McConnell condemned for comments about Black votersDemocrats fail to advance voting rights bill in SenateSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  clarified his comments about a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine, after the president appeared to downplay the threat of a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D into Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CIf any \u8211\'20\'13 any \u8211\'20\'13 assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet there be no doubt at all that, if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden\u8217\'20\'19s initial comments about Ukraine had set off a flurry of criticism and a frantic clean-up effort by White House officials. The president of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2 , said in response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations. Just as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  issued sanctions against four Ukrainian officials believed to be involved in a Russian conspiracy to discredit Zelensky\u8217\'20\'19s government. \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has directed its intelligence services to recruit current and former Ukrainian government officials to prepare to take over the government of Ukraine and to control Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical infrastructure with an occupying Russian force,\u8221\'20\'1D the Treasury statement accompanying the sanctions said.\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection requested the voluntary cooperation of \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 . According to the letter sent by committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , investigators are seeking information from \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to pressure \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to attempt to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate failed to pass Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill or approve a change to the filibuster, underscoring the significant challenges that Biden faces in enacting his legislative agenda. During yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Senate session, the voting rights bill failed along party lines, while Democrats \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  joined their Republican colleagues in opposing a change to the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 * The Supreme Court rejected the latest bid by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19 law banning abortions as early as six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 when many people do not even know they are pregnant. In a dissent, justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, for the fourth time, this court declines to protect pregnant Texans from egregious violations of their constitutional rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court rejected the latest bid by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19 law banning abortions as early as six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 when many people do not even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 In a dissent, justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CToday, for the fourth time, this court declines to protect pregnant Texans from egregious violations of their constitutional rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In December, the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/22/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed}}}\uc2  the Texas anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, one of the strictest in the US, to remain in place, but left open the possibility of future challenges. The law encourages anyone to sue people suspected of providing or facilitating abortions, effectively giving rise to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounty hunters. It has led to an 80% reduction in abortions in state, Texas clinics say.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnce again the supreme court has betrayed the people of Texas, who have been callously stripped of their constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than four months now,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president of Planned Parenthood Federation of America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Setbacks for Biden at home and abroad as he marks challenging year in office\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on Thursday marked a year since his inauguration as president obliged to confront the same urgent crises he inherited when he took the oath of office: an unrelenting pandemic, economic uncertainty and a democracy threatened by partisan division and lies.\par \par \uc2 But now those challenges have been compounded by a string of setbacks, both at home and abroad, that have eroded confidence in his leadership.\par \par \uc2 In his first public appearance of the day, 12 months on from the one where he swept \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  out of the White House, Biden was in a position of having to clarify loose remarks he made the day before about a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 During a marathon press conference on Wednesday afternoon to mark the anniversary of his presidency, Biden alarmed Kyiv by appearing to suggest that allies were divided over how to respond should a move by Moscow be a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, speaking at the White House, he said \u8220\'20\'1Cany\u8221\'20\'1D Russian movement across the Ukrainian border would be met with a \u8220\'20\'1Csevere and coordinated economic response\u8221\'20\'1D from Nato. He also vowed a response should Russia \u8220\'20\'1Cuse measures other than overt military actions\u8221\'20\'1D, such as \u8220\'20\'1Cparamilitary tactics\u8221\'20\'1D and other methods of warfare.\par \par \uc2 Warning the Russian president, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CLet there be no doubt at all: if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s clarification came after the Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  tweeted in English and Ukrainian: \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations. Just as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden made the initial remarks at a Wednesday press conference, during which he also mounted a nearly two-hour defense of his first year in office. He insisted that the administration had handled the coronavirus \u8220\'20\'1Cremarkably well\u8221\'20\'1D, noting that tens of millions of Americans had been fully vaccinated. On the economy, he touted record low unemployment, and outlined his plans for taming inflation and alleviating supply chain bottlenecks.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/20/biden-russia-ukraine-presidency-anniversary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Setbacks for Biden at home and abroad as he marks challenging year in office}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  clarified his comments about a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine, after the president appeared to downplay the threat of a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D into Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CIf any \u8211\'20\'13 any \u8211\'20\'13 assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet there be no doubt at all that, if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden\u8217\'20\'19s initial comments about Ukraine had set off a flurry of criticism and a frantic clean-up effort by White House officials. The president of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said in response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations. Just as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  issued sanctions against four Ukrainian officials believed to be involved in a Russian conspiracy to discredit Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s government. \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has directed its intelligence services to recruit current and former Ukrainian government officials to prepare to take over the government of Ukraine and to control Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical infrastructure with an occupying Russian force,\u8221\'20\'1D the Treasury statement accompanying the sanctions said.\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection requested the voluntary cooperation of \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 . According to the letter sent by committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , investigators are seeking information from \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to pressure \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to attempt to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 * The Senate failed to pass Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill or approve a change to the filibuster, underscoring the significant challenges that Biden faces in enacting his legislative agenda. During yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Senate session, the voting rights bill failed along party lines, while Democrats \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  joined their Republican colleagues in opposing a change to the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  seemed to suggest that she did not have any relevant information to share with the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Committee already knows, Ivanka did not speak at the January 6 rally,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said in a statement provided to CBS News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs she publicly stated that day at 3:15 pm, \u8216\'20\'18any security breach or disrespect to our law enforcement is unacceptable. The violence must stop immediately. Please be peaceful.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNew- Statement from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IvankaTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @IvankaTrump}}}\uc2  Spokesperson to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CBSNews}}}\uc2  on January 6th committee request to cooperate w/its inquiry. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rSGG2EpgMn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rSGG2EpgMn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Fin G\u243\'00\'F3mez (@finnygo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/finnygo/status/1484243057277030404?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 However, in his letter to \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  specifically said the panel is interested in any conversations she had with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 So even though \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  did not speak at the January 6 rally that preceded the insurrection, it is still quite likely that she has relevant information for the investigation.\par \par \uc2 The statement makes it seem even less likely that \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  will voluntarily agree to cooperate with the select committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Jamie Raskin, a member of the House select committee investigating the Capitol insurrection, said \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  could be a \u8220\'20\'1Cmaterial fact witness\u8221\'20\'1D for the panel\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the former president has no executive privilege to hide evidence of an attempted coup or insurrection, neither do his family or friends,\u8221\'20\'1D the Maryland congressman said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  was with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the attack unfolded, she is a material fact witness. I look forward to her testimony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrIf the former president has no executive privilege to hide evidence of an attempted coup or insurrection, neither do his family or friends. If \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  was with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the attack unfolded, she is a material fact witness. I look forward to her testimony.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Jamie Raskin (@RepRaskin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRaskin/status/1484263661334110211?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the letter that committee chairman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2  sent to \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2 , the panel is seeking information she may have about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to pressure \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to attempt to overturn the results of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs January 6th approached, President Trump attempted on multiple occasions to persuade Vice President Pence to participate in his plan,\u8221\'20\'1D Thompson said in the letter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the President\u8217\'20\'19s discussions with the Vice President occurred by phone on the morning of January 6th. You were present in the Oval Office and observed at least one side of that telephone conversation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thompson also requested information from \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  on \u8220\'20\'1Cany other conversations you may have witnessed or participated in regarding the President\u8217\'20\'19s plan to obstruct or impede the counting of electoral votes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  asked to cooperate with Capitol attack committee\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack is asking {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ivanka-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivanka Trump}}}\uc2 , the daughter of the former president, to appear for a voluntary deposition to answer questions about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to stop the certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 The move by the panel marks an aggressive new phase in its inquiry into the 6 January insurrection, as House investigators seek for the first time testimony from a member of the Trump family about potential criminality on the part of the former president.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Select Committee is requesting that \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  provide information for the committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigation.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Ms. Trump seeking a voluntary interview, Chair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BennieGThompson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BennieGThompson}}}\uc2  underscored evidence that Trump was in direct contact with the former President on Jan 6th.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 January 6th Committee (@January6thCmte)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/January6thCmte/status/1484215368877019138?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the chair of the select committee, said in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://january6th.house.gov/sites/democrats.january6th.house.gov/files/2022-1-20.BGT%20Letter%20to%20Ivanka%20Trump%20-%20Cover%20Letter%20and%20Enclosures_Redacted%202.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an 11-page letter to Ivanka Trump}}}\uc2  that the panel wanted to ask about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan to stop the certification, and his response to the Capitol attack, including delays to deploying the national guard.\par \par \uc2 The questions to Ivanka appear directed at a key issue: whether her father {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/08/capitol-attack-committee-donald-trump-white-house-stop-biden-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oversaw a criminal conspiracy}}}\uc2  on 6 January that also involved obstructing a congressional proceeding \u8211\'20\'13 a crime.\par \par \uc2 The letter said that the panel first wanted to question \uc2 Ivanka Trump\uc2  about what she recalled of a heated Oval Office meeting on the morning of the 6 January insurrection when the former president was trying to co-opt \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  into rejecting Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win.\par \par \uc2 Read \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/20/ivanka-trump-capitol-attack-committee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ivanka Trump asked to cooperate with Capitol attack committee}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , the White House press secretary, pointed to the Treasury Department\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?page=with:block-61e9c0508f085e8f4015b8a5#block-61e9c0508f085e8f4015b8a5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newly announced sanctions}}}\uc2  against four Ukrainian officials as an example of how the US is proactively responding to Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not waiting to take action to counter Russia. We see what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing. We\u8217\'20\'19re disrupting it,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said at her daily briefing this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd these actions are also of course separate and distinct from the broad range of high-impact, severe measures we and our allies are prepared to impose in order to inflict significant costs should they invade.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrPsaki says the U.S. is not waiting to take action against Russia over troop buildup on the Ukraine border after the Treasury Department announced sanctions against supposed Russian spies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/676DFgKgHT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/676DFgKgHT}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/X0J53QwFM9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/X0J53QwFM9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bloomberg Quicktake (@Quicktake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Quicktake/status/1484253325314953222?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US accuses Russia of conspiring to take over Ukraine government\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger, Luke Harding and Andrew Roth report:\par \par \uc2 The US has alleged that Russian intelligence is recruiting current and former Ukrainian government officials to take over the government in Kyiv and cooperate with a Russian occupying force.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  on Thursday imposed sanctions on two Ukrainian members of parliament and two former officials it said were involved in the alleged conspiracy, which involved discrediting the current government of the president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/volodymyr-zelenskiy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has directed its intelligence services to recruit current and former Ukrainian government officials to prepare to take over the government of Ukraine and to control Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s critical infrastructure with an occupying Russian force,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0562"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Treasury statement}}}\uc2  accompanying the sanctions said.\par \par \uc2 The claims suggest US intelligence fears Russia is preparing a full-scale invasion and not the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/19/russia-could-act-against-ukraine-at-any-moment-says-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  referred to as a possibility in remarks on Wednesday that triggered alarm in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Online researchers have identified Russian troops and military vehicles within just ten miles of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s borders, increasing the risk that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could launch a military offensive on short notice.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/20/us-russia-ukraine-government-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US accuses Russia of conspiring to take over Ukraine government}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As she wrapped up her daily briefing, White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  plans to do more press conferences in the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStay tuned,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki replied. \u8220\'20\'1CBuckle up, bring snacks next time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press conference yesterday lasted nearly two hours, after the president decided to extend the event by calling on reporters who were not on the original list provided to him by his staff.\par \par \uc2 After taking questions for about an hour and a half, Biden looked at his watch and decided to keep talking for another 20 minutes -- likely to the chagrin of his press staff.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  for further clarification on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments about the possibility of Russia executing a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6#block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 minor incursion}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D into Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The president has since sought to clear up those comments, saying this morning, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been absolutely clear with President Putin. He has no misunderstanding. If any -- any -- assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki said Biden was making the point yesterday that the US and its allies have \u8220\'20\'1Ca range of tools\u8221\'20\'1D to respond to Russian aggression, which may take the form of paramilitary tactics like cyberattacks.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary also addressed Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comment that there are \u8220\'20\'1Cdifferences in Nato as to what countries are willing to do, depending on what happens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been focused on ensuring that we remain united with Nato,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow united doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that everything will be identical, right? It means we\u8217\'20\'19re united in taking actions should they decide to invade. And we are united.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A reporter pressed \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  again on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments yesterday about the legitimacy of the upcoming 2022 elections in the face of new voting restrictions in many states.\par \par \uc2 The reporter, Peter Alexander of NBC News, noted that Biden said yesterday, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to say it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be legit. The increase and the prospect of being illegitimate is in direct proportion to us not being able to get these reforms passed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked if Pres. Biden is confident that the midterm elections will be legitimate even if federal voting rights legislation doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass Congress, White House press sec. \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  says \u8220\'20\'1Cyes.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y5SVieyPLg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Y5SVieyPLg}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zsZXFgD41T"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zsZXFgD41T}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1484243323720282115?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Alexander asked Psaki, \u8220\'20\'1CYes or no: does the president believe, if all remains as it is right now, that the elections this fall will be legitimate?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki replied, \u8220\'20\'1CYes, but the point that he was making was that, as recently as 2020 as we know, the former president was trying to work with local officials to overturn the vote count and not have ballots counted. And we have to be very eyes wide open about that and clear-eyed that that is the intention potentially of him and certainly of members of his party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alexander then asked for clarification that Biden is confident in the legitimacy of the upcoming elections if no changes are made in voting rights legislation moving forward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki responded.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing, and she is continuing her efforts to clean up some of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comments from his press conference yesterday.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked Psaki whether Biden has confidence in the legitimacy of the 2022 elections, as Democrats struggle to pass their voting rights bill.\par \par \uc2 During his press conference, Biden was asked whether he had faith in the legitimacy of the upcoming midterm elections if Democrats are unable to pass their bill.\par \par \uc2 Biden responded, \u8220\'20\'1CIt all depends on whether or not we\u8217\'20\'19re able to make the case to the American people that some of this is being set up to try to alter the outcome of the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Psaki reiterated that Biden was not intending to cast doubt upon the legitimacy of the 2022 election but was instead making a point about how the 2020 election would have been illegitimate if election officials had cooperated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s demands to overturn the results in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The press secretary made the same point over \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this morning:\par \par \uc2 enltrLets be clear: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @potus}}}\uc2  was not casting doubt on the legitimacy of the 2022 election. He was making the opposite point: In 2020, a record number of voters turned out in the face of a pandemic, and election officials made sure they could vote and have those votes counted.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1484166808894640131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is attracting intense criticism for his comments about Black voters, which he made last night after Republican senators blocked Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill (again).\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61e96f748f08cd8f34646199#block-61e96f748f08cd8f34646199"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after the bill failed}}}\uc2  and the Senate rejected a change to the filibuster, McConnell was asked for his message to minority voters who are concerned that they will not be able to vote unless the Democratic bill is enacted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe concern is misplaced, because if you look at the statistics, African-American voters are voting in just as high a percentage as Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D McConnell said.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LeaderMcConnell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LeaderMcConnell}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe concern is misplaced, because if you look at the statistics, African-American voters are voting in just as high a percentage as American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yikes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WXR1WCZh5T"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WXR1WCZh5T}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 BG (@TheBGates) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheBGates/status/1484208681482960905?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That comment sparked a lot of confusion among those who pointed out that African American voters are, in fact, Americans.\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Bobby Rush called out McConnell\u8217\'20\'19s comment, saying in a tweet, \u8220\'20\'1CAfrican Americans ARE Americans. #MitchPlease\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also worth noting that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/impact-voter-suppression-communities-color"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 studies indicate}}}\uc2  the voting restrictions enacted by 19 states in the past year will disproportionately impact voters of color.\par \par \uc2 enltrAfrican Americans ARE Americans. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MitchPlease?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MitchPlease}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/N3dSsQ9Jqn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/N3dSsQ9Jqn}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SRnTTVJdJ4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SRnTTVJdJ4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bobby L. Rush\uc2  (@RepBobbyRush)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepBobbyRush/status/1484233883130511366?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  arrested outside Capitol amid voting rights protests - report\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators are right now outside the US Capitol demanding action to protect voting rights and election integrity in the US, following the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/19/voting-rights-senate-democrats-filibuster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resounding refusal}}}\uc2 , once again, to pass legislation on this issue last night.\par \par \uc2 New York congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 . Photograph: Eduardo Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz/AP\par \par \uc2 New York first-term Democratic congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  appears to have been arrested as part of the protests in Washington, DC.\par \par \uc2 enltrRep. \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  was arrested outside the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  as part of a voting rights protest, per his spox: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HXOAi9rcqf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HXOAi9rcqf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nicholas Wu (@nicholaswu12) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nicholaswu12/status/1484220984819392513?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 His office has reported that at least 20 others were arrested, including \u8220\'20\'1Cfaith leaders and youth who have been hunger striking for our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D according to spokesman Marcus Frias.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamaalBowmanNY?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JamaalBowmanNY}}}\uc2  engages and thanks a group of of us fighting for voting rights outside the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CapitolPolice}}}\uc2  cuff him and put him under arrest with the group. Thanks for always standing with the people! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/VotingRightsNow?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #VotingRightsNow}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LetsUnpac?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @LetsUnpac}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/peoplefor?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @peoplefor}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Py2YHNAMUL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Py2YHNAMUL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Markus Batchelor (@MarkusforDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarkusforDC/status/1484222934717808644?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Demonstrators began gathering around midday, which is the time 12 months ago when Biden\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration began on the Capitol front overlooking the crowds on the national mall.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Young people on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HungerStrike4Democracy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HungerStrike4Democracy}}}\uc2  and activists are risking arrest in front of the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  RIGHT NOW condemning the Senate for failing to pass the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/FreedomToVote?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #FreedomToVote}}}\uc2  John Lewis Act! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xi7FQLbMGu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xi7FQLbMGu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Un-PAC (@LetsUnpac) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LetsUnpac/status/1484209849617559556?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Capitol Police\uc2  also put out a statement via \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CJust before 12:00 pm, demonstrators started blocking one side of the North Barricade outside the U.S. Capitol. We have already issued them three warnings. The demonstrators refused to move out of the driveway, so we are making arrests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJust before 12:00 pm, demonstrators started blocking one side of the North Barricade outside the U.S. Capitol.\par \par \uc2 We have already issued them three warnings.\par \par \uc2 The demonstrators refused to move out of the driveway, so we are making arrests. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GqlmyGQ1KD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GqlmyGQ1KD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1484217634258309126?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here is one protester\u8217\'20\'19s tweet:\par \par \uc2 enltrOut here protesting for voting rights and \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2  just got arrested with us!\par \par \uc2 Also I just got arrested lol\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barred and Boujee (@AudreLawdAMercy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AudreLawdAMercy/status/1484216826011729926?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia DA requests grand jury to investigate Trump efforts\par \par \uc2 The district attorney for Fulton county, Georgia, \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , is requesting a special grand jury to aid in her investigation of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election results, when he was still president but had lost the race to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , a new report this afternoon reveals.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County Georgia District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  photographed in her office on Tuesday, Jan. 4, 2022. The prosecutor weighing whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others committed crimes by trying to pressure Georgia officials to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential election victory said a decision on whether to bring charges could come as early as the first half of this year. Photograph: Ben Gray/AP\par \par \uc2 The news {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/news/atlanta-news/breaking-fulton-da-requests-special-grand-jury-for-trump-probe/E5HCDM2P75ETRAEUHBK2Q7L3FY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been broken}}}\uc2  by the Atlanta Journal-Constitution, so that newspaper can take up the story about the prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s actions:\par \par \uc2 In a Thursday letter to \uc2 Christopher S. Brasher\uc2 , chief judge of Fulton County\u8217\'20\'19s Superior Court, Willis said the move was needed because a \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant number of witnesses and prospective witnesses have refused to cooperate with the investigation absent a subpoena requiring their testimony.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She cited comments Secretary of State \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  made during an October 2021 interview with NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Chuck Todd, in which he said \u8220\'20\'1Cif she wants to interview me, there\u8217\'20\'19s a process for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So-called special purpose grand juries are rarely used in Georgia but could be a valuable tool for Willis as she takes the extraordinary step of investigating the conduct of a president while he was in office.\par \par \uc2 Her probe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/fultons-da-opens-criminal-investigation-into-trump-demand-to-overturn-election/YWJPS4B4BREHDLHQCZYDDWBVIA/?d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched in February}}}\uc2 , is centered on the Jan. 2 phone call Trump placed to Raffensperger, in which he urged the Republican to \u8220\'20\'1Cfind\u8221\'20\'1D the votes to reverse \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s win in Georgia in November 2020.\par \par \uc2 Special grand juries, which typically have 16 to 23 members, can\u8217\'20\'19t issue indictments. But they can subpoena witnesses, compel the production of documents, inspect and enter into certain offices for the purposes of the investigation.\par \par \uc2 Willis said a special grand jury would be beneficial because jurors can be impaneled for a longer period and would be focused on the one probe. A regular Fulton County grand jury is seated for two months. Jurors typically hear hundreds of felony cases before their service ends.\par \par \uc2 The DA also requested that a Fulton County superior court judge be assigned to assist and supervise the special grand jury in carrying out its investigation and duties.\par \par \uc2 Willis\u8217\'20\'19 request {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://law.justia.com/codes/georgia/2020/title-15/chapter-12/article-4/part-2/section-15-12-100/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must be approved}}}\uc2  by a majority of the county\u8217\'20\'19s superior court judges.\par \par \uc2 This is a developing story.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  clarified his comments about a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine, after the president appeared to downplay the threat of a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D into Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CIf any -- any -- assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet there be no doubt at all that, if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * Biden\u8217\'20\'19s initial comments about Ukraine had set off a flurry of criticism and a frantic clean-up effort by White House officials. The president of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said in response to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations. Just as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 * The Senate failed to pass Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill or approve a change to the filibuster, underscoring the significant challenges that Biden faces in enacting his legislative agenda. During yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Senate session, the voting rights bill failed along party lines, while Democrats \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  joined their Republican colleagues in opposing a change to the filibuster.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While emphasizing the severe consequences that Russia will suffer if \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  launches a full-scale invasion of Ukraine, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  noted that the US and its allies are also prepared to respond to other forms of Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia has a long history of using measures other than overt military action to carry out aggression and paramilitary tactics, so-called gray zone attacks and actions by Russian soldiers not wearing Russian uniforms,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told reporters at the start of his infrastructure meeting.\par \par \uc2 The president added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to be ready to respond to these as well in a decisively united way with the range of tools at our disposal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that the Ukrainian foreign minister has indicated confidence in America\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to protecting Ukraine, and he echoed that assessment.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ukraines-foreign-minister-says-bidens-minor-incursion-comment-invites-russian-attack-11642686159"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CWe in Ukraine have no doubt that President Biden is committed to Ukraine \u8230\'20\'26 and he wants to prevent the conflict and deter Russia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Kuleba also issued a warning about the danger of downplaying any threat from Russia, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe should not give Putin the slightest chance to play with quasi-aggression or small incursion operations. This aggression was there since 2014. This is the fact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden clarifies Ukraine comments: 'Russia will pay a heavy price' for invasion\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  sought to clarify his comments from yesterday about a potential Russian invasion of Ukraine, after the US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6#block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared to downplay}}}\uc2  the threat of a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D into Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the start of a meeting on infrastructure, Biden told reporters moments ago, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been absolutely clear with President Putin. He has no misunderstanding. If any -- any -- assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden said such an invasion would be met with a \u8220\'20\'1Csevere and coordinated economic response,\u8221\'20\'1D which he has \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed in detail with our allies as well as laid out very clearly for President Putin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added, \u8220\'20\'1CBut there is no doubt \u8212\'20\'14 let there be no doubt at all that, if Putin makes this choice, Russia will pay a heavy price.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"I've been absolutely clear with President Putin...If any, any assembled Russian units move across the Ukrainian border, that is an invasion," Pres. Biden says. "It will be met with severe and coordinated economic response." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aWy2ej1jCo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aWy2ej1jCo}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z5d2pDVEnw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z5d2pDVEnw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1484206319620042753?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments come one day after he seemed to imply that Nato was at odds over how to respond to Russian aggression depending upon the type of attack that was launched against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see is that Russia will be held accountable if it invades,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at his press conference yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it depends on what it does. It\u8217\'20\'19s one thing if it\u8217\'20\'19s a minor incursion and then we end up having a fight about what to do and not do, et cetera.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That comment required a coordinated clean-up effort from Biden administration officials, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?page=with:block-61e984f58f08215096bfca1d#block-61e984f58f08215096bfca1d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/20/biden-presidency-democrats-senate-voting-rights-trump-live-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6#block-61e97bad8f080fbff79debb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jen Psaki}}}\uc2 , the White House press secretary, seeking to clarify that the US and its allies are united in responding to Russian aggression.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'There are no minor incursions,' Ukrainian president says after Biden's flub\par \par \uc2 The president of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , delivered some thinly veiled criticism of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s remarks yesterday about a potential Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones. I say this as the President of a great power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWe want to remind the great powers that there are no minor incursions and small nations. Just as there are no minor casualties and little grief from the loss of loved ones. I say this as the President of a great power ????\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1484171183264129025?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 That appeared to be a direct reference to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comment at his press conference yesterday, when the US president outlined the various responses that Nato is considering if Russia escalates its aggression toward Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see is that Russia will be held accountable if it invades,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it depends on what it does. It\u8217\'20\'19s one thing if it\u8217\'20\'19s a minor incursion and then we end up having a fight about what to do and not do, et cetera.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden and his aides later tried to clarify that he was attempting to distinguish between an actual invasion and other threats against Ukraine, such as cyberattacks.\par \par \uc2 However, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s flippant remark has clearly sparked some anxiety among Ukrainian officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has joined in on the White House\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to repair \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s flub on Ukraine in his press conference on Wednesday, where he revealed Nato is divided on how to respond to a \u8220\'20\'1Cminor incursion\u8221\'20\'1D from Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president of the United States has been very clear, and we as the United States are very clear: if Putin takes aggressive action, we are prepared to levy serious and severe costs. Period,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in a Thursday morning appearance on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Today Show.\par \par \uc2 Host Savannah Guthrie countered that the White House had been \u8220\'20\'1Cless than clear\u8221\'20\'1D, issuing a statement just minutes after Biden\u8217\'20\'19s press conference affirming the \u8220\'20\'1Cunited response\u8221\'20\'1D between the US and its allies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSavannah, I\u8217\'20\'19m being clear with you right now. If you\u8217\'20\'19re interested, I\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to be clear,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in response.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe President has been very clear \u8230\'20\'26 if Putin takes aggressive action, we are prepared to levy serious and severe costs.\u8221\'20\'1D - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VP}}}\uc2  Kamala Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hMcmceE0A3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hMcmceE0A3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 TODAY (@TODAYshow) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TODAYshow/status/1484136998222839810?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 During his press conference yesterday, Biden said there were \u8220\'20\'1Cdifferences in Nato as to what countries are willing to do, depending on what happens\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris went on the defense for Biden when Guthrie asked how \u8220\'20\'1Cdamaging\u8221\'20\'1D it was that Biden \u8220\'20\'1Copenly talked about division within Nato countries and Nato allies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think your audience knows {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  has been working as the former head of foreign relations, and as the former vice-president and a senator in a role of leadership on foreign policy, for years,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have witnessed him continuously engage in direct and honest conversations with our partners and allies, and this is no exception.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/20/kamala-harris-ukraine-joe-biden-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris insists US will respond aggressively on Ukraine after Biden flub}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden faces backlash after downplaying 'minor incursion' into Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  held a nearly two-hour-long press conference yesterday, taking questions from dozens of reporters as he marked one year in office.\par \par \uc2 One answer that the president gave in response to a question about Ukraine is attracting a lot of attention (and often scorn) both at home and abroad.\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked the president about whether he believed the threatened economic sanctions against Russia would be enough to deter \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  from approving an invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see is that Russia will be held accountable if it invades,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 He then added, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it depends on what it does. It\u8217\'20\'19s one thing if it\u8217\'20\'19s a minor incursion and then we end up having a fight about what to do and not do, et cetera.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBIDEN: "It's one thing if it's a minor incursion\u8230\'20\'26But if they actually do what they're capable of doing\u8230\'20\'26it is going to be a disaster for Russia\u8230\'20\'26The cost\u8230\'20\'26in terms of physical loss of life for the Russians, they will be able to prevail over time. But it's going to be heavy." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xqSJIHmZQU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xqSJIHmZQU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JM Rieger (@RiegerReport) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RiegerReport/status/1483919997042929666?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 19, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden later clarified that he was distinguishing between Russia actually moving troops across Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s border and the Kremlin continuing to launch cyberattacks on its neighbor.\par \par \uc2 But the comment sparked fears that Biden was essentially giving Putin permission to launch an invasion, prompting White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  to release a statement further clarifying his position last night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden has been clear with the Russian President: If any Russian military forces move across the Ukrainian border, that\u8217\'20\'19s a renewed invasion, and it will be met with a swift, severe, and united response from the United States and our Allies,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden also knows from long experience that the Russians have an extensive playbook of aggression short of military action, including cyberattacks and paramilitary tactics. And he affirmed today that those acts of Russian aggression will be met with a decisive, reciprocal, and united response.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  sharply criticized Senate Republicans for blocking Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill, which passed the House in a party-line vote last week.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Monday, our nation celebrated the birthday of civil rights hero \uc2 Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr\uc2 . for his courage, leadership and sacrifice for our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D the House speaker said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, Senate Republicans have dishonored his leadership and legacy by blocking passage of urgently needed legislation to protect voting rights and our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOn Monday, our nation celebrated the birthday of civil rights hero \uc2 Dr. Martin Luther King, Jr\uc2 . Last night, Senate Republicans dishonored his leadership and legacy by blocking passage of urgently needed legislation to protect voting rights and our democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1484171561762500615?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Pelosi described the voting restrictions that have been enacted in 19 states over the past year, combined with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbig lie\u8221\'20\'1D of widespread voter fraud in the 2020 election, as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most severe and sinister threat to our democracy since the era of Jim Crow\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYet, an arcane Senate Rule \u8211\'20\'13 one that clearly conflicts with the intentions of our Founders and has long been used to block progress on civil rights \u8211\'20\'13 continues to stand in the way of enacting this vital legislation,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the fight for voting rights, nothing less than our democracy is at stake. Democrats will never relent in our mission to safeguard the sacred right to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights proposals have failed in the Senate before, but Wednesday marks the first time senators have taken a formal vote on changing the filibuster. Its likely failure marks a profound setback for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential agenda.\par \par \uc2 The president spent an enormous amount of political capital in recent weeks pressuring Senators \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  to support rule changes to the filibuster, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/11/joe-biden-to-back-filibuster-rule-change-to-push-voting-rights-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  giving a speech in Atlanta}}}\uc2  and traveling to Capitol Hill to try to get support.\par \par \uc2 In stirring remarks just before the vote on the voting rights bill, \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , a Democrat from Georgia, said senators could not praise the legacy of \uc2 Dr Martin Luther King, Jr\uc2  while voting against voting rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot remember MLK and dismember his legacy at the same time,\u8221\'20\'1D Warnock said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not sit quietly while some make Dr King a victim of identity theft.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The bill that failed on Wednesday, Freedom to Vote: \uc2 John R Lewis\uc2  Act, combined two major voting rights bills into a single mega bill.\par \par \uc2 It would have set a national baseline for election access, guaranteeing 15 days of early voting as well as online voter registration. It protected local election officials from harassment and partisan interference in their jobs and curbed gerrymandering, the severe distortion of partisan district lines.\par \par \uc2 It also restored a key piece of the 1965 Voting Rights Act that required places with a history of voting discrimination to get their changes approved by either the justice department or a federal court in Washington before they go into effect.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/19/voting-rights-senate-democrats-filibuster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats fail to advance voting rights law as Senate holdouts defend filibuster}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  expressed severe disappointment in the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s failure to pass Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill or amend the filibuster for the legislation.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released after the votes, the president condemned the \u8220\'20\'1Cunprecedented effort to suppress the sacred right to vote\u8221\'20\'1D unfolding in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state legislatures across the country}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the face of those threats, I am profoundly disappointed that the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  has failed to stand up for our democracy. I am disappointed \u8212\'20\'14 but I am not deterred,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 enltrI am profoundly disappointed that the Senate has failed to stand up for our democracy. I am disappointed \u8212\'20\'14 but I am not deterred.\par \par \uc2 We will continue to advance necessary legislation and push for Senate procedural changes that will protect the fundamental right to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1484008266116050948?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The president pledged that his administration would continue its efforts to protect voting rights and strengthen election systems, even in the face of the demoralizing defeat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy Administration will never stop fighting to ensure that the heart and soul of our democracy \u8212\'20\'14 the right to vote \u8212\'20\'14 is protected at all costs,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs dangerous new Republican laws plainly designed to suppress and subvert voting rights proliferate in states across the country, we will explore every measure and use every tool at our disposal to stand up for democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Filibuster failure shows Biden's struggle to enact agenda\par \par \uc2 Greetings, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats suffered painful failures on two fronts last night \u8211\'20\'13 first on voting rights and then on filibuster reform.\par \par \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill failed to advance because of a Republican filibuster, which requires 60 votes for legislation to move forward.\par \par \uc2 The final vote on the voting rights bill was 49-51, with every Republican voting against the proposal. (Majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  changed his vote from \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D because that will allow him to bring up the matter again later.)\par \par \uc2 enltrBy a vote of 49-51, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Senate?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Senate}}}\uc2  did not invoke cloture on the motion to concur in the House amendment to the Senate amendment to H.R.5746.\par \par \uc2 ML Schumer switched his vote from yes to no in order to enter a motion to reconsider the vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Senate Press Gallery (@SenatePress)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenatePress/status/1483982277185097730?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 20, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Senate then voted on a rule change that would have allowed the voting rights legislation to circumvent the traditional legislative filibuster.\par \par \uc2 That measure was defeated in a vote of 48 to 52, with Democrats \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  joining their Republican colleagues in opposing the proposal.\par \par \uc2 The results of the votes demonstrate that challenges that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  faces in enacting his agenda, as he marks one year since he took office.\par \par \uc2 With a 50-50 Senate, it will be extremely difficult to pass another other major bills before the midterm elections. And if Democrats cannot enact their agenda, they will likely face some angry voters in November.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 2022-01-20T14:35:11Z 2022-01-21T00:33:38Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/1d99262c62f26c6b111b18e5b397479015e74088/0_40_3447_2068/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/1d99262c62f26c6b111b18e5b397479015e74088/0_40_3447_2068/500.jpg}}}\uc2  New York congressman \uc2 Jamaal Bowman\uc2 . Fulton County Georgia District Attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  photographed in her office on Tuesday, Jan. 4, 2022. The prosecutor weighing whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and others committed crimes by trying to pressure Georgia officials to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential election victory said a decision on whether to bring charges could come as early as the first half of this year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220120ei1k002ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
