\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US \u8216\'20\'18concerned\u8217\'20\'19 Russia preparing for an invasion in Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Johana Bhuiyan, Gloria Oladipo and Joan E Greve \par \uc2 8,401 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 January 2022\par 01:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 White House: feared invasion \u8216\'20\'18may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes\u8217\'20\'19Biden pledges to improve US bridges and water and create jobs via infrastructure billUS to start shipping free at-home Covid tests next weekSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Politics recap\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from us today.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened:\par \par \uc2 * The White House warned Russia is preparing a false flag operation to justify an invasion of Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that the Russian government is preparing for an invasion in Ukraine that may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes, should diplomacy fail to meet their objectives,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the federalgovernment will pay 100% of the costs to repair small bridges in communities with limited funds to do so. The policy is part of the implementation of the bipartisan infrastructure law, which Biden signed in November. The law includes $27.5bn to repair the nation\u8217\'20\'19s bridges.\par \par \uc2 * Biden acknowledged this has been a disappointing few weeks for Democrats, after the party suffered defeats on a voting rights bill and the Build Back Better Act. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of talk about disappointments on things we haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot of them done, I might add.\u8221\'20\'1D His comments came one day after Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin indicated they would not support changing the filibuster to pass a voting rights bill, killing any hope of a swift passage for the legislation.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration will start shipping free at-home Covid tests next week. Biden announced last month that his administration would order 500 m at-home tests to be given free of charge to Americans, and the president has since announced the purchase of an additional 500m tests.\par \par \uc2 * The Ohio supreme court struck down the congressional map drawn by Republican legislators, which would have given the party a significant advantage in the midterm elections. Writing for the majority in his ruling, Justice Michael Donnelly, a Democrat, argued the proposed map had violated the Ohio state constitution, which forbids district lines that unfairly favor one party or its incumbents.\par \par \uc2 * Stewart Rhodes, the founder of far-right militia group the Oathkeepers pleaded not guilty to seditious conspiracy this afternoon after being arrested in Plano, TX on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 * Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg and Google CEO \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  were allegedly aware of and approved a deal to collaborate on the potential manipulation of advertising sales, according to newly unredacted documents that were filed as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/google-misled-publishers-and-advertisers-unredacted-lawsuit-alleges-11642176036?mod=Searchresults_pos1&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state attorneys general-led lawsuit against Google. }}}\par \par \uc2 * More than 40 states have appealed a decision to throw out an antitrust lawsuit against \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , arguing it\u8217\'20\'19s in the public interest for the attorneys general to pursue the case. Judge \uc2 James E Boasberg\uc2  dismissed the lawsuit last June because it was filed too long after \uc2 Facebook\uc2  made the acquisitions that are in question in the complaint.\par \par \uc2 See you again next week!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has appointed actress Star Jones to serve on the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/tag/u-s-commission-for-the-preservation-of-americas-heritage-abroad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Commission for the Preservation of America\u8217\'20\'19s Heritage Abroad}}}\uc2 . The agency is in charge of identifying monuments, cemeteries, and historic buildings in Eastern and Central Europe that are associated with US heritage.\par \par \uc2 From Deadline\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2022/01/star-jones-joe-biden-u-s-commission-1234913188/amp/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 story}}}\uc2  on the appointment: \u8220\'20\'1CBiden also appointed six others to the commission, including G Jonathan Greenwald, Nicole Mavis Isaac, Nancy Kaufman, Michael Marquardt, Maureen Pikarski and Bill Shaheen.\par \par \uc2 The commission was set up to ensure that such sites \u8211\'20\'13 historically important for populations impacted by Nazism and communism \u8211\'20\'13 are preserved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jones is also scheduled to replace Faith Jenkins as the judge on the television show Divorce Court this fall.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 States ask judge to reconsider antitrust case against \uc2 Facebook\par \par \uc2 More than 40 states have appealed a judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision to throw out an antitrust lawsuit against \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  is reporting.\par \par \uc2 Last June, Judge \uc2 James E Boasberg\uc2  dismissed the lawsuit because it was filed too long after \uc2 Facebook\uc2  made the acquisitions that are in question in the complaint.\par \par \uc2 In their appeal, the states attorneys generals, led by New York\u8217\'20\'19s Letitia James, argue that they should have more latitude than private individuals when it comes to limitations on filing lawsuits. They also said it was in the public interest to pursue the case against the social media giant.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit scrutinizes \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s acquisition of photo-sharing app \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and messaging service WhatsApp in 2012 and 2014, respectively. The lawsuit alleges the acquisitions were predatory and were done in order to crush competition and that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  further worked to harm competitors, including video-sharing platform Vine, by cutting off their access to data and tools on \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s platform.\par \par \uc2 Read more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/14/technology/facebook-antitrust-case.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 DirecTV\uc2  is dropping conservative news channel, One America News Network, according to Bloomberg News. The network is known for spreading misinformation and was one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favorite channels during his presidency. \uc2 DirecTV\uc2  notified OANN owner Herring Networks Inc. that it would not carry the channel once the contract is up in early April, according to the Bloomberg report. It\u8217\'20\'19s a major blow to OANN, oh which \uc2 DirecTV\uc2  is the largest distributor.\par \par \uc2 From the story: \u8220\'20\'1CThe channel is still carried on Verizon FiOS and smaller pay-TV providers, according to its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oann.com/wheretowatch/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2 . The broadcast can also be streamed via an online-TV service called KlowdTV. OANN has never been carried by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/CMCSA:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Comcast Corp.}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/CHTR:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charter Communications Inc.}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/DISH:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dish Network Corp.}}}\uc2 , three other major providers.\par \par \uc2 DirecTV\uc2 , which is owned by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/T:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AT&T Inc.}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/TPG:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TPG}}}\uc2  via a joint venture, has offered OANN to customers since April 2017 after Herring Networks won a lawsuit that forced the satellite-TV provider to carry the channels.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-01-14/directv-to-drop-one-america-news-in-blow-to-conservative-channel?sref=6flipp83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here. }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Lawsuit alleges \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  CEOs approved deal on ad manipulation\par \par \uc2 Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg and Google CEO \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  were allegedly aware of and approved a deal to collaborate on the potential manipulation of advertising sales, according to newly unredacted documents that were filed as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/google-misled-publishers-and-advertisers-unredacted-lawsuit-alleges-11642176036?mod=Searchresults_pos1&page=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state attorneys general-led lawsuit against Google. }}}\uc2  The lawsuit was first filed in December 2020 and claimed \uc2 Google\uc2  misled publishers and advertisers alike about the price and process of advertising auctions. At that time, many documents and parts of the lawsuit were redacted but have since become accessible to the public as a result of multiple court rulings.\par \par \uc2 While the lawsuit is not new, details about how much both companies\u8217\'20\'19 C-Suite was aware of and whether they approved the coordination between \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  had not been known previously.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP, the lawsuit indicates that in a 2018 email thread Facebook\u8217\'20\'19s chief operating officer, \uc2 Sheryl Sandberg\uc2 , called the collaboration between the companies \u8220\'20\'1C a big deal strategically\u8221\'20\'1D. Zuckerberg was included on that and other threads discussing the deal, the lawsuit says.\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  have seen increased scrutiny over potentially monopolistic practices from both regulators and other players in the market. In this case, the lawsuit alleges \uc2 Google\uc2  maintained control over the advertising sales market - a market that it dominates - by inflating the price of advertisements for brands and suppressing competition from other advertising exchanges.\par \par \uc2 According to the Wall Street Journal, the complaint alleges \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Google\uc2  pocketed the difference between what it told publishers and advertisers that an ad cost and used the pool of money to manipulate future auctions to expand its digital monopoly.\u8221\'20\'1D The documents further cite internal messages in which \uc2 Google\uc2  employees said it was like they were using \u8220\'20\'1Cinsider information\u8221\'20\'1D to grow the business.\par \par \uc2 If Pichai is found to have personally approved the deal, he may be found to be complicit in the expansion of \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s monopoly over the advertising market through manipulation. A Google spokesperson told the AP that while the deal was not a secret, it was inaccurate Pichai approved it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe sign hundreds of agreements every year that don\u8217\'20\'19t require CEO approval, and this was no different,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?221+ful+HB781"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill}}}\uc2  to ban the teaching of \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive concepts\u8221\'20\'1D in schools in Virginia ran into ridicule when among historical events deemed suitable for study, it described a nonexistent debate between Abraham Lincoln and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2018/oct/28/david-blight-on-frederick-douglass-i-call-him-beautifully-human"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Frederick Douglass}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lincoln did engage in a series of historic debates hinged on the issue of slavery, in the Illinois Senate campaign of 1858. But he did so against Stephen Douglas, a senator who had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/75d7c8729ab5f7a5c4399386f676cb28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ties to slavery}}}\uc2 , and not against Douglass, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2018/oct/28/david-blight-on-frederick-douglass-i-call-him-beautifully-human"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great campaigner}}}\uc2  for the abolition of slavery who was once enslaved himself.\par \par \uc2 The Virginia bill was sponsored by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/local/virginia-politics/wren-williams-virginia-republican-house/2021/06/24/4f5e6ff2-cf8d-11eb-8cd2-4e95230cfac2_story.html?itid=lk_inline_manual_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wren Williams}}}\uc2 , a freshman Republican sent to Richmond in a tumultuous November election.\par \par \uc2 History has become a divisive concept in states across the US, as rightwingers spread alarm about the teaching of race issues. In November, the winning candidate for governor in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Virginia}}}\uc2 , the Republican Glenn Youngkin, made history a wedge issue in his win over the Democrat, \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Youngkin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/03/republicans-critical-race-theory-winning-electoral-issue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seized upon critical race theory}}}\uc2 , an academic discipline that examines the ways in which racism operates in US laws and society \u8211\'20\'13 but which is not taught in Virginia schools.\par \par \uc2 The elementary error in Williams\u8217\'20\'19s bill attracted national attention, including from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/history/2022/01/14/virginia-lincoln-douglas-frederick-douglass/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 . However, reports that the bill had been withdrawn were in error, a spokesperson for the politician said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://townhall.com/tipsheet/rebeccadowns/2022/01/14/author-of-bill-against-crt-discusses-honest-mistake-of-inaccurate-point-lincoln-d-n2601843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided}}}\uc2  to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  a statement from the Virginia division of legislative services, which said the error \u8220\'20\'1Cwas inserted at the drafting level, following receipt of a historically accurate request from the office of Delegate Wren Williams\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Williams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://townhall.com/tipsheet/rebeccadowns/2022/01/14/author-of-bill-against-crt-discusses-honest-mistake-of-inaccurate-point-lincoln-d-n2601843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Townhall.com}}}\uc2  he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfrustrated\u8221\'20\'1D but realised \u8220\'20\'1Cmistakes happen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, many were happy to point out the error.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNew rule,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1482002764788027396"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote Steve Vladeck}}}\uc2 , a University of Texas law professor. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you don\u8217\'20\'19t know the difference between Frederick Douglass and Stephen Douglas, you don\u8217\'20\'19t get to tell anyone else what to teach.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sidney Blumenthal, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sidneyblumenthal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian contributor}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/08/sidney-blumenthal-lincoln-politics-trump-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lincoln biographer}}}\uc2 , pointed out that Lincoln and Douglass did meet three times when Lincoln was president, from 1861 to 1865 and through a civil war that ended with slavery abolished.\par \par \uc2 Blumenthal also offered a way in which students in Virginia and elsewhere might use Douglass\u8217\'20\'19s life and work to examine divisive concepts today.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after two centrist Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/13/kyrsten-sinema-democrats-filibuster-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sank Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s push for voting rights reform}}}\uc2 , Blumenthal said: \u8220\'20\'1CFrederick Douglass\u8217\'20\'19s great cause became that of voting rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there is any debate that is going on now, it is not between Lincoln and Frederick Douglass. It is between Frederick Douglass and all the Republican senators who refuse to support voting rights \u8211\'20\'13 and Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For further reading, here\u8217\'20\'19s Ibram X Kendi on why Frederick Douglass matters:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2018/jul/05/frederick-douglass-andrew-johnson-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why Frederick Douglass's struggle for justice is relevant in the Trump era | Ibram X Kendi}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group that had an advertisement signed and endorsed by Amy Coney Barrett before she became a supreme court justice has been accused of encouraging the harassment of doctors, according to my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from her story:\par \par \uc2 An Indiana group whose anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign was endorsed in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed advertisement by Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  before she became a supreme court justice, keeps a published list of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their place of work on its website, in what some experts say is an invitation to harass and intimidate the doctors and their staff.\par \par \uc2 In one case, court records show, a doctor whose name was published by the group, which is called Right to Life Michiana, was warned by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  of a kidnapping threat that had been made online against her daughter.\par \par \uc2 The threat prompted the doctor to temporarily stop providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services at the Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health Care clinic in South Bend, which is also named on the Michiana group\u8217\'20\'19s website. The doctor said in the court document that the clinic regularly attracts large gatherings of protesters, who she feared could identify her.\par \par \uc2 Barrett signed a two-page advertisement in 2006, while she was working as a professor at Notre Dame, that stated that those who signed \u8220\'20\'1Coppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand and defend the right to life from fertilization to natural death\u8221\'20\'1D. The second page of the ad called Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbarbaric\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The advertisement, which was published in the South Bend Tribune and signed by hundreds of people, was sponsored by a group called St Joseph County Right to Life, which merged with another anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group in 2020 and is now called Right to Life Michiana.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to rule this year on challenges to Roe v Wade that many court experts expect will gut the rights of women in the US to obtain legal abortions. In arguments before the court, Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 who has said her personal views do not affect her legal judgment \u8211\'20\'13 argued that passage of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/12/what-are-safe-haven-laws-supreme-court-case-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe haven laws}}}\uc2 , which allow parents to relinquish their newborns at hospitals or other designated centers without the threat of legal consequences, had in effect given women options outside of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for those who did not want to become parents.\par \par \uc2 During her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rev.com/blog/transcripts/amy-coney-barrett-senate-confirmation-hearing-day-2-transcript"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 confirmation hearing}}}\uc2 , Barrett said she had signed the advertisement as a private citizen, while she was making her way out of church, and had not recalled signing it until it became public following a report in \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was consistent with the views of my church,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, in response to senators\u8217\'20\'19 questions about the statement. She later added: \u8220\'20\'1CI do see as distinct my personal, moral, religious views and my task of applying the law as a judge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/14/anti-abortion-group-indiana-amy-coney-barrett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Group whose anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ad Amy Barrett signed accused of promoting harassment of doctors}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Johana here, reporting in from San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 The founder of far-right militia group the Oathkeepers pleaded not guilty to seditious conspiracy this afternoon. Elmer Stewart Rhodes was arrested on Thursday in Texas and charged with conspiring with 10 others to oppose the transfer of presidential power by force.\par \par \uc2 enltrNOW: Stewart Rhodes, founder of far-right Oath Keepers militia group, entered a not guilty plea to seditious conspiracy in a Plano federal courtroom on Friday.\par \par \uc2 His attorneys will argue for his release from custody in a hearing on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 He faces 20yrs in prison. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCDFW?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCDFW}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/spGJXyqXX7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/spGJXyqXX7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Goins (@dgoins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dgoins/status/1482107972037877773?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As my {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/14/oath-keepers-leader-charges-armed-plot-us-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  colleague Sergio Olmos reported}}}\uc2 , unsealed court documents have revealed evidence of an armed plot as well as detailed tactical pre-planning that included \u8220\'20\'1Cthe creation of rapid-response teams of armed militia members, the deployment of tactical gear and the stockpiling of weapons\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More from Sergio\u8217\'20\'19s reporting:\par \par \uc2 The Oath Keepers even discussed a naval operation to ferry in guns to the militia. One Oath Keeper, Thomas Caldwell, asked fellow members if anyone had a boat that could handle crossing the Potomac River. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we had someone standing by at a dock ramp (one near the Pentagon for sure) we could have our Quick Response Team with the heavy weapons standing by, quickly load them and ferry them across the river to our waiting arms,\u8221\'20\'1D the documents quoted him as saying.\par \par \uc2 Rhodes went on a buying spree in the days leading up to the attack, spending more than $20,000 on guns and equipment for the attack. In December, Rhodes bought two pairs of night-vision goggles and a weapons sight for about $7,000 and shipped them to Virginia. In January he spent another $5,000 on a shotgun, scope, magazine, sights, optics, a bipod, a mount, a case of ammunition and gun cleaning supplies. Two days later he spent $6,000 more, and then about $4,500 the next day.\par \par \uc2 In group chats, the Oath Keepers discussed how their quick reaction force (QRF) teams would set up at the Comfort Inn in Ballston Arlington, Virginia, to \u8220\'20\'1Cuse as its base of operations for January 6, 2021\u8221\'20\'1D. They reserved three rooms; one was occupied by the so-called North Carolina \u8220\'20\'1CQRF\u8221\'20\'1D team while Arizona and Florida \u8220\'20\'1CQRF teams\u8221\'20\'1D stayed in the two others. They used the hotel rooms to store firearms and ammunition.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Johana Bhuiyan, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The White House warned Russia is preparing a false flag operation to justify an invasion of Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that the Russian government is preparing for an invasion in Ukraine that may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes, should diplomacy fail to meet their objectives,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the federalgovernment will pay 100% of the costs to repair small bridges in communities with limited funds to do so. The policy is part of the implementation of the bipartisan infrastructure law, which Biden signed in November. The law includes $27.5bn to repair the nation\u8217\'20\'19s bridges.\par \par \uc2 * Biden acknowledged this has been a disappointing few weeks for Democrats, after the party suffered defeats on a voting rights bill and the Build Back Better Act. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of talk about disappointments on things we haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot of them done, I might add.\u8221\'20\'1D His comments came one day after Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin indicated they would not support changing the filibuster to pass a voting rights bill, killing any hope of a swift passage for the legislation.\par \par \uc2 * The Biden administration will start shipping free at-home Covid tests next week. Biden announced last month that his administration would order 500 m at-home tests to be given free of charge to Americans, and the president has since announced the purchase of an additional 500m tests.\par \par \uc2 * The Ohio supreme court struck down the congressional map drawn by Republican legislators, which would have given the party a significant advantage in the midterm elections. Writing for the majority in his ruling, justice Michael Donnelly, a Democrat, argued the proposed map had violated the Ohio state constitution, which forbids district lines that unfairly favor one party or its incumbents.\par \par \uc2 Johana will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pence attacks Democrats' voting rights bill as 'federal power grab'\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has penned a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2022/01/14/mike-pence-filibuster-nationalize-elections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post op-ed}}}\uc2  attacking Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 voting rights bill as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfederal power grab over our state elections\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former vice-president opened the op-ed by reflecting on the January 6 insurrection, which he witnessed firsthand. Pence was at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  that day to preside over the congressional certification of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow that the anniversary of Jan. 6 has come and gone, some of us who lived through that tragic day in 2021 are getting a clearer picture of what was and is at stake,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence writes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Jan. 6, an angry mob ransacked the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 , largely to try to get Congress and me, as the president of the Senate, to use federal authority to overturn results of the presidential election that had been certified by all 50 states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Pence then makes an argument that is certain to outrage Democrats; the Republican asserts that the dozens of voting restrictions recently approved by state legislatures are an effort to \u8220\'20\'1Crestore confidence in the integrity of our elections while ensuring access to voting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite this steady progress of state-based reforms, now come President Biden and Senate Democrats with plans to use the memory of Jan. 6 to attempt another federal power grab over our state elections and drive a wedge further into our divided nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence writes.\par \par \uc2 In 2021, 19 states passed 34 laws restricting access to voting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Brennan Center for Justice}}}\uc2 . Voting rights advocates warn that the restrictions disproportionately impact people of color, and experts say the laws threaten to inject partisan bias into election systems.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhiteHouse/status/1482072718208081920"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  on delivering free at-home Covid tests starting 19 January underscores the current difficulty of finding affordable at-home Covid-19 tests.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Carly Olsen wrote about price gouging happening across the country for rapid at-home Covid tests:\par \par \uc2 With at-home Covid tests running scarce during the Omicron surge, the price gouging has begun, and everyone from restaurants to pet food stores appear to be trying to cash in.\par \par \uc2 Recent reporting by Vice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/wxdxnb/restaurants-are-price-gouging-rapid-tests-on-food-delivery-apps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found a}}}\uc2  Manhattan deli advertised an Abbott BinaxNOW rapid test (retail: $24) on the Seamless delivery app for $80. Meanwhile, an online-only pet store, Pet Foods by Village Farm, offered to deliver the same type of test for $50, and a liquor store was selling a \u8220\'20\'1CCovid fighter pack\u8221\'20\'1D, including rapid tests and hand sanitizer, for more than $100.\par \par \uc2 There have been reports across the country of vendors charging double or triple the normal costs of at-home Covid tests. One New York restaurant worker paid $180 for four test kits, the \uc2 Los Angeles Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2022-01-05/rapid-covid-tests-are-reselling-for-triple-the-retail-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . And a Covid testing site in San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s Mission district is reportedly charging between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeremyR1992/status/1478451048029118469"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $99 and $250 for rapid tests}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Authorities have warned that this is a growing problem. In a December statement, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2  attorney general, Letitia James, encouraged people to report price hikes. \u8220\'20\'1CFraudsters are on notice that if they attempt to price gouge during this new surge, we will not hesitate to take action,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that her office had already seen reports of test kits \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing unlawfully sold for more than $40 and up to $70 per package\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/07/covid-rapid-test-price-gouging-omicron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden administration will start shipping free at-home Covid tests next week\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration will begin shipping {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.covidtests.gov/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  free at-home Covid tests starting next week}}}\uc2 , following an announcement earlier last week that the tests would become more widely available amid the Omicron surge.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden admin to start offering free at-home Covid tests on Jan. 19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/koIrIOHKr9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/koIrIOHKr9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 POLITICO Pro (@POLITICOPro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POLITICOPro/status/1482083379902394371?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The tests will be available through a government website starting on 19 January, though receiving the tests could take longer. Shipping for the at-home tests typically takes \u8220\'20\'1Cseven to 12 days\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/white-house/biden-administration-start-shipping-free-home-covid-tests-next-week-n1287539"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  according to senior official in the Biden administration. }}}\uc2  Additionally, households will only able to order four tests at a time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more background on at-home test availability according to a piece from Politco:\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official told reporters the government has 420 million tests under contract and tens of millions already in its possession. Officials are finalizing contracts for the 80 million tests remaining out of an initial order of 500 million. The effort to procure and distribute the tests will have a total cost of about $4 billion.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the government can meet demand as soon as the website goes live, the senior administration official said the Biden administration is confident \u8220\'20\'1Cthat we can meet all of our timelines and get these to all Americans that want them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full piece {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/01/14/biden-free-at-home-covid-tests-527131"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Following the Ohio Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strike the state\u8217\'20\'19s new congressional districts on Friday, questions remain about what the next steps are for the legislative maps.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an article from Jessie Balmert of the Columbus Dispatch that breaks down the next steps following the court\u8217\'20\'19s decision:\par \par \uc2 Now, the commission has 10 days to get back together, craft new maps and approve them. If the maps receive bipartisan support from two Democrats and at least two Republicans, they could last for 10 years. If they are passed along party lines again, they would last for four years.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio Supreme Court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/2022/01/13/key-takeaways-ohio-supreme-court-legislative-redistricting/9198392002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in its 4-3 decision}}}\uc2 , made clear that the commission must follow all of the voter-approved changes to the Ohio Constitution to curb gerrymandering. That includes Section 6, which required the commission to attempt to match the statewide voting preferences of Ohioans.\par \par \uc2 Justice Melody Stewart, writing for the majority, defined Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s statewide preferences as about 54% of voters preferring GOP candidates and about 46% preferring Democratic candidates over the past decade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe commission is required to attempt to draw a plan in which the statewide proportion of Republican-leaning districts to Democratic-leaning districts closely corresponds to those percentages,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 Senate President Matt Huffman, R-Lima, said he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet read the decision himself. \u8220\'20\'1COur lawyers are trying to figure out what it will take for us to comply with whatever it is that the court ordered.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dispatch.com/story/news/politics/2022/01/13/ohio-supreme-court-struck-down-legislative-maps-what-comes-next/6510994001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Ohio supreme court ordered the state\u8217\'20\'19s general assembly to redraw more maps that complied with the partisan fairness requirements in the Ohio constitution. It also denounced the consequences of gerrymandering.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGerrymandering is the antithetical perversion of representative democracy. It is an abuse of power,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice Michael Donnelly, a Democrat. \u8220\'20\'1CIts singular allure is that it locks in the controlling party\u8217\'20\'19s political power while locking out any other party or executive office from serving as a check and balance to power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the dealer stacks the deck in advance, the house usually wins,\u8221\'20\'1D he also wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThat perhaps explains how a party that generally musters no more than 55 percent of the statewide popular vote is positioned to reliably win anywhere from 75 percent to 80 percent of the seats in the Ohio congressional delegation. By any rational measure, that skewed result just does not add up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ohio Republicans had insisted that the districts they drew were competitive, but the majority of justices said that requirement appears nowhere in the constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ohio supreme court strikes down gerrymandered congressional map\par \par \uc2 The Ohio supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.ohio.gov/rod/docs/pdf/0/2022/2022-Ohio-89.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down}}}\uc2  the state\u8217\'20\'19s new congressional districts on Friday, saying they were so egregiously distorted to benefit Republicans that they violated the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 The 4-3 ruling marked the first time during the 2021 redistricting cycle where new congressional districts have been blocked. Republicans had been poised to win 12 of the state\u8217\'20\'19s 15 congressional districts, in a state where Republicans usually win a little more than half of the statewide vote.\par \par \uc2 Writing for the majority, Justice Michael Donnelly, a Democrat, wrote that the map violated a provision of the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution that says districts can\u8217\'20\'19t be drawn in a way that \u8220\'20\'1Cunduly favorsor disfavors a political party or its incumbents.\u8221\'20\'1D The districts also violated a provision that says districts can\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cunduly\u8221\'20\'1D split counties.\par \par \uc2 Voters amended the state constitution to add those provisions in 2018 along with a new procedure meant to foster bipartisanship in redistricting. This is the first redistricting cycle that they are in effect.\par \par \uc2 Republicans made little attempt to abide by them. The decision comes days after the court struck down new GOP-drawn state legislative districts for similar reasons.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republican senator who \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  called a \u8220\'20\'1Cmoron\u8221\'20\'1D in a congressional hearing wants to introduce a bill both targeting and named after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief White House adviser.\par \par \uc2 Roger Marshall of Kansas will introduce the \u8220\'20\'1CFinancial Accountability for Uniquely Compensated Individuals [Fauci \u8211\'20\'13 geddit] Act\u8221\'20\'1D, after claiming Fauci\u8217\'20\'19s financial records were not readily accessible to the public.\par \par \uc2 The senator attacked Fauci on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand why you\u8217\'20\'19re asking me that question,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fauci, 81. \u8220\'20\'1CMy financial disclosure is public knowledge and has been so for the last 37 years or so.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CAll you have to do is ask for it. You\u8217\'20\'19re so misinformed, it\u8217\'20\'19s extraordinary.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fauci was then heard on a \u8220\'20\'1Chot mic\u8221\'20\'1D to say: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a moron. Jesus Christ.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHOT MIC MOMENT: After clashing with GOP Sen. Roger Marshall, Dr. Fauci was caught muttering, "what a moron," followed by "Jesus Christ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/merKU3BGAJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/merKU3BGAJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mediaite (@Mediaite) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mediaite/status/1480976894589906950?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Marshall repeated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/11/us-covid-hospitalizations-record-number-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack lines pursued}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  of Kentucky \u8211\'20\'13 producing another confrontation with Fauci, and said: \u8220\'20\'1CCalling me a moron during a Senate hearing may have alleviated the stress of the least trusted bureaucrat in America, but it didn\u8217\'20\'19t take away from the facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Center for Public Integrity\uc2  subsequently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://publicintegrity.org/health/coronavirus-and-inequality/analysis-fauci-finances-public-easier-find/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  Marshall was wrong, but that Fauci\u8217\'20\'19s records were not easy to obtain.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/11/us-covid-hospitalizations-record-number-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fauci clashes with Rand Paul at Senate hearing as daily Covid cases soar}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Third anti-Trump Republican to retire\par \par \uc2 Another House Republican who voted to impeach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will retire at the next election.\par \par \uc2 John Katko\uc2 . Photograph: Reuters\par \par \uc2 John Katko\uc2  of New York follows \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  of Illinois and \uc2 Anthony Gonzalez\uc2  of Ohio in deciding to step down rather than take on a Trump-endorsed challenger for his seat.\par \par \uc2 Seven other House Republicans voted to impeach Trump for inciting the insurrection at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  on 6 January, around which five people died and over which more than 725 people have been charged, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/13/oath-keepers-capitol-attack-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 11 of them, yesterday, with sedition}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That made it the most bipartisan impeachment. Trump escaped conviction, however, when only seven Republican senators could be convinced to vote for his guilt.\par \par \uc2 The most prominent among the 10 members of the House who voted for impeachment is \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , like Kinzinger a member of the select committee investigating 6 January, thereby confronting and infuriating pro-Trump party leaders. Cheney faces a Trump-backed primary challenger in Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CatieEdmondson/status/1482030331956166656"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , Katko said he was retiring so he could \u8220\'20\'1Cenjoy my family and life in a fuller and more present way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * The White House warned Russia is preparing a false flag operation to justify an invasion of Ukraine. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that the Russian government is preparing for an invasion in Ukraine that may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes, should diplomacy fail to meet their objectives,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced the federalgovernment will pay 100% of the costs to repair small bridges in communities with limited funds to do so. The policy is part of the implementation of the bipartisan infrastructure law, which Biden signed in November. The law includes $27.5bn to repair the nation\u8217\'20\'19s bridges.\par \par \uc2 * Biden acknowledged this has been a disappointing few weeks for Democrats, after the party suffered defeats on a voting rights bill and the Build Back Better Act. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of talk about disappointments on things we haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot of them done.\u8221\'20\'1D His comments came one day after Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin indicated they would not support changing the filibuster to pass a voting rights bill, killing any hope of a swift passage for the legislation.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden announces federal government will pay 100% of costs to repair small bridges\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  touted that the bipartisan infrastructure law includes funding for the largest investment in the country\u8217\'20\'19s bridges since the creation of the interstate highway system.\par \par \uc2 The president noted there are currently 45,000 bridges in the US that are in poor condition and need repairs, resulting in longer commutes for millions of Americans.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden announces federal government will pay 100% for repairing small bridges nationwide, getting rid of requirement for counties and towns to share the costs\par \par \uc2 "With this investment, we're sending a message to those communities and to the people who call them home \u8212\'20\'14 you matter" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ubiQKFjPCs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ubiQKFjPCs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1482056306051661826?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 As part of the infrastructure law, the federal government will spend $27.5bn to repair those bridges. Biden also announced that the federal government will pay 100% of the costs to repair small bridges in communities with limited funds to do so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith this investment, we\u8217\'20\'19re sending a message to those communities and to the people who call them home: you matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese investments are consequential, and we\u8217\'20\'19re just getting started.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president then concluded his prepared remarks, and he walked away from the podium without taking any questions from reporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  emphasized that the bipartisan infrastructure law will help to create good-paying jobs for Americans, in addition to improving roads and bridges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we invest in infrastructure, we\u8217\'20\'19re really investing in opportunity,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are investments that will build a better America. It sounds like hyperbole, but it\u8217\'20\'19s real.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that many Americans have written to him explaining how the country\u8217\'20\'19s failing infrastructure has personally impacted them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hear you,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou do matter to me, and we are going to get it done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'There's a lot of talk about disappointments,' Biden says after voting rights defeat\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now delivering remarks on the implementation of the bipartisan infrastructure law, which he signed in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of talk about disappointments on things we haven\u8217\'20\'19t gotten done. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get a lot of them done, I might add,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at the top of his remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut this is something we did get done, and it\u8217\'20\'19s of enormous consequence to the country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of the infrastructure law.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech comes one day after he acknowledged Democrats may not be able to pass a voting rights bill, after Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin said they would not support changing the filibuster to do so.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden: "There's a lot of talk about disappointments and things we haven't gotten done -- we're gonna get a lot of them done, I might add -- but this is something we did get done. And it's of enormous consequence to the country." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Dr79mcZBaD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Dr79mcZBaD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1482054754461171712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 During her White House briefing today, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  also addressed the situation in Ukraine, as fears intensify over a potential Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 US officials have now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/14/biden-infrastructure-law-voting-rights-defeat-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61e19e3a8f0838cf9ed78723#block-61e19e3a8f0838cf9ed78723"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the Kremlin of planning a false flag operation to justify an invasion, despite recent efforts to deescalate tensions in the region.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that the Russian government is preparing for an invasion in Ukraine that may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes, should diplomacy fail to meet their objectives,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWe are concerned that the Russian government is preparing for an invasion in Ukraine that may result in widespread human rights violations and war crimes, should diplomacy fail to meet their objectives,\u8221\'20\'1D White House press sec. Psaki says at briefing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UElvJTWtvq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UElvJTWtvq}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AFsPtOapfY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AFsPtOapfY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News (@ABC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC/status/1482049853517619200?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon deliver remarks at the White House on the bipartisan infrastructure law, which the president signed in November.\par \par \uc2 The White House said Biden would be joined by Mitch Landrieu, the former New Orleans mayor who is overseeing implementation of the infrastructure law.\par \par \uc2 According to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s official schedule, his remarks will focus on \u8220\'20\'1Chow the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law will rebuild America\u8217\'20\'19s bridges, which are critical for getting to school and work, moving commerce, and connecting communities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  was asked for the White House\u8217\'20\'19s message to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s supporters who are disappointed that they have not seen significant progress made on voting rights, climate change and student debt, among other issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur message to them is that we\u8217\'20\'19re still fighting for absolutely every component of what you just listed,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with the realities of the fact that we have a very slim majority in the Senate and in the House. That makes things more challenging than they have been in the past.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: "What's your message to Dem voters" who are disappointed with the lack of action on Biden's campaign promises?\par \par \uc2 Psaki: "We're still fighting... right now we're dealing with the realities of the fact that we have that we have a very slim majority in Senate and House." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XiJl4yGIWW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XiJl4yGIWW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1482037889299066885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki argued the administration had seen major successes on a variety of other fronts, including boosting coronavirus vaccination rates and helping schools reopen safely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the message from the president to them is, he is committed to continuing to fight,\u8221\'20\'1D Psaki said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to stay at it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden will likely reiterate that message next Wednesday, when he holds a formal press conference to mark one year since he took office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to hold press conference next week\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , is now holding her daily briefing with reporters, and she opened her remarks with an important announcement about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s schedule.\par \par \uc2 The president will hold a formal press conference next Wednesday at 4pm, as he marks one year in office.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PressSec}}}\uc2  : "Next Wednesday the president will hold a formal press conference at 4pm in the afternoon. So, we look forward to seeing you there and the president looks forward to speaking directly to the American people." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VLCgSbU48p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VLCgSbU48p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1482038277389623298?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 14, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden will likely face an array of difficult questions about his failures to pass the Build Back Better Act or a voting rights bill, which are two of his top legislative priorities.\par \par \uc2 In comparison to his recent predecessors, the president has held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-joe-biden-entertainment-health-media-ce99c9856653c3e292be3dd0438e3855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relatively few press conferences}}}\uc2  over his first year in office, although the Psaki often emphasizes that Biden frequently takes questions from reporters in more informal settings.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US allegations of Russia planning a false flag operation to justify invading Ukraine come just as Ukraine is reeling from a massive cyber-attack that affected the websites of several government departments.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Luke Harding reports:\par \par \uc2 Officials said it was too early to draw any conclusions but they pointed to a \u8216\'20\'18long record\u8217\'20\'19 of Russian cyber assaults against Ukraine, with the attack coming after security talks between Moscow and the US and its allies this week ended in stalemate.\par \par \uc2 Suspected Russian hackers left a message on the foreign ministry website, according to reports. It said: \u8216\'20\'18Ukrainians! \u8230\'20\'26 All information about you has become public. Be afraid and expect worse. It\u8217\'20\'19s your past, present and future.\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The message reproduced the Ukrainian flag and map crossed out. It mentioned the Ukrainian insurgent army, or UPA, which fought against the Soviet Union during the second world war. There was also a reference to \u8216\'20\'18historical land\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/14/ukraine-massive-cyber-attack-government-websites-suspected-russian-hackers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine hit by \u8216\'20\'18massive\u8217\'20\'19 cyber-attack on government websites}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the White House briefing yesterday, national security adviser Jake Sullivan said the US has been \u8220\'20\'1Cvery clear with Russia on the costs and consequences of further military action or destabilization in Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sullivan also sent the message that the Biden administration is prepared for all possible outcomes, whether Russia chooses to invade Ukraine or not.\par \par \uc2 enltrNational security adviser Jake Sullivan says diplomatic discussions with Russia were \u8220\'20\'1Cfrank and direct.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been very clear with Russia on the costs and consequences of further military action or destabilization in Ukraine." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/I2Uefa27hY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/I2Uefa27hY}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1HzDr7NzVl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1HzDr7NzVl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1481726400159698944?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 13, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re ready either way,\u8221\'20\'1D Sullivan said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re ready to make progress at the negotiating table \u8211\'20\'13 serious, tangible progress on important issues of concern to us, to Europe, and to Russia in an environment of de-escalation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we\u8217\'20\'19re ready to take the necessary and proper steps to defend our allies, support our partners, and respond robustly to any naked aggression that might occur.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sullivan said the White House has made its case that diplomacy, rather than increased aggression, is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe more sensible path\u8221\'20\'1D for Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Russians will have to make their own assessment,\u8221\'20\'1D he concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US claims Russia planning \u8216\'20\'18false-flag\u8217\'20\'19 operation to justify Ukraine invasion\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger and Luke Harding report:\par \par \uc2 The US has alleged Russia has already positioned saboteurs in Ukraine to carry out a false flag operation to use as a pretext for a Russian attack which Washington says could begin in the coming month.\par \par \uc2 The allegations, following similar claims by the government in Kyiv, come after the failure of a week of diplomacy to defuse the crisis provoked by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s massing of over 100,000 troops near Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s borders. Moscow has persistently portrayed the crisis as a military threat from Ukraine against Russia, without providing any evidence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia is laying the groundwork to have the option of fabricating a pretext for invasion, including through sabotage activities and information operations, by accusing Ukraine of preparing an imminent attack against Russian forces in eastern Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D a US official said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have information that indicates Russia has already prepositioned a group of operatives to conduct a false-flag operation in eastern Ukraine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussian influence actors already starting to fabricate Ukrainian provocations in state and social media,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said, noting that Russia used similar tactics ahead of the annexation of Crimea in 2014.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/14/us-russia-false-flag-ukraine-attack-claim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US claims Russia planning \u8216\'20\'18false-flag\u8217\'20\'19 operation to justify Ukraine invasion}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Suzan DelBene, chair of the centrist New Democrat Coalition, called on her colleagues to recommit themselves to extending the expanded child tax credit program as families {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/jan/14/biden-infrastructure-law-voting-rights-defeat-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-61e194718f0846d1f1b71149#block-61e194718f0846d1f1b71149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 missed out}}}\uc2  on payments today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is the first time in six months that 36 million families will not receive their monthly Child Tax Credit payments after the Senate failed to act at the end of last year,\u8221\'20\'1D DelBene said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile parents will not be receiving this critical lifeline this month, bills are still coming in, food still needs to be put on the table, and the other costs of raising a family still need to be paid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DelBene said the expanded program had \u8220\'20\'1Cprovided a historic tax cut to middle-class families and lifted 3.8 million children out of poverty,\u8221\'20\'1D underscoring the need to renew the policy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m committed to continuing the discussion about how we continue to deliver for American families and show that governance can work for them,\u8221\'20\'1D DelBene said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is significant energy from Democrats in both chambers and the White House to get this over the finish line. American families cannot afford further inaction or delay.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The monthly checks from the expanded child tax credit program would have gone out today \u8211\'20\'13 if congressional Democrats had been able to pass their Build Back Better bill to extend the program.\par \par \uc2 Instead, millions of American families will have to go without the money this month because Democrats were unable to pass the $1.75tn spending package due to objections from Senator Joe Manchin, a Democrat of West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Announcing his opposition last month, Manchin expressed concern about the cost of the legislation, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot take that risk with a staggering debt of more than $29 trillion and inflation taxes that are real and harmful to every hard-working American at the gasoline pumps, grocery stores and utility bills with no end in sight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But for the thousands of families in West Virginia who had come to rely on the checks, Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s stance means they will have to find another way to balance their budgets this month.\par \par \uc2 According to the West Virginia Center for Budget and Policy, 50,000 children in the state are at risk of falling into poverty now that the checks have come to an end.\par \par \uc2 Read Zack Harold\u8217\'20\'19s story about the impact that the checks have had on West Virginia families:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/12/west-virginians-child-tax-credits-manchin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginians scramble to get by after Manchin kills child tax credits}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Politico has some details on what happened behind closed doors yesterday, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  met with Senate Democrats to discuss filibuster reform and voting rights.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/01/13/manchin-sinema-sink-filibuster-reform-527082"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Even as Democrats filed into their caucus meeting with Biden about changing Senate rules to reform federal elections, a response to GOP-backed state laws designed to restrict ballot access, a good portion of them were unaware they had already lost. Just minutes before the group\u8217\'20\'19s meeting with Biden, [ Kyrsten Sinema] slammed the door on weakening the filibuster during a speech on the Senate floor Biden once called home.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People were just surprised when we went in there. Because no one knew she was on the floor speaking\u8217\'20\'19 in defense of the filibuster, said a Democratic senator who missed Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s remarks. \u8216\'20\'18There were probably 20 people in there that didn\u8217\'20\'19t even know that she had said anything.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Biden had prepared remarks for the meeting but instead opted to speak off-the-cuff, recalling that he got the late Sen. Strom Thurmond (R-S.C.) to support the Voting Rights Act while they were both in Congress and arguing that a majority of today\u8217\'20\'19s Republicans today wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t support that landmark bill. Biden told senators he couldn\u8217\'20\'19t remember a time in U.S. history where a party had been so enthralled to one person as the GOP is to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  held a meeting with Joe Manchin and \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  at the White House last night for another discussion on filibuster reform and voting rights.\par \par \uc2 The White House described the three Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 conversation as \u8220\'20\'1Ca candid and respectful exchange of views about voting rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Both Biden and Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  will likely still try to sway Manchin and Sinema on changing the filibuster, in the hopes of getting a voting rights bill passed before the midterms.\par \par \uc2 But Manchin and Sinema have sounded quite adamant that they will not support rule changes to get a voting rights bill passed, so Biden and Schumer will have their work cut out for them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema took to the Senate floor yesterday opposing any changes to the filibuster, the Senate rule that requires 60 votes to advance legislation , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  currently hold a bare majority in the 100-seat chamber and two voting rights bills are stalled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I continue to support these [voting rights] bills, I will not support separate actions that worsen the underlying disease of division infecting our country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must address the disease itself, the disease of division, to protect our democracy, and it cannot be achieved by one party alone. It cannot be achieved solely by the federal government. The response requires something greater and, yes, more difficult than what the Senate is discussing today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sinema\u8217\'20\'19s speech came at an extremely perilous moment for US democracy. Republican lawmakers in 19 states have enacted 34 new laws, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/voting-laws-roundup-december-2021"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Brennan Center for Justice}}}\uc2 , that impose new voting restrictions.\par \par \uc2 They have also passed a slew of bills that seek to inject more partisan control into election administration and the counting of votes, an unprecedented trend experts are deeply concerned about and call election subversion.\par \par \uc2 Many of those measures have been passed in state legislatures on simple majority, party-line votes.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jan/13/kyrsten-sinema-democrats-filibuster-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sinema says no to filibuster reform to scuttle Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voting rights hopes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to tout infrastructure law after major defeat on voting rights\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to deliver a speech this afternoon on the bipartisan infrastructure law, which he signed in November.\par \par \uc2 The remarks will focus on how the law \u8220\'20\'1Cwill rebuild America\u8217\'20\'19s bridges, which are critical for getting to school and work, moving commerce, and connecting communities,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The speech comes one day after Biden was dealt a major defeat by two members of his own party in the debate over voting rights and filibuster reform.\par \par \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema on the left and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the right. Composite: Senate TV | \uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Senators Kyrsten Sinema and Joe Manchin made it clear yesterday that they will not support changing the filibuster, leaving Democrats with no path for passing a voting rights bill.\par \par \uc2 Simultaneously, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better bill has also stalled in the Senate due to Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s objections to the $1.75tn spending package.\par \par \uc2 So, as Biden touts the infrastructure law today, keep in mind that it may be his last significant legislative accomplishment for the time being.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220114ei1e001uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
