\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Group whose anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ad Amy Barrett signed accused of promoting harassment of doctors\b0\par\par\uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner in Washington \par \uc2 1,264 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2022\par 13:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 38\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In one case, a doctor whose name was published by Indiana group was warned by \uc2 FBI\uc2  of kidnapping threat against her daughter\par \par \uc2 An Indiana group whose anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign was endorsed in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/01/amy-coney-barrett-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  signed advertisement by Amy Coney Barrett}}}\uc2  before she became a supreme court justice, keeps a published list of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and their place of work on its website, in what some experts say is an invitation to harass and intimidate the doctors and their staff.\par \par \uc2 In one case, court records show, a doctor whose name was published by the group, which is called Right to Life Michiana, was warned by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  of a kidnapping threat that had been made online against her daughter.\par \par \uc2 The threat prompted the doctor to temporarily stop providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services at the Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health Care clinic in South Bend, which is also named on the Michiana group\u8217\'20\'19s website. The doctor said in the court document that the clinic regularly attracts large gatherings of protesters, who she feared could identify her.\par \par \uc2 Barrett signed a two-page advertisement in 2006, while she was working as a professor at Notre Dame, that stated that those who signed \u8220\'20\'1Coppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand and defend the right to life from fertilization to natural death\u8221\'20\'1D. The second page of the ad called Roe v Wade, the landmark 1973 decision that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cbarbaric\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The advertisement, which was published in the South Bend Tribune and signed by hundreds of people, was sponsored by a group called St Joseph County Right to Life, which merged with another anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group in 2020 and is now called Right to Life Michiana.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is expected to rule this year on challenges to Roe v Wade that many court experts expect will gut the rights of women in the US to obtain legal abortions. In arguments before the court, Barrett \u8211\'20\'13 who has said her personal views do not affect her legal judgement \u8211\'20\'13 argued that passage of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://19thnews.org/2021/12/what-are-safe-haven-laws-supreme-court-case-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safe haven laws}}}\uc2 , which allow parents to relinquish their newborns at hospitals or other designated centers without the threat of legal consequences, had in effect given women options outside of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for those who did not want to become parents.\par \par \uc2 During her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rev.com/blog/transcripts/amy-coney-barrett-senate-confirmation-hearing-day-2-transcript"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 confirmation hearing}}}\uc2 , Barrett said she had signed the advertisement as a private citizen, while she was making her way out of church, and had not recalled signing it until it became public following a report in \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was consistent with the views of my church,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, in response to senators\u8217\'20\'19 questions about the statement. She later added: \u8220\'20\'1CI do see as distinct my personal, moral, religious views and my task of applying the law as a judge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An examination by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  of Right to Life Michiana, which publishes the same advertisement denouncing Roe v Wade as \u8220\'20\'1Cbarbaric\u8221\'20\'1D every year, reveals that the group does more than publish statements in newspapers: it urges supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake action\u8221\'20\'1D against what it calls a \u8220\'20\'1Clocal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In one section of the website, which is titled Local \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Threat: The Abortionist, the group lists the names and educational background of six doctors that it claims performs abortions at the Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health Clinic in South Bend.\par \par \uc2 Among them is a doctor \u8211\'20\'13 who \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  is declining to name \u8211\'20\'13 who testified in 2021, in a case involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in Indiana, that she started traveling to South Bend once a month \u8211\'20\'13 beginning in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 in order to perform first trimester abortions at the South Bend clinic. She stopped making the trip \u8211\'20\'13 a 2.5 hour car trip each way from her home \u8211\'20\'13 after she was alerted by Planned Parenthood, who had been alerted by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , that a kidnapping threat had been made against her daughter online.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt it would be best for me to limit my travel and exposure during that time,\u8221\'20\'1D the doctor said in testimony. \u8220\'20\'1CI was concerned that there may be people who would be able to identify me during that travel, as well as it\u8217\'20\'19s a very small clinic without any privacy for the people who are driving in and out, and so therefore, people could directly see me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jackie Appleman\uc2 , the executive director of Right to Life Michiana, said in response to questions from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  that the information on its website was \u8220\'20\'1Cpublicly available information\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight to Life Michiana does not condone or encourage harm, threats or harassment towards anyone, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  business employees and escorts. We encourage pro-choice groups to also accept our nonviolent approach when it comes to the unborn,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The group has also previously stated that it supports the criminalization of doctors who perform abortions and the criminalization of procedures that routinely occur in the in vitro fertilization process, including the discarding of frozen embryos or selective reduction of embryos.\par \par \uc2 The publication of doctors\u8217\'20\'19 names \u8211\'20\'13 and in some other cases, their home addresses \u8211\'20\'13 is a well known tactic used by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups.\par \par \uc2 The practice gained attention in the 1990s and early 2000s because of a legal battle over a website called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2001/mar/30/internetnews.usnews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nuremberg Files}}}\uc2 , which was supported by radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents and published the names, photos, home addresses, and licence plate numbers of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers. In some cases, spouses and children were also identified. Doctors who had been murdered had a line crossed through their names.\par \par \uc2 One of the most high-profile cases of violence against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers surrounded the case of George Tiller, who was one of the few doctors who performed late-term abortions when he was killed while attending church in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Sharon Lau, the midwest advocacy director for Whole Woman\u8217\'20\'19s Health Alliance, and serves as its security specialist, said Michiana Right to Life regularly protested at the group\u8217\'20\'19s South Bend clinic, approaching patients and blocking its driveway.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the naming of doctors on the Michiana website, Lau said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is clearly something that is threatening, so we take it seriously and we know that these types of things have consequences. The language is saying, \u8216\'20\'18these people are a threat\u8217\'20\'19. Which spurs people to action. We saw that with Dr Tiller.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 WWHA has been frustrated in part, she said, by what appeared to be a reluctance by local prosecutor to charge protesters who it said were violating trespassing rules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe law is not enforced. We know that if you enforce the fairly minor crimes, it can prevent escalation, so we\u8217\'20\'19ve tried to impress that on them,\u8221\'20\'1D Lau said.\par \par \uc2 Melissa Fowler, program director at the \uc2 National \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Federation\uc2 , said anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters have been emboldened by the recent passage of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans in Texas and Mississippi, and that the group had documented an increase in aggressiveness, including protesters taking advantage of \u8220\'20\'1Copen carry\u8221\'20\'1D laws to stand near health clinics with visible weapons.\par \par \uc2 Mira Shah, a doctor who travels in order to performs abortions in underserved communities, including in South Bend, who is listed on the Michiana website, said such groups aimed to instill fear in medical professionals and try to get them to stop doing their work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt can honestly be scary,\u8221\'20\'1D Dr Shah said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am really careful and do what I need to do to stay safe. We\u8217\'20\'19re trying to care for our patients and do the best we can do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s chambers at the supreme court was forwarded questions by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2  but did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220114ei1e000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
