\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 Saving Roe v Wade is not just a US battle but one for women across the Americas\b0\par\par\uc2 Mariana Prandini Assis \par \uc2 780 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 December 2021\par 09:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 campaign to undermine the landmark ruling threatens progress in reproductive freedom in Latin America\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  prepares to decide a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/11/supreme-court-roe-v-wade-gay-rights-contraceptives-fertility-treatments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case that could deny women the right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in much of the US, Latin American activists like me are holding our collective breaths.\par \par \uc2 The continent has some of the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the world, in spite of recent progressive reforms in the past decade in countries including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2012/sep/25/uruguay-legalise-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uruguay}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/dec/30/argentina-legalises-abortion-in-landmark-moment-for-womens-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Argentina}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade?eType=EmailBlastContent&eId=44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end of Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  would deliver a frightening message throughout the region.\par \par \uc2 El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s courts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2015/dec/17/el-salvador-anti-abortion-law-premature-birth-miscarriage-attempted-murder"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sentenced women who have had a miscarriage to 30 years in prison}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 treating an obstetric emergency as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In Honduras, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already illegal in all circumstances, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2021/jan/21/honduras-abortion-constitutional-reform-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congress amended the constitution}}}\uc2  to state that life starts at conception.\par \par \uc2 If Mississippi succeeds in overturning Roe v Wade, we will lose this crucial legal precedent and endanger progress on reproductive rights throughout Latin America\par \par \uc2 Against this dismal legal backdrop, Roe v Wade has long been a source of inspiration to women in Latin America fighting for their basic rights. It has given us a strategic model as well as strong legal arguments against constitutional obstacles. Like women in the US, we have taken our cases to court, sometimes securing significant and progressive gains in the last decade.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Freproductiverights.org%2Flandmark-decision-by-colombias-highest-court-liberalizes-one-of-the-worlds-most-restrictive-abortion-laws%2F&data=04%7C01%7Ccsirica%40burness.com%7C0df8d9ad89114d4d317a08d9c097a76f%7Cd90becc13cbc4b5f813209073da19766%7C0%7C0%7C637752579878236759%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=YmHF2sdxLq2krgEGBBU5Wk7wrtdU%2BiPRSoCQJfja5cw%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colombia}}}\uc2 , the constitutional court ruled in 2006 that women could have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cases involving rape or incest, when it posed a risk to the pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s life or health or when the foetus was diagnosed with severe malformations.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the supreme court in 2012 authorised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iwhc.org/2012/04/brazil-supreme-court-makes-abortion-legal-in-cases-of-anencephaly/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foetus is found to have anencephaly}}}\uc2 , a condition that leads to miscarriage, or death in the first weeks of life. And the court is considering another case that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2018/08/03/world/americas/brazil-abortion-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decriminalise all abortions in the first 12 weeks}}}\uc2 . Most recently, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2021%2F09%2F07%2Fworld%2Famericas%2Fmexico-supreme-court-decriminalize-abortion.html&data=04%7C01%7Ccsirica%40burness.com%7C0df8d9ad89114d4d317a08d9c097a76f%7Cd90becc13cbc4b5f813209073da19766%7C0%7C0%7C637752579878236759%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=H7z%2FaMvvpnwG1keUQsAqWv5IEuilvcuSywQoNHnKKwM%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexican supreme court}}}\uc2  declared the criminalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unconstitutional and mandated that state legislatures across the country act on that ruling.\par \par \uc2 In all of these cases, activists drew on the arguments in Roe v Wade for their successful litigation strategy and judges cited the landmark case and related rulings in making their decisions.\par \par \uc2 If the US state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/five-takeaways-us-supreme-court-mississippi-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi succeeds in overturning Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  after nearly 50 years, we will lose this crucial legal precedent and endanger progress on reproductive rights throughout Latin America.\par \par \uc2 Just this month, the Brazilian senate approved the nomination of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20211202-brazil-senate-approves-bolsonaro-backed-pastor-for-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative Christian pastor to the country\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court}}}\uc2 . President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s choice is expected to oppose expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 One glimmer of hope for Americans is the \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision last week to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-us-canada-59692830"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 permanently lift restrictions}}}\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. This reaffirms that Latin American activists have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/26410397.2020.1779633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long made}}}\uc2  the right choice to bet on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/26410397.2020.1779633"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 self-managed \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  for ensuring access}}}\uc2  while waiting for rights to be granted through the legislative process.\par \par \uc2 Funders must now expand their support for these direct action strategies throughout the Americas. But few are willing to associate their names with an issue as stigmatised as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which means financial backing is scarce for activists working to expand rights and access.\par \par \uc2 Philanthropists in the US have been fundamental to our success, and they will most likely want to redirect their funding to American organisations if the era of Roe v Wade does come to an end. They would be right to do so, but it would be a mistake to turn away from organisations and activists in other parts of the world that have made so much progress.\par \par \uc2 Emboldened by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ips-journal.eu%2Ftopics%2Fdemocracy-and-society%2Fthe-globalisation-of-anti-gender-campaigns-2761%2F&data=04%7C01%7Ccsirica%40burness.com%7C0df8d9ad89114d4d317a08d9c097a76f%7Cd90becc13cbc4b5f813209073da19766%7C0%7C0%7C637752579878236759%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=YfFdlbhrAg%2F%2BdNeVCykuF%2F8xB95S%2F61G5UJVWB7cO8o%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-gender movements}}}\uc2 , powerful forces have swept Latin America, Europe and Africa, seeking to undermine the quest for greater sexual and reproductive freedom \u8211\'20\'13 particularly access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and birth control \u8211\'20\'13 for the women who are least likely to advocate for themselves. We cannot fight them alone.\par \par \uc2 Funding community-based self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiatives in countries where access is highly restricted may be the only way to save women\u8217\'20\'19s lives while we battle repressive policies on multiple fronts across the global south.\par \par \uc2 It may require funders to be less prescriptive in supporting our reproductive justice struggles, and to trust local advocates and the solutions we propose. Doing so will make clear that the lives of women matter, no matter who we are or where we live. We may lose Roe, but never the commitment to our fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnewvoicesfellows.aspeninstitute.org%2Ffellow%2Fmariana-assis%2F&data=04%7C01%7Ccsirica%40burness.com%7C0df8d9ad89114d4d317a08d9c097a76f%7Cd90becc13cbc4b5f813209073da19766%7C0%7C0%7C637752579878236759%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=MReNptNXdbMXQgJXYCNN1TvZlqlmO71h%2BCCWUC7n6yo%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mariana Prandini Assis}}}\par \par \uc2 is an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnewvoicesfellows.aspeninstitute.org%2Fnominations%2F&data=04%7C01%7Ccsirica%40burness.com%7C0df8d9ad89114d4d317a08d9c097a76f%7Cd90becc13cbc4b5f813209073da19766%7C0%7C0%7C637752579878236759%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=rnRXA%2BFeMqmKLfEj8O3pgq1aSNYVi0AK%2F5LuufEUCTY%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aspen New Voices Fellow}}}\par \par \uc2 and a Brazilian human rights lawyer, researcher and activist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211222ehcm001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
