\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden sounds warning for those not vaccinated against Covid- as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Joan E Greve (earlier) \par \uc2 7,121 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 December 2021\par 05:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 CDC\uc2  advisers recommend \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna Covid vaccine over J&JTalks between Biden and Manchin \u8216\'20\'18going very poorly\u8217\'20\'19, report saysDemocrats want voting rights bill before 2022 elections, Schumer saysUS hospitals brace for potential Omicron surge in JanuarySign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * Americans should receive the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna coronavirus vaccine rather than the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine, a panel of outside advisors recommended to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . The \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine has been linked to rare but serious blood clots and the two-shot \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines have shown to be more effective in preventing infection.\par \par \uc2 * US hospitals are bracing for another potential surge in coronavirus cases as the Omicron variant spreads across the country. Omicron now accounts for nearly 3% of all Covid cases in the US as of Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 up from only 0.4% the week before, according to data from the \uc2 CDC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * After getting a briefing on the pandemic from advisers, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the Omicron variant is \u8220\'20\'1Cnow spreading and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to increase\u8221\'20\'1D.\u8220\'20\'1CFor the unvaccinated, we are looking at a winter of severe illness and death,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, urging Americans to get vaccinated and get their boosters as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court has returned the case involving Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to a federal appeals court. Much to the disappointment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, the case was sent to a court that has twice upheld the controversial law.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US Food and Drug Administration\uc2  said it would permanently ease restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, allowing patients to receive the medication without having to go to a clinic or doctor\u8217\'20\'19s office in person.\par \par \uc2 The medications are used to end pregnancies in the early stages, up to 10 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation. The policy comes as the date of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights remains uncertain in the hands of the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said he wants to pass a voting rights bill \u8220\'20\'1Cin time for the 2022 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1471515861198516227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per CNN}}}\uc2 . As of now, the Democratic leader does not have the votes to pass voting rights legislation because centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  remains opposed to altering the filibuster to clear the way for such a bill.\par \par \uc2 * Centrist Senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the Build Back Better Act have stalled negotiations, essentially eliminating the possibility of Democrats passing the bill before the end of the year. Manchin has reportedly expressed concern about the cost of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s provision to continue the expanded child tax credit program.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Joan E Greve and Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has conceded that his Build Back Better plan is unlikely to pass this year.\par \par \uc2 In discussions, Joe Manchin \u8220\'20\'1Chas reiterated his support for Build Back Better funding at the level of the framework plan I announced in September. I believe that we will bridge our differences and advance the Build Back Better plan, even in the face of fierce Republican opposition,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Centrist Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the Build Back Better Act have stalled negotiations. Most recently, he has reportedly been concerned about the cost of expanding the child tax credit program, a provision of the legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy team and I are having ongoing discussions with Senator Manchin; that work will continue next week. It takes time to finalize these agreements, prepare the legislative changes, and finish all the parliamentary and procedural steps needed to enable a Senate vote. We will advance this work together over the days and weeks ahead; Leader Schumer and I are determined to see the bill successfully on the floor as early as possible,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 FDA\uc2  permanently eases restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail\par \par \uc2 The US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) \uc2 said it would permanently ease restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail, allowing patients to receive the medication by mail without having to go to a clinic or doctor\u8217\'20\'19s office in person.\par \par \uc2 The medications are used to end pregnancies in the early stages, up to 10 weeks\u8217\'20\'19 gestation. The policy change from the \uc2 FDA\uc2  comes as the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  considers an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in Mississippi at 15 weeks. During oral arguments this month, justices signaled they are open to rolling back or gutting Roe v Wade, the landmark decision that established the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  initially temporarily lifted restrictions on getting the pill mailed during the pandemic when it was risky for patients to visit doctor\u8217\'20\'19s offices and clinics in person.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US postmaster appointed under Trump is still raising alarm \u8211\'20\'13 but can he be stopped?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jake-bittle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jake Bittle}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  this month took another step toward the removal of the controversial postmaster general \uc2 Louis DeJoy\uc2 , even as the Trump-era appointee continues to make his mark on the embattled postal service, rolling out new plans to slow down delivery and close postal stations around the country.\par \par \uc2 DeJoy, a Republican logistics executive, caused a national furor last year over his attempts to slow down mail delivery {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/aug/17/louis-dejoy-usps-postmaster-general-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before the 2020 presidential election}}}\uc2 , in which millions of Americans voted by mail.\par \par \uc2 Biden has not said outright whether he wishes to oust DeJoy, although his press secretary, \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 , has said she is \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply troubled\u8221\'20\'1D by his leadership. Even so, the president lacks the authority to dismiss the postmaster general. That power rests with the USPS Board of Governors, a nine-member panel that can remove DeJoy with a majority vote. There were three vacancies on the board when Biden took office, and he filled those vacancies with Democratic allies earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Now the president has taken a further step toward reshaping the board by nominating two new governors to replace those whose terms are expiring. His decision not to renominate the Democratic board chairman, \uc2 Ron Bloom\uc2 , is significant, since Bloom was one of DeJoy\u8217\'20\'19s biggest allies on the board and earlier this year said he considered DeJoy \u8220\'20\'1Cthe proper man for the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the postmaster general {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2021/08/13/dejoy-usps-bloom-bonds-brookfield/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bought }}}\uc2  as much as $305,000 in bonds from Bloom\u8217\'20\'19s asset management firm earlier this year, according to DeJoy\u8217\'20\'19s financial disclosure paperwork. Bloom has said he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t benefit from the purchase. The asset purchases and Bloom\u8217\'20\'19s continued support for DeJoy led some Democratic senators to say they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t support Bloom\u8217\'20\'19s renomination.\par \par \uc2 Even as Biden appears to inch closer to ousting DeJoy, the embattled postmaster general has begun to leave his mark on the agency. DeJoy abandoned his initial attempts to slow down mail delivery ahead of the 2020 election after he faced lawsuits and backlash, but soon after he announced a significant reduction in the agency\u8217\'20\'19s 60,000-member administrative workforce.\par \par \uc2 DeJoy also released in April a 10-year plan for revamping postal operations. Some provisions are supported by unions and postal advocates, such as a $40bn investment in the agency\u8217\'20\'19s vehicle fleet and logistics network, and modernizing thousands of retail post offices. The plan also calls for an end to a mandate that requires the USPS to fund retiree health benefits decades in advance, which postal management has decried for years as an unnecessary burden on its finances.\par \par \uc2 DeJoy\u8217\'20\'19s plan would attempt to fill the postal service\u8217\'20\'19s $160bn funding hole through a wide variety of cost-cutting measures.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/dec/16/louis-dejoy-us-postal-service-postmaster-general-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US postmaster appointed under Trump is still raising alarm \u8211\'20\'13 but can he be stopped?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Melody Schreiber reports:\par \par \uc2 A wave of new Omicron cases is beginning to surge in America and could peak as early as January, the Centers for Disease Controls (\uc2 CDC\uc2 ) has warned, as states are scrambling to prepare for overloaded hospitals. The US has passed 800,000 deaths, including 1 in 100 Americans over the age of 65.\par \par \uc2 The Omicron variant accounted for nearly 3% of Covid cases in the US as of Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 up from only 0.4% the week before, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#variant-proportions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 CDC\uc2 . The variant is expected to continue rising rapidly, based on the experiences of other countries and could be dominant within weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI suspect that those numbers are going to shoot up dramatically in the next couple of weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D said C\u233\'00\'E9line Gounder, infectious disease specialist and epidemiologist at \uc2 New York University\uc2  and Bellevue Hospital, on Wednesday. She expects an Omicron wave to peak in late January and then come down sometime in February.\par \par \uc2 In a meeting with state health leaders on Tuesday, the \uc2 CDC{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/12/14/omicron-us-spread/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presented}}}\uc2  two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/14/science/omicron-cdc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scenarios}}}\uc2 , based on models, for how the variant might drive infections in the next few weeks and months. Omicron and Delta cases could peak as soon as January or a smaller surge of Omicron could happen in the spring.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear which variant, Delta or Omicron, will dominate in the next few months or if they will coexist, Gounder said. Regardless, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe anticipate an increase in hospitalizations, an increase in deaths and an increase in the burden on the health care system over the next couple of months\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US was already in the grips of a Delta wave that began before the Thanksgiving holiday, and officials fear that travel and gatherings over holidays like Christmas and New Year\u8217\'20\'19s could add explosive growth to an already strained situation.\par \par \uc2 Schools across the US are seeing rises in cases, and some are closing early or cutting back on in-person activities. In New York, \uc2 Cornell University\uc2  reported 903 cases among students this week \u8211\'20\'13 many of them cases of the Omicron variant among fully vaccinated people. The school closed early and went virtual.\par \par \uc2 In several states, hospitals are already close to being overwhelmed. In Michigan, hospital workers are now volunteering to work for free in ICUs, one doctor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iwashyna/status/1469698237963636742"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/16/us-hospitals-brace-for-potential-omicron-surge-in-january"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US hospitals brace for potential Omicron surge in January }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says the unvaccinated face \u8220\'20\'1Ca winter of severe illness and death" Biden speaks during a meeting with the White House COVID-19 Response Team, including National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases Director Anthony Fauci (R), in the Roosevelt Room of the White House. Photograph: Drew Angerer/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 After getting a briefing on the pandemic from advisers, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said the omicron variant is \u8220\'20\'1Cnow spreading and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to increase\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor the unvaccinated, we are looking at a winter of severe illness and death,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, urging Americans to get vaccinated and get their boosters as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today. My west coast colleague, Maanvi Singh, will take over the blog for the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Americans should receive the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna coronavirus vaccine rather than the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine, a panel of outside advisors recommended to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . The \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine has been linked to rare but serious blood clots, and the two-shot \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines have shown to be more effective in preventing infection.\par \par \uc2 * US hospitals are bracing for another potential surge in coronavirus cases as the Omicron variant spreads across the country. Omicron now accounts for nearly 3% of all Covid cases in the US as of Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 up from only 0.4% the week before, according to data from the \uc2 CDC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court has returned the case involving Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to a federal appeals court. Much to the disappointment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, the case was sent to a court that has twice upheld the controversial law.\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said he wants to pass a voting rights bill \u8220\'20\'1Cin time for the 2022 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1471515861198516227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per CNN}}}\uc2 . As of now, the Democratic leader does not have the votes to pass voting rights legislation because centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  remains opposed to altering the filibuster to clear the way for such a bill.\par \par \uc2 * Centrist Senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the Build Back Better Act have stalled negotiations, essentially eliminating the possibility of Democrats passing the bill before the end of the year. Manchin has reportedly expressed concern about the cost of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s provision to continue the expanded child tax credit program.\par \par \uc2 Maanvi will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 CDC\uc2  advisers recommend \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines over \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\par \par \uc2 A panel of outside advisers to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  has voted to recommend that Americans receive the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna coronavirus vaccine rather than the \uc2 Johnson & Johnson\uc2  vaccine.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-science-business-health-coronavirus-vaccine-dee1a2f0becff4090aa2775b19f04158"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The strange clotting problem has caused nine confirmed deaths after J&J vaccinations \u8212\'20\'14 while the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  and Moderna vaccines don\u8217\'20\'19t come with that risk and also appear to be more effective, advisers to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an unusual move and the CDC\u8217\'20\'19s director, \uc2 Dr. Rochelle Walensky\uc2 , must decide whether to accept the panel\u8217\'20\'19s advice.\par \par \uc2 Until now the U.S. has treated all three COVID-19 vaccines available to Americans as an equal choice, since large studies found they all offered strong protection and early supplies were limited. J&J\u8217\'20\'19s vaccine initially was welcomed as a single-dose option that could be especially important for hard-to-reach groups like homeless people who might not get the needed second dose of the \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  or Moderna options.\par \par \uc2 The news comes amid intensifying fears of a potential surge in US coronavirus cases linked to the Omicron variant, which has already been reported in at least 36 states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/16/cdc-recommends-pfizer-moderna-covid-vaccines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CDC advisers recommend Pfizer and Moderna vaccines over Johnson & Johnson}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A reporter asked \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would support separating the expanded child tax credit program from the Build Back Better Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have 60 votes in the Senate to do that as a stand-alone,\u8221\'20\'1D the deputy White House press secretary said.\par \par \uc2 The question comes as reports indicate Joe Manchin has voiced concern about the cost of the expanded program if it is continued for the next decade, although the current version of the Build Back Better Act only extends it for one year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The principal deputy White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , was asked whether \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  believes Senate Democrats should focus on voting rights before passing the Build Back Better Act.\par \par \uc2 The question comes one day after Biden told reporters, \u8220\'20\'1CIf we can get the congressional voting rights done, we should do it. If we can\u8217\'20\'19t, we got to keep going. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing domestically more important than voting rights. It\u8217\'20\'19s the single-biggest issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CProtecting the cornerstone of our democracy should not be a partisan issue, but sadly what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is that has been the case,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is nothing more urgent than passing voting rights and getting that done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Jean-Pierre did not specifically say whether the Build Back Better Act should take a lower priority than voting rights as Democrats continue to negotiate over both issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Deputy national climate advisor Ali Zaidi expressed confidence that the Biden administration will have the resources to replace millions of lead pipes in the US, even though the final infrastructure bill included significantly less funding than the White House initially sought.\par \par \uc2 Zaidi noted that $3bn of the $15bn for lead pipe replacement in the infrastructure law will be sent out over the course of the next year.\par \par \uc2 Asked when the first lead pipes might be replaced, Zaidi said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s already making a difference in communities right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr$3 billion out of $15 billion will be sent out in 2022 for the Biden-Harris Lead Pipe and Paint Action Plan. Asked when the first lead pipes will be replaced, Deputy nat'l climate advisor Ali Zaidi tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/edokeefe?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @edokeefe}}}\uc2  "It's already making a difference in communities right now." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uGpqCqcKab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uGpqCqcKab}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CBS News (@CBSNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews/status/1471588929916882947?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The principal deputy White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , is now holding the daily briefing with reporters, and she is joined by deputy national climate advisor Ali Zaidi.\par \par \uc2 Zaidi outlined the Biden administration \u8217\'20\'19s plans to replace lead pipes across the US, which he described as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccenterpiece of the bipartisan infrastructure law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The climate adviser noted that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  met with child health advocates and labor leaders today to share the White House\u8217\'20\'19s pledge to eliminate lead pipe and lead paint threats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 She is married to former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but now you, too, can stare into the \u8220\'20\'1Ccobalt blue eyes\u8221\'20\'1D of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/melania-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania Trump}}}\uc2  at the touch of a button and with your very own piece of trendy, digital art.\par \par \uc2 The former first lady has jumped into the latest internet craze by launching a non-fungible token (NFT) just in time for Christmas. It puts Melania right in the middle of a fashion frenzy in hi-tech art circles \u8211\'20\'13 though critics may regard it as the latest attempt by the Trump family to cash in on political success.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/nfts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An NFT}}}\uc2  is a digital asset \u8211\'20\'13 typically pictures, songs or videos \u8211\'20\'13 bought in an online marketplace and stored on blockchain, a secure public ledger. Blockchain allows anyone to verify the NFT\u8217\'20\'19s authenticity and keeps a record of who owns what.\par \par \uc2 In Melania\u8217\'20\'19s first public venture since leaving the White House almost a year ago, an NFT named Melania\u8217\'20\'19s Vision can be bought between 16 and 31 December with the SOL cryptocurrency or an old-fashioned credit card.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MELANIATRUMP/status/1471468919810670603?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An irony-free statement}}}\uc2  from her office says it is \u8220\'20\'1Ca breathtaking watercolor art by Marc-Antoine Coulon, and embodies Mrs Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cobalt blue eyes, providing the collector with an amulet to inspire.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe limited-edition piece of digital artwork will be 1 SOL (approximately $150) and includes an audio recording from Mrs Trump with a message of hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/dec/16/melania-trump-nft-business"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Melania Trump launches NFT venture, promising \u8216\'20\'18an amulet to inspire\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will attend \uc2 South Carolina State University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s commencement ceremony tomorrow, the White House has just announced.\par \par \uc2 In its advisory, the White House said the president will travel to Orangeburg, South Carolina, to celebrate the graduates of the historically Black university.\par \par \uc2 Biden is expected to deliver remarks, and House majority whip \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2 , who graduated from the university in 1961, will participate in a ceremonial march during the ceremony.\par \par \uc2 enltrWhen I earned my diploma from S.C. State in 1961, I did not have the opportunity to walk the stage.\par \par \uc2 Next week, 60 years later, I'll have that chance \u8212\'20\'14 an occasion made all the more special as I have the honor of welcoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  back to my alma mater. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FqFHIqd5A2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/FqFHIqd5A2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 James E. Clyburn\uc2  (@WhipClyburn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhipClyburn/status/1469689886722699275?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 11, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/12/16/biden-clyburn-college-diploma/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explains}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In December 1961, \uc2 James E. Clyburn\uc2  was a 21-year-old at \uc2 South Carolina State University\uc2  who had completed all his credits and was set to graduate. However, because the school at the time allowed only one commencement ceremony a year \u8212\'20\'14 usually in the spring \u8212\'20\'14 Clyburn received his diploma in the mail instead of marching alongside his classmates. He could have returned to walk in the 1962 ceremony, but by then he was busy with a new teaching job in Charleston.\par \par \uc2 Sixty years later, Clyburn, now an 81-year-old Democratic congressman from South Carolina and the House majority whip, will get the opportunity to experience the pomp and circumstance of the college graduation ceremony he never had. And a special guest will hand him his diploma: President Biden, who is giving the commencement address at the school on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It means a great deal to me,\u8217\'20\'19 Clyburn said Thursday on MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Morning Joe.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  posthumously awarded the Medal of Honor to Army Sergeant First Class Alwyn Cashe, and the medal was received by Cashe\u8217\'20\'19s widow, Tamara Cashe.\par \par \uc2 enltrArmy Sergeant First Class Alwyn Cashe is posthumously awarded the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MedalofHonor?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MedalofHonor}}}\uc2  for his distinguished service in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 Watch: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0bpjpa4HYw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0bpjpa4HYw}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wmRswHfISI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wmRswHfISI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1471564488956600322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The medal was also posthumously awarded to Army Sergeant First Class Christopher Celiz, whose wife Katherine and daughter Shannon accepted the award on his behalf.\par \par \uc2 Army Master Sergeant Earl Plumlee received the award for \u8220\'20\'1Cacts of gallantry and intrepidity above and beyond the call of duty on August 28th, 2013,\u8221\'20\'1D when he was serving in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 enltrArmy Master Sergeant Earl Plumlee is awarded the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MedalofHonor?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MedalofHonor}}}\uc2  for his distinguished service in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 Watch: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/0bpjpa4HYw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/0bpjpa4HYw}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dkSSBrTI7l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dkSSBrTI7l}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1471570092056006664?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Medal of Honor was also awarded to Sergeant First Class Christopher A. Celiz of the \uc2 US Army\uc2  and Master Sergeant Earl D. Plumlee of the \uc2 US Army\uc2 , both of whom served in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 According to a White House statement, Celiz participated in a July 2018 mission during which he \u8220\'20\'1Cvoluntarily exposed himself to intense enemy machine gun and small arms fire to retrieve and employ a heavy weapon system, thereby allowing U.S. and partnered forces to regain the initiative, maneuver to a secure location and begin treatment of a critically wounded partnered force member\u8221\'20\'1D. He later died of injuries sustained during the mission.\par \par \uc2 Plumlee was recognized for his actions in Afghanistan in August 2013, when he \u8220\'20\'1Cinstantly responded to a complex enemy attack that began with a massive explosion that tore a sixty-foot breach in the base\u8217\'20\'19s perimeter wall,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden awards Medal of Honor to three troops who fought in Iraq and Afhganistan\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is now awarding the Medal of Honor, America\u8217\'20\'19s highest military award to valor, to three troops who fought in Iraq and Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 The three troops receiving the award are:\par \par \uc2 * Sergeant First Class Alwyn C. Cashe, \uc2 United States Army\par \par \uc2 * Sergeant First Class Christopher A. Celiz, \uc2 United States Army\par \par \uc2 * Master Sergeant Earl D. Plumlee, \uc2 United States Army\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that Cashe, who was killed in Iraq in 2005, is the first African American to receive the Medal of Honor since the Vietnam War.\par \par \uc2 According to a statement from the White House, Cashe\u8217\'20\'19s squadron was attacked on October 17, 2005, during a nighttime patrol in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 Cashe sustained second- and third-degree burns trying to help his teammates reach safety, and he selflessly insisted that other injured troops be evacuated before he was. His actions saved several lives and cost him his own.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court returns Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case to federal appeals court\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has returned the case involving Texas\u8217\'20\'19 six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to a federal appeals court, but much to the disappointment of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates, the case was sent to a court that has twice upheld the controversial law.\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/health-texas-lawsuits-neil-gorsuch-d74dbd6deb60e7e9cd1777328c03dee5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  on Thursday signed the court\u8217\'20\'19s order that granted the request of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics for the court to act speedily. But the clinics wanted the case sent directly to U.S. Judge Robert Pitman, who had previously though briefly blocked enforcement of the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban known as S.B. 8.\par \par \uc2 When Pitman ordered the law blocked in early October, the appeals court countermanded his order two days later.\par \par \uc2 Texas has said it will seek to keep the case bottled up at the appeals court for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court ruled last week that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can move forward with their lawsuit over the ban, but the court, which skews six to three in favor of conservatives, allowed the law to remain in effect for now.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme court rules Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers can sue over ban but won\u8217\'20\'19t stop law}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican political fixer \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  is going to appear tomorrow before the House special committee investigating the insurrection at the US Capitol on January 6 by extremist supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but Stone will plead the fifth, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2 's attorney suggests his client will appear before the Jan 6 committee to plead the 5th.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Stone will be complying w/ the subpoena & will... assert his 5th Amendment rights to each question posed,\u8221\'20\'1D he told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SaraMurray?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SaraMurray}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Deposition is scheduled for Dec. 17.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zachary Cohen (@ZcohenCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZcohenCNN/status/1471531708197613572?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/22/roger-stone-alex-jones-subpoenas-capitol-attack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued a subpoena}}}\uc2  last month for Stone and others, demanding documents and testimony to expand the select committee\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry focused on the planning and financing of the rally at the Ellipse, near the White House, by Trump on January 6, at which he exhorted his supporters to go to the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and try to stop the certification by Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 Now the panel members faced with the prospect of Stone sitting down with them but deflecting all of their questions, exercising his constitutional right to protection against self-incrimination.\par \par \uc2 enltrCONFIRMED: \uc2 Roger Stone\uc2  will appear for a Jan. 6 committee deposition tomorrow and plead the Fifth to each question asked, his lawyer says.\par \par \uc2 Confirming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SaraMurray?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SaraMurray}}}\uc2  / CNN report.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1471538478504714243?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden signs bill raising the debt ceiling, averting potential default\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has officially signed the bill raising the debt ceiling by $2.5tn, averting a default that would have had disastrous effects on the domestic and global economy.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the White House noted that Biden also signed a bill awarding the Congressional Gold Medal to the US troops who were killed during the Kabul evacuation mission earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The House approved the debt ceiling bill yesterday in a vote of 221 to 209, sending the legislation to the president\u8217\'20\'19s desk.\par \par \uc2 The House vote came after Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  and minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  reached an agreement to approve a temporary rule change allowing Democrats to end a Republican filibuster of the bill with just 51 votes. The debt ceiling bill ultimately passed the Senate in a vote of 50 to 49.\par \par \uc2 The one-time change to the filibuster has led to suggestions from some Senate Democrats that the chamber should be able to make similar adjustments to approve a voting rights bill.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe think it\u8217\'20\'19s so important that we change the rule in order to save the economy,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Raphael Warnock{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/senator-sees-debt-limit-increase-model-pass-voting-legislation-rcna8762"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told NBC News this week}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, the warning lights on our democracy are blinking right now, and we seem unwilling to respond with the same urgency to protect the democracy that we have to protect the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tommy Vietor, who previously served as National Security Council spokesperson under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , criticized Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  for his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/16/build-back-better-voting-rights-manchin-sinema-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?page=with:block-61bb6d958f080842de5faac2#block-61bb6d958f080842de5faac2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new deadline}}}\uc2  to pass a voting rights bill before the 2022 elections.\par \par \uc2 enltrI don't understand making pronouncements like this without any discernible path to success. I would love for the Senate to focus on and pass voting rights legislation, but this just feels like lurching from one rhetorical cul de sac to another... {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vnDoGmVJRj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vnDoGmVJRj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tommy Vietor (@TVietor08) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TVietor08/status/1471523969324912642?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t understand making pronouncements like this without any discernible path to success,\u8221\'20\'1D Vietor said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI would love for the Senate to focus on and pass voting rights legislation, but this just feels like lurching from one rhetorical cul de sac to another.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of now, Schumer does not have the votes to pass a voting rights bill because centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  remains opposed to altering the filibuster, which would be necessary to approve such a bill.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where the day stands so far:\par \par \uc2 * Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  said he wants to pass a voting rights bill \u8220\'20\'1Cin time for the 2022 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D per CNN. As of now, the Democratic leader does not have the votes to pass voting rights legislation because centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  remains opposed to altering the filibuster to clear the way for such a bill.\par \par \uc2 * Centrist Senator Joe Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s concerns about the Build Back Better Act have stalled negotiations, essentially eliminating the possibility of Democrats passing the bill before the end of the year. Manchin has reportedly expressed concern about the cost of the bill\u8217\'20\'19s provision to continue the expanded child tax credit program.\par \par \uc2 * US hospitals are bracing for another potential surge in coronavirus cases as the Omicron variant spreads across the country. Omicron now accounts for nearly 3% of all Covid cases in the US as of Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 up from only 0.4% the week before, according to data from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer, the senate majority leader, said Thursday that he wants to pass Democrats \u8217\'20\'19 two sweeping voting bills in time for the 2022 election. But that looks increasingly more difficult the longer Democrats delay.\par \par \uc2 Advocates don\u8217\'20\'19t think the window to do anything about the 2022 elections has passed, but it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/06/voting-rights-biden-democrats-voting-rights-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rapidly closing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Texas, a state that has some of the most gerrymandered maps in the country, the period for candidates to file for office next year ended on Monday. Overseas voters will begin to get mail-in ballots for the state\u8217\'20\'19s 1 March primary in January. And the state\u8217\'20\'19s voter registration deadline is 31 January.\par \par \uc2 Those fast-approaching deadlines puts Democrats at a huge disadvantage. Courts will likely be more hesitant to step in and make sweeping election changes now that the election process is well underway since doing so could potentially mean changing ballots and risk voter confusion.\par \par \uc2 Several provisions in the Freedom to Vote Act would require states to make significant overhauls to the way their elections are run, including implementing systems for same-day and automatic voter registration. Those changes take time to implement, and while it\u8217\'20\'19s not impossible, would be increasingly difficult to do ahead of fast approaching spring primaries.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that it\u8217\'20\'19s doable. But if we want to ensure that it\u8217\'20\'19s done correctly and well, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to take some time and definitely some resources,\u8221\'20\'1D Tammy Patrick, a senior adviser at the Democracy Fund, said back in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo the sands in the hour glass are slipping away and it is not something that if it\u8217\'20\'19s not passed relatively soon, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there are ways in which many facets of the bill would be able to be implemented well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/06/voting-rights-biden-democrats-voting-rights-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Time is running out\u8217\'20\'19: can Congress pass a voting rights bill after months of failure?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats want voting rights bill before 2022 elections, Schumer says\par \par \uc2 Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is now saying Democrats want to pass a voting rights bill \u8220\'20\'1Cin time for the 2022 elections,\u8221\'20\'1D according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 enltrSchumer now saying that they want to get voting rights bill done "in time for the 2022 elections."\par \par \uc2 What Schumer didn't promise: a vote (which would fail) before Christmas\par \par \uc2 With Manchin/Sinema opposed to changing rules, there's no path to getting bill done even next year\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1471515861198516227?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 There had been signs that Democrats were hoping to approve filibuster rule changes and pass a voting rights bill before the end of the year, as negotiations over the Build Back Better Act have stalled.\par \par \uc2 However, centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/16/build-back-better-voting-rights-manchin-sinema-joe-biden-us-politics-latest?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61bb48058f080842de5fa7d7#block-61bb48058f080842de5fa7d7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has indicated}}}\uc2  she is still opposed to amending the filibuster, leaving Schumer with no path to pass a voting rights bill this month.\par \par \uc2 If Sinema remains staunchly opposed to filibuster reform, Schumer will also not be able to pass a voting rights bill next year, as he needs all 50 members of his caucus on board to approve any rule changes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Even fully vaccinated Americans may not be protected against the Omicron variant, particularly if they have not yet received their booster shots.\par \par \uc2 Ed Yong {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/health/archive/2021/12/america-omicron-variant-surge-booster/621027/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes in the Atlantic}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 As a crude shorthand, assume that Omicron negates one previous immunizing event\u8212\'20\'14either an infection or a vaccine dose. Someone who considered themselves fully vaccinated in September would be just partially vaccinated now (and the official definition may change imminently). But someone who\u8217\'20\'19s been boosted has the same ballpark level of protection against Omicron infection as a vaccinated-but-unboosted person did against Delta. The extra dose not only raises a recipient\u8217\'20\'19s level of antibodies but also broadens their range, giving them better odds of recognizing the shape of even Omicron\u8217\'20\'19s altered spike. In a small British study, a booster effectively doubled the level of protection that two \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  doses provided against Omicron infection.\par \par \uc2 But, but, but: those who have received booster shots should not assume they are entirely immune from contracting Omicron. Yong notes:\par \par \uc2 In South Africa, the variant managed to infect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=3981711"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a cluster of seven people}}}\uc2  who were all boosted. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/wr/mm7050e1.htm?s_cid=mm7050e1_w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a CDC report}}}\uc2 , boosted Americans made up a third of the first known Omicron cases in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Governments are bracing for high coronavirus case counts as the Omicron variant spreads around the world. More than 75 countries have now reported cases of Omicron, the director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention said yesterday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/16/briefing/omicron-update-spread-vaccines.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The news over the past few days \u8212\'20\'14 both scientific studies and real-world data \u8212\'20\'14 has added to the evidence that Omicron is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/article/omicron-coronavirus-variant.html?te=1&nl=the-morning&emc=edit_nn_20211216"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more contagious}}}\uc2  than any previous version of the Covid-19 virus.\par \par \uc2 In South Africa, where Omicron was first identified, the recent rise has been steeper than during any previous surge. \u8216\'20\'18When Omicron enters a community, the increase in case numbers looks like a vertical line,\u8217\'20\'19 Dr. Paul Sax of \uc2 Brigham and Women\u8217\'20\'19s Hospital\uc2  in Boston said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are scheduled to receive a briefing from the White House pandemic response this afternoon to hear the latest updates on the spread of Omicron.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 France will dramatically tighten restrictions on travel from Britain to slow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2021/dec/16/covid-news-live-south-korea-reimpose-dining-curfews-south-africa-daily-cases-record-omicron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spread of the new Omicron variant}}}\uc2 , effectively banning all non-essential journeys.\par \par \uc2 The government announced in a statement that incoming travellers would require \u8220\'20\'1Can essential reason to travel to, or come from, the UK, both for the unvaccinated and vaccinated\u8221\'20\'1D from midnight on Saturday (11pm GMT Friday).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople cannot travel for tourism or professional reasons,\u8221\'20\'1D it said, adding that the \uc2 British government\uc2  had itself said that the UK would face \u8220\'20\'1Ca tidal wave\u8221\'20\'1D of new infections fuelled by the Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 France had therefore \u8220\'20\'1Cchosen to reinstate the need for an essential reason for travel from and to the UK\u8221\'20\'1D, it said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, all arrivals from the UK will need a negative PCR or antigen test taken within the previous 24, rather than 48 hours, and will have to quarantine in France for seven days \u8211\'20\'13 reduced to 48 hours if they can produce a new negative test.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/16/france-tighten-covid-restrictions-travel-omicron-uk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 France to tighten Covid restrictions on travel from Omicron-hit UK}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite the growing concerns over the Omicron variant, \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  expressed hope that families will still be able to gather for the holidays if people are vaccinated and boosted.\par \par \uc2 enltr"If you and your family are vaccinated and boosted hopefully, you should feel comfortable about having a holiday situation where you have dinners and gatherings in your own home."\par \par \uc2 Dr. Anthony Fauci\uc2  speaks on the COVID surge heading into the holidays. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9OSjXvpVmJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/9OSjXvpVmJ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CtYzFHGs3W"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CtYzFHGs3W}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Good Morning America (@GMA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GMA/status/1471454908532629511?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 16, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you and your family are vaccinated and boosted hopefully, you should feel comfortable about having a holiday situation where you have dinners and gatherings in your own home with family and friends,\u8221\'20\'1D the president\u8217\'20\'19s chief medical adviser told \u8220\'20\'1CGood Morning America\u8221\'20\'1D today.\par \par \uc2 Fauci added, \u8220\'20\'1CBut that will only be safe if people get vaccinated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of now, 65% of the Americans aged five or older are fully vaccinated against coronavirus, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#vaccinations_vacc-people-onedose-pop-5yr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data compiled by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention}}}\uc2 . But only 30% of American adults have received booster shots as of now.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US hospitals brace for potential Omicron surge in January\par \par \uc2 A wave of new Omicron cases is beginning to surge in America and could peak as early as January, the Centers for Disease Controls (\uc2 CDC\uc2 ) has warned, as states are scrambling to prepare for overloaded hospitals. The US has passed 800,000 deaths, including 1 in 100 Americans over the age of 65.\par \par \uc2 The Omicron variant accounted for nearly 3% of Covid cases in the US as of Saturday \u8211\'20\'13 up from only 0.4% the week before, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://covid.cdc.gov/covid-data-tracker/#variant-proportions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 CDC\uc2 . The variant is expected to continue rising rapidly, based on the experiences of other countries and could be dominant within weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI suspect that those numbers are going to shoot up dramatically in the next couple of weeks,\u8221\'20\'1D C\u233\'00\'E9line Gounder, infectious disease specialist and epidemiologist at \uc2 New York University\uc2  and Bellevue Hospital, told reporters on Wednesday. She expects an Omicron wave to peak in late January and then come down sometime in February.\par \par \uc2 In a meeting with state health leaders on Tuesday, the \uc2 CDC{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/health/2021/12/14/omicron-us-spread/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presented}}}\uc2  two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/14/science/omicron-cdc.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scenarios}}}\uc2 , based on models, for how the variant might drive infections in the next few weeks and months. Omicron and Delta cases could peak as soon as January or a smaller surge of Omicron could happen in the spring.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/16/us-hospitals-brace-for-potential-omicron-surge-in-january"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US hospitals brace for potential Omicron surge in January }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Although Joe Manchin \u8217\'20\'19s criticism is the most significant issue in the Build Back Better negotiations right now, it is far from the only hurdle that the bill faces in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Punchbowl News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://email.punchbowl.news/t/ViewEmailArchive/t/E2B24D9F96920D302540EF23F30FEDED/C67FD2F38AC4859C/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Democrats are fighting among themselves over [the state and local income tax deduction] and immigration. That\u8217\'20\'19s not Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s fault. And the parliamentarian hasn\u8217\'20\'19t finished scrubbing the bill for possible Byrd Rule problem. And that isn\u8217\'20\'19t Manchin\u8217\'20\'19s fault.\par \par \uc2 So let\u8217\'20\'19s be real. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just Manchin. He\u8217\'20\'19s a big problem for the leadership and White House, easily the most high profile headache, but hardly the only one. They don\u8217\'20\'19t have the text of the legislation finished. The parliamentarian is still grinding away. [Centrist Senator \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2 ] hasn\u8217\'20\'19t publicly endorsed the package, which makes some Senate Democrats uneasy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/us-policy/2021/12/15/biden-manchin-spending-democrats/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 , Joe Manchin has expressed criticism of the proposal to continue the expanded child tax credit program through the Build Back Better Act.\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus relief package that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signed in March included changes to the program, such as allowing families with children to receive monthly checks (rather than an annual lump sum after filing taxes) and making the credit fully refundable (so more low-income families could access the benefit).\par \par \uc2 Democrats want to continue the expanded program for one year through their $1.75tn spending package, but Manchin has reportedly expressed concern about the cost of doing so.\par \par \uc2 The main issue is that Manchin believes all the programs in the bill should be viewed on a 10-year basis, even though some of them expire after just a year or a few years.\par \par \uc2 And if the expanded child tax credit program were extended through the next decade, which the current version of the bill does not call for, it would require significantly more funding than the bill allocates.\par \par \uc2 But the expanded tax credit is a point of pride for Biden and other Democrats from the relief bill, so they will likely be very hesitant to cut it from the spending package. The negotiations continue, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Centrist senators throw up roadblocks for Build Back Better and voting rights\par \par \uc2 Greetings from Washington, live blog readers.\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats had initially hoped to pass their Build Back Better Act before the end of the year, but that deadline is slipping away, as talks between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Joe Manchin drag out.\par \par \uc2 Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/12/15/biden-manchin-megabill-524776"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The legislation looks increasingly likely to stall over the impending holiday break, prompting Biden himself to bemoan the slow pace. And Manchin (D-W.Va.) grew frustrated on Wednesday when questioned about whether he opposes a provision in the bill to extend the expanded child tax credit, deeming those queries \u8216\'20\'18bullshit\u8217\'20\'19 and denying that he wants to end the $300 monthly check many families receive for children....\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The talks between [Biden] and Manchin have been going very poorly. They are far apart,\u8217\'20\'19 the source said.\par \par \uc2 Because of the stalled negotiations, Democrats were instead looking to pass a voting rights bill this month, by approving changes to Senate rules to circumvent a Republican filibuster on the issue.\par \par \uc2 But now Kyrsten Sinema is putting the brakes on that idea as well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2021/12/15/sinema-democrats-filibuster-changes-524809"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is Politico again}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Arizona moderate is making clear that she intends to keep protecting the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s 60-vote requirement on most legislation and she isn\u8217\'20\'19t ready to entertain changing rules to pass sweeping elections or voting legislation with a simple majority....\par \par \uc2 In a statement to POLITICO, a spokesperson said that Sinema \u8216\'20\'18continues to support the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s 60-vote threshold, to protect the country from repeated radical reversals in federal policy which would cement uncertainty, deepen divisions, and further erode Americans\u8217\'20\'19 confidence in our government.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 This centrist opposition means that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of ending his first year in office with a significant legislative accomplishment are quickly disappearing, along with Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 agenda.\par \par \uc2 The blog will have more coming up, so stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211216ehcg0025v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
