\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 California to let citizens enforce ban on assault weapons, echoing Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang and agencies \par \uc2 453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2021\par 10:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pledge draws inspiration from Texas law that allows citizens to enforce ban on abortions from about six weeks of pregnancy\par \par \uc2 California governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  has pledged to empower private citizens to enforce a ban on the manufacture and sale of assault weapons in the state, citing the same authority claimed by conservative lawmakers in Texas to outlaw most abortions there after only around six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will work to create the ability for private citizens to sue anyone who manufactures, distributes, or sells an assault weapon or ghost gun kit or parts in California,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor\u8217\'20\'19s office said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAgovernor/status/1469865007517089798?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 For three decades, California has banned the manufacture and sale of various assault-style weapons. However, in June, a federal judge overturned that ban, much to the ire of Democrats and gun-control activists, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jun/05/california-assault-rifles-ban-gavin-newsom-judge-roger-benitez-ar-15-swiss-army-knife"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CLike the Swiss army knife, the popular AR-15 rifle is a perfect combination for home defense weapon and homeland defense equipment. Good for both home and battle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s ban remained in place while the state appealed.\par \par \uc2 Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s move draws inspiration from a controversial Texas law that allows private citizens to enforce the ban on abortions after the earliest fetal cardiac activity is detected, thus empowering them to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics and anyone else who \u8220\'20\'1Caids and abets\u8221\'20\'1D with the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Last Friday, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  that Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can sue over the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions, but allowed the law, the strictest such regulation in the US to date, to remain in effect, causing outrage within the court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-abortion-ruling-texas-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 liberal-leaning minority}}}\uc2  and among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/us-supreme-court-abortion-texas-law-critics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-choice advocates}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Newsom condemned the ruling, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI am outraged by yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  decision allowing Texas\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services to remain in place \u8230\'20\'26 But if states can now shield their laws from review by the federal courts that compare assault weapons to Swiss Army knives, then California will use the authority to protect people\u8217\'20\'19s lives, where Texas used it to put women in harm\u8217\'20\'19s way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The governor added that he has directed his staff to work with California\u8217\'20\'19s legislature and its Democratic attorney general to pass a law that would let private citizens sue to enforce California\u8217\'20\'19s ban on assault weapons.\par \par \uc2 Newsom said people who sue could win up to $10,000 per violation plus other costs and attorney fees.\par \par \uc2 Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s declaration is a fulfilled prophecy for some gun rights groups who had predicted progressive states would attempt to use Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to restrict access to guns.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211214ehce001hb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
