\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Women are capable of doing this\u8217\'20\'19: the doctor defying local laws to provide safe abortions by sea or mail\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,877 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 December 2021\par 10:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dr Rebecca Gomperts made waves providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in international waters around the world. Now she\u8217\'20\'19s prepared to help American women\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Sunday morning, less than a week after the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/dec/02/supreme-court-signalling-end-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  that it was ready to pave the way for new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US, and I\u8217\'20\'19m on the phone with a Dutch \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider who has watched the proceedings from half a world away.\par \par \uc2 Dr Rebecca Gomperts tells me that she\u8217\'20\'19s shocked with the situation in Texas, which recently enacted a near total ban on legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 not because the state government passed the law, but because doctors in the state are largely complying with it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would have thought that all these clinics would have said, \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19ll just do it,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she tells me.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Gomperts has been doing just that. Gomperts has made her career providing free or very low-cost abortions to patients in need around the world, regardless of local law. In 2018, she founded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aid Access}}}\uc2 , a site that allows women in the US to get abortions with the help of 10 US-based providers.\par \par \uc2 The doctors \u8220\'20\'1Cdo it [via telemedicine] in their own states, like New York, California, Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D Doctors write prescriptions for drugs that induce miscarriage, which then get sent to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/health/archive/2018/10/women-on-web-safe-abortion-mail/573322/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pharmacy in India}}}\uc2  that Gomperts vetted herself. And from India, the drugs get shipped to women\u8217\'20\'19s homes \u8211\'20\'13 including in states, like Texas, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is practically inaccessible and legally all but banned. Founded especially to help American women \u8211\'20\'13 and to evade legal challenges in the US \u8211\'20\'13 Aid Access is one of the most affordable ways to get a safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in America. \u8220\'20\'1CThey only charge $150,\u8221\'20\'1D Gomperts says. The website says they try to help women who cannot pay, too.\par \par \uc2 The project has already come under fire from the anti-choice powers that be. In 2019, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  issued Gomperts a cease-and-desist letter. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/european-doctor-prescribes-abortion-pills-u-s-women-over-internet-n1012676"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She didn\u8217\'20\'19t comply}}}\uc2 . When Trump health department secretary \uc2 Alex Azar\uc2  began blocking payments to Aid Access and seizing its packages from the mail, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2019/09/09/758871490/european-doctor-who-prescribes-abortion-pills-to-u-s-women-online-sues-fda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she sued him}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Gomperts has been helping women who face restrictive legal regimes get safe abortions since long before the advent of Aid Access. Her career as an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist didn\u8217\'20\'19t start online, but on a boat.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 In the late 1990s, when Gomperts was a young activist, she travelled to countries where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was illegal and met woman after woman whose lives and health had been warped by unwanted pregnancies or unsafe procedures. But Gomperts had an idea. Twelve miles off a coast, in international waters, local laws don\u8217\'20\'19t apply \u8211\'20\'13 instead, vessels must follow the laws of the country whose flag they fly. Gomperts was from the Netherlands, a nation with some of the most permissive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the world. A boat flying a Dutch flag could legally dock in a country that banned or criminalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pick up local women in need, and then take them out to sea, to perform safe abortions on the water, beyond the reach of misogynist laws. The project espoused a kind of radical pragmatism \u8211\'20\'13 clever in its evasion of the law, defiant in its determination to grant women the choice that their governments denied them. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenonwaves.org/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women on Waves}}}\uc2  was born.\par \par \uc2 It was the beginning of Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 career as perhaps the world\u8217\'20\'19s most inventive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access activist. Few human rights campaigners have been so daring and incendiary in their tactics, and few have provoked the ire of so many different national governments. In Morocco, she was chased out of a port. In Poland, a group of rageful men greeted her at a dock, screaming that she was a Nazi. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t even make it to Portugal \u8211\'20\'13 the government sent two warships to stop her boat from entering territorial waters.\par \par \uc2 But the massive and hostile resistance to her work didn\u8217\'20\'19t make her back down; it made her diversify her tactics. She came to see her job as a combination of direct provision, legal challenges, lobbying, public health education campaigns and scientific research.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the combination is extremely important,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of our work is advocacy. Direct provision makes visible the obstacles to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, and that\u8217\'20\'19s also where we do most of the research \u8230\'20\'26 We were the first ones that were writing about the safety of telemedical abortions and self-managed abortions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gomperts never visits another country without an invitation from a local women\u8217\'20\'19s group, and once she arrives, she not only provides abortions but also shares best practices for helping women end their pregnancies once she\u8217\'20\'19s gone. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have trained all the women\u8217\'20\'19s organizations\u8221\'20\'1D that they work with, she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe started training them to run [\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  help] hotlines in 2008. So, we\u8217\'20\'19ve done all of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much of her work, too, has involved publicity. For years, wherever the boat went, cameras followed, and Gomperts, for all her radicalism, proved a savvy and skilful manipulator of the media. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was founding \uc2 Women on Waves\uc2 , that was one of the criticisms actually,\u8221\'20\'1D she tells me. \u8220\'20\'1CMany of the classic \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activists, they said, \u8216\'20\'18You cannot combine these two\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 provision and publicity \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18because it\u8217\'20\'19s about vulnerable women.\u8217\'20\'19 But what I found is actually that women that need abortions, that are living in a situation where their rights are being denied \u8211\'20\'13 they want to be a part of [changing] that.\u8221\'20\'1D She recalls one woman she met on a trip to Mexico, who had been offered a way to have a safe, but clandestine, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in her home town. \u8220\'20\'1CShe says, \u8216\'20\'18No. I want to have a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D The woman insisted on boarding the boat.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 In the two decades since she began \uc2 Women on Waves\uc2 , the organization has spun off into multiple different projects, all meant to increase practical access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in places where it is illegal. There are the sister sites {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/en/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aid Access}}}\uc2  (for the US) and Women on Web (for the rest of the world), which stretch the technicalities of the law to ship pills to women in the mail. There is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hesperian.org/books-and-resources/our-mobile-applications/safe-abortion-sa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Safe \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  app}}}\uc2 , which helps users calculate gestational time, tells them which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  methods could be effective, and provides instructions for how to use \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 approved drugs.\par \par \uc2 And there are the hotlines and email addresses that Gomperts and her team have set up in countries around the world, where women can speak to a real human being who will give them accurate information about how to access drugs without a prescription, how to take the medication, and how to stay safe before, during, and after the termination.\par \par \uc2 Her interventions range from the strictly practical to the intrepidly cheeky. In 2015, she travelled to Frankfurt an der Oder, a German town on the border with Poland, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal. Once there, she flew \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills over the border into the Polish town of Slubice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewer.gutools.co.uk/world/2015/jun/24/abortion-drone-border-poland-germany-women-on-waves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a drone}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 These pills \u8211\'20\'13 mifepristone and misoprostol \u8211\'20\'13 are Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 real life\u8217\'20\'19s work. The boat, the websites, the drones \u8211\'20\'13 all these are mere vessels for the true message that safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible with medication, even in countries where it is illegal. Women need not ingest poison, or insert long, sharp objects through their cervix. They can just take some pills.\par \par \uc2 In our conversation, Gomperts is adamant on this point: there is no reason, she argues, to require extensive medical exams or interventions before administering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 She cites studies showing both the safety of the medications themselves, and the reliability of prescribing them without the expensive and often inaccessible prerequisites of in-person doctor\u8217\'20\'19s visits and ultrasounds. Recent pandemic history backs her up. Since the advent of Covid, \u8220\'20\'1CThe UK has been massively returning to telemedical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout ultrasounds, without any of those things.\u8221\'20\'1D The results? Women in early pregnancy have been having perfectly safe, effective abortions on their own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are capable of doing this,\u8221\'20\'1D Gomperts says. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s not very different from a miscarriage, and we trust women to have miscarriages on their own without medical intervention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One of the things that we try to do by providing the services is to strengthen their dignity and empowerment.\par \par \uc2 Rebecca Gompert\par \par \uc2 In fact, if a self-managed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patient does run into complication \u8211\'20\'13 a rare event \u8211\'20\'13Gomperts and her organizations recommend that she go to a local doctor, and tell them that she is having a spontaneous miscarriage. A doctor can\u8217\'20\'19t tell that she\u8217\'20\'19s taken pills, and the treatment is the same.\par \par \uc2 To Gomperts, there is little question that the risks of providing abortions to women who lack legal permission to get them are outweighed by the moral righteousness of her mission. This is part of what is so refreshing about her: the frankness of her feminist commitment. Many people will say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is a human rights issue, but too few are willing to treat it with the urgency that that label demands. This is part of Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 argument: that principled people have a moral obligation to break unjust laws.\par \par \uc2 Which brings us to the question of dignity. I\u8217\'20\'19m struck, again and again, at the sheer amount of effort \u8211\'20\'13 logistical, legal, monetary \u8211\'20\'13 that Gomperts and her colleagues must put into providing abortions.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, this effort is a testament to their dedication; on the other hand, the fact that such exertion is necessary at all in order to allow women to control their own lives is degrading and cruel. But to Gomperts, her great effort to grant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access signifies a great respect for her patients. \u8220\'20\'1COne of the things that we try to do, actually, by providing the services, is to strengthen their dignity and empowerment,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CIt shows them that we trust them.\u8221\'20\'1D In this way, her work gives women back some of the respect that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans take away from them. All her projects are based upon this radical premise: That women are adults, who can be trusted with their own lives.\par \par \uc2 On the phone, Gomperts is friendly and vivacious. Even in hostile interviews, she projects an almost preternatural calm. The writer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thedailybeast.com/abortion-at-sea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michelle Goldberg}}}\uc2  once referred to this quality as Gomperts\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cserene audacity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Towards the end of our call, I ask her how she manages to retain her composure, even in conversations where people challenge women\u8217\'20\'19s right to refuse pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 the cause to which she has devoted her life. I expect her to tell me about her media training or her self-discipline, the strategies she deploys to keep her face straight and her voice steady.\par \par \uc2 But for the first time in our conversation, the line goes silent. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a hard question,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, finally. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know \u8230\'20\'26 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to answer that.\u8221\'20\'1D Later, I realize that it is as if I had asked her how she remains calm while explaining that the Earth is not flat, that the sky is not green. She has the confidence of a bone-deep conviction: Women deserve to choose.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211213ehcd001ht\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
