\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden \u8216\'20\'18concerned\u8217\'20\'19 over supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s Texas  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling, says White House \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 6,662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2021\par 01:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 President is \u8216\'20\'18deeply committed\u8217\'20\'19 to Roe v Wade, says PsakiTexas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can sue over ban but Scotus won\u8217\'20\'19t stop lawBiden speaks at memorial for former US senator Bob DoleSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all for today, thanks for following along. Some key links:\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled on Friday that Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers can sue}}}\uc2  over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state\u8217\'20\'19s ban}}}\uc2  on most abortions, but the justices are allowing the law, the strictest such regulation in America to date, to remain in effect.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , the liberal-leaning justice on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-abortion-ruling-texas-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said lawmakers in the Republican-controlled legislature of Texas}}}\uc2  had \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially suspended a constitutional guarantee: a pregnant woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her own body\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?page=with:block-61b3ae338f0819fcb698dec6#block-61b3ae338f0819fcb698dec6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned\u8221\'20\'1D about the Texas law staying in effect and is \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply committed\u8221\'20\'1D to Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 * Responding to new inflation figures that cite US inflation at its highest level since 1982, Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?page=with:block-61b3aa598f087461a36a4084#block-61b3aa598f087461a36a4084"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that inflation is a \u8220\'20\'1Creal bump in the road\u8221\'20\'1D and that current figures are at \u8220\'20\'1Cthe peak of the crisis\u8221\'20\'1D with positive change coming.\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/10/capitol-attack-committee-trump-officials-subpoenas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued new subpoenas}}}\uc2  on Friday against two Trump White House officials involved in organizing the rally and march that descended into the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 * Some areas in the US are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/dec/10/covid-vaccine-booster-pharmacy-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing shortages of pharmacy staff}}}\uc2  to administer vaccines.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 US judge blocks Tennessee law that restricted mask requirements\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has temporarily blocked a Tennessee law that sharply restricts public schools from requiring masks and prohibits local officials from making decisions about quarantines, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-health-lawsuits-tennessee-nashville-6b9d4ae5344c4f38e23f7ed469b8393e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 . From the AP:\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit against the state was filed on behalf of eight students between the ages of seven and 14 who have disabilities and who are deemed by federal health officials as being more vulnerable to serious illness or death if they get Covid-19. The ruling also blocks the law\u8217\'20\'19s provision that says local health and school officials can\u8217\'20\'19t make their own coronavirus quarantining decisions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is also in the public\u8217\'20\'19s interest to slow the spread of COVID-19 in Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s schools,\u8221\'20\'1D Crenshaw wrote in his ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants have proffered absolutely nothing to suggest that any harm would come from allowing individual school districts to determine what is best for their schools, just as they did prior to the enactment of (the law.)\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The judge, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tennessean.com/story/news/politics/2021/12/10/federal-judge-blocks-tennessee-law-preventing-schools-issuing-mask-mandates/8800549002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessean reported}}}\uc2 , raised concerns that the new law \u8220\'20\'1Coffers no protection to students, let alone those that are disabled\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CThis does not serve the public interest... Allowing children to safely attend school does.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-health-lawsuits-tennessee-nashville-6b9d4ae5344c4f38e23f7ed469b8393e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2  that the governor has faced scrutiny for signing the legislation even though his administration had allegedly warned lawmakers that the bill could violate federal disability laws and risk the state losing federal funding.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 The journalists \uc2 Maria Ressa\uc2  and Dmitry Muratov received the Nobel peace prize on Friday at a ceremony that Ressa was almost blocked from attending because of travel restrictions related to legal cases filed against her in the Philippines, \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Rebecca Ratcliffe reports:\par \par \uc2 Ressa, 58, the chief executive and co-founder of the online news platform Rappler, praised for exposing abuses of power and growing authoritarianism under the Philippine president, \uc2 Rodrigo Duterte\uc2 , is facing charges that could lead to about 100 years in jail. Having been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/oct/08/journalists-maria-ressa-and-dmitry-muratov-win-nobel-peace-prize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 awarded the prize alongside Muratov in October}}}\uc2 , she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/03/philippines-court-allows-nobel-laureate-maria-ressa-norway-journalist-travel-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted permission to attend}}}\uc2  the ceremony earlier this month by the Philippine court of appeals, which ruled she was not a flight risk.\par \par \uc2 Muratov, 59, the editor-in-chief of Novaya Gazeta, who shared the 2021 Nobel peace prize, was described as one of the most prominent defenders of freedom of speech in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  today. \u8220\'20\'1CNovaya Gazeta is the most independent newspaper in Russia today, with a fundamentally critical attitude towards power,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Berit Reiss-Andersen\uc2 , the chair of the Norwegian Nobel committee, said at the ceremony at Oslo City Hall.\par \par \uc2 More here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/10/journalists-maria-ressa-and-dmitry-muratov-receive-nobel-peace-prize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Journalists Maria Ressa and Dmitry Muratov receive Nobel peace prize in Oslo}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More US states faced with Covid-19 surges are calling on the National Guard and military personnel to provide assistance at hospitals, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/coronavirus-pandemic-business-health-new-york-michigan-f80c396cc06d3b072c49e5fa57f5ab36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 . From the AP:\par \par \uc2 People who became sick after refusing to get vaccinated are overwhelming hospitals in certain states, especially in the Northeast and the Upper Midwest. New York, meanwhile, announced a statewide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/new-york-mask-mandate-coronavirus-cfe8fb80401bb0fe66f3260bf5f51dda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indoor mask order}}}\uc2 , effective Monday and lasting five weeks through the holiday season.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re entering a time of uncertainty, and we could either plateau here or our cases could get out of control,\u8221\'20\'1D governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  warned Friday.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, health director Elizabeth Hertel was equally blunt: \u8220\'20\'1CI want to be absolutely clear: You are risking serious illness, hospitalization and even death\u8221\'20\'1D without a vaccination.\par \par \uc2 Johns Hopkins\uc2  university data shows that the seven-day rolling average for daily new cases in the US rose over the past two weeks to 117,677 by Thursday, compared to 84,756 on 25 November, which was Thanksgiving day, the AP said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former Houston police officer has been sentenced to 45 days in jail for his involvement in the 6 January riot at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltr??JAIL TIME?? Former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/houstonpolice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @houstonpolice}}}\uc2  Ofc Tam Pham gets 45 days in prison for misdemeanor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/CapitolRiot?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #CapitolRiot}}}\uc2  charge. Judge strongly considered probation but said Pham violated sworn duties to uphold constitution and added air of legitimacy to riot because Pham was police officer at time {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n7GaKEMh2M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n7GaKEMh2M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Eric Flack (@EricFlackTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EricFlackTV/status/1469371007027023872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 In September, Pham {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox7austin.com/news/u-s-capitol-riot-former-houston-police-officer-sentenced-to-45-days-in-jail?taid=61b3d8744bd3090001f02e62&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=trueanthem&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty}}}\uc2  to parading, demonstrating or picketing in a Capitol building. He was caught on video saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re taking the house back,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1469422744542629892"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to sentencing documents}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrSentencing in 10 minutes in Jan 6 case of former Houston police officer Tam Pham, who admits being unlawfully in Capitol & posing "for a picture in front of a bronze statue of President Gerald Ford in whose arms a flag had been placed that read, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump \u8211\'20\'13 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 No More Bullsh**\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UfCLQ5CVoy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UfCLQ5CVoy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott MacFarlane (@MacFarlaneNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1469319240498835456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Pham had worked for the Houston police department for 18 years, but resigned after the department learned of his involvement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox7austin.com/news/u-s-capitol-riot-former-houston-police-officer-sentenced-to-45-days-in-jail?taid=61b3d8744bd3090001f02e62&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=trueanthem&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox 7 in Texas reported}}}\uc2 . He was off duty when he was at the \uc2 Capitol\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sworn officers from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/16/us-capitol-riot-police-neo-nazis-far-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across the country}}}\uc2  were caught traveling to the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and participating in the protest and entering the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  while off duty.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The mother of Austin Tice, the journalist who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/oct/18/austin-tice-parents-syria-missing-journalist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went missing in Syria in 2012}}}\uc2 , met today with the White House\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sacbee.com/news/politics-government/article256484786.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national security advisor}}}\uc2 , Jake Sullivan.\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary confirmed the meeting but did not provide reporters with an update on the status of the case: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t give you an assessment. Obviously we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything we can,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sacbee.com/news/politics-government/article256484786.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jen Psaki said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s our standard practice not to share any specific details about any potential meetings or specific cases out of respect for the families, and to preserve confidentiality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Debra Tice criticized Biden earlier in the week in a press conference, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.charlotteobserver.com/news/politics-government/article256453726.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 McClatchy reported}}}\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not been able to get a meeting with him.: \u8220\'20\'1CHe has never said Austin\u8217\'20\'19s name publicly. And I wonder if he\u8217\'20\'19s allowed himself to forget about Austin. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have any indication otherwise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/austin-tice-syria-jake-sullivan-03ef4368-1bba-48fb-badd-98a7e2c79b7e.html?utm_campaign=organic&utm_medium=socialshare&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reported}}}\uc2 , Sullivan held a Zoom call with families of dozens of hostages after some of them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/hostage-families-biden-fb064b7b-cf21-4bfa-b29c-d03b727f2828.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly expressed frustration}}}\uc2  that they had not yet been able to meet with Biden.\par \par \uc2 enltrAustin Tice's mother {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DebraTice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DebraTice}}}\uc2  says Secretary Blinken is "all in" on bringing her son home. The hurdle is with the White House.\par \par \uc2 She hasn't gotten a meeting with Biden yet: "I wonder if he's allowed himself to forget Austin's name." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jSyzAQNckE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jSyzAQNckE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Hagedorn (@ElizHagedorn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ElizHagedorn/status/1468958639121584131?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 9, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden condemns \uc2 Kellogg's\uc2  'attack on the union' amid strike\par \par \uc2 Hi all \u8211\'20\'13 Sam Levin here taking over our live coverage for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 Biden has released a statement on the reports that \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  is permanently replacing 1,400 workers who have been on strike since October:\par \par \uc2 Permanently replacing striking workers is an existential attack on the union and its members\u8217\'20\'19 jobs and livelihoods. I have long opposed permanent striker replacements and I strongly support legislation that would ban that practice.\par \par \uc2 And such action undermines the critical role collective bargaining plays in providing workers a voice and the opportunity to improve their lives while contributing fully to their employer\u8217\'20\'19s success.\par \par \uc2 The full statement here:\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden statement on Kellogg {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/boFGNYf2Dl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/boFGNYf2Dl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeff Stein (@JStein_WaPo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JStein_WaPo/status/1469409956151578625?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The 1,400 \uc2 Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  workers at four plants in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/oct/07/kelloggs-workers-strike-offshore-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike after their current union contracts expired}}}\uc2 . The workers across four plants are represented by the \uc2 Bakery, Confectionery, Tobacco Workers and Grain Millers International Union\uc2  (\uc2 BCTGM\uc2 ) and produce cereals for brands, including Rice Krispies, Fruit Loops, Frosted Flakes and Raisin Bran, at plants in Michigan, Tennessee, Nebraska and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 More on the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/07/kellogg-strike-workers-pay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kellogg to replace 1,400 strikers as deal is rejected}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/oct/07/kelloggs-workers-strike-offshore-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Death of 1,000 cuts\u8217\'20\'19: Kellogg\u8217\'20\'19s workers on why they\u8217\'20\'19re striking}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me today! I\u8217\'20\'19ll be handing over the blog to Sam Levin.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of today\u8217\'20\'19s events:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b38f698f0819fcb698dcd8#block-61b38f698f0819fcb698dcd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  its score for the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better agenda, saying the social package will add $3tn to the US deficit. Democrats dispute the figures.\par \par \uc2 * Biden addressed new inflation figures, saying inflation is at \u8216\'20\'18peak of the crisis\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18real bump in the road\u8217\'20\'19, but that positive changes in the economy are expected and occurring.\par \par \uc2 * The White House said Biden is \u8216\'20\'18deeply committed\u8217\'20\'19 to Roe v Wade and \u8216\'20\'18concerned\u8217\'20\'19 following a decision by Scotus on the Texas near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 * The US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0#block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed}}}\uc2  America\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, in Texas, to remain in place, even as it permitted clinics to go ahead with legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the funeral for \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  at the national cathedral in Washington, DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?page=with:block-61b383438f0819fcb698dbb6#block-61b383438f0819fcb698dbb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  the former senator \u8220\'20\'1Cone of our greatest patriots\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The US president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0#block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrapped up}}}\uc2  the two-day inaugural White House summit for democracy, with world leaders attending virtually because of the pandemic, by defending fair elections and a free press.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s an excerpt from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  on more information concerning the House investigating committee\u8217\'20\'19s additional subpoenas issued today on the events of 6 January:\par \par \uc2 The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack on Friday issued new subpoenas against two Trump White House officials involved in organizing the rally and march that descended into the 6 January insurrection, as they inquire into the extent of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  involvement.\par \par \uc2 The select committee issued orders compelling documents and testimony to Brian Jack, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House director of political affairs, now working for the House minority leader Kevin McCarthy, and Max Miller, a former deputy manager for the Trump campaign.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the chairman of the select committee, said in the subpoena letter for Miller that the panel targeted him as he attended a 4 January meeting with Trump in a private White House dining room about who should speak at the rally on the morning of 6 January.\par \par \uc2 Miller also communicated with the then deputy secretary of the interior and the then-acting director of the National Park Service to strong-arm career officials, who had declined to allow the rally from taking place on the Ellipse, to reverse course, Thompson said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full Guardian article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/10/capitol-attack-committee-trump-officials-subpoenas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, J oe Biden said that he will speak to West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  next week, but is unsure if he c an get Manchin to support the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better bill.\par \par \uc2 While taking questions at his virtual Summit for Democracy, Biden responded to a question if he could get Manchin to vote for the bill given that inflation is at a record high:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know the answer to that. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be talking to him at the beginning of the week,\u8221\'20\'1D answered Biden.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden's full answer when asked if he thinks he can get Manchin to vote yes on Build Back Better if inflation is this high: "Well, I don't know the answer to that. I'm going to be talking to him at the beginning of the week..." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2yqFZjX9qt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2yqFZjX9qt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1469405325350551552?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Manchin is a key moderate holding up the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better agenda, a social spending package, though some democrats don\u8217\'20\'19t think that Manchin is willing to secure a vote on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s agenda by Christmas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/585218-democrats-dont-think-manchin-wants-biden-agenda-vote-by-christmas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Hill. }}}\par \par \uc2 During today\u8217\'20\'19s press briefing, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  responded to questions on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comment saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is exactly the time to pass this bill and move it forward so that we can lower costs for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrJen Psaki tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Phil_Mattingly?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Phil_Mattingly}}}\uc2  to expect Biden to make the case to West Virginia Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  "that this is exactly the time to pass this bill and move it forward so that we can lower costs for the American people," next week, hitting Republicans for voting against BBB {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KxWGGas9mD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KxWGGas9mD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DJ Judd (@DJJudd) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DJJudd/status/1469398126733709318?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When asked if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  would consider a pardon of \uc2 WikiLeaks\uc2  founder Julian Assange, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is an advocate for free speech and freedom of the press.\par \par \uc2 Psaki referred questions regarding the Julian Assange case to the justice department, noting that it is still an ongoing case.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, Psaki responded to an inquiry about how some view prosecuting Assange as an attack on freedom of press, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe president has been an advocate for freedom of speech, freedom of press\u8221\'20\'1D, also noting the virtual Summit for Democracy the president is wrapping up today.\par \par \uc2 The questions came after a ruling today that Assange can be extradited to the US to face espionage charges. Here is more on the case from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/benquinn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ben Quinn}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Julian Assange can be extradited to the US, according to the high court, as it overturned a judgment earlier this year and sparked condemnation from press freedom advocates.\par \par \uc2 The decision deals a major blow to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/wikileaks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WikiLeaks}}}\uc2  co-founder\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to prevent his extradition to the US to face espionage charges, although his lawyers announced they would seek to appeal.\par \par \uc2 Two of Britain\u8217\'20\'19s most senior judges found on Friday that a then district judge based her decision earlier this year on the risk of Assange being held in highly restrictive US prison conditions.\par \par \uc2 In their ruling, they sided with the US authorities after a package of assurances were put forward that Assange would not face those strictest measures unless he committed an act in the future that required them.\par \par \uc2 Read the full Guardian article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/dec/10/julian-assange-can-be-extradited-to-us-to-face-espionage-charges-court-rules"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House select committee overseeing the investigation into the January 6 insurrection just subpoenaed six more people, including an Ohio Congressional candidate who has been backed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The committee says that Max Miller, the candidate and former Trump aide, met with Trump two days before the rally held outside the White House to discuss details of the event.\par \par \uc2 Others included in the subpoena are Brian Jack, a former Trump aide and current adviser to House minority leader Kevin McCarthy, and Ed Martin, an organizer of the \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D rallies that claimed Democrats stole the election.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2021/12/10/house-committee-subpoenas-six-individuals-linked-jan-6-rally-including-trump-backed-ohio-congressional-candidate/?utm_source=feedly&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wp_politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 , the House select committee say the witnesses \u8220\'20\'1Capparently worked to stage the rallies on January 5th and 6th\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome appeared to have had direct communication with the former president regarding the rally at the Ellipse directly preceding the attack on the US Capitol,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Committee subpoenas individuals involved in the planning of January 5th and 6th rallies, including individuals who worked directly with the former President:\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Bryan Lewis\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Ed Martin\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Kimberly Fletcher\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Robert \u8220\'20\'1CBobby\u8221\'20\'1D Peede, Jr.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Max Miller\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 Brian Jack\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 January 6th Committee (@January6thCmte) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/January6thCmte/status/1469390129500504066?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden 'deeply committed' to Roe v Wade and 'concerned' by Scotus decision\par \par \uc2 Following the Scotus decision on the Texas near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the White House has said that Biden is \u8220\'20\'1Cconcerned\u8221\'20\'1D about the Texas law staying in effect and is \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply committed\u8221\'20\'1D to Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The White House also said that the ruling today is a reminder that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should be codified.\par \par \uc2 During a press briefing today, press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  spoke on the Scotus ruling today, saying that Biden is concerned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban will remain in place.\par \par \uc2 Psaki also noted \u8220\'20\'1Chow much these rights are at risk\u8221\'20\'1D and the need to legislate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access through Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, which passed the House in September but has been stuck in limbo in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Psaki would not say how the bill would get passed through the Senate, saying there was nothing new to add on that.\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden is \u8216\'20\'18very concerned\u8217\'20\'19 about the Supreme Court allowing Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to remain in place, said press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 . She added that the ruling is a reminder of \u8216\'20\'18how much these rights are at risk.\u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CaRtDkP1fC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CaRtDkP1fC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NowThis (@nowthisnews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nowthisnews/status/1469392951163994114?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Psaki also said that a statement on the ruling on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s behalf will be coming shortly as Biden spent most of the day at a memorial for former US senator \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden addresses new inflation figures, says inflation at 'peak of the crisis' and 'real bump in the road'\par \par \uc2 Responding to new inflation figures that cite US inflation at its highest level since 1982, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  today said that inflation is a \u8220\'20\'1Creal bump in the road\u8221\'20\'1D and that current figures are at \u8220\'20\'1Cthe peak of the crisis\u8221\'20\'1D with positive change coming.\par \par \uc2 During questions following closing remarks at his virtual Summit for Democracy, Biden responded to a question from a CNN reporter about inflation, saying that US consumers are seeing the peak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think you\u8217\'20\'19ll see it change sooner, quicker, more rapidly than people think. Every other aspect of the economy is racing ahead,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Biden takes a question from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kaitlancollins}}}\uc2  on whether we\u8217\'20\'19re seeking the peak of inflation:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think you\u8217\'20\'19ll see it change sooner, quicker, more rapidly than people think. Every other aspect of the economy is racing ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nIZEcOmlRX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nIZEcOmlRX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joey Garrison (@joeygarrison) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joeygarrison/status/1469386971411849222?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, Biden provided a statement in response to new inflation figures, noting that prices for several goods are coming down, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-12-10/biden-says-inflation-slowing-after-hitting-39-year-high?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_content=politics&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&cmpid%3D=socialflow-twitter-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported Bloomberg}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s numbers reflect the pressures that economies around the world are facing as we emerge from a global pandemic -- prices are rising,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement after a Labor Department report showed a 6.8% annual gain in the consumer price index in November...\par \par \uc2 Biden said that \u8220\'20\'1Chalf of the price increases in this report are in cars and energy costs from November\u8221\'20\'1D and that since then, prices have begun to slide in both sectors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven with this progress, price increases continue to squeeze family budgets,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are making progress on pandemic related challenges to our supply chain which make it more expensive to get goods on shelves, and I expect more progress on that in the weeks ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the Bloomberg article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-12-10/biden-says-inflation-slowing-after-hitting-39-year-high?utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social&utm_content=politics&utm_campaign=socialflow-organic&cmpid%3D=socialflow-twitter-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here (paywall).}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden promoted the Freedom to Vote act and the John Lewis Voting Rights Advancement act during his closing remarks at the virtual Summit for Democracy, saying that Congress will get the bills passed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sacred right to vote, to vote freely, the right to have your vote counted, is the threshold liberty for democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout it, virtually nothing\u8217\'20\'19s possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden did not mention how the two key voting rights bills will get passed, as disdain mounts among voting rights advocates who say Biden is failing on addressing voting rights.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  has covered anger towards the Biden administration among voting rights advocates with many noting that \u8220\'20\'1Ctime is running out\u8221\'20\'1D to get key legislation passed:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/the-fight-to-vote-newsletter-biden-voting-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Frustrating\u8217\'20\'19 White House meeting escalates fears Biden is failing on voting rights | The fight to vote}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/06/voting-rights-biden-democrats-voting-rights-legislation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Time is running out\u8217\'20\'19: can Congress pass a voting rights bill after months of failure?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will now be giving remarks for the last day of his virtual Summit for Democracy event that began yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivers remarks, as \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , United States Secretary of State listens on, at the virtual Summit for Democracy at the White House in Washington, D.C. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-europe-elections-media-voting-rights-85d99ee88c6122f21e55d5727eb20e13?user_email=&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=MorningWire_Dec10&utm_term=Morning%20Wire%20Subscribers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier that Biden will be focusing on election integrity and bolstering independent media during the today\u8217\'20\'19s half of the summit.\par \par \uc2 Press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  will be holding a press briefing afterwards.\par \par \uc2 More information on what Biden said during the first day of the summit is available {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/joe-biden-summit-for-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  in a piece written by \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/shah-meer-baloch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shah Meer Baloch}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/joe-biden-summit-for-democracy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18An urgent matter\u8217\'20\'19: Biden warns democracy is under threat at summit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been a lively morning in US politics, stay tuned for all the latest coverage this afternoon, too.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b38f698f0819fcb698dcd8#block-61b38f698f0819fcb698dcd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released}}}\uc2  its score for the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better agenda, saying the social package will add $3tn to the US deficit. Democrats dispute the figures.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at the funeral for \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  at the national cathedral in Washington, DC, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?page=with:block-61b383438f0819fcb698dbb6#block-61b383438f0819fcb698dbb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling}}}\uc2  the former senator \u8220\'20\'1Cone of our greatest patriots\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * The supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0#block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed}}}\uc2  America\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, in Texas, to remain in place, even as it permitted clinics to go ahead with legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 * The US president planned to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/dec/10/joe-biden-democracy-summit-supreme-court-abortion-texas-us-politics-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0#block-61b36a4d8f08cfef2cf643e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrap up}}}\uc2  the two-day inaugural White House summit for democracy, with world leaders attending virtually because of the pandemic, by defending fair elections and a free press.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2 : Build Back Better will add $3tn to deficit\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Congressional Budget Office\uc2  has released their score for the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Build Back Better agenda, saying the social package will add $3tn to the US deficit.\par \par \uc2 The GOP-requested estimate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2021-12/57673-BBBA-GrahamSmith-Letter.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  available here}}}\uc2 , provides data for programs in areas like housing, child care, and other social initiatives that Democrats say they have not committed to making permanent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/12-10-2021/cbos-gop-estimate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports Politico. }}}\uc2  Democrats have also said that any future extensions for programs will be fully offset.\par \par \uc2 Republicans are hoping that these new estimates will entice moderates like Senator \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  of West Virginia to help stop the spending package, but Democrats have pushed back, saying that estimates are in response to a bill that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been finalized, with majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  calling the scores {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/minutes/congress/12-10-2021/where-are-we/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfake.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Coming as a surprise to almost no one, Republican Senator Ted Cruz of Texas was reportedly not wearing a facial mask during the memorial service despite rising cases of Covid-19 nationwide and several older attendees present.\par \par \uc2 enltrAlmost everyone else is wearing a mask at Bob Doles funeral, but not \u8230\'20\'26.. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dcElYHhgVU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dcElYHhgVU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Molly Jong-Fast (@MollyJongFast) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MollyJongFast/status/1469336339359412228?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 For more information on rising Covid-19 cases and concerns sparked by the Omicron variant, check out \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Eric Berger piece linked below.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/us-covid-cases-surge-vaccine-progress-slows-omicron-variant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Covid cases surge as vaccine progress slows and Omicron variant sparks fears}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In other news, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just wrapped up speaking at the memorial for former US senator \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  which started at 11 am ET.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy fellow Americans, America has lost one of our greatest patriots,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJill and I will always be there for you... as you and Bob were always there for us in ways nobody knows.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSpeaking to former Sen. Bob Dole's wife and daughter during his eulogy of the longtime statesman, Pres. Biden says, "Jill and I will always be there for you... as you and Bob were always there for us in ways nobody knows." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bB2f4FFZV5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bB2f4FFZV5}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Pdl36hZzki"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Pdl36hZzki}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1469346334868221954?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 During the eulogy, Biden spoke about Dole\u8217\'20\'19s willingness to go against his own party, helping pass initiatives such as creating a federal holiday to commemorate Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and to continue funding \uc2 Amtrak\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden: "Over the opposition of many in his own party\u8212\'20\'14and some in mine\u8212\'20\'14he managed to...create a federal holiday in the name of Martin Luther King, Jr."\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  did that." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x9IGonh92g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/x9IGonh92g}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NF35SnFajF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NF35SnFajF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1469347458203406345?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden remembers when \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  angered his party by casting deciding vote to continue \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  funding.\par \par \uc2 "My guess is he was asked why? Why would you do that? He says, 'It's the best to get \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  the hell out of here at night." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x9IGonh92g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/x9IGonh92g}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ciGrdNj0pv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ciGrdNj0pv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1469349081025761285?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Biden also spoke on Dole\u8217\'20\'19s service during World War II, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s something that connects that past and present, wartime and peace, then and now: the courage, the grit, the goodness and the grace of 2nd Lt. named \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRecounting \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 's heroism during World War Two, Pres. Biden says "There's something that connects that past and present, wartime and peace, then and now: the courage, the grit, the goodness and the grace of 2nd Lt. named \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fguG7NUC8I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fguG7NUC8I}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EF1VVjCQO5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EF1VVjCQO5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1469345151546011648?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBob was taking his final journey. He\u8217\'20\'19s sitting back now, watching us. Now it\u8217\'20\'19s our job to start standing up for what\u8217\'20\'19s right for America. I salute you my friend, your nation salutes you,\u8221\'20\'1D said Biden during the eulogy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A number of pro-choice advocacy groups have reacted to the SCOTUS decision.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPFA/status/1469333458015199233"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted out a statement}}}\uc2 , saying:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has once again failed to put an end to Texas\u8217\'20\'19s bounty hunting scheme and protect our constitutional rights. They have failed to bring relief to Texas patients and providers who\u8217\'20\'19ve suffered for 100 days under this unconstitutional law. We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep fighting.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Supreme Court has once again failed to put an end to Texas\u8217\'20\'19s bounty hunting scheme and protect our constitutional rights. They have failed to bring relief to Texas patients and providers who\u8217\'20\'19ve suffered for 100 days under this unconstitutional law. We\u8217\'20\'19ll keep fighting. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7YiI3z2kQU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7YiI3z2kQU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Planned Parenthood (@PPFA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPFA/status/1469333458015199233?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 NARAL Pro-Choice also posted a number of tweets about the decision, explaining what the ruling meant and the impact that Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has had on those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%23SB8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SB8}}}\uc2  has caused untold harm\u8212\'20\'14forcing those who can afford it to travel out of state for the care they need, and those who can\u8217\'20\'19t to remain pregnant against their will. As it stands, SB 8 makes accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in Texas nearly impossible. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%23SCOTUS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  should have blocked it.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SB8?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SB8}}}\uc2  has caused untold harm\u8212\'20\'14forcing those who can afford it to travel out of state for the care they need, and those who can\u8217\'20\'19t to remain pregnant against their will. As it stands, SB 8 makes accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care in Texas nearly impossible. And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  should have blocked it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NARAL (@NARAL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NARAL/status/1469336751483195392?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  shared a statement via \uc2 Twitter\uc2  concerning the ruling:\par \par \uc2 BREAKING: The Supreme Court has once again failed to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Make no mistake: SB8 continues to wreak havoc on people\u8217\'20\'19s lives every additional day it\u8217\'20\'19s in effect. More to come on what this means from our legal experts soon.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Supreme Court has once again failed to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake: SB8 continues to wreak havoc on people's lives every additional day it's in effect.\par \par \uc2 More to come on what this means from our legal experts soon.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 ACLU\uc2  (@ACLU) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLU/status/1469342804170133507?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The National Organization for Women\uc2  called the decision a \u8220\'20\'1Cpartial win for reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D while providing an explanation of the SCOTUS ruling.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  has not overturned SB8, the Texas restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, but has allowed Texas lower courts to hear cases challenging this unconstitutional law. This is a partial win for reproductive freedom! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BansOffOurBodies?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BansOffOurBodies}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 National NOW (@NationalNOW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NationalNOW/status/1469326399974555655?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic Representative \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  of Washington, who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/sep/30/congresswomen-personal-abortion-stories-cori-bush-barbara-lee-pramila-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoken about her own experience getting an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  with other congressional democrats, has reacted to the SCOTUS decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy allowing this cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to remain in effect, SCOTUS is turning a blind eye to the direct attacks on the rights of pregnant people in Texas and across America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jayapal on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  following the decision. In the same tweet, Jayapal encouraged the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  to pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, writing, \u8220\'20\'1CEnough of the political games.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBy allowing this cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to remain in effect, SCOTUS is turning a blind eye to the direct attacks on the rights of pregnant people in Texas and across America.\par \par \uc2 Enough of the political games \u8212\'20\'14 it\u8217\'20\'19s imperative that the Senate pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act now. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GWGgeoIzz8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GWGgeoIzz8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Pramila Jayapal\uc2  (@PramilaJayapal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PramilaJayapal/status/1469334862310031365?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Previously, Jayapal has spoken about her decision to terminate a pregnancy after experiencing severe postpartum depression following a previous pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhether the choice to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is easy or hard, whether there are traumatic situations or not, none of that should be the issue. It is simply nobody\u8217\'20\'19s business what choices we as pregnant people make about our own bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jayapal back in September.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is a breakdown of the effects of the SCOTUS ruling on the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from Steven Vladeck, a legal scholar with the University of Texas School of Law.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BREAKING?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BREAKING}}}\uc2  : By 8-1 vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  holds that Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers *can* challenge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SB8?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SB8}}}\uc2  by suing *some* state licensing officials in federal court, but by a 5-4 vote, the Court does *not* allow their suit to go forward against state court clerks: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eHQZNbnKpy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/eHQZNbnKpy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1469322132249186308?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Vladeck, along with other experts, also discussed the implications of the decision.\par \par \uc2 enltrBeyond the implications for pregnant people in Texas, this is perhaps the most alarming feature of today's decision.\par \par \uc2 Instead of disincentivizing states from playing such procedural games with our constitutional rights going forward, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SCOTUS?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SCOTUS}}}\uc2  has provided a blueprint for doing so. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bBedHtCgQ1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bBedHtCgQ1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Steve Vladeck (@steve_vladeck) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/steve_vladeck/status/1469328513563967491?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a take from Joyce Alene, former United States Attorney for the Northern District of Alabama.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe only clarity in today's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling is about how fractured the Court is on this issue. SB8 remains in effect in Texas. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are severely restricted. No reason to believe it won't get worse when the Court decides Dobbs, where it will reverse or gut Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joyce Alene (@JoyceWhiteVance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoyceWhiteVance/status/1469333105441972224?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Lawrence Hurley, a Reuters reporter who covers the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  and related issues, also provided additional context for the decision as well as a breakdown of Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s partial dissent.\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Sotomayor, dissenting in part, blasts colleagues for failing to "put an end to this madness" and says other states could still copy Texas b/c court isn't allowing AG or state court judges to be sued\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1469330148193357826?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 This ruling on the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case is separate from the pivotal case about a Mississippi law that is a direct challenge to Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme court heard arguments on the Mississippi law case last week, with conservative justices, who have a supermajority in the court, signaling that they are leaning towards {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curbing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access in the future}}}\uc2  across the country. A decision on that case is not expected til the summer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren reacts to the recent SCOTUS decision that leaves the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in effect but allows providers to sue.\par \par \uc2 In a tweet posted shortly after the decision, Warren echoed sentiments of many pro-choice advocates at the SCOTUS decision that allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to remain in place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile SCOTUS has allowed challenges to SB 8 to proceed, it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous that the Court has again decided not to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19 unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1469326405032886273"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted Warren.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CMore Texans are harmed every day this law is allowed to stand. The Senate must pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhile SCOTUS has allowed challenges to SB 8 to proceed, it's outrageous that the Court has again decided not to block Texas' unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. More Texans are harmed every day this law is allowed to stand. The Senate must pass the Women's Health Protection Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@SenWarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1469326405032886273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Court won't stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban but votes to allow providers to sue over Texas law\par \par \uc2 In a blow to pro-choice advocates and those seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t stop the Texas near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from being enforced, but has voted to allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to sue over the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The Supreme Court allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to continue to pursue their challenge to Texas' near-total ban on abortions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uIydz88kz8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/uIydz88kz8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1469322091736485889?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 10, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 The law, known as Senate Bill 8, bans the procedure after roughly six weeks gestation or before most women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The outcome is, in the best case, a partial victory for pro-choice advocates and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, says the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The law has been in place since 1 September.\par \par \uc2 More details, including reactions to the ruling, coming shortly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Prices for US consumers in November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/dec/10/us-inflation-rate-rise-2021-highest-increase-since-1982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased by 6.8%}}}\uc2 , with US inflation hitting its highest level since 1982.\par \par \uc2 The Labor Department also reported that between October to November, prices jumped by 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 The rising cost of goods has put greater economic pressure on people across all incomes, especially for lower-income households. Everyday goods such as food and gas have also become more expensive, according to tracking indexes.\par \par \uc2 Rising inflation has also mitigated the impact of higher wages many workers have received, complicating the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plans to reduce its aid for the US economy and coinciding with flailing public approval rates for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Experts say that ongoing inflation in the US is due to a number of factors: increased government stimulus, continued supply shortages, and low rates manufactured by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , reports AP.\par \par \uc2 For more news on US inflation, follow \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2021/dec/10/uk-economy-slows-gdp-october-us-inflation-lv-bain-takeover-business-live?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-61b356be8f0819fcb698d818#block-61b356be8f0819fcb698d818"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will close out his virtual Summit for Democracy today with remarks about electoral integrity, fighting against foreign interference in elections, and bolstering independent media.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  delivers remarks at Summit for Democracy at the White House, Washington, District of Columbia, USA. Photograph: REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, on the first day, Biden announced a plan for the US to spend up to $424mn to support independent media around the world, anti-corruption work, and other initiatives.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what happened during the first day from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/shah-meer-baloch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shah Meer Baloch}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Facing video links with 80 world leaders arrayed on two oversize electronic panels, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2021/12/09/remarks-by-president-biden-at-the-summit-for-democracy-opening-session/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US president said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an urgent matter on all our parts, in my view, because the data we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is largely pointing in the wrong direction.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden cited studies that found that global freedom has now been in retreat for 15 consecutive years and that more than half of all democracies experienced a decline in the past decade.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that one of those countries in democratic decline was his own. Since the November 2020 elections \u8211\'20\'13 the result of which is still not accepted by many supporters of the loser, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 voting rights have been under assault from Republicans on the state level, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2021/nov/12/gerrymander-redistricting-map-republicans-democrats-visual"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gerrymandering is still rife}}}\uc2 , carried out by both Republicans, and to a lesser extent, Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Biden has been accused by American progressives of hosting a global summit while not doing enough to combat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/24/us-world-democracy-rankings-freedom-house-new-low"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  democratic backsliding at home}}}\uc2 . In New York, activists staged a \u8220\'20\'1Cfuneral for democracy\u8221\'20\'1D outside the United Nations, in protest of US voter suppression laws.\par \par \uc2 Biden also repeatedly spoke on the value of democracies as better vehicles for governance than autocracies, with the ambassadors to the US from Russia and China releasing a joint statement that condemned the Biden administration for adopting a divisive \u8220\'20\'1Ccold-war mentality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president will be finishing his remarks this afternoon and is scheduled to speak at 1:45 pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to discuss election integrity and media at close of democracy summit\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  live blog readers! Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s coming up today:\par \par \uc2 * The US president will be closing the virtual Summit for Democracy this afternoon. Bidenwill be focusing on election integrity and bolstering independent media, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/joe-biden-europe-elections-media-voting-rights-85d99ee88c6122f21e55d5727eb20e13?user_email=&utm_source=Sailthru&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=MorningWire_Dec10&utm_term=Morning%20Wire%20Subscribers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , with remarks at 1.45pm ET\par \par \uc2 * The president, the first lady, Jill Biden, the vice-president, Kamala Harris and second gentleman Doug Emhoff will be attending the memorial service for former US senator \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2  at 11 am ET. Biden will share remarks.\par \par \uc2 * A supreme court ruling will be coming out today at 10am ET. Most people are expecting a decision on the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law.\par \par \uc2 * New data out shows that inflation is impacting people across all incomes, reports Axios . The consumer price index for November {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/dec/10/us-inflation-rate-rise-2021-highest-increase-since-1982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows rising inflation}}}\uc2  despite economic data showing an increase in wages, falling gas prices, and other markers of economic recovery amid the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211210ehca002bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
