\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Sotomayor decries  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling but court\u8217\'20\'19s conservatives show their muscle\b0\par\par\uc2 Ed Pilkington in New York \par \uc2 1,060 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 December 2021\par 21:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The highest court in the US has been defied by a group of extremist Republicans openly flouting the court\u8217\'20\'19s own rulings\par \par \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , the liberal-leaning justice on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , put it plainly. For almost three months, lawmakers in the Republican-controlled legislature of Texas had \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially suspended a constitutional guarantee: a pregnant woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to control her own body\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court should have put an end to this madness months ago,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor said.\par \par \uc2 But when the supreme court issued on Friday its majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opinion}}}\uc2  on SB8, the extreme Texas law that bans abortions effectively at six weeks, in blatant violation of the court\u8217\'20\'19s own constitutional rulings, it still didn\u8217\'20\'19t put an end to the madness.\par \par \uc2 It allowed the law, the most restrictive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/01/texas-abortion-law-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently in force}}}\uc2  in the US, to remain in effect.\par \par \uc2 And by varying margins, the new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/04/us-supreme-courrt-sonia-sotomayor-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative supermajority}}}\uc2  of the court, consolidated by Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointment of three new rightwing justices, restricted the legal route by which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers could challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 From now on the legal battle would have to be focused narrowly on just four state employees responsible for medical licensing in the state. Other Texas officials involved, notably the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  and clerks in state courts, would be let off the hook.\par \par \uc2 Even more provocatively, while the court sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fight back to a federal district court in Austin, it let the ban itself stand. That adds insult to injury given the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s much-criticised refusal to stay the ban at the start, not to mention the many weeks it has taken to hand down its decision.\par \par \uc2 Over those weeks, Texas women have paid a heavy price. \u8220\'20\'1CThe court\u8217\'20\'19s delay in allowing this case to proceed has had catastrophic consequences for women seeking to exercise their constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor said in a powerful dissenting opinion.\par \par \uc2 In September alone, the first month of the ban, the number of legal abortions performed in Texas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://liberalarts.utexas.edu/txpep/research-briefs/sb8-initial-impact-brief.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plummeted}}}\uc2  to about half the level a year ago. That was the largest recorded decline in the state\u8217\'20\'19s recent history, with untold numbers of women forced to seek abortions out of state or carry unwanted pregnancies to term.\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor, who is emerging as a pivotal voice of resistance within the post-Trump court, was forthright in her choice of words. Her disagreement with the conservative justices went far beyond a \u8220\'20\'1Cquibble\u8221\'20\'1D over which state officials \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can sue, she said.\par \par \uc2 The question was: is the supreme court prepared to stand up in the name of constitutional rights to the cynical antics of ideologically driven Republicans in states such as Texas?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice to shrink from Texas\u8217\'20\'19s challenge to federal supremacy will have far-reaching repercussions,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor warned. \u8220\'20\'1CI doubt the court, let alone the country, is prepared for them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nobody can doubt that SB 8 is a flagrant violation of the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  enshrined in the 1973 landmark ruling Roe v Wade. While Roe sets the bar of fetal viability at about 24 weeks, Texas now puts it at the point of earliest cardiac activity, around six weeks \u8211\'20\'13 before many women even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , one of the three Trump appointees, who wrote Friday\u8217\'20\'19s majority opinion, said that the issue of the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not under consideration in this case. The matter at hand in the Texas law was whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers could press on with their challenge to the ban by suing specific state officials.\par \par \uc2 That will do little to assuage the jitters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 80% of Americans}}}\uc2  who think that abortions should be legal in all or certain circumstances. In a separate case before the supreme court based on a new Mississippi ban at 15 weeks, which is now blocked by a lower court, Roe v Wade is very much up for grabs, and the signs are ominous.\par \par \uc2 In oral arguments in the Mississippi case less than two weeks ago, several of the conservative justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  they were willing to sharply restrict or even overturn the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite its rock-steady standing as a pillar of constitutional law for almost 50 years.\par \par \uc2 Nor does Gorsuch\u8217\'20\'19s protestation that Friday\u8217\'20\'19s case was merely focused on procedural matters offer much comfort. SB 8 was devised by Texas Republicans as a juridical trick to skirt around constitutional protections by making it more difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to challenge the law in federal court.\par \par \uc2 At the heart of the legislation is a ruse designed to make a mockery of federal oversight. Enforcement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is transferred from state officials who are vulnerable to federal challenge to private individuals, armed with financial inducements of up to $10,000 to cover legal fees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSB 8 is structured to thwart review and result in \u8216\'20\'18a denial of any hearing\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Sotomayor decried. \u8220\'20\'1CThe events of the last three months have shown that the law has succeeded in its endeavor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That is why the vote of the court\u8217\'20\'19s new post-Trump majority to issue such a narrow opinion over SB 8 is more than a \u8220\'20\'1Cquibble\u8221\'20\'1D. The highest court in the nation has been defied by a group of extremist Republicans openly flouting the court\u8217\'20\'19s own rulings.\par \par \uc2 In response, the conservative majority emboldened by Trump has opted not to insist on respect for the constitutional law of the land, but instead to blithely play along.\par \par \uc2 As Sotomayor put it: \u8220\'20\'1CBy so doing, the court leaves all manner of constitutional rights more vulnerable than ever before, to the great detriment of our constitution and our republic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Perhaps most tellingly, the idea of appeasing Texas Republicans in their attempt to undermine the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s own precedents proved too much even for \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , the chief justice.\par \par \uc2 In important aspects of Friday\u8217\'20\'19s decision, he broke with his five fellow conservative justices and sided pointedly with Sotomayor and the liberal minority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe clear purpose and actual effect of SB 8 has been to nullify this court\u8217\'20\'19s rulings,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts said, in words which may reverberate down the years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe role of the supreme court in our constitutional system is at stake.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211210ehca003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
