\par\par \uc2 Law\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The court should have put an end to this madness\u8217\'20\'19: reproductive health advocates criticize  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 694 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 December 2021\par 19:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pro-choice advocates and Democrats say supreme court did not do enough to abolish Texas law that many say nullifies a constitutionally protected right\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/dec/10/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has ruled}}}\uc2  that Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can sue over the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban on most abortions, but the justices are allowing the law to remain in effect, much to the dismay of pro-choice advocates and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 The so-called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/sep/01/democrats-condemn-supreme-court-texas-abortion-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CHeartbeat Act\u8221\'20\'1D,}}}\uc2  which was signed into law by Greg Abbott, the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, and went into effect in September, bans abortions at six weeks and does not make exceptions for incest and rape.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, it empowers private citizens to enforce the law, rather than the authorities, giving them the right to sue any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider whom they believe has violated the law or anyone aiding the provision of the service, although not the patient receiving the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  service.\par \par \uc2 The law provides for a $10,000 penalty against defendants found to have violated the law.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive health advocates and Democrats have sharply criticized the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, arguing that the court did not do enough to abolish a law that many say nullifies a constitutionally protected right.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , alongside the court\u8217\'20\'19s other two liberal-leaning members, \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  and Elena Kagan, wrote that they disagreed with the conservative majority\u8217\'20\'19s refusal to stop the law, known as SB8, completely.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe court should have put an end to this madness months ago, before SB8 first went into effect. It failed to do so then, and it fails again today \u8230\'20\'26 I dissent \u8230\'20\'26 from the court\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous departure from its precedents \u8230\'20\'26 The court thus betrays not only the citizens of Texas, but also our constitutional system of government,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZoeTillman/status/1469331136727891974?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  wrote}}}\uc2  Sotomayor.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThe dispute is over whether states may nullify federal constitutional rights by employing schemes like the one at hand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2  of New Jersey called the ruling wrong, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CoryBooker/status/1469329842969665540?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThis half measure from the supreme court is wrong. It continues to deny Texans their constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is causing harm at this very moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts Democratic senator and former presidential candidate Elizabeth Warren said the Friday decision in the Texas case was outrageous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile SCOTUS has allowed challenges to SB8 to proceed, it\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous that the Court has again decided not to block Texas\u8217\'20\'19 unconstitutional \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenWarren/status/1469326405032886273"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted Warren.}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CMore Texans are harmed every day this law is allowed to stand. The Senate must pass the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That law would codify the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US into national legislation. The bill passed the House in September and is in limbo in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Laurence Tribe, co-founder of the American Constitution Society and constitutional law scholar at Harvard University, also condemned the ruling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLetting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics sue to challenge SB8 but leaving that outrageous six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban remain in place \u8211\'20\'13 just as it was clear this radically rightwing court would do \u8211\'20\'13 reaffirms my view that this court needs major reform and needs it now,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tribelaw/status/1469335474401681414?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  wrote}}}\uc2 , and called the court with its new conservative supermajority \u8220\'20\'1Cbroken\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Others criticized what they saw as the conservatives\u8217\'20\'19 religious motive, influenced by Republicans, AKA the GOP. Dean Obeidallah, an American lawyer and host of a SiriusXM show, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DeanObeidallah/status/1469335869194739714?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  wrote}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe GOP Supreme Court allows religious supremacy to continue by not halting the Texas GOP \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. That law is about imposing the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s extreme religious beliefs upon the rest of us. The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  should sue the GOP for trademark infringement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some praised the ruling, including \uc2 Dan Patrick\uc2 , the Republican lieutenant governor of Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas is a solidly pro-life state, and I will never stop fighting to protect innocent life from the radical abortionist left. A great victory for the unborn!\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanPatrick/status/1469346206337929228?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the \uc2 Susan B Anthony\uc2  List, a nonprofit anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  organization, welcomed the ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBAList/status/1469337661227913216?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writing,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CThis is good news because the law will remain in effect, already saving thousands of lives, and we hope more to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211210ehca00336\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
