\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans confident supreme court will overturn  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Oliver Laughland \par \uc2 617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 December 2021\par 18:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mississippi governor \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2  says state \u8216\'20\'18snap-back\u8217\'20\'19 legislation will ban almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe v Wade is thrown out entirelyOpinion: the supreme court is coming for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights\par \par \uc2 As the supreme court weighs the future of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/05/abortion-opposition-focus-white-evangelical-anger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access in America}}}\uc2 , Republicans on Sunday expressed confidence that the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade decision would soon be overturned, paving the way for a raft of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation around the country next year.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the supreme court heard arguments over a Mississippi law that bans abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/03/opinion/abortion-supreme-court.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Observers suggested}}}\uc2  that the conservative supermajority on the court appeared poised to uphold the law and potentially go further by overturning Roe, which protects a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose. A decision is not expected until June next year.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Tate Reeves\uc2 , told CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union he had \u8220\'20\'1Csome reason for optimism\u8221\'20\'1D after this week\u8217\'20\'19s arguments.\par \par \uc2 He also confirmed that if the landmark ruling was overturned entirely, Mississippi would enforce a ban on almost all abortions in the state under a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is a yes,\u8221\'20\'1D Reeves said when asked if he would enforce the \u8220\'20\'1Csnap-back\u8221\'20\'1D legislation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause if you believe as I believe very strongly that that innocent, unborn child in the mother\u8217\'20\'19s womb is in fact a child, the most important word when we talk about unborn children is not unborn, but it\u8217\'20\'19s children.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The position is not representative of the majority of Americans. According {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2019/08/29/u-s-public-continues-to-favor-legal-abortion-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade/#most-americans-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to recent polling}}}\uc2 , seven in 10 are opposed to overturning Roe v Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/06/17/key-facts-about-the-abortion-debate-in-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 while 59% believe}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a global research and policy organisation \u8220\'20\'1Ccommitted to advancing sexual and reproductive health and rights\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 21 US states are certain}}}\uc2  to attempt some form of ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should Roe be overturned, using laws already on the books.\par \par \uc2 Reeves caveated his answer by cautioning that Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s response to the forthcoming supreme court ruling would be \u8220\'20\'1Cdependent upon how the court rules and exactly what those opinions allow us to do\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also noted that any decision would not lead to a national ban but could permit states to make their own determinations.\par \par \uc2 Mike Braun\uc2 , a Republican senator for Indiana, echoed a number of Reeves\u8217\'20\'19 arguments. He told NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press he wanted \u8220\'20\'1Cabortions to be eliminated from the landscape\u8221\'20\'1D but would not be drawn into specifics regarding potential laws in his state.\par \par \uc2 Indiana has enacted 55 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions and bans in the past decade, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , but does not have a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger law\u8221\'20\'1D or equivalent on the books.\par \par \uc2 It is listed by the institute as one of five states without these laws that are still likely to move towards almost total bans should Roe be overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen it comes to things like \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think it\u8217\'20\'19s clear it\u8217\'20\'19s time to turn it back to the states,\u8221\'20\'1D Braun told NBC.\par \par \uc2 Since former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  installed three conservative justices to the supreme court in just four years, both sides of the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been preparing for a legal showdown.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, campaign finance data reveals that pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access groups donated $8m in 2018 and more than $10m in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Those numbers outpace the public contributions of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, which donated $2.6m in 2018 and $6.3m in 2020, according to data.\par \par \uc2 But the complexity of the network of nonprofits and \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money\u8221\'20\'1D funds makes it difficult to produce a full accounting of the money flows.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211205ehc500233\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
