\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Supreme court case prompts California lawmaker to share her  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  experience\b0\par\par\uc2 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton in Los Angeles \par \uc2 748 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 December 2021\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Buffy Wicks speaks out about emergency procedure amid threat to Roe v Wade: \u8216\'20\'18This story is not uncommon\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Early one morning this fall, the California state assemblywoman Buffy Wicks felt a type of pain she had never experienced before.\par \par \uc2 Wicks, 44, found herself doubled over in pain, barely able to walk or get her daughter ready for school. At her doctor\u8217\'20\'19s shortly after, she learned that she was pregnant and having a miscarriage and would need an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Twenty-four hours later she had the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Wicks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BuffyWicks/status/1466580538643288065"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared}}}\uc2  the deeply personal account of what happened that September morning on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  on Thursday, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/five-takeaways-us-supreme-court-mississippi-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oral arguments}}}\uc2  in the most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case heard by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Wicks decided to tell her story to illustrate the urgency of easily accessible reproductive care and warn of the risks this care faces if a Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law is upheld by the nation\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, she told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 How do I begin to unpack how deeply disturbed I was by yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s Supreme Court arguments?\par \par \uc2 Justice Sotomayor spoke for so many of us with this question. She spoke for me. \u176\'00\'B0\u176\'00\'B0In September, I had a miscarriage requiring an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedure \u8212\'20\'14\par \par \uc2 (tw // miscarriage) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Bn1HozwZ3H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Bn1HozwZ3H}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Buffy Wicks (@BuffyWicks) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BuffyWicks/status/1466580538643288065?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 3, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe often debate these policy matters in theory, but in reality people like me experience the outcomes when lawmakers and policymakers make these decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D Wicks said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think this is a story that is not uncommon,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have a platform that I want to use to help further the cause and say: \u8216\'20\'18This is my body and I can make my own decisions.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In her tweets, Wicks described how hard it had been to process what was going on \u8211\'20\'13 working through intense emotions while feeling intense pain. She described asking her doctor whether she would have had access to the procedure she was undergoing had she been in Texas, which this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/22/supreme-court-texas-abortion-ban-arguments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned}}}\uc2  abortions once cardiac activity is detected.\par \par \uc2 The doctor told her that even though the procedure would have been legal, given access issues, it could have been very difficult to obtain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThink about the cruelty involved in making it your aim to make life more difficult for someone in that situation: in great pain, bleeding profusely, barely able to walk, confused about what\u8217\'20\'19s happening to them, unsure about where to go, and then forcing them to endure multi-state drives or frantic rushes to the airport for the next flight to a state where getting the medically necessary healthcare they need is still *legal* & *available*,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s assuming they have the privilege & means to get those options.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Similar issues are at stake with the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case in front of the supreme court, Wicks said. On Wednesday, the court heard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 oral arguments}}}\uc2  in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, which pits the leadership of the state of Mississippi against the state\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. The state seeks to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks gestation and is asking the court to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was coming of age as a young adult, I thought Roe v Wade was the law of the land and that we had overcome oppressive draconian measures. But here we are again,\u8221\'20\'1D Wicks said.\par \par \uc2 In the hearings on Wednesday, the majority of the court appeared supportive of the Mississippi rules, with the newest supreme court justice, Amy Coney Barrett, asking whether women could simply \u8220\'20\'1Cterminate their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/amy-coney-barrett-asks-safe-haven-laws-solutions-unwanted-motherhood-2021-12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 parental rights}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D at the end of pregnancy by giving a child up for adoption, instead of seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Under the Mississippi law, Wicks would still have been able to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but similar to the situation in Texas, the impact of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/22/mississippi-clinic-fighting-future-abortion-rights-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closing clinics}}}\uc2  due to restrictions would make it hard for women to access care in their own communities, even in emergency situations like hers.\par \par \uc2 But if the Mississippi law is upheld, women across the nation may have to travel for hours to find a hospital or clinic, which can make abortions inaccessible for low-income women who are in need of care, she added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was doubled over in pain at 4am. I had never experienced that, there\u8217\'20\'19s no way I could have gotten on an airplane or driven miles to get care,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211204ehc400107\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
