\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s earth-shattering\u8217\'20\'19: Democrats and allies vow midterm fight over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Washington \par \uc2 1,073 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 December 2021\par 21:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Pro-choice groups and lawmakers will focus voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention on the threat to reproductive rights after Mississippi case\par \par \uc2 With the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seemingly poised}}}\uc2  to exploit its conservative supermajority to undermine or overturn the landmark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  decision, Democrats are vowing to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a defining issue of next year\u8217\'20\'19s midterm elections, embracing what they view as a political silver lining in an otherwise nightmare scenario.\par \par \uc2 As the justices weigh whether to uphold a Mississippi law banning most abortions after 15 weeks, far earlier than Roe allows, and a request by the state that they explicitly overturn the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic 1973 ruling}}}\uc2 , Democrats and their allies have promised a fight.\par \par \uc2 Across the electoral battlefield, they are kindling what they hope will be a political reckoning over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s earth-shattering,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jenny Lawson, vice-president of organizing and engagement campaigns for \uc2 Planned Parenthood Action Fund\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe court\u8217\'20\'19s actions are going to change the way people think about reproductive freedom and how essential it is. It will be a driving force of the election, undoubtedly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During oral arguments on Wednesday, the six conservative justices on the nine-member bench signaled they were comfortable with Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, despite the precedent established by Roe in 1973, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 affirmed}}}\uc2  in 1992, that women have a right to end their pregnancy until the point of fetal viability, at about 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 That law has been blocked by lower courts and the state appealed. The case, Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, pits Mississippi against the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in the state.\par \par \uc2 Several justices appeared willing to overturn Roe entirely, in what would be a momentous decision allowing states to govern the procedure, though the signals were less clear on that pivotal point.\par \par \uc2 A decision is expected in June or July, arriving in the heat of the 2022 political campaign season.\par \par \uc2 While the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traditionally been a more powerful motivator for Republican and evangelical voters, Democrats say there are signs the political debate is shifting in their favor as the latest and fundamental threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights comes into clearer focus.\par \par \uc2 Already facing daunting odds next year, given \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sinking poll numbers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/11/us-redistricting-voting-maps-gerrymandering"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican gerrymandering}}}\uc2 , and a poor showing in last month\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/02/glenn-youngkin-wins-virginia-governor-election-result"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 off-year elections}}}\uc2 , Democrats were searching for a new approach to reset the political dynamics.\par \par \uc2 They are hopeful that an intense focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not only rally their base but win back suburban swing voters who have shifted toward the Republican party since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exit from the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElected officials should be unapologetic about championing and protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access,\u8221\'20\'1D Lawson said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing to spin. The threat is so real and there\u8217\'20\'19s no state in the nation where banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is popular.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the oral arguments, Democrats and party officials signaled they were prepared to use \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a cudgel against Republicans in battleground states like Nevada, Florida, Arizona and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Democratic Senatorial Campaign Committee, the campaign arm of Senate Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dscc.org/news/dscc-statement-on-the-scotus-mississippi-abortion-ban-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cdefining issue\u8221\'20\'1D of next year\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are hanging in the balance at the supreme court, and the threat to Roe is very real,\u8221\'20\'1D Senator \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  of Washington, the No 3 Senate Democrat, said in a floor speech on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhy? Because for decades, extreme Republicans have attacked \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights from every angle and they are continuing their non-stop efforts to build a country where patients are forced to remain pregnant and carry their pregnancies to term against their will.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans see political advantages as well, after a decades-long conservative campaign to push the federal judiciary to the right, with the ultimate goal of overruling Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is our day,\u8221\'20\'1D congressman Steve Scalise of Louisiana, the No 2 House Republican, told supporters outside the supreme court on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what we\u8217\'20\'19ve been working for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 court overrules Roe}}}\uc2 , 21 states have currently unenforceable laws on the books that would ban or severely restricts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access almost immediately.\par \par \uc2 Already, Republican-controlled legislatures are pushing new restrictions and copycat legislation of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Texas law}}}\uc2  that effectively prohibits abortions after six weeks and makes no exceptions for rape or incest. The supreme court allowed the ban to go into effect while the justices consider challenges to the law.\par \par \uc2 Molly Murphy , a pollster with the Democratic consulting firm ALG Research who recently surveyed battleground state voters on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it could be a potent issue for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 But to be successful, she said Democrats must \u8220\'20\'1Cconnect the dots\u8221\'20\'1D for voters who support Roe but don\u8217\'20\'19t yet perceive the threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as likely or imminent.\par \par \uc2 She encouraged them to highlight \u8220\'20\'1Cpunitive measures,\u8221\'20\'1D like the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, as a way to brand Republicans as extreme on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAwareness of the Texas law is very, very high,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut for a lot of these voters, they don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily believe that it\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen where they live. They don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily know the Republicans are trying to do this across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emphasizing Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to curtail abortions would also serve to undermine their economic message, Murphy said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not going to fix the economy or bring down costs. They\u8217\'20\'19re going to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, boiling down the argument for Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what they want to do and that\u8217\'20\'19s what their priorities are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic strategists believe Republicans face a \u8220\'20\'1Cdog who caught the car\u8221\'20\'1D conundrum over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For decades, Republicans have energized their conservatives with promises to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But now the political landscape has shifted and Democrats say Republicans will have to defend their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views in a way they didn\u8217\'20\'19t when the threat was theoretical.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans are between a rock and a hard place here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chris Hayden, a spokesperson for the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee.\par \par \uc2 John Fetterman, the Pennsylvania lieutenant governor and a Democratic candidate for the state\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat, called on Senate Democrats to abolish the filibuster and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/24/house-democrats-abortion-federal-right-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pass federal legislation }}}\uc2  codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you won\u8217\'20\'19t do what it takes to pass this bill now, when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are on the line, then you\u8217\'20\'19re not pro-choice,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s that simple.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211203ehc3002s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
