\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Capitol attack committee recommends contempt prosecution for Jeffrey Clark \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh (now) and Vivian Ho and Joanna Walters (earlier) \par \uc2 8,552 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2021\par 00:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Former Trump official refused to comply with panel subpoena\u8216\'20\'18Constitution \u8230\'20\'26 leaves the issue to the people to resolve,\u8217\'20\'19 says justiceBiden reiterates support for the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in USFirst US case of Omicron Covid variant identified in CaliforniaA timeline of US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights since Roe v WadeSign up to receive First Thing \u8211\'20\'13 our daily briefing by email\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Today's politics recap\par \par \uc2 * The Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case, that could overturn the landmark ruling in Roe v Wade, has officially been submitted to the supreme court following a morning of oral arguments. However, a final ruling is not expected until June 2022. Conservative supreme court justices signaled they support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  in their questioning.\par \par \uc2 * The first case of the Omicron variant has been identified in the US, \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  confirmed. \u8220\'20\'1CWe knew it was just a matter of time,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said. The case was identified in California.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  announced she will be running for governor of Georgia once again. \u8220\'20\'1CIf our Georgia is going to move to its next and greatest chapter, we are going to need leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said in her announcement video.\par \par \uc2 * There appears to be little movement on Republicans and Democrats coming together on an agreement on a continuing resolution to fund the federal government and avoid a government shutdown by the 3 December deadline. In particular, a handful of Republicans in both the Senate and the House have been adamant that they will not vote to fund a government with a vaccine mandate\par \par \uc2 * The House select committee investigating the Capitol attack recommended the criminal prosecution of former Trump justice department official Jeffrey Clark for his refusal to comply with a subpoena in the inquiry into the 6 January insurrection. Clark\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have told the committee that he is ready to appear for a deposition on Saturday. But he is expected to refuse to answer questions and assert his Fifth Amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 Vivian Ho, Hugo Lowell, Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 The committee unanimously voted to recommend Clark be held in criminal contempt of Congress. Next, the House will vote on whether to send the criminal referral to the DoJ.\par \par \uc2 However, Clark will be given an opportunity to appear in front of the committee on Saturday for a new deposition and could be spared the charge.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeffrey Clark\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have told the committee that Clark is ready to appear for a deposition on Saturday. But he is expected to refuse to answer questions and assert his Fifth Amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not finalize this contempt process if Mr. Clark genuinely cures his failure to comply with this subpoena this Saturday,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 If Clark feels \u8220\'20\'1Cthat answering questions about his discussions with President Trump and others in November and December 2020 and January 2021 could incriminate him, and he, therefore, wishes to invoke privilege on that basis, the committee would certainly consider that\u8221\'20\'1D, she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Right now, the House select committee investigating the Capitol attack is meeting to take up a criminal contempt referral for former Trump justice department official Jeffrey Clark, determining whether to punish his refusal to comply with a subpoena in the inquiry into the 6 January insurrection.\par \par \uc2 If the committee approves the criminal contempt resolution, it will head to the full House of Representatives, which could refer Clark for prosecution in a vote that could come as soon as next week.\par \par \uc2 Bennie Thompson\uc2 , the chairman of the select committee, indicated that panel was seeking criminal prosecution to demonstrate their resolve in enforcing subpoenas, and to warn other Trump aides about the penalties for non-compliance.\par \par \uc2 The select committee\u8217\'20\'19s recommendation would bring grave consequences for Clark.\par \par \uc2 Once passed by the House, the justice department is required to take the matter before a federal grand jury, which last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/12/steve-bannon-indicted-capitol-attack-subpoena"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted the former Trump adviser Steve Bannon}}}\uc2  over his subpoena defiance.\par \par \uc2 A successful contempt prosecution could result in up to a year in federal prison, $100,000 in fines, or both \u8211\'20\'13 although the misdemeanor offence may not ultimately lead to his cooperation, and pursuing the charge could still take years.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Why the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case is so important\par \par \uc2 Today, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  heard oral arguments in what has been called the most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case in almost half a century \u8211\'20\'13 a case that could redefine reproductive rights across the country and have repercussions abroad for generations.\par \par \uc2 Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization could lead to weakening or overturning the landmark 1973 supreme court ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which effectively legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US. If that were to happen, tens of millions people of reproductive age across the country would be affected.\par \par \uc2 What is happening at the supreme court?\par \par \uc2 In Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Dobbs refers to \uc2 Dr Thomas Dobbs\uc2 , Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s health department director, and the official who would enforce the law. Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization is the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi, which is also known as the Pink House.\par \par \uc2 The highest court in the US will hear from attorneys in the case, which centers on whether Mississippi can outlaw nearly all abortions at and after 15 weeks gestation.\par \par \uc2 The case directly challenges the precedent in Roe v Wade, which guarantees the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade protects the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the point a fetus can survive outside the womb, widely regarded as 24 weeks gestation. A full term pregnancy is 39 weeks gestation.\par \par \uc2 The court is now dominated by conservatives, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/11/us-supreme-court-john-roberts-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six of the nine}}}\uc2  justices leaning to the right. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  advocates}}}\uc2  see the Mississippi case as especially perilous for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights because justices could have dismissed Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s law as unconstitutional under Roe. However, the court chose to take the case, indicating at least four justices see a reason to revisit the historic ruling. A decision is expected in June 2022, but the hearing on 1 December could provide clues as to the justices\u8217\'20\'19 thinking.\par \par \uc2 What could happen to Roe v Wade?\par \par \uc2 Congress never enshrined the right to terminate a pregnancy in law. Instead, pregnant people in the US have relied on Roe v Wade for almost 50 years, and the precedent is now considered to be under threat.\par \par \uc2 The justices could decide to dismiss the Mississippi case, upholding Roe v Wade. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates worry that the court could instead rule in a way that may weaken or even overturn it.\par \par \uc2 The justices could decide that the 15-week law does not put a significant burden on people in Mississippi, and issue a ruling that would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be banned at a much earlier stage of pregnancy. This is would considerably restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and weaken Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 If Roe is overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  are expected to move to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in various ways, through state constitutional amendments, \u8220\'20\'1Ctrigger\u8221\'20\'1D laws which go into effect as soon as possible should Roe be overturned, or limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  beginning at six weeks gestation, before most know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why the Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights case is so important}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  in Washington and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth}}}\uc2  in Moscow report:\par \par \uc2 The US says it has evidence Russia has made plans for a \u8220\'20\'1Clarge scale\u8221\'20\'1D attack on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  and that Nato allies are \u8220\'20\'1Cprepared to impose severe costs\u8221\'20\'1D on Moscow if it attempts an invasion.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Nato ministers meeting in Latvia, the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , said it was unclear whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vladimir-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin}}}\uc2  had made a decision to invade but added: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s putting in place the capacity to do so in short order, should he so decide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo despite uncertainty about intention and timing, we must prepare for all contingencies while working to see to it that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  reverses course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said he had found solidarity among his fellow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato}}}\uc2  ministers in the Latvian capital, Riga, saying the alliance was \u8220\'20\'1Cprepared to impose severe costs for further Russian aggression in Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D and would \u8220\'20\'1Creinforce its defences on the eastern flank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While repeating the US position that Washington is \u8220\'20\'1Cunwavering in our support for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s sovereignty and territorial integrity, and committed to our security partnership with Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D, the secretary of state stopped well short of saying the US or the alliance would intervene militarily. \u8220\'20\'1CShould Russia follow the path of confrontation, when it comes to Ukraine, we\u8217\'20\'19ve made clear that we will respond resolutely, including with a range of high impact economic measures that we have refrained from pursuing in the past,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 He did not specify the nature of those measures, but most observers believe that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/truss-urges-nato-allies-to-block-russias-nord-stream-2-gas-pipeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nord Stream 2 pipeline project}}}\uc2 , intended to bring Russian gas to Europe, could be cancelled if there is another invasion. The new German coalition government is already sceptical about the scheme.\par \par \uc2 Blinken said the US would spell out the consequences to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cat the appropriate time\u8221\'20\'1D. His remarks represent the strongest warning from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/biden-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden administration}}}\uc2  so far, and were delivered a day before Blinken is due to meet his Russian counterpart, Sergei Lavrov, in Stockholm under increasingly tense circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/us-warns-russia-plans-large-scale-attack-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US warns Russia has plans for \u8216\'20\'18large scale\u8217\'20\'19 attack on Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Deluge of plastic waste\u8217\'20\'19: US is world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest plastic polluter\par \par \uc2 The US is the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest culprit in generating plastic waste and the country urgently needs a new strategy to curb the vast amount of plastic that ends up in the oceans, a new report submitted to the federal government has found.\par \par \uc2 The advent of cheap, versatile plastics has created \u8220\'20\'1Ca global scale deluge of plastic waste seemingly everywhere we look\u8221\'20\'1D, the report states, with the US a leading contributor of disposable plastics that ends up entangling and choking marine life, harming ecosystems and bringing harmful pollution up through the food chain.\par \par \uc2 Plastic waste has increased sharply in the US since 1960, with the country now generating about 42m metric tons of plastic waste a year, amounting to about 130kg of waste for every person in America. This total is more than all \uc2 European Union\uc2  member countries combined. The overall amount of municipal waste created in the US is also two to eight times greater than comparable countries around the world, the report found.\par \par \uc2 Recycling infrastructure has failed to keep pace with the huge growth in American plastic production. Littering, dumping and inefficient waste disposal in landfills has caused up to 2.2m tons of plastic \u8211\'20\'13 including everything from plastic bottles and straws to packaging \u8211\'20\'13 to \u8220\'20\'1Cleak\u8221\'20\'1D into the environment each year. The total waste may be even greater than this due to data gaps in tracking it.\par \par \uc2 Much of this plastic ends up, via rivers and streams, in the world\u8217\'20\'19s oceans.\par \par \uc2 Worldwide, at least 8.8m tons of plastic waste enters the marine environment each year, the equivalent of dumping a garbage truck filled with plastic into the ocean every single minute. If current trends continue, scientists have estimated this total could leap to 53m tons annually by 2030, which is roughly half of the weight of all fish caught from the oceans globally each year.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/dec/01/deluge-of-plastic-waste-us-is-worlds-biggest-plastic-polluter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Deluge of plastic waste\u8217\'20\'19: US is world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest plastic polluter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 * The Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization case, that could overturn the landmark ruling in Roe v Wade, has officially been submitted to the supreme court following a morning of oral arguments.\par \par \uc2 * Conservative supreme court justices signaled they support {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restricting \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  in their questioning.\par \par \uc2 * The first case of the Omicron variant has been identified in the US, \uc2 Dr Anthony Fauci\uc2  confirmed.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  announced she will be running for governor of Georgia once again.\par \par \uc2 * There appears to be little movement on Republicans and Democrats coming together on an agreement on a continuing resolution to fund the federal government and avoid a government shutdown by the 3 December deadline. In particular, a handful of Republicans in both the Senate and the House have been adamant that they will not vote to fund a government with a vaccine mandate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While House Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t doing much when it comes to admonishing far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  for her Islamophobic comments about congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , House progressives will be pushing Democrat leaders for action:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse progressives plan to ratchet up calls to strip \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  from her committee spots bc of her comments on \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 and will soon go public with a letter to that effect, per two sources\par \par \uc2 Dem leaders have not made a decision yet on how to proceed.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466159352730071045?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republicans went full high school drama {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2021/nov/30/us-congress-government-shutdown-washington-us-politics-live?page=with:block-61a63ed48f08cf1826dd7de7#block-61a63ed48f08cf1826dd7de7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 yesterday on Twitter}}}\uc2 , with Majorie Taylor Greene calling Nancy Mace \u8220\'20\'1Ctrash\u8221\'20\'1D and Mace calling Greene \u8220\'20\'1Cbatshit crazy\u8221\'20\'1D via emojis.\par \par \uc2 This comes because far-right congresswoman \uc2 Lauren Boebert\uc2  made Islamophobic remarks about Democrat congresswoman \uc2 Ilhan Omar\uc2 , who has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/ilhan-omar-airs-death-threat-and-presses-republicans-on-anti-muslim-hatred"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received death threats}}}\uc2  related to these remarks. Republican congressman \uc2 Adam Kinzinger\uc2  called Boebert \u8220\'20\'1Ctrash\u8221\'20\'1D, and called out House minority leader Kevin McCarthy for his silence on her remarks.\par \par \uc2 It appears McCarthy has finally weighed in - but not directly about the bigoted bullying. Instead, he\u8217\'20\'19s just telling everyone in his party to behave.\par \par \uc2 enltrGOP Rep. Don Bacon paraphrases McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s message on GOP infighting this AM: \u8220\'20\'1CStop it. Quit acting like you\u8217\'20\'19re in high school.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If McCarthy\u8217\'20\'19s private talks w/ MTG don\u8217\'20\'19t work, \u8220\'20\'1Cat some point, the conference as a whole is gonna be frustrated, speak up\u8230\'20\'26 I know that\u8217\'20\'19s bubbling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1466136276445376519?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not here to be a burden, but at some point you have to defend yourself too\u8221\'20\'1D - Bacon on attacks from MTG & co.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not here to get the most clicks, to be TV celebrities. We\u8217\'20\'19re here to govern, and you don\u8217\'20\'19t do that by calling each other names, tearing each other apart.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Solender (@AndrewSolender) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewSolender/status/1466137832796397571?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  announces that she is running for governor of Georgia\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , who many have credited for being among those who helped turn Georgia blue in 2020, has announced that she will be running for governor once again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf our Georgia is going to move to its next and greatest chapter, we are going to need leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D Abrams said in her announcement video. \u8220\'20\'1CLeadership that knows how to do the job. Leadership that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take credit without also taking responsibility. Leadership that works hard. Leadership that measures progress not by stats but by our ability for everyone to move up and thrive. Leadership that understands the true pain folks are feeling and has real plans. That\u8217\'20\'19s the job of governor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m running for Governor because opportunity in our state shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be determined by zip code, background or access to power. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}\par \par \uc2 Be a founding donor to my campaign: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gk2lmBINfW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/gk2lmBINfW}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/z14wUlo8ls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/z14wUlo8ls}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  (@staceyabrams) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/staceyabrams/status/1466140248887418885?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More on government funding, the continuing resolution and a possible government shutdown: House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2 , who told reporters yesterday that he planned to pass a CR in the House today, now doesn\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s possible.\par \par \uc2 enltrFrom colleague Jason Donner. Hoyer when asked if they could pass the CR to avoid a gov't shutdown today: "I don't think so."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1466138709577945093?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrHoyer on an interim spending bill to avert a shutdown. Says "Schumer and McConnell are negotiating." He adds "It's incomprehensible today that we can't pass a simple CR."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chad Pergram (@ChadPergram) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChadPergram/status/1466138826280157192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Whew, a lot happening today. Let\u8217\'20\'19s hop back to Congress, where a handful of Republican s are threatening a government shutdown over the vaccine mandate for the private sector.\par \par \uc2 To recap: In September, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced a federal mandate that all companies in the US with 100 employees or more must ensure either that their workers are fully vaccinated against Covid-19 or that they test negative for the coronavirus at least once a week. The deadline for this is 4 January.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives across the country have taken issue with this, ranging the gamut of being fully anti-vax to arguing that vaccinations are a deeply personal issue, one in which the government should not be involved. There have been several challenges in courts that have sided against the mandate - the White House has since been urging private companies to act on their own to set their own vaccine mandates, as many have already.\par \par \uc2 On top of all this, the federal government runs out of funding on 3 December - yep, two days from now. Congress must pass a stopgap funding bill, also known as a continuing resolution (CR), to prevent a government shutdown that would put hundreds of thousands out of work right before the holidays.\par \par \uc2 Since early November, some Republican senators have made it clear that they will not vote for any short-term funding of a federal government with a vaccine mandate. Other conservative members of Congress have since joined in.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick update on the situation:\par \par \uc2 enltrHere's what Sen. Roger Marshall (one of a handful of conservatives who are threatening a brief government shutdown) want before agreeing to a quick vote on the continuing resolution. He told us he wants language in CR that would prohibit OSHA from enforcing vaccine mandate. BUT\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466135065512001551?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMarshall would be OK with a quick final passage vote if there's an amendment to that effect with a 51-vote threshold. But Ds are likely to insist on a 60-vote threshold. So would he object to a quick vote to pass the funding bill if the amendment were set at a 60-vote threshold?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466135066879442951?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"We'll see," he said. "There's a long time between now and Friday. But at a minimum, I think at a minimum it deserves a 50-person vote."\par \par \uc2 At GOP lunch, a number of senators told Marshall and Lee that their goal won't be achieved if there's brief shutdown. So I asked him about that\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466135068284493832?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAnd he said: "Yeah, I think the folks back home want to know how hard we're fighting for them, that the jobs back home are as important as keeping the federal government open. That's the hypocrisy up here. It just seems like we have rules for back home that don't apply here."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466135069517561860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s David Smith was out front of the supreme court during the oral arguments in the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  supporters waved models of fetuses and held prayer circles, while pro-choice advocates waved signs reading, \u8220\'20\'1C a bortion is healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/abortion-political-divisions-play-out-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America\u8217\'20\'19s deep political divisions play out on courthouse steps as justices hear \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  smiled wryly earlier when asked by reporters whether he thought the former president, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , put him at risk when Trump had received a positive coronavirus test just three days before the first presidential debate in the 2020 election campaign, according to a new book by former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/trump-tested-positive-covid-before-biden-debate-chief-staff-mark-meadows-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported exclusively}}}\uc2  by Guardian US this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think about the former president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. That was his only word on the topic.\par \par \uc2 Top health official \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  said a little later, at the White House briefing, that he had not been aware of that positive test for Trump at that time. Trump subsequently tested negative, according to the Meadows book, but shortly after revealed publicly that he had coronavirus, following which he was admitted to hospital.\par \par \uc2 Speaking generally, Fauci said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you test positive, you should quarantine yourself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/trump-tested-positive-covid-before-biden-debate-chief-staff-mark-meadows-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not done that}}}\uc2  and had not only stood a few feet from Biden, in person and unmasked, for that first debate, but he continued to travel and hold events in close proximity to people.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/trump-tested-positive-covid-before-biden-debate-chief-staff-mark-meadows-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump tested positive for Covid few days before Biden debate, chief of staff says in new book}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  is continuing to answer media questions at the White House. The top US public health official and chief medical adviser to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , said that the molecular profile of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/28/us-covid-omicron-variant-fifth-wave-fauci"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Omicron variant}}}\uc2  suggests it might be more transmissible than previous strains - and might have a higher risk of evading vaccine protection.\par \par \uc2 He emphasized, however, that it is still too early to say what will happen in the pandemic with the emergence of the Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 Fauci urged those who have consistently adopted protection protocols, such as wearing a face mask in indoor settings with crowds, to continue to do so and said those who have stopped such practices should resume.\par \par \uc2 Fauci said: \u8220\'20\'1CDo the things we have been saying every single day, not just for ourselves but internationally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said, however, that long term he believes there is \u8220\'20\'1Can end game\u8221\'20\'1D to the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no doubt that this will end, I promise you that, this will end,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Fauci has now finished his section of the briefing and left the media room at the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , the director of the national institute of allergies and infectious diseases and chief medical adviser to the US president, has taken the podium in the White House press briefing room.\par \par \uc2 He has confirmed what we all just found out - the first case of the omicron strain of coronavirus has been identified in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe knew it was just a matter of time,\u8221\'20\'1D Fauci said.\par \par \uc2 The case was confirmed moments ago by the Centers of Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), the federal health agency, and was identified in California.\par \par \uc2 Fauci just said that the case was confirmed by the CDC and the California and the San Francisco health authorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the first case of Covid-19 caused by the omicron variant detected in the US,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fauci.\par \par \uc2 He said the case involved an individual who returned to the US from South Africa on 22 November and tested positive for coronavirus on 29 November.\par \par \uc2 Fauci added that the individual was fully vaccinated but to his knowledge had not received a booster shot. He said the patient has experienced mild symptoms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel good that this patient had only mild symptoms and seems to be improving,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He said the patient was isolating and those whom they had come into close contact with had been reached and tested and shown to be negative for coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Fauci reiterated that as many people as possible should get vaccinated and, if they have been vaccinated, get boosted if eligible.\par \par \uc2 He told people not to wait to see if there will be a new vaccination designed to deal specifically with variants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now I would not be waiting. If you are eligible... get boosted now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is not yet known for certain if the current vaccines combat omicron, Fauci said. Many experts are optimistic that they provide protection but confirmation of protection or the level of protection are awaited.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First confirmed case of Omicron Covid variant in US\par \par \uc2 The federal authorities have identified the first confirmed case of the Omicron coronavirus variant in the United States.\par \par \uc2 We are awaiting a live briefing from the White House from \uc2 Anthony Fauci\uc2 , chief medical adviser to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the top infectious diseases public health official in the US, and press sec \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you that.\par \par \uc2 But meanwhile, this news is breaking across various wires services and TV news that the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  have the first confirmed US case of Omicron, identified in California.\par \par \uc2 The dominant variant in the US at this point is still the Delta strain, which emerged and spread across the country from the summer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden reiterates support for the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in US\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  gave a simple endorsement of reproductive rights in America moments ago as he remarked after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high-stakes hearing}}}\uc2  at the Supreme Court in Washington, DC, earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Washington, DC, today. Photograph: Evan Vucci/AP\par \par \uc2 Asked about the case by reporters, as the US president took a handful of questions after delivering remarks about the economy, Biden said he had not listened to today\u8217\'20\'19s oral arguments in the key case, which were live streamed from the in-person hearing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did not see any of the presentation today,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 But he then added: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I support Roe v Wade. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s the rational position to take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He didn\u8217\'20\'19t add further details. Biden is the second US president who is a Catholic, following the milestone passed by the first, John F Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 Conservative Catholic leaders {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/jun/19/biden-threatened-with-communion-ban-over-position-on-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had pushed}}}\uc2  in vain to ban Biden from being allowed to take communion because of his pro-choice political position, a move opposed by the Pope, whom Biden and his wife Jill Biden met with on his way to the G7 talks and Cop26 climate conference a few weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Roe v Wade is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark supreme court decision}}}\uc2  from 1973 that established the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US, up to around 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 That precedent is now under direct threat from a case brought by Mississippi, which asks the court point blank to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Read a timeline of the law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8216\'20\'18fundamental\u8217\'20\'19 right: a timeline of US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights since Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 * Oral arguments before the s upreme court began today in the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization that is a direct challenge to the landmark ruling in Roe v Wade, which legalized abortions across the US in 1973.\par \par \uc2 * Conservative justices signalled their support for overturning the Roe ruling, while justices like \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  called the law out of Mississippi being argued before them a purely political play.\par \par \uc2 * Meanwhile, in Congress, Republicans are threatening to not vote for a stopgap funding bill that would fund the federal government and prevent a government shutdown ahead of the 3 December deadline because of the federal vaccine mandate for private sectors.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  arrested 33 people near the supreme court, where widespread anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pro-choice demonstrations were taking place during the oral arguments of Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization.\par \par \uc2 enltrUS Capitol Police gave three warnings, now they are beginning to arrest the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights protesters blocking Constitution Avenue. A protester I talked to said she was willing to be arrested. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qQWB75qg1B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qQWB75qg1B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Roussey (@tomroussey7news) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tomroussey7news/status/1466096082031714324?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have given the demonstrators three warnings and are now arresting them for violating DC Code \u167\'00\'A7 22\u8211\'20\'131307- Crowding, Obstructing or Incommoding in an area where protesting is prohibited.\par \par \uc2 This does not affect the lawful demonstrators who are in front of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1466096502783234053?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe arrested a total of 33 people for Crowding, Obstructing or Incommoding (DC Code \u167\'00\'A7 22\u8211\'20\'131307). They were blocking traffic on Constitution Avenue.\par \par \uc2 This does not affect the lawful demonstrators who are in front of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We will update this if anything changes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R9qWxFPe9x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R9qWxFPe9x}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1466103419773628420?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Quick update from Congress, and the stopgap funding bill that House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  hoped would be introduced in the house today:\par \par \uc2 Reminder that the deadline is 3 December - yep, this Friday:\par \par \uc2 enltrStill no agreement on bill to fund the government, but Senate Appropriations Chairman \uc2 Patrick Leahy\uc2  just told reporters that they are still talking about extending funding into late January/early February. Money dries up after 11:59p Friday\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1466094076131000322?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With the oral arguments in the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization concluded, reaction seems dejectedly certain that the supreme court will rule to overturn Roe v Wade, therefore putting into question safe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access across the country.\par \par \uc2 enltrSupreme Court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  arguments have concluded. It seems conservative justices have the votes to uphold Mississippi's 15-week ban but the question is how far will they go in either gutting or completely overturning Roe v. Wade\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lawrence Hurley (@lawrencehurley) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lawrencehurley/status/1466089273036316672?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThe case is submitted. The Supreme Court will overturn Roe v. Wade in June 2022. Half the states will have complete or near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  within six months.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Joseph Stern (@mjs_DC)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mjs_DC/status/1466088658092670976?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWhy is 15 weeks not enough time?\u8221\'20\'1D asks a man who has never had a period arrive late, never been an underage victim of rape, never been in impoverished circumstances without access to basic services, never been hundreds of miles from the nearest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alice Driver (@reporterdriver) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/reporterdriver/status/1466075612280414231?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrBy the end of this Supreme Court term, it will likely be far easier for a teenage boy to acquire a firearm in Michigan than for an adult woman to procure an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dana Nessel (@dananessel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dananessel/status/1466043023792517132?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Thomas doesn't have a thing to say for decades but this morning he can't stop talking about the justification of banning abortions. Curious.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Lockhart (@joelockhart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joelockhart/status/1466083542144794627?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After a quick rebuttal from Scott Stewart, the solicitor general of Mississippi, the supreme court has adjourned for the day. The case is officially submitted.\par \par \uc2 This was a lot, but a ruling is not expected in the Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization - which could possibly overturn the landmark ruling in the Roe v Wade case that legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide - until June 2022.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Conservative supreme court justice Amy Coney Barrett keeps going on about safe haven law s and how all 50 states have safe haven laws which would an unwilling parent to safely give up their child, no questions asked.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis question from Amy Coney Barrett is basically game over for Roe. She says: Now that all 50 states have "safe haven" laws that let women relinquish parental rights after birth, the burdens of parenthood discussed in Roe and Casey are irrelevant, and the decisions are obsolete. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/omyhGISVmN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/omyhGISVmN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mark Joseph Stern (@mjs_DC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mjs_DC/status/1466076071514812418?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAmy Coney Barrett is turning to safe haven laws, which allow parents to surrender parental rights. She\u8217\'20\'19s talking about \u8220\'20\'1Cforced parenting\u8221\'20\'1D being something one can opt out of without reckoning with the violations of forced pregnancy or forced birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Irin Carmon (@irin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/irin/status/1466073972089438210?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US solicitor general \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2  is now before the supreme court :\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Solicitor General \uc2 Elizabeth Prelogar\uc2 : "The Court has never revoked a right that is so fundamental to so many Americans and so central to their ability to participate fully and equally in society. The Court should not overrule the central component of women's liberty." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x0ZB8XDj4k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/x0ZB8XDj4k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CSPAN (@cspan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1466083466555150348?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh signals support for curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 Questioning from conservative supreme court justice Brett Kavanuagh is signalling that he might be open to curbing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Constitution is neither pro-life nor pro-choice... and leaves the issue to the people to resolve in the democratic process,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He asked if the court should be neutral on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, which would require overturning Roe v Wade. He argued that if Mississippi wins, overturning Roe wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide, but would just let states regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  themselves as they want (though at least 26 states are poised to outright ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe fails).\par \par \uc2 enltr24. Kavanaugh now returns to his extremely worrisome line of questioning. Isn\u8217\'20\'19t it better for supreme Ct not to pick sides and leave it up to states and people.\par \par \uc2 Challenger makes great point that roe and Casey decided exactly that issue. And that constitution guarantees liberty\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1466079535208800261?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr25\u8230\'20\'26. And so a decision to overrule roe and Casey isn\u8217\'20\'19t neutral.\par \par \uc2 Kavanaugh now has list of major cases where scotus overruled past decisions. What\u8217\'20\'19s difft about this, he asks? This is a very very bad sign for those who hoped Mississippi law might get struck down. He has said\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1466080192301084681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr26. \u8230\'20\'26nothing so far sympathetic to the challengers. And a lot that has been very hostile.\par \par \uc2 Again, must take w a grain of salt as scotus questions often are just trying to understand a lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s position. But the tea leaves here are ominous.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Neal Katyal\uc2  (@neal_katyal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neal_katyal/status/1466080193911611402?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 During his heated confirmation hearings in 2018, Kavanaugh said he considered Roe v Wade to be settled law. This appears to be quite a turnaround.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  asked attorney \uc2 Julie Rikelman\uc2  about the constitutional right that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThomas asks Rikelman to identify the constitutional right that protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Is it privacy? Autonomy? What would it be?"\par \par \uc2 "It\u8217\'20\'19s liberty," she says. "It\u8217\'20\'19s the textual protection in the 14th Amendment that the state can\u8217\'20\'19t deny someone liberty without the due process of law."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466079654423543816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRikelman, in response to questions from Alito: \u8220\'20\'1CAllowing a state to take control of a woman\u8217\'20\'19s body" and force her to bear the burdens of pregnancy "is a fundamental violation of her liberty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466080608225046541?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 ABC and Washington Post conducted a poll and found that the majority of Americans support maintaining Roe v Wade and oppose state legislation making it harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to operate.\par \par \uc2 enltrPer this {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ABC}}}\uc2  News/WaPo poll, majorities of Americans:\par \par \uc2 - Support maintaining Roe v. Wade\par \par \uc2 - Oppose states making it harder for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to operate\par \par \uc2 - See \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  primarily as a decision to be made by a woman and her doctor, not lawmakers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NkCRPVtEG1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NkCRPVtEG1}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jPiUrF5qdI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jPiUrF5qdI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Politics (@ABCPolitics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCPolitics/status/1466051036649603074?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 According to the poll, 60% wanted the supreme court to uphold Roe v Wade, 58% opposed state legislation that made it harder for clinics to operate and 75% believe that the decision of whether a woman can have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the woman and her doctor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Julie Rikelman\uc2 , representing Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization - the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Mississippi - is now before the supreme court.\par \par \uc2 enltrRikelman begins by saying that stare decisis presents \u8220\'20\'1Can especially high bar here\u8221\'20\'1D because Casey rejected \u8220\'20\'1Cevery possible reason\u8221\'20\'1D for overturning Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466072682341060620?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRoberts asks what the effects would be of moving the Roe/Casey viability line back earlier in pregnancy. (As a reminder, viability is at around 24 weeks. Mississippi's law would nearly all abortions after 15 weeks.)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466073431175270406?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrRoberts: "If you think that the issue is one of choice... viability, it seems to me, doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything to do with choice. If it really is an issue about choice, why is 15 weeks not enough time?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466073790081810435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a very significant line of questioning from Roberts that suggests he is at least mulling the possibility of a ruling that would not formally overturn Roe & Casey but would discard the viability line -- opening the door to prohibitions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466074320891953159?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Quick update on government funding : House majority leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  told reporters yesterday that he planned to bring a stopgap funding bill - also known as a continuing resolution (CR) - to the house floor as early as Wednesday - leaving enough time before the 3 December deadline.\par \par \uc2 Well. It appears Republicans - in particular senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  - have an issue with how long the funding will extend to.\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse Majority Leader \uc2 Steny Hoyer\uc2  said in the caucus meeting moments ago Dems will not vote for a CR today bc McConnell will not agree to a funding date.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daniella Diaz (@DaniellaMicaela) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DaniellaMicaela/status/1466053272238792707?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Elena Kagan jumped in to talk about stare decisis - a Latin term that means \u8220\'20\'1Cto stand by things decided\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrElena Kagan says a major goal of stare decisis is "to prevent people from thinking that this court is a political institution that will go back and forth" depending on the court's changing membership or who "yells the loudest."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466068294637690882?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrKagan: For the court to overturn a prior precedent, "usually there has to be a justification, a strong justification," beyond the fact that some people think the precedent is wrong.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466068599248932873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot much has changed since Roe and Casey, \u8221\'20\'1D Kagan said. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople think it\u8217\'20\'19s right or wrong, for the same reasons they\u8217\'20\'19ve always thought it was right or wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  has been strong in her questioning of Scott Stewart, the solicitor general of Mississippi\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow is your interest anything but a religious view?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s debated in religions, so when you say this is the only right that takes away from the start the ability to protect the life, that\u8217\'20\'19s a religious view isn\u8217\'20\'19t it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere does the life of a woman and putting her life at risk enter the calculus?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice Amy Coney Barrett, who had advocated against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/11/amy-coney-barrett-member-right-to-life-organization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly supported}}}\uc2  the reversal of Roe v Wade before her nomination to the court, has sounded in with her first question:\par \par \uc2 enltrAmy Coney Barrett, another key vote, asks Stewart whether a ruling in favor of Mississippi would endanger other constitutional rulings on issues like the right to use birth control and the right to same-sex marriage.\par \par \uc2 Stewart says no, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is different.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466066273452937222?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Scott Stewart, the solicitor general of Mississippi : Undue burden is \u8220\'20\'1Cperhaps the most unworkable standard in American law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about how in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thirteen.org/wnet/supremecourt/rights/landmark_casey.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood v Casey}}}\uc2 , the supreme court upheld the essential ruling in Roe v Wade but allowed states to pass more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions as long as they did not pose an \u8220\'20\'1Cundue burden\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What does that mean now? That means that Texas was allowed to ban abortions at six weeks of gestation, which reproductive right advocates say constitutes pretty much a full \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban - most don\u8217\'20\'19t even know they\u8217\'20\'19re pregnant at six weeks.\par \par \uc2 Conservative justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/sep/04/texas-abortion-ruling-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed Texas to undermine Roe}}}\uc2  within its borders by arguing that the law\u8217\'20\'19s unusual enforcement mechanism, which allowed private citizens to sue anyone who helped a pregnant person obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks, made it difficult to block.\par \par \uc2 More than 6 million women of reproductive age reside in Texas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  comes in hot, asking Scott Stewart, the solicitor general of Mississippi, about the politics around this case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Fifteen justices over 30 years have reaffirmed that basic viability line,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, alluding to how Roe v Wade has been upheld since the 1992 Planned Parenthood v Casey decision. \u8220\'20\'1C Four have said no, two of them members of this court. But fifteen justices have said yes, of varying political background.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, the sponsors of this bill, this house bill in Mississippi, are saying, \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re doing this because we have new justices on the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19. Will this institution survive the stench that this creates in the public perception that the constitution and its reading are just political acts?\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor continued with the question: \u8220\'20\'1CIf people believe it\u8217\'20\'19s all political, how will we survive? How will the court survive?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The first question was from supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrClarence Thomas asks the first question. He notes that the court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases have generally focused on "privacy and autonomy" rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  specifically. "Does it make a difference that we focus on privacy and autonomy, or more specifically on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466060738192195593?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 For those listening live to the oral arguments, you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear some mentions of \u8220\'20\'1CCasey\u8221\'20\'1D. This is in reference to the 1992 case, Planned Parenthood v Casey, in which the court upheld the essential ruling in Roe v Wade but allowed states to pass more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions as long as they did not pose an \u8220\'20\'1Cundue burden\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 For more background on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the US, read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8216\'20\'18fundamental\u8217\'20\'19 right: a timeline of US \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights since Roe v Wade}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Oral arguments have begun before the s upreme court in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, a case with the potential of overturning the landmark ruling in Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe court's marshal has gaveled in today's session, and the chief justice has called the case.\par \par \uc2 Arguing first: Scott Stewart, the solicitor general of Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466059996257521670?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrStewart begins by saying that Roe (which established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1973) and Casey (which re-affirmed Roe's core holding in 1992) "damaged the democratic process" and "poisoned the law."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SCOTUSblog (@SCOTUSblog)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SCOTUSblog/status/1466060362210549761?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Listen to the arguments live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/live.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans threaten government shutdown over vaccine mandate\par \par \uc2 Over at Capitol Hill, several important deadlines continue to loom: Congress has until 3 December to fund the federal government and prevent a government shutdown and 15 December to raise the debt limit and prevent the US from defaulting on its debts, causing global economic catastrophe. No pressure.\par \par \uc2 Add to that the ambitious Build Back Better Act \u8211\'20\'13 Democrats have set a 25 December goal of passing it through the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s a full wish list for the holiday season.\par \par \uc2 We started off the week with pundits predicting low drama around both government funding and the debt limit. On Tuesday, senate minority leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  told reporters:\par \par \uc2 enltrMcConnell says the US won\u8217\'20\'19t default on its debt and says the government won\u8217\'20\'19t shut down on Friday\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Manu Raju (@mkraju)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mkraju/status/1465763024208375818?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 30, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Well, it\u8217\'20\'19s now Wednesday, so that has completely changed. Republicans are now discussing forcing a government shutdown in an effort to foil the federal vaccine mandate on the private sector.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure we would all like to simplify the process for resolving the CR (continuing resolution), but I can\u8217\'20\'19t facilitate that without addressing the vaccine mandates,\u8221\'20\'1D senator Mike Lee told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/playbook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico Playbook}}}\uc2  in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CGiven that federal courts across the country have raised serious issues with these mandates, it\u8217\'20\'19s not unreasonable for my Democratic colleagues to delay enforcement of the mandates for at least the length of the continuing resolution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Congressmen Chip Roy and Matt Rosendale appear to also be taking a stand against the National Defense Authorization Act because it would require women to register for the draft as well as men.\par \par \uc2 enltr??????\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CContinuing to fund this kind of garbage is inexcusable and is precisely what our constituents want us to oppose, and oppose loudly... we should never vote to fund immoral, unlawful, and repugnant policies.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DefundTheMandates?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DefundTheMandates}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DontDraftOurDaughters?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DontDraftOurDaughters}}}\par \par \uc2 More below: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PZQrUEa6s4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PZQrUEa6s4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Chip Roy Press Office (@RepChipRoy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepChipRoy/status/1465869693001031682?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrI will not vote for a NDAA that forces America\u8217\'20\'19s daughters to enter the draft and I will not vote for any government funding bill that allows \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s COVID-19 vaccine mandates to stand.\par \par \uc2 Proud to join {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepChipRoy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RepChipRoy}}}\uc2  to oppose these immoral and misguided policies. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/b8JcOCbECL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/b8JcOCbECL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Rosendale (@RepRosendale) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RepRosendale/status/1466034202030313479?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, this is not a new strategy. In early November, senator Roger Marshall {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marshall.senate.gov/press-releases/sen-marshall-leads-effort-to-defund-the-vaccine-mandate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spearheaded a letter}}}\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  saying he would not vote for government funding that \u8220\'20\'1Cenables the enforcement of President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s employer vaccine mandate\u8221\'20\'1D. The letter was signed by senator Lee, as well as senators \uc2 Marsha Blackburn\uc2 , Ted Cruz, Steve Daines, \uc2 Jim Inhofe\uc2 , Ron Johnson, Cynthia Lummis, Rick Scott, Tommy Tuberville and \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With arguments set to begin before the supreme court momentarily, scenes outside the courthouse grew lively and, at times, heated, with supporters from both sides of the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights gathering.\par \par \uc2 enltrNow: Outside the Supreme Court where supporters and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are awaiting the start of arguments over the most direct challenge to Roe v. Wade in generations. At least a dozen different groups have plans for a presence out here all morning. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OivffPDv6Z"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OivffPDv6Z}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alejandro Alvarez (@aletweetsnews)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aletweetsnews/status/1466031231141879814?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAbortion rights protesters dance to Cardi B\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CWAP\u8221\'20\'1D blasting from speakers outside the Supreme Court. An anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protester calls them \u8220\'20\'1Cwicked murderers.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wk0u6gKU1m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wk0u6gKU1m}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ellie Silverman (@esilverman11) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/esilverman11/status/1466035394500308996?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrEnergy heated as some of the pro-life demonstrators shifted over to the pro-choice side of the barricade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JLUEKTFrkO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JLUEKTFrkO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Khalil (@JoeKhalilTV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeKhalilTV/status/1466027893155368966?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 1, 2021}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With the landmark Roe v Wade ruling being directly challenged today by Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization in the supreme court, endangering this country\u8217\'20\'19s access to safe abortions, here are some stats from \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza:\par \par \uc2 * If Roe v Wade were overturned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states are }}}\uc2  expected to move to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  illegal.\par \par \uc2 * About 40 million women of reproductive age, or about 58% of the people who can get pregnant in the US, live in states considered hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 * Pro-choice advocates and legal experts warn that fetus-related prosecutions that over-criminalize women \u8211\'20\'13 in particular poor women of color \u8211\'20\'13 will increase should Roe be overturned. Already, Alabama has prosecuted nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2015/09/when_the_womb_is_a_crime_scene.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 500 women}}}\uc2  since 2006 for allegedly exposing a fetus to a \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrolled substance\u8221\'20\'1D in the womb, even including prescription painkillers.\par \par \uc2 * Six of the nine supreme court justices learn to the right, meaning the court is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2021/oct/11/us-supreme-court-john-roberts-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominated by conservatives}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/may/18/us-supreme-court-abortion-test-case-mississippi-precedent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  advocates}}}\uc2  see the Dobbs case as especially perilous for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights because justices could have outright dismissed law as unconstitutional under Roe. But the court chose to take the case, indicating at least four justices see a reason to revisit the historic ruling.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why the Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights case is so important}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning...\par \par \uc2 Greetings, live blog readers. We\u8217\'20\'19re in for a busy day today.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court is set to begin hearing oral arguments today in a case that could reverse the landmark ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which effectively legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the US.\par \par \uc2 In the 1973 Roe decision, the court affirmed that access to safe and legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a constitutional right. The court ruled that states could not ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a fetus can survive outside the womb \u8211\'20\'13 24 weeks gestation (a full term pregnancy is considered to be 39 weeks).\par \par \uc2 Now, with this direct challenge of Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Clinic, the supreme court justices must consider whether the state of Mississippi can ban nearly all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of today\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, more than 250 doctors and medical professionals across the country signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dropbox.com/s/kdsjvv8e6ord9l7/CTP_ReproductiveHealthCareProfessionals_OpenLetter_11_30_21.pdf?dl=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an open letter}}}\uc2  organized by the Committee to Protect Health Care, urging the courts and policymakers to uphold to uphold Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPatients may need an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of pregnancy complications that endanger their health,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads. \u8220\'20\'1CForcing people with chronic illnesses, following a miscarriage, or after a serious medical condition diagnosis to carry a pregnancy to term against their will could have life-threatening consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If the supreme court were to overturn Roe v Wade, at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 26 states}}}\uc2  hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  either immediately or as quickly as possible, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a pro-choice research organization. For example, Louisiana has passed a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2020/02/louisiana-has-passed-89-abortion-restrictions-roe-its-about-control-not-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trigger law}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D designed to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe is overturned, meaning a person from Louisiana seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would need to travel as far as Kansas to obtain one legally.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza and David Smith will be bringing in live reports from the scene all day. For more information on what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake, read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What will US\u8217\'20\'19s future look like if \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  becomes a crime again?}}}\par \par \uc2 2021-12-01T14:10:53Z 2021-12-02T00:49:56Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/4e8d192e02ccc916ef9ec63bb6efc22a304d61c1/0_155_4644_2786/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/4e8d192e02ccc916ef9ec63bb6efc22a304d61c1/0_155_4644_2786/500.jpg}}}\uc2  The Capitol attack committee recommended that former Trump official Jeffrey Clark be held in contempt for failure to comply with a subpoena. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Washington, DC, today.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211201ehc10020f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
