\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights advocates vow to fight on after supreme court hearing\b0\par\par\uc2 Jessica Glenza \par \uc2 957 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2021\par 18:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leaders say they will look to statehouses and lower courts if justices allow undermining of Roe v Wade\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court hearing in which a majority of justices appeared willing to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly curb \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , reproductive rights advocates said they would continue to fight in statehouses and lower courts for the right to choose.\par \par \uc2 The supreme court heard oral arguments in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, widely regarded as the most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case in nearly five decades.\par \par \uc2 The case before the court pits Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, also known as the \u8220\'20\'1CPink House\u8221\'20\'1D, against the state health director, Dr Thomas Dobbs. A decision is expected in June 2022.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi intends to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/supreme-court-set-dive-mississippi-abortion-case-challenging-roe-v-n1285114"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 move blocked}}}\uc2  so far by lower courts.\par \par \uc2 While a significant blow to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is far from a foregone conclusion, questions from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices on Wednesday appeared to show a willingness to allow restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks and perhaps earlier in a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The case also requests the court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  overturn Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/abortion-rulings-history-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landmark 1973 supreme court decision}}}\uc2  that established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is the only safeguard for such rights in dozens of conservative US states.\par \par \uc2 Under present law, pregnant people have a right to terminate a pregnancy up to the point a fetus can survive outside the womb, widely regarded as 24 weeks gestation. A full-term pregnancy is considered 39 weeks gestation.\par \par \uc2 In a consensus shared across the political spectrum, at least five justices appeared divided over whether to significantly curb or overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 Six of the nine justices lean to the right, with three of them nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his one-term presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongress could fix the issue right now,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president and CEO of the Center for Reproductive Rights (CRR), the organization that represented \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the supreme court on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Although \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legalized in 1973 and has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/08/catastrophic-implications-un-health-expert-condemns-us-over-threat-to-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relied upon by women nationally since then}}}\uc2 , Congress has never affirmed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in legislation. That left the Roe v Wade precedent as the principal protection of the option for termination, while anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaigners have brought many legal challenges and also pushed laws undermining access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll these bans and undue burdens in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care would be addressed by the Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup said, referring to a bill recently passed by the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat would make sure women can access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without unnecessary bans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thus far, the bill has been viewed as highly unlikely to pass into law because it would need to overcome the Senate filibuster rule, requiring a 60-vote majority in the evenly divided chamber, where the Republicans would oppose it.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Wednesday: \u8220\'20\'1CI support Roe v Wade. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a rational position to take.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Julie Rikelman\uc2 , CRR\u8217\'20\'19s litigation director, who argued before the justices, said campaigners would continue to fight if the supreme court went against reproductive choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to make every argument we can in the federal courts, we will continue to litigate in the state courts \u8230\'20\'26 we will not stop fighting, because it is just too important,\u8221\'20\'1D Rikelman said.\par \par \uc2 Shannon Brewer, the director of the Pink House, said the coming months would be tough, with her providers \u8220\'20\'1Csitting and waiting and twiddling our thumbs\u8221\'20\'1D in anticipation of a decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a difficult day for everybody [but] I listened to the arguments and I think they did a great job at representing women today,\u8221\'20\'1D Brewer said.\par \par \uc2 Following what was widely viewed as a hearing favorable to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  forces, conservatives chimed in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we want to see is the court do the right thing and overturn Roe,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chip Roy, a Republican US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailySignal/status/1466091082274455552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 representative from Texas}}}\uc2 . He decried fears over a threat to choice as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwailing and gnashing of teeth from the left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sam Brownback\uc2 , the former US ambassador at large for international religious freedom under Trump, said it was time to overturn Roe \u8220\'20\'1Cand let states address the issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Overturning Roe v Wade would effectively {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/nov/29/us-abortion-supreme-court-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return the issue to be decided at state level}}}\uc2 , where much of the south and midwest would be \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/article/2021/10/26-states-are-certain-or-likely-ban-abortion-without-roe-heres-which-ones-and-why"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certain or likely}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to ban most \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Already, several states have banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at six weeks, though all those laws have been blocked by courts, with the prominent exception {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/19/texas-abortion-ban-law-greg-abbott"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 of Texas}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some reproductive rights advocates remained optimistic.\par \par \uc2 Schaunta James-Boyd, co-executive director of Trust Women, an organization dedicated to providing abortions in underserved states, said her group \u8220\'20\'1Clook[s] forward to a positive outcome later in 2022\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The pressure to legislate an affirmative right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states not openly hostile is likely to increase as a supreme court decision nears. While 26 states are \u8220\'20\'1Ccertain or likely\u8221\'20\'1D to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if Roe v Wade were overturned, states such as New York and Illinois have worked to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Polling shows about six in 10 Americans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2021/05/06/about-six-in-ten-americans-say-abortion-should-be-legal-in-all-or-most-cases/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all or most}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the House speaker and California Democrat \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe House is committed to defending women\u8217\'20\'19s health freedoms and to enshrining into law our House-passed Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Protection Act, led by Congresswoman Judy Chu, to protect reproductive health care for all women across America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added that the supreme court \u8220\'20\'1Chas the opportunity and responsibility to honor the constitution, the law and this basic truth: every woman has the constitutional right to basic reproductive healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211202ehc2000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
