\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Five takeaways from \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mississippi  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights case hearing\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 731 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2021\par 17:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Oganization case could weaken the provisions of the landmark 1973 Roe v Wade ruling\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  heard oral arguments on Wednesday in the most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case since the landmark 1973 supreme court ruling in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2 , which effectively legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/nov/30/explainer-mississippi-abortion-rights-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2 , Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, pits the leadership of Mississippi against the state\u8217\'20\'19s last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic. The state seeks to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks gestation and asks the highest court to overturn Roe.\par \par \uc2 Here are five key takeaways from the crucial court session.\par \par \uc2 Conservative justices signal support for Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions\par \par \uc2 Some conservative justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/oral-arguments-mississippi-abortion-case-begin-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled}}}\uc2  a readiness to back Mississippi and threaten Roe. Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  appeared to challenge the principle of precedent and listed numerous landmark cases where the court overturned previous decisions, such as Brown v Board of Education on school segregation.\par \par \uc2 Justice Amy Coney Barrett, nominated by Donald Trump like Kavanaugh, suggested adoption services could nullify the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by removing the burdens of \u8220\'20\'1Cforced parenting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Veteran justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  challenged the notion that there is a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that it is not clearly laid out the way the second amendment is on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right to bear arms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives question fetal viability line, unclear on overturning Roe\par \par \uc2 Chief justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  asked what the effects would be of moving the Roe limit \u8211\'20\'13 allowing termination until a fetus is viable outside the womb, around 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 earlier in the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you think that the issue is one of choice... viability \u8230\'20\'26 doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything to do with choice. If it really is an issue about choice, why is 15 weeks [Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s limit] not enough time?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  questioned whether fetal viability is even an appropriate line for the court to have drawn.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf a woman wants to be free of the burdens of pregnancy, that interest does not disappear the moment the viability line is crossed,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Liberals defend precedent, test religious motive\par \par \uc2 Justice Elena Kagan said a major goal of precedent is \u8220\'20\'1Cto prevent people from thinking that this court is a political institution that will go back and forth depending on what part of the public yells the loudest... usually, there needs to be a strong justification in a case like this, beyond the fact that you think the case is wrong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , nominated by Barack Obama like Kagan, signaled she believes Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s motive in restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/supreme-court/sotomayor-suggests-supreme-court-won-t-survive-stench-overturning-roe-n1285166"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is religious}}}\uc2 . She feared a further threat to precedents that protect rights to birth control access and same-sex marriages.\par \par \uc2 And Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  quoted from the 1992 ruling in Planned Parenthood v Casey which reaffirmed Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo overrule under fire in the absence of the most compelling reason to re-examine a watershed decision would subvert the court\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy beyond any serious question,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat exactly is new here?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Liberal justices asked what is novel about the Mississippi case when so many others have not changed precedent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot much has changed since Roe and Casey,\u8221\'20\'1D Kagan said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason people agree or not are the same reasons they\u8217\'20\'19ve always had \u8230\'20\'26 aren\u8217\'20\'19t we in the exact same place, except that we\u8217\'20\'19ve had 50 years of women relying on this right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor added: \u8220\'20\'1CFifteen justices over 30 years have reaffirmed that basic viability line \u8230\'20\'26 15, of varying political background.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Liberals warn public trust in the institution is shaky\par \par \uc2 Sotomayor suggested reversing Roe v Wade could hit public confidence in the court as a nonpartisan body \u8211\'20\'13 after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s three traditionalist nominees (\uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2 , Kavanaugh and Coney Barrett) tilted the majority sharply right.\par \par \uc2 She said to Scott Stewart, Mississippi\u8217\'20\'19s solicitor general: \u8220\'20\'1CThe sponsors of this bill... in Mississippi are saying \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re doing this because we have new justices on the supreme court.\u8217\'20\'19 Will this institution survive the stench that this creates in the public perception that the constitution and its reading are just political acts?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CIf people believe it\u8217\'20\'19s all political \u8230\'20\'26 how will the court survive?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Breyer added that the risk in a \u8220\'20\'1Csuper case\u8221\'20\'1D like this is that the American public will regard justices as \u8220\'20\'1Cjust politicians\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what kills us,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211202ehc2000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
