\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing:  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  rights advocates vow to fight on\b0\par\par\uc2 Nicola Slawson \par \uc2 1,352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2021\par 12:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leaders won\u8217\'20\'19t give up after \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices signal support for restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Plus, have you got the pandemic body?Don\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court hearing in which a majority of justices appeared willing to significantly curb \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/01/abortion-rights-supreme-court-states-roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reproductive rights advocates said they would continue to fight}}}\uc2  in statehouses and lower courts for the right to choose.\par \par \uc2 While a significant blow to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is far from a foregone conclusion, questions from the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative justices yesterday appeared to show a willingness to allow restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 15 weeks and perhaps earlier in a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Julie Rikelman\uc2 , litigation director at the \uc2 Center for Reproductive Rights\uc2 , who argued before the justices, said campaigners would continue to fight if the supreme court went against reproductive choice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to make every argument we can in the federal courts, we will continue to litigate in the state courts \u8230\'20\'26 we will not stop fighting, because it is just too important,\u8221\'20\'1D Rikelman said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What happened yesterday? The supreme court heard oral arguments in Dobbs v Jackson Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health Organization, widely regarded as the most important \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights case in nearly five decades. A decision is not expected until June 2022.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Here are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/five-takeaways-us-supreme-court-mississippi-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five key takeaways}}}\uc2  from the crucial court session yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Revealed: how \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2  could be disbarred for lying in court for Trump\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has learned that \uc2 Sidney Powell\uc2 , the former lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who filed lawsuits across America for the former president hoping to overturn the results of the 2020 presidential election, has on several occasions represented to federal courts that people were co-counsel or plaintiffs in her cases {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/02/revealed-sidney-powell-trump-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without seeking their permission to do so}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some of these individuals say that they only found out that Powell had named them once the cases were already filed.\par \par \uc2 During this same period of time, Powell also named several other lawyers \u8211\'20\'13 with their permission in those instances \u8211\'20\'13 as co-counsel in her election-related cases, despite the fact that they played virtually no role whatsoever in bringing or litigating those cases.\par \par \uc2 Both Powell\u8217\'20\'19s naming of other people as plaintiffs or co-counsel without their consent and representing that other attorneys were central to her cases when, in fact, their roles were nominal or nonexistent, constitute serious potential violations of the \uc2 American Bar Association\uc2  model rules for professional conduct, top legal ethicists told \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Will she be disbarred? The Texas bar held its first closed-door hearing regarding the allegations but investigations by state bar associations are ordinarily conducted behind closed doors and thus largely opaque to the public.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What has Powell said? She has not responded to multiple requests for comment via phone, email, and over social media.\par \par \uc2 Ghislaine Maxwell accuser says she met Trump at 14 and flew with Prince Andrew\par \par \uc2 The first accuser in Ghislaine Maxwell\u8217\'20\'19s child sex trafficking trial testified yesterday that Jeffrey Epstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/ghislaine-maxwell-accuser-cross-examination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced her to Donald Trump when she was 14}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The woman, who used the pseudonym \u8220\'20\'1CJane\u8221\'20\'1D in court, also claimed that she was on a flight with Prince Andrew. She did not accuse Trump or the Duke of York of any misconduct.\par \par \uc2 When Jane\u8217\'20\'19s testimony concluded, prosecutors called one of her former boyfriends to the stand. The man, who testified under the pseudonym \u8220\'20\'1CMatt\u8221\'20\'1D to keep Jane\u8217\'20\'19s identity confidential, said she had discussed a godfather-like figure who helped cover her expenses as a child.\par \par \uc2 He said she eventually told him who the man was but did not share details of what happened. Asked how Jane reacted to questions about Epstein, Matt said: \u8220\'20\'1CShe would say to me: \u8216\'20\'18Matt, the money wasn\u8217\'20\'19t fucking free.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who is Maxwell? She is the daughter of the late British press baron Robert Maxwell. Prosecutors have alleged that she was Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbest friend and right hand\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What is she accused of? She is on trial for six counts related to her alleged involvement in Epstein\u8217\'20\'19s sexual abuse of teenage girls. She has pleaded not guilty to all counts.\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Omicron variant has fuelled a \u8220\'20\'1Cworrying\u8221\'20\'1D surge in coronavirus cases in South Africa and is rapidly becoming the dominant strain, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/02/omicron-variant-fuelling-exponential-rise-in-covid-cases-say-south-africa-officials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 local health officials have said}}}\uc2 , as more countries including the US detected their first cases of the new variant. The United Arab Emirates and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/south-korea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Korea}}}\uc2  also confirmed cases of Omicron.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans are preparing to shut down the American government on Friday, in the latest attempt by the party to thwart White House efforts to increase vaccine take-up, by undermining vaccine mandates across the country. Clamor is growing for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/republicans-government-shutdown-vaccine-mandates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican senators to oppose a stopgap funding bill}}}\uc2 , which would fund the government for the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the Georgia Democrat and leading voting rights activist, has announced she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/stacey-abrams-running-georgia-governor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will launch another campaign}}}\uc2  to become the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first Black female governor. The announcement could set up a rematch between Abrams and the incumbent Republican governor, Brian Kemp.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Beijing has urged US business groups with interests in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cspeak out\u8221\'20\'1D and lobby the \uc2 US government\uc2  in its defence, warning that as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/02/beijing-warns-china-linked-us-businesses-you-cannot-make-a-fortune-in-silence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bilateral relations deteriorate they cannot make money \u8220\'20\'1Cin silence\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . The vice-foreign minister Xie Feng, also urged against political boycotts of the Beijing Winter Olympics.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: 1,500 unhoused LA residents died on the streets during pandemic, report reveals\par \par \uc2 Nearly 1,500 unhoused people are estimated to have died on the streets of Los Angeles during the pandemic, according to a new report that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/01/1500-unhoused-la-residents-died-on-the-streets-during-pandemic-report-reveals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raises alarms about authorities\u8217\'20\'19 handling of a worsening humanitarian crisis}}}\uc2 . Authored by researchers from the \uc2 University of California, Los Angeles\uc2  (UCLA), and a coalition of unhoused residents, the report analyzed the LA county coroner\u8217\'20\'19s records to identify 1,493 cases of people who died between March 2020 and July 2021 on the streets and were probably unhoused. The most common cause of death was accidental overdose.\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: how the Covid era changed our bodies \u8211\'20\'13 from hair loss to weight gain\par \par \uc2 Living through the pandemic has had surprising health consequences \u8211\'20\'13 even for people who have not caught coronavirus. It has recently emerged, for instance, that the Covid era has been a global hair-loss event \u8211\'20\'13 a clear manifestation of the stress people have been under. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2021/dec/02/the-pandemic-body-how-the-covid-era-changed-us-from-hair-loss-to-weight-gain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What else have these unprecedented times written on our bodies?}}}\uc2  Sore, blurry eyes, decaying teeth, spreading feet \u8211\'20\'13 the strange, difficult years of coronavirus have had unexpected effects on our general health.\par \par \uc2 Climate check: Californian firm touts \u8216\'20\'18mushroom leather\u8217\'20\'19 as sustainability gamechanger\par \par \uc2 Vegan alternatives to leather could save more than just animals. The scientists behind fashion\u8217\'20\'19s new latest must-have \u8211\'20\'13 the \u8220\'20\'1Cmushroom leather\u8221\'20\'1D handbag \u8211\'20\'13 believe that mycelium, a material grown from fungi which can be engineered to look and feel like calfskin or sheepskin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2021/dec/02/californian-firm-touts-mushroom-leather-as-sustainability-gamechanger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could help save the planet}}}\uc2 . Speaking to \uc2 the Guardian\uc2 , \uc2 Dr Matt Scullin\uc2 , CEO of biomaterials company MycoWorks, forecast that mushroom leather could be a sustainability gamechanger, \u8220\'20\'1Cunlocking a future of design which begins with the material, not with the object\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Want more environmental stories delivered to your inbox?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/ng-interactive/2021/oct/20/sign-up-for-down-to-earth-the-best-way-to-make-sense-of-the-biggest-environment-stories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to our new newsletter Down to Earth}}}\uc2  to get original and essential reporting on the climate crisis every week\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: Dancing cactus toy that raps in Polish about cocaine goes viral\par \par \uc2 A word of warning before you go toy shopping this Christmas: beware the rapping cactus. The toy, marketed as educational, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/nov/30/dancing-cactus-toy-raps-polish"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may teach your children more than you want them to know}}}\uc2 , as a woman in Brampton, Ontario, discovered the hard way. The miniature, bright green dancing cactus Ania Tanner bought sings in English, Spanish and Polish while squirming to the beat. After buying it for her granddaughter, Tanner realised one of the songs was an explicit tune about cocaine and hopelessness. \u8220\'20\'1C??It just so happens that I am Polish, and when I started to listen to the songs and I heard the words \u8230\'20\'26 I was in shock,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211202ehc2001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
